window.AKK_REBORN_I_CHOSE_A_PLAYBOY_AS_MY_FATHER_BUT_HE_ENDED_UP_BECOMING_THE_EMPEROR_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_REBORN_I_CHOSE_A_PLAYBOY_AS_MY_FATHER_BUT_HE_ENDED_UP_BECOMING_THE_EMPEROR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: Father Emperor, I beseech You to Grant Me a Feudatory","paragraphs":["Emperor Yuanyou was so delighted that he drank cup after cup of wine.","The inevitable consequence was that when the Emperor returned to the Zichen Hall that night, Wu Qi nearly got a hole burned through him by Mei Zhilin's glare.","\"Wu Qi, first thing tomorrow, spread the news about the old Song family's ancestral grave emitting auspicious smoke. The farther it spreads, the better.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was quite drunk, his steps unsteady. \"What's the progress from the Ministry of Rites on the date calculations?\"","Wu Qi: ...","Your Majesty only gave the order to the Ministry of Rites this afternoon.","\"Tomorrow, have the Ministry of Rites... give me an answer. I intend to perform the Heaven Worship ceremony with the Crown Prince.\"","After saying this, Emperor Yuanyou stared at Mei Zhilin. \"Why does it look like Old Man Mei is here? I haven't been drinking.\"","Outside the Zichen Hall, Mei Zhilin's expression was stiff.","Who in this world could possibly understand him?","Who!","...","Early the next morning.","The moment Song Shihuan opened her eyes, she was met with Baoxia's face, instantly magnified before her.","\"Young Mistress, you're finally awake.\"","Song Shihuan had also had a few cups of fruit wine the previous night. Feeling sorry for her, Baoxia hadn't woken her at the usual time for morning exercises. \"His Highness... the Crown Prince is waiting for you in the courtyard.\"","As she spoke, Baoxia lightly slapped her own mouth.","Stupid mouth, can't even get the title right.","Song Shihuan smiled faintly. Thinking of the day's agenda, the smile on her face widened even more.","Today... was the day Song Yanming was to receive fifty strokes of the court rod.","She had to go and witness the punishment.","Not just her; Emperor Yuanyou had demanded that all princes and imperial grandsons be present to observe.","The intention to make an example was clear.","\"Ah Huan, do you think Song Yanming can withstand fifty strokes today? I even specially prepared a place for his confinement. It would be a shame to waste it.\"","In the carriage, Song Yu sighed.","\"Father, Your Highness should refer to yourself as 'This Solitary One',\" Song Shihuan said, propping her chin in her hands. \"The prison guards know how to control the force of the blows; they won't beat anyone to death. Don't worry, Father.\"","Killing an imperial grandson was no small matter.","Song Yu nodded, a slight curl at the corner of his mouth. \"I don't like the term 'Solitary One'. It sounds lonely and pitiful.\"","He wasn't solitary at all.","Song Shihuan hadn't expected Song Yu to be particular about the royal pronoun and couldn't help but chuckle quietly.","If people knew the Crown Prince disliked the self-address 'Solitary One',","it would probably infuriate the likes of Prince Qi to no end.","The carriage stopped outside the Imperial Prison. The carriages from the Ping Prince's residence and Prince Qi's residence were already parked nearby.","Inside the prison, Song Yanming was pinned to a bench, with guards holding court rods standing on either side.","Lady Chang and Song Xiyan stood on one side, Prince Qi on the other.","\"Everyone's quite early,\" Song Yu said in a deliberately provoking tone. \"Let's begin then.\"","Upon hearing this, Song Yanming's whole body stiffened, trembling violently.","\"No!\"","Song Yanming looked up at Song Yu. \"Uncle, please spare me. I'm willing to be confined for life. Fifty strokes... my legs will be crippled.\"","\"You only lose the use of your legs, but your second brother lost his life,\" Song Yu said with a pained expression. \"Song Yanming, it is already a royal mercy that His Majesty did not demand your life in return.\"","\"Proceed with the beating!\"","The rods fell on Song Yanming's body one after another. Instantly, pig-slaughter-like screams erupted from him.","Song Xiyan was frightened into tears.","Prince Qi's lips turned deathly pale with fear.","Only Song Shihuan stared fixedly at the agonized Song Yanming.","\"You're just a wild girl, unworthy of being my sister.\"","\"My missed shot today is surely because you bring me bad luck.\"","The face of Song Yanming from her past life flashed before her eyes. Song Shihuan curled the corner of her mouth. Now the tables had turned. Heaven had eyes.","After only thirty strokes, Song Yanming passed out.","The moment before losing consciousness, Song Yanming's lips trembled, uttering a single phrase:","\"Ah Huan.\"","Seeing this, a sharp glint flashed in Song Yu's eyes:","\"We cannot disobey the Emperor's decree. Continue.\"","Song Yu said this while looking directly at Prince Qi.","After fifty strokes, Song Yanming's back was a bloody, mangled mess, and his legs bent at unnatural angles.","\"Guards, drag him to the confinement quarters.\"","Before leaving, Song Yu gave Prince Qi a chilling look.","Thud—","Prince Qi's legs gave way, and he collapsed to the ground.","...","Zichen Hall.","Emperor Yuanyou was studying several auspicious dates submitted by the Ministry of Rites.","\"Your Majesty, Prince Qi has arrived.\"","\"I won't see him.\" Emperor Yuanyou didn't even look up.","A troublemaker. Better not to see him.","\"Father! Please see your son, just once, just once is enough!\"","Soon, a sound of wailing and howling came from outside the hall. Emperor Yuanyou's brush paused, leaving a drop of ink on the memorial.","A vein began to throb on Emperor Yuanyou's forehead.","\"Tell him to get in here. Now.\"","Prince Qi entered, a mess of tears and snot, and immediately began crying before the Emperor.","He cried about his inability to produce a son, he cried about his deceased mother, and he cried about...","\"If you keep crying, I'll send you to see your mother.\"","\"Hic...\" Prince Qi was choked into a hard hiccup.","\"State your business directly. I have no patience.\"","Emperor Yuanyou spoke irritably. Couldn't he see he was busy choosing an auspicious day for the ceremony?","\"Father, I beg you to grant me permission to leave for my fief.\"","Prince Qi's voice was thick with tears. \"Even a harsh, cold place like the Northern Desert, I will accept it.\"","Emperor Yuanyou paused, set down his brush, and looked squarely at Prince Qi.","\"You wish to leave for your fief?\"","Had the sun risen from the west?","\"Father, now that the heir is settled, elder brother is immensely talented and governs the people like his own children. He will undoubtedly lead Great Qi to greater prosperity in the future. I only wish to live a leisurely life in my fiefdom.\"","Prince Qi spoke with great difficulty.","He naturally didn't want to leave, but he was afraid of death...","Today, that Song Yu showed complete disregard for Song Yanming's life. Even if Song Yanming had died, Song Yu probably would have had the corpse thrown into a mass grave.","Since when had his elder brother become so deranged?","He didn't want to follow in Song Yanming's footsteps.","\"Your words are quite correct. With your elder brother here, leaving for your fief is indeed your only option.\" Emperor Yuanyou's words pierced Prince Qi's fragile heart like a sharp sword.","But to secure his fief and save his life, Prince Qi was willing to endure it.","\"You said earlier that even the Northern Desert would be acceptable?\"","Upon hearing the Emperor's words, a sense of foreboding spread in Prince Qi's heart.","\"In that case, you shall go to the Northern Desert for your fief.\"","Pop—","A snot bubble burst.","Prince Qi looked utterly ridiculous.","\"You will depart in three days. That lad Gu Mingning has been guarding the Northern Desert bitterly for many years. Your going can help share his burden.\" Emperor Yuanyou wore an approving expression. \"I expect that in another three years, you'll be able to hold your own in the Northern Desert. Then, I can recall Gu Mingning to the capital.\"","Prince Qi was dumbfounded.","Wu Qi helpfully reminded him from the side, \"Your Highness, you should thank His Majesty for his grace.\"","Thank?","Prince Qi's vision went dark, and he collapsed to the floor with a thud."]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: State affairs consist of worship and warfare.","paragraphs":["The King of Qi was carried away.","As he was being carried off, he passed right by Song Yu and Song Shihuan.","\"Did the fourth brother drop dead?\"","Song Yu pointed at the King of Qi as he spoke.","Even someone as seasoned as Wu Qi couldn't help but shiver. The Crown Prince truly had a way with shocking words.","\"Your Highness, he is not dead.\"","\"Oh.\" A hint of disappointment was audible in Song Yu's tone.","\"Eunuch Wu, what happened?\"","Facing Song Shihuan, Wu Qi's smile became much more sincere. Dealing with the lovely and clever little princess was far more reassuring.","\"His Highness the King of Qi came to beg His Majesty to grant him his fiefdom. His Majesty then assigned the northern deserts to the King of Qi, ordering him to depart in three days, and then...\"","\"So, Fourth Uncle fainted.\"","Song Shihuan smiled brightly. \"Baoxia, send people to escort Fourth Uncle and help Fourth Uncle and Fourth Aunt pack their belongings. In three days, personally see them onto their carriage.\"","\"This servant will go at once.\"","While flies don't cause substantial harm, their constant buzzing before one's eyes is nothing but an annoyance.","It's more convenient to just shoo them away.","Hearing this, Wu Qi bowed. Among the several princes now, some were dead, some imprisoned, and others granted their fiefs. His Majesty was truly clearing all obstacles for the Crown Prince.","Song Yu's already good mood improved even further.","Cheerfully, he led Song Shihuan to the Zichen Hall.","\"The twenty-sixth day of the fourth month is an auspicious day.\"","Emperor Yuanyou finally settled on the nearest suitable date. \"We shall hold the Heaven Worship ceremony on that day.\"","\"Excellent. I have no objections.\"","Song Yu curled the corner of his mouth. \"After the Heaven Worship, it should be time to dispatch the troops, right? Gu Zheng has asked me numerous times when we will march.\"","\"That old fellow, all he wants is to rush to the battlefield.\"","Emperor Yuanyou chuckled and cursed lightly. \"Very well, we shall dispatch the troops after the Heaven Worship.\"","...","On the twenty-sixth day of the fourth month, a spring breeze caressed faces, and the sunlight was bright and beautiful.","The imperial sedans of Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu emerged from the palace gates. Wherever they passed, the common people knelt and loudly proclaimed, \"Long live the Emperor! Long live the Crown Prince!\"","Even more eye-catching was a relatively smaller sedan following behind the two.","Song Shihuan sat upright inside it.","She wore pearls and jade in her hair, dressed in brocade robes befitting a princess.","Long after the three sedans had passed, some commoners dared to speak up, \"The person in the last sedan just now was...\"","“That was the Princess of Fu'an, the Crown Prince's only daughter.”","The soldiers guarding both sides spoke up. \"Today, His Majesty and His Highness have personally granted the princess permission to ride in a sedan and participate in the Heaven Worship.\"","Upon hearing this, the commoners were quite astonished.","Such treatment was almost on par with that of a prince.","Half an hour later, the sedans arrived at the Altar of Heaven.","The sacrificial offerings had long been neatly arranged. All civil and military officials knelt below, looking up at layer upon layer of steps.","Emperor Yuanyou raised his left hand, signaling for Song Yu to step forward and support him.","Then... he raised his right hand.","Song Shihuan was taken aback.","Even the assembled officials were stunned.","Song Shihuan supported Emperor Yuanyou's right hand. The three of them ascended step by step to the highest platform of the Altar of Heaven.","The prayer official recited the prayer text. Emperor Yuanyou raised high the wine vessel in his hand.","After the recitation was completed, he offered the wine and performed the ritual kowtow.","Song Yu followed closely behind, paying homage to the heavens in his capacity as the Crown Prince of Great Qi.","As for the third wine offering...","Emperor Yuanyou patted Song Shihuan's shoulder. \"Ahuan, go offer the wine.\"","He wanted the heavens to witness that Great Qi's blessings were continuous, with worthy successors in every generation.","Even as she knelt, the shock in Song Shihuan's heart had not yet faded.","But at the moment of kowtowing, her mind was filled with only one thought:","Bless Great Qi's military expedition with smooth progress and invincibility.","The affairs of state lie in sacrifices and warfare.","As long as they could swallow Great Yue, a rival power on equal footing with Great Qi, it would ensure Great Qi's stability for centuries to come.","Therefore, Song Shihuan kowtowed with exceptional piety.","After the three rounds of kowtows were completed, an official from the Court of State Ceremonial read aloud the edict Emperor Yuanyou had prepared long ago.","A general amnesty was declared.","Taxes were reduced.","This was to share the celebration with the people.","With this edict, on the journey back to the palace, the voices of the kneeling common people were clearly much more fervent. The cries of \"Long live!\" seemed powerful enough to shake the mountains and rivers.","Emperor Yuanyou wore a smile throughout the journey. The successful completion of the Heaven Worship ceremony signified that heaven and earth had acknowledged Yu'er's position as Crown Prince and would bless their Great Qi to be invincible in war.","Emperor Yuanyou looked up at the sky.","War was coming.","...","A ray of sunlight pierced into a dungeon that rarely saw the light of day.","In the dungeon, Rong Lingchen instinctively raised his hand to shield his eyes. Accustomed to darkness, he found the sunlight blinding.","\"Prince Min, it's been a long time.\"","Just hearing Shen Qingping's voice made Rong Lingchen feel pain shooting through his limbs and bones. The person before him was a devil through and through.","Rong Lingchen was brought out.","He wore tattered prisoner's garb, his body covered in scars, his hair dry, brittle, and disheveled. Nothing about him suggested the status of a Great Yue prince.","\"What is it? Is Lord Shen going to torture me again?\"","\"Wrong. Not only will I not torture you, but I will also treat you to fine wine and delicious food.\"","Shen Qingping snapped his fingers. Immediately, someone brought in a large table laden with dishes.","For Rong Lingchen, who had been surviving on only steamed buns and water daily, this was an immense temptation.","Rong Lingchen pounced on the food, devouring it ravenously.","He ate for a full half hour.","\"Full?\"","Shen Qingping raised an eyebrow. \"Since you're full, it's time to do some work for me.\"","Several days later.","Rong Lingchen was dumped on the busiest, most bustling street in the capital.","Just as curious onlookers surrounded Rong Lingchen in thick layers, they saw him kneel on the ground, kowtowing incessantly towards the direction of the imperial palace.","\"It was my selfishness, my sinister and vicious nature.\"","\"I used a secret technique unique to the Great Yue imperial family on the Great Qi Emperor, harming the Emperor's imperial health. I have wronged Great Qi.\"","With an almost frenzied demeanor, Rong Lingchen laid out the events of that time in full detail.","Inside a carriage in a corner.","Song Yu watched Rong Lingchen for quite a while before turning to Shen Qingping. \"What method did you use to make him so obedient?\"","\"Just a minor trick. Would Your Highness like to hear the details?\"","\"No. Please shut up.\"","Song Yu pressed the book in his hand against Shen Qingping's face, rolling his eyes exaggeratedly. He shouldn't have asked.","The news that Rong Lingchen had used a Great Yue imperial secret technique on Emperor Yuanyou spread rapidly.","Many officials who had attended the palace banquet that night served as witnesses, adding vivid details to the tragic experiences suffered by Emperor Yuanyou. In no time, the people of Great Qi were furious to the extreme.","Last year, that so-called Prince Min of Great Yue had dared to attack their Emperor, and yet Great Yue people were still eating the grain they provided as relief?","No one could tolerate this.","Harnessing the immense public fury, an edict personally written by Emperor Yuanyou was issued from the palace, reaching every corner of Great Qi's territory:","Crown Prince Song Yu is appointed Commander-in-Chief, with Gu Zheng as Deputy Commander. Dispatch troops to attack Great Yue. Do not return without victory!"]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: Song Yu's Expedition: The Kinsmen Who Came Knocking","paragraphs":["The imperial edict declaring war was issued, stirring fervent emotions among the people.","Everyone watched to see what action the Gu family would take, as they had always held special sacrificial rites in the past.","Little did they know, Gu Zheng was already nowhere to be found within the Gu household at this time.","All that remained was a woman with a prominent belly, and a mischievous monkey, chased and jumping about after stealing pastries from the sacrificial altar.","Zichen Palace.","\"Father, all military forces are in position.\"","Song Yu, dressed in the crown prince's python robe, looked pleasing to Emperor Yuanyou's eyes, putting him in a much better mood.","Emperor Yuanyou nodded. All the prior arrangements and groundwork were laid precisely to catch Da Yue by surprise.","By the time Da Yue received the news, Yu'er would likely already be standing atop the city walls.","\"Pack your things and set off first thing tomorrow morning.\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt somewhat uneasy. \"On matters of troop deployment and strategy, you must listen more to Gu Zheng's advice. You are, after all, lacking in experience.\"","Song Yu merely smiled without saying much.","After Song Yu left, Emperor Yuanyou heaved a heavy sigh of relief. Thankfully, the rascal hadn't mentioned taking Ah Huan with him this time. He could take her along for the imperial examinations, but surely not for war, right?","Yet, early the next morning, Wu Qi, pale-faced, presented Emperor Yuanyou with a handwritten letter left by Song Yu.","\"Outrageous!\"","Emperor Yuanyou was so angry his beard quivered.","He slipped away under cover of night, and even took his granddaughter with him?","Under the fine pretext that Ah Huan possessed exceptional martial skills and could protect the Crown Prince of Da Qi during wartime.","What kind of talk was that? A father relying on his daughter for protection?","He had no shame!","Half an hour later, Shen Mingwen was urgently summoned to the palace.","\"Minister Shen, you be the judge. Isn't that scoundrel going too far this time?\" Emperor Yuanyou fumed, then quickly added, \"Your third son hasn't left, has he?\"","\"He has not.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's anger subsided a fraction. At least he knew to leave someone behind to handle affairs.","\"Your Majesty, this subject believes His Highness the Crown Prince's words... have merit.\"","Emperor Yuanyou widened his eyes in disbelief. \"Minister Shen, you...\"","\"When necessary, His Highness the Crown Prince may indeed require the protection of the Princess.\"","Shen Mingwen hadn't forgotten the look in Gu Zheng's eyes when he regarded the Princess—it was like looking at a fine sword.","As for his gaze towards the Crown Prince... it was more like looking at a piece of wrought iron.","\"But my granddaughter on the battlefield... swords and arrows have no eyes, I...\" Emperor Yuanyou was frantic. After much thought, he decided to send Shen Xiao to bring Song Shihuan back.","Just then, Shen Xiao appeared.","He materialized so silently that he gave Shen Mingwen a start.","\"What has happened?\" Emperor Yuanyou's expression turned serious as well.","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, someone at the city gates claims to be a member of the imperial clan.\"","If not for such a significant matter, Shen Xiao wouldn't have startled Shen Mingwen like a ghost.","\"A member of the imperial clan?\"","Emperor Yuanyou narrowed his eyes.","His father had fathered four brothers. He was the eldest. The three younger brothers had either died or gone missing during the wars.","Not a single one remained.","But he had sat on the throne for forty years. That was plenty of time to come forward and claim kinship. Why had they never appeared before?","With many doubts in mind, Emperor Yuanyou still agreed to meet the man who claimed imperial kinship.","...","\"This commoner, Mu Heng, pays homage to Your Majesty. May Your Majesty live ten thousand years.\"","Emperor Yuanyou looked at the man before him, about the same age as Prince Qi. His clothing was not opulent, but neither could it be called poor. His features did bear some resemblance to the old Song family.","\"Uncle.\"","Before Emperor Yuanyou could react, Mu Heng's eyes welled up with tears. \"My father has passed. It was only on his deathbed that he told me my surname is Song. After settling my father's affairs, I rushed to the capital. These are my father's belongings.\"","Emperor Yuanyou glanced at the so-called belongings, then at Mu Heng. So, this was the son of his third brother.","Looking at the young man and girl behind Mu Heng, Emperor Yuanyou raised an eyebrow. \"And these behind you...\"","\"They are twins, a dragon and a phoenix. The boy is named Mu Liu, the girl Mu Hui.\"","Twins.","Liu (flow) and Hui (return flow). The meaning of returning to one's ancestral roots was evident.","Emperor Yuanyou rotated the thumb ring on his hand. With that third brother's sorry state, could he really have fathered twins?","No matter how many thoughts raced through his mind, Emperor Yuanyou maintained a stern expression. \"The imperial bloodline cannot be confused. You shall stay in the capital for now. I will have the Imperial Guards investigate this matter thoroughly.\"","\"Thank you, Uncle.\"","\"Thank you, Grand-Uncle.\"","Hearing this form of address, Emperor Yuanyou's brow twitched.","Half an hour later, only Emperor Yuanyou and Shen Mingwen remained in Zichen Palace.","The ruler and his minister familiarly set up a game of chess.","\"Wasn't Your Majesty going to have Commander Shen bring the Princess back?\"","Hearing this, Emperor Yuanyou paused the piece in his hand. \"With new developments in the capital, Ah Huan is shy around strangers. It's better for her to stay by her father's side.\"","What a fine phrase—'the Princess is shy around strangers.'","Shen Mingwen's mouth twitched, nearly uncontrollably.","It was simply worry that the temperaments of those twins might not suit the Princess's liking and that they might offend her.","After a few more moves, Shen Mingwen couldn't hold back and spoke again:","\"Has Your Majesty considered using these twins to add some difficulty for Da Yue?\"","\"I knew you wouldn't be able to resist.\"","Emperor Yuanyou laughed heartily. \"Go on.\"","\"If the identities of those individuals are genuine, then at the very moment Da Qi and Da Yue go to war, long-lost members of the imperial clan are found, and the royal family gains a pair of dragon-phoenix twins—this is a great auspicious omen!\"","Shen Mingwen spoke with animated excitement. \"In other words, doesn't that make Da Yue the long-lost kin of Da Qi?\"","\"Heaven has sent a sign, hinting that Da Yue should return to Da Qi's rule.\"","\"Perfectly logical.\" Emperor Yuanyou, having read dozens of storybooks, gave a high evaluation.","This was exactly what had crossed Emperor Yuanyou's mind when he saw the twins earlier.","\"Thus, this war becomes one where Da Qi follows the will of heaven and upholds rightful principle.\"","Having said this, Emperor Yuanyou was satisfied.","Throughout history, whenever raising troops for a campaign, it was essential to have an absolutely righteous justification.","Now Da Qi's justification was as perfect as it could possibly be.","\"Wu Qi, tell Shen Xiao to investigate faster.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was growing impatient. Wu Qi immediately scurried out.","...","\"Father, Grand-Uncle didn't seem particularly happy.\"","Mu Hui whispered. That Grand-Uncle hadn't smiled once the entire time, and his voice was cold.","But mother had clearly said that she and her brother were twins, and Grand-Uncle would surely be pleased.","\"Hui'er, your Grand-Uncle is the Emperor.\"","Mu Heng looked at his now graceful and elegant daughter. \"I've made inquiries. None of the royal princesses are older than you. You will have your hair-pinning ceremony next year. If you can please your Grand-Uncle, your marriage prospects will be smoother.\"","Mu Hui nodded. \"Father, I will.\"","Seeing this, Mu Heng let out a sigh. In his heart, he felt some resentment towards his deceased father. Why did he have to wait until his deathbed to reveal their true origins?","If not for that, Liu'er and Hui'er's path could have been smoother.","\"Alright, let's settle in and get organized first.\"","As their status was yet to be confirmed, Shen Xiao arranged for them to stay in a residence outside the palace.","Outside the courtyard, lively voices rose, all discussing the war with Da Yue."]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: Da Qi Has Gone Mad, Like a Ghost","paragraphs":["The Great Yue Imperial Palace.","\"Your Majesty! Something terrible has happened!\"","The Chief Eunuch's shrill cry startled Emperor Mingde so much that the jade-bone fan he was toying with clattered to the floor.","Crack—","A clear fissure appeared at the base of the fan.","Emperor Mingde's face turned as dark as ink, his gaze sinister as he looked at the Chief Eunuch. \"This had better be important, or I'll send you to mourn for your parents.\"","\"Your Majesty, Great Qi is mobilizing its army to attack Great Yue.\"","\"What?!\"","Emperor Mingde's vision went blank.","\"Prince Min cast a secret art on the Great Qi Emperor—said to be a unique art of the Great Yue royal family, the 'Eyes of Love and Hate'—causing the Great Qi Emperor's health to deteriorate rapidly day by day,\" the Chief Eunuch reported, silently cursing Rong Lingchen in his heart. \"Now, Great Qi has established a new Crown Prince, and this new Crown Prince intends to send troops to attack Great Yue to seek justice for his father.\"","Upon hearing this, Emperor Mingde felt as if struck by lightning.","\"That scoundrel Rong Lingchen actually dared to disregard our ancestors' decrees and recklessly use the secret art.\"","\"Summon all officials to the palace immediately.\"","When Chancellor Cheng Guang and the other court ministers arrived at the palace, Emperor Mingde's face was ashen, bearing an expression of profound bitterness.","\"My ministers, what do you think? Should we sue for peace or prepare for war?\"","Cheng Guang's heart sank upon hearing this. At a time like this, the Emperor still harbored thoughts of negotiation?","From what he knew, this new Crown Prince of Great Qi... was not one to sit down for peaceful talks.","Yet, the majority of the court ministers supported seeking peace.","\"Your Majesty, this incident was entirely provoked by Prince Min. As long as we hand Prince Min over to Great Qi completely, allowing them to deal with him as they wish, there is room for negotiation.\"","\"Indeed, Great Yue is currently in a period of recuperation. It is not advisable to go to war.\"","Emperor Mingde nodded repeatedly.","\"Your Majesty, I believe that going to war is Great Yue's only viable path.\"","Cheng Guang's statement plunged the entire hall into silence.","\"Chancellor, your words are rather alarmist, are they not? Regardless of the fact that Great Yue and Great Qi have comparable military strength, making our chances even in a war, we still don't know the scale of Great Qi's forces this time. How can you call it the 'only viable path'?\" Emperor Mingde spoke, directly challenging Cheng Guang.","Just as Cheng Guang was preparing to debate the entire court single-handedly,","Another urgent military dispatch arrived via express courier:","\"The Great Qi Crown Prince's forces have reached Yongping County.\"","Yongping County, the border region between Great Qi and Great Yue.","Adjacent to it is Great Yue's Licheng.","......","Yongping County.","\"Men.\"","In the military camp, Song Yu's voice, carried by a gentle breeze, resonated amidst the gleaming eyes of the assembled soldiers.","\"This battle, we aim to swallow the entirety of Great Yue whole. Not just that, we will devour it in one gulp.\"","\"Great Yue has insulted our Great Qi Emperor. Such wolfish ambition is something Great Qi absolutely cannot tolerate.\"","The Song Yu of now was no longer the prince who once trembled with fear upon visiting the military camps.","\"Once we win this battle, Great Qi will become the most powerful nation under heaven. No one will dare to bully the people of Great Qi. Your parents, wives, and daughters will enjoy greater peace and security.\"","\"I, along with my only daughter, will fight alongside you to win this war.\"","Song Yu raised his wine cup high and drained it in one go.","Beside him, Song Shihuan also wore well-fitted armor, her long hair tied up, looking valiant and heroic.","\"Long live Great Qi!\" Gu Zheng raised his arm and shouted.","A tidal wave of cheers followed. A smile of certain victory spread across Song Yu's face. \"Deploy the troops. Let's take the first city.\"","Great Yue was caught completely off guard; all its mobilized forces were still en route.","Song Yu, clad in a yellow robe, stood on the city wall like a stabilizing pillar. Gu Zheng deployed troops and arranged formations with seasoned expertise.","Song Shihuan...","Raised the drumsticks high and beat out the rhythm of war.","Combined, these elements left no possibility of defeat.","By the time they encountered Great Yue's main forces, Great Qi had already captured six cities in succession.","\"Impossible...\" Emperor Mingde stared at the military report before him, his gaze fierce and ruthless.","\"Great Qi has gone mad, completely disregarding that Great Yue is also a powerful nation.\"","\"Great Qi appeared at our border like ghosts, suddenly and without warning.\"","Listening to the discussions of the ministers below, Emperor Mingde tightened his grip on the report.","\"I want the Great Qi Crown Prince to come never to return.\"","Having said that, Emperor Mingde looked at his eldest son beside him. \"You, go to the front lines personally. If you return victorious, I will name you Crown Prince.\"","\"Father, your son will not fail this mission.\"","The atmosphere was instantly stirred by Emperor Mingde's actions. Only Cheng Guang wore a bitter, distressed expression.","That Gu Zheng... was notoriously difficult to deal with.","\"Chancellor, you have faced Gu Zheng in battle before. Tell me, what is his fatal weakness?\"","Emperor Mingde's eldest son, Prince Rui, addressed Cheng Guang.","......","\"Prince Rui is skilled in underhanded schemes, the conduct of a petty man.\"","Gu Zheng offered this assessment of the so-called Great Yue prince without the slightest restraint.","As he spoke, Gu Zheng couldn't help but glance at Song Shihuan. Several of the recent siege formations had been provided by the Princess. They were truly... alarmingly effective.","The Princess truly was a genius.","\"What are your plans next, Princess?\"","\"Great Yue is beginning to fight back.\" Song Shihuan stared at the military map. \"Let's keep Yu Fan's position unchanged for now. Gather intelligence while waiting for the perfect opportunity to strike with certainty.\"","Yu Fan was hidden too well. It would be a shame to act rashly.","Song Yu only had a superficial understanding of troop deployments and battle formations, so from the start, he had correctly positioned himself as a morale-boosting figurehead.","But seeing Gu Zheng seek Song Shihuan's advice on every matter, Song Yu began to feel uneasy.","\"Gu Zheng, do you have no mind of your own?\"","Song Yu asked seriously.","If not for Song Yu's expression, Gu Zheng might have thought the Crown Prince was mocking him.","\"Your Highness, my own ideas are not worth mentioning compared to the Princess's.\"","Gu Zheng replied with equal seriousness.","A few moments later.","Song Yu left the command tent to get some air.","The sky was painted with the fiery red of the setting sun. Song Yu took several deep breaths.","In this war, who exactly was the commander-in-chief?","The next day.","The two armies faced each other from a distance. Gu Zheng and the opposing commander each rode at the forefront of their forces, while Song Yu and Song Shihuan stood atop the city wall.","\"Gu Zheng, it's been years, but you're still as shameless as ever.\"","The enemy commander's opening salvo was potent.","But Gu Zheng seemed completely unfazed, replying with a smile, \"Likewise.\"","\"Your Prince Rui hasn't even arrived yet. Why not wait for him before starting the battle? Otherwise, the disgrace of losing another city will fall on your shoulders.\" Gu Zheng's tone was almost considerate of the enemy commander.","Watching the two commanders trade insults below, Song Yu looked up at the sky in exasperation.","\"Military men cursing is still rather vulgar.\"","He felt like covering A'Huan's ears.","After several rounds of verbal sparring, the enemy commander suddenly turned his gaze toward Song Shihuan on the city wall, his tone strange and mocking.","\"Has Great Qi run out of men, that you bring a mere girl to make up the numbers? Send the little girl home quickly, lest she starts crying for her mother all over the battlefield.\"","Gu Zheng's expression changed abruptly. Not just Gu Zheng, but all the Great Qi soldiers behind him had murderous intent burning in their eyes.","Song Shihuan picked up the drumsticks.","Boom—","The familiar beat of the war drums began to sound.","Gu Zheng tightened his grip on his longsword and shouted,","\"I'm going to rip your lying mouth apart today.\""]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: Northern Desert, behold your king.","paragraphs":["While Song Yu and Song Shihuan were engaged in fierce battles with Dayue, Prince Qi arrived, trembling, at the northern desert.","\"Greetings, Your Highness Prince Qi.\"","Gu Mingning stood unwavering in his military armor, letting the wind and sand whip around him.","Prince Qi, however, had already covered his face with both hands, his eyes tightly shut, letting out a strange wail:","\"The sand! The sand has gotten into this prince's eyes!\"","\"Attendants, bring a headscarf for His Highness.\"","Gu Mingning couldn't help but speak up, a trace of mockery flashing in his eyes, his mind filled with treasonous thoughts.","Such an incompetent man, yet born into the royal family.","With the headscarf shielding him, Prince Qi finally felt somewhat more comfortable. Peering through the cloth at his surroundings, all he saw was desolation.","Prince Qi couldn't help but swallow hard. Was it too late for him to return to the capital now?","Gu Mingning led Prince Qi to the pre-prepared princely mansion and had his military advisor brief the prince on the situation in the northern desert.","\"How can the northern desert be so impoverished?\"","\"Still relying on imperial handouts to survive?\"","\"Then what is this prince supposed to do here?\"","Ever since reviewing the desert's accounts, Prince Qi hadn't stopped his torrent of complaints.","Gu Mingning's brow furrowed almost imperceptibly. \"Naturally, to govern the northern desert, in accordance with His Majesty's decree.\"","He, Gu Mingning, had indeed sent no fewer than ten memorials to the Emperor, lamenting the lack of support in the desert, how he had to both secure the border and constantly guard against administrative issues.","But that didn't mean he had wanted Prince Qi.","\"Very well!\"","Prince Qi lowered his head in deep thought for a long moment, then suddenly looked up.","\"Only a barren place like the northern desert can truly showcase this prince's talents.\" Prince Qi slammed the table emphatically. \"This prince will prove to Father that I, too, am a worthy prince!\"","Northern desert, prepare to welcome your ruler!","Watching Prince Qi brimming with lofty ambitions, Gu Mingning felt nothing but a headache.","He could only hope Prince Qi wouldn't stir up any major trouble here in the north.","......","Meanwhile.","In this battle, Daqi experienced Dayue's counterattack for the first time. The engagement was brief, ending with the sounding of gongs to withdraw.","However... Gu Zheng had truly managed to tear the enemy general's mouth apart.","Inside the command tent.","\"You can curse me, Gu Zheng, all you want, but cursing the Commandery Princess is unacceptable.\"","Gu Zheng held a curved bow, his eyes glaring so fiercely they could have been used as a New Year's print to ward off evil spirits.","\"Thank you, General, for your unwavering protection.\" Song Shihuan spoke slowly. Since arriving on the battlefield, her speech had noticeably decelerated.","Every sentence was preceded by careful mental calculation.","Seeing this, Song Yu clasped his hands behind his head. \"It's rare to see General Gu throw his longsword to his deputy on the battlefield and shoot an arrow straight into an enemy general's mouth with a curved bow.\"","That was how Gu Zheng had torn the man's mouth apart.","\"When I capture that enemy general alive, I'll cut off his head and hang it on the city wall to vent your anger, Commandery Princess.\"","Song Shihuan shuddered violently. General Gu in the capital had been far too restrained.","On the battlefield, he was like a different person.","\"General Gu, during the engagement with Dayue just now, did you notice anything?\"","Song Shihuan steered the conversation back to serious matters. According to intelligence from Yu Fan, they already knew the enemy general Deng Xian was leading a hundred thousand troops.","Another two hundred thousand troops were rushing to reinforce them, led by Prince Rui.","Daqi currently had two hundred thousand troops here. If Prince Rui arrived, their advantage would turn into a disadvantage.","Daqi was surrounded by foreign tribes on all sides, with many troops stationed at various borders. Coupled with having seized the initiative, it was impossible for Daqi to mobilize all its forces here.","\"The Dayue soldiers are skilled with shields, and being on the defensive gives them some advantage,\" Gu Zheng also adopted a serious expression. \"But with two hundred thousand against one hundred thousand, the advantage lies with us.\"","\"Therefore,\" Song Shihuan lifted her gaze to look outside the tent, her eyes seeming to pierce through the air and reach the battlefield, \"we must make Dayue bleed further before Prince Rui's reinforcements arrive.\"","\"I have a plan.\"","As Song Shihuan's voice rang out, Song Yu, who had been idly playing with the jade pendant at his waist, quietly pricked up his ears.","His daughter was too capable, leaving her old father with little to contribute.","It was somewhat awkward.","\"Commandery Princess, please speak.\"","......","That evening, Song Yu ordered the soldiers to slaughter several sheep for a feast.","For no other reason than he felt his only use now was in boosting morale.","As they ate and drank their fill, a deputy general, thoroughly drunk, spoke up.","\"General, in the past, battle formations were always decided through our collective discussions. Why is it that in this campaign, you always listen to a young girl like the Commandery Princess?\"","Silence—","The entire atmosphere fell still.","But the deputy general continued, \"I've long heard of the Commandery Princess's wisdom, but the battlefield is unlike anything else. The slightest misstep means gambling with our brothers' lives.\"","\"Old Li, you've had too much to drink!\"","A comrade dared to try and stop him.","Gu Zheng's heart was practically in his throat. \"Li Laoba, are you fucking looking for death?\"","\"We've captured so many cities in a row, all under the Commandery Princess's command. Isn't that proof enough of her strategies?\"","Though he heard Gu Zheng's words, the deputy general still felt it was just Gu Zheng protecting Song Shihuan.","Just as Song Yu's temper was about to erupt, a laugh rang out, utterly different from the deep, robust voices of the men in the camp.","It was clear and crisp, instantly reminding them of their own young daughters at home.","\"'The Art of War' states: In battle, use the orthodox to engage, use the extraordinary to win.\"","Song Shihuan sat on the grass like everyone else, yet her bearing was uniquely noble. \"The art of war lies in the interplay between the orthodox and the extraordinary. If you don't trust me, tomorrow's battle formation won't need to go through General Gu. I will explain it to you all clearly myself first thing in the morning.\"","\"If we win, I shall play a tune on the zither upon the city wall, and you gentlemen shall toast me with a cup.\"","\"And if we lose?\" A young soldier blurted out, only to be kicked by his squad leader. Who wants to think about losing a battle?","The night was pitch black, only the crackling of the campfire breaking the silence.","Then, Song Shihuan suddenly smiled.","\"Since my arrival at Yongping County until now, Daqi has not suffered a single defeat.\"","\"The record is there to be checked.\"","\"Therefore, Daqi will not lose.\"","In that instant, all the Daqi soldiers found themselves believing the words of the young girl before them. They would not be defeated.","......","\"Ahuan, that man looked down on you like that. You can tolerate it, but this prince cannot.\"","Song Yu had his sleeves rolled up, looking ready to go deal with that deputy general.","He admitted his Ahuang was indeed a bit excessively talented, but that didn't mean she could be questioned so casually.","Just as Liuxi was about to fail in restraining Song Yu, Song Shihuan pursed her lips:","\"Li Laoba, since the campaign against Dayue began, has killed two hundred enemies, sustained five wounds, and is known in the army as 'Li the Formation-Breaker'.\"","Song Yu instantly deflated like a punctured balloon, his bluster gone.","\"It's fine. After we win tomorrow, he'll have to toast me properly.\"","Song Shihuan secretly took another sip of fruit wine.","Gu Zheng trusted her completely, hence he dared to use her battle formations.","But the soldiers knew little about her. In their eyes, she was just a girl not yet of age.","\"It's understandable.\" Song Shihuan pleaded leniency for Li Laoba.","\"But let there be no next time.\"","Song Yu had no choice but to agree, his eyes still glinting with a trace of frost."]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: This Tactic Is So Unethical","paragraphs":["The first light of dawn was breaking.","Gu Zheng and four deputy generals had already been standing outside Song Shihuan's tent for a long time.","Only when sounds came from inside, \"Baoxia, please show them in,\" did Gu Zheng finally shift his somewhat stiffened feet, not forgetting to glare back at Li Laoba.","He, Gu Zheng, would practically enshrine the Commandery Princess, yet this Li Laoba had the gall to speak disrespectfully right off the bat.","If the Commandery Princess decided to quit and wash her hands of this, he would surely whip Li Laoba's backside until it bloomed.","\"The morning mist is heavy. Please, have some hot tea.\"","\"This humble general and other rough men aren't accustomed to fine tea. Commandery Princess, you may simply issue the battle arrangements. This humble general will listen and then go out to make the preparations.\"","It was that troublemaker Li Laoba again.","Gu Zheng's fists clenched hard, but Song Shihuan was not angered.","On the contrary, she felt that a fierce general in the army ought to have a bit of a temper.","Meanwhile, Song Yu was glaring fixedly at Li Laoba. Unfortunately, Li Laoba was slow-witted everywhere except on the battlefield and failed to notice Song Yu's fury.","\"Today, we'll give Deng Xian a classic 'catch the turtle in the jar'.\"","Song Shihuan picked up a stick she had casually picked up from outside and began demonstrating on the sand table.","\"We will mainly divide our forces into three routes, deploying the 'Crane Wing Formation'.\"","The military texts that Song Shihuan had been forced by her master to thoroughly study had finally come into play. The texts recorded that the Crane Wing Formation imitated the spread wings of a crane: the center was weak in military strength, while the two wings were strong. It could lure the enemy deep into the center, then have the two wings close in to complete the encirclement and annihilation.","Not only that, Song Shihuan had also modified the Crane Wing Formation.","\"The soldiers on the central route must be equipped with ample crossbows and arrows. After feigning a rout, they are to turn around and shoot at the pursuing enemy.\"","Turn around and shoot...","The expressions of the several deputy generals changed.","They were experienced in battle, but they had rarely seen defeated troops capable of turning around to shoot arrows. What was the difference between that and changing one's face on a whim?","\"The soldiers on the other two routes must combine cavalry and infantry to ensure mobility and lock the enemy troops firmly within the encirclement.\"","With the most innocent expression, Song Shihuan spoke the most brutal words, \"Additionally, set aside two separate squads. One... specifically tasked with locating and capturing Deng Xian amidst the chaotic army. The other... armed with fireballs. If any enemy troops attempt to break out of the encirclement, just blast them.\"","Shiver.","Gu Zheng couldn't help but shiver, looking at Song Yu, his eyes clearly holding a hint of accusation.","Your Highness, how did you raise this child?","To teach a perfectly good child to be so... terrifying.","Even Li Laoba fell silent, cupping his hands towards Song Shihuan before retreating.","A few moments later, Gu Zheng and the four deputy generals stood outside the tent, each with a faint trace of worry on their faces.","\"General, this humble general has fought many battles, even the bloodiest ones, but never one so... unscrupulous as this.\"","One of the deputy generals spoke up.","He could already imagine that after today, the Crane Wing Formation would become famous from this single battle.","\"This humble general finally understands. This Crane Wing Formation is just toying with the enemy. Never mind the troops on the two wings; just the sight of a supposedly routed army turning around to shoot back is enough to shatter the morale of those grandsons from Dayue.\"","On the battlefield, morale and courage come first. Lose either one, and defeat is inevitable.","\"Stop being so fussy! Being able to win the battle is what matters!\"","Gu Zheng made the decision, \"All of you, hurry back and muster your troops. If you delay the Commandery Princess's arrangements, watch your heads.\"","Inside the tent, Song Shihuan looked at the face that had been magnified several times before her.","She was the first to yield, \"Father, if you keep staring like that, you'll bore a hole right through me.\"","Hearing this, Song Yu felt somewhat deflated, \"Ahuan, from whom did you learn these tactics of troop deployment and formation? Don't say it was from the military texts the Gu family provided. I've read those texts too; they're utterly useless.\"","Song Shihuan wanted to interrupt and defend the reputation of those military texts, but under Song Yu's gaze, she didn't dare.","Better not crush Father's spirit.","Lost in thought for a moment, she then heard Song Yu continue, \"I am grateful to that person in my heart, for at least teaching you this skill. Yet, I also feel displeased.\"","\"They only know you are skilled in tactics, but I can see you conducting simulation after simulation on this sand table, not sleeping until the candlelight is extinguished at night.\" Song Yu sighed softly, \"Since ancient times, the capable bear more burdens. But if the cost is draining one's vital energy, I would rather you be carefree and happy.\"","Like Gu Mingzhu, a tiger girl from a military family, who at this age should still be mischievous and playful.","Yet his daughter was here directing an army of a hundred thousand.","Setting aside the so-called title of genius, the pressure behind it was something Song Yu saw more clearly than anyone.","\"Father, being able to do something for Great Qi, for you and for His Majesty the Emperor, makes me happy.\"","Song Shihuan put down the stick in her hand, \"Back when I was living outside, besides Granny, there was also an old man. That old man taught me military strategy and tactics, but then he disappeared without reason, so I never mentioned him.\"","\"From the day I learned these tactics until now, I have hoped every day for an opportunity like this to turn the knowledge in my mind into real formations on the battlefield. This is precisely what I sought.\"","The phrase \"precisely what I sought\" completely disarmed Song Yu.","\"Fine then. I'll go brew some ginseng soup for you.\"","Song Yu gestured at Song Shihuan's height and muttered, \"Don't stunt your growth from exhaustion.\"","Upon hearing this, Song Shihuan's expression cracked slightly.","She was at the age for growing taller; she couldn't end up being short, could she?","...","Noon, the sun blazing directly overhead.","Li Laoba led a contingent of troops and began hurling a stream of colorful insults at Deng Xian. In less time than it takes for a stick of incense to burn, the provoked Dayue soldiers charged forward with their weapons.","\"Is this all you've got? Not even enough to stuff between my teeth! Get all your men out here, kneel on the ground, and call me Great-Grandfather!\"","On the city wall, although Song Shihuan couldn't hear Li Laoba's words clearly, just by reading his lips and seeing the enemy's reaction, she knew it wasn't anything polite.","Perhaps Li Laoba's face was just too punchable, for another large wave of Dayue soldiers emerged. Seeing that the numbers were about right, Li Laoba began leading his troops in a desperate run back the way they came.","You flee, they chase.","\"To think that with less than ten thousand troops, they dare to provoke us like this.\" Deng Xian raised his weapon high, \"Soldiers, wipe them all out in one go! Let's secure a first victory for our Great Yue!\"","Great Yue, after a string of defeats, desperately needed a victory.","A hundred thousand against ten thousand—the seemingly effortless victory had clearly gone to the heads of the Dayue soldiers, who chased after Li Laoba as if he were a dog.","Finally, Li Laoba reached the pre-arranged location with the other two contingents.","Suddenly, Li Laoba tightened his reins and turned around.","The surrounding Great Qi soldiers did the same.","The next moment, a sky-blotting rain of arrows descended upon Dayue. Before Dayue could even react, the thunderous sound of troops and horses suddenly arose from both flanks.","Watching the Dayue soldiers all fall into the encirclement,","Li Laoba spat lightly.","This tactic might be unscrupulous, but damn if it wasn't effective!"]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: It's the formation I had in mind, how about it","paragraphs":["\"Deng Xian and his men are trapped!\"","On the city wall, Song Yu held a telescope, his voice brimming with undeniable excitement.","Song Shihuan glanced at Song Yu, who was acting like a child who had found a new toy, her expression shifting slightly. He looked... somewhat lacking in the dignity expected of a Crown Prince.","But for Song Yu, seeing the battle formation personally devised by his daughter take effect, he naturally couldn't be bothered with anything else.","\"The flanking troops have already charged. Within two hours, this battle will be over.\"","Song Shihuan's gaze returned to the battlefield. Clearly, Deng Xian and the others were utterly bewildered upon seeing the Daqi soldiers suddenly turn and fire arrows back at them.","\"Disaster! We've fallen into a trap!\"","Deng Xian ordered a retreat, but as soldiers tried to break through the encirclement, a series of crackling explosions rang out, and fireballs were hurled at them one after another.","Deng Xian, who shared Gu Zheng's wealth of combat experience, paled completely. That old dog Gu Zheng was actually playing dirty tricks.","Deng Xian also understood that Dayue had no way out.","With no retreat, they could only fight desperately.","But the formation Song Shihuan had laid out was flawless, and with soldiers like Li Laoba who fought fearlessly, the Dayue forces were gradually worn down, falling one by one.","Seizing the moment when the Dayue army was in complete disarray and devoid of any formation, another small team arranged by Song Shihuan precisely located Deng Xian.","The battle lasted for an hour and a half.","Until the sunset burned like fire, casting its glow, and the war banner of Daqi was planted atop the newly captured city walls—another city taken.","The army medics silently led the cleanup of the battlefield. Song Shihuan had specifically ordered that the bodies of every fallen Daqi soldier be retrieved. A geomancer would then find an auspicious burial site to inter the sacrificed soldiers.","A monument was also to be erected.","\"In past battles, the bodies of fallen brothers were never properly buried.\"","Li Laoba suddenly spoke, his attitude towards Song Shihuan now one of utmost respect.","In the past, winning a battle was achievement enough; who could afford to care about so much? Returning to the capital, tallying the numbers against the military roster, and sending condolence payments to the families of the sacrificed soldiers was already the best that could be done.","But with Song Shihuan, everything had changed.","Gu Zheng also looked up at Song Shihuan. Previously, he hadn't understood why the Princess had brought a geomancer when leaving the capital, but now he fully comprehended.","\"When we are strong and the enemy is weak, we have the time to do something for our fallen soldiers.\"","Song Shihuan looked down at the tallied roster: over forty thousand Dayue soldiers slain, with Daqi casualties numbering less than ten thousand.","\"Where is Deng Xian?\"","Song Shihuan asked. She wanted to meet this general hailed as the God of War by Dayue.","Now a prisoner.","......","Gu Zheng and his men treated Deng Xian with rare civility, merely binding his hands behind his back.","Upon entering the command tent, Deng Xian immediately began cursing:","\"Gu Zheng, you shameless old fool, using such underhanded tactics in battle! How is this any different from having your pants pulled down on the street?\"","Several of Daqi's deputy generals couldn't help but laugh. Song Yu swiftly covered Song Shihuan's ears.","\"Just tell me, did we win or not?\"","Gu Zheng's eyes held a hint of smugness. \"And you call yourself the God of War? You couldn't even see through such a formation. With two hundred thousand Daqi soldiers at my disposal, would I only send a weak, outnumbered squad to provoke you?\"","\"You even rallied your other troops to give chase. Meat delivered right to our doorstep! Thank you, God of War of Dayue.\"","Gu Zheng's every word was laced with sarcasm, revealing a personal grudge between the two.","Song Shihuan thought to herself silently, but refrained from showing any reaction, especially since her father was still covering her ears—though not very effectively.","There were some gaps.","Deng Xian let out a heavy sigh and sat down on a chair of his own accord.","\"In war, all is deception. I admit I am no match for you.\"","\"You calculated every detail perfectly.\"","\"You calculated that Li Laoba's foul mouth would provoke me, calculated my desperate desire for a victory to restore Dayue's national prestige, and led me step by step into your trap.\"","\"After decades apart, Gu Zheng, how have you become so cunning?\"","Deng Xian's eyes were filled with desolation. The previously lost cities could be blamed on Dayue being unprepared, caught by surprise.","But this time...","This battle was likely to break Dayue's backbone.","It was then that Gu Zheng spoke up to clarify. \"It wasn't me.\"","\"What?\" Deng Xian was momentarily confused.","\"The one who devised this battle strategy and formation wasn't me.\"","Deng Xian gave a grim smile. \"Gu Zheng, I never took you for the type who'd deny responsibility after the deed is done. I know exactly what your deputy generals are capable of.\"","\"And your Crown Prince here... he doesn't look like someone who could command a large army...\"","\"It was me.\"","An unexpected voice spoke up. The young girl who had been keeping her head down revealed her face.","Behind her, Song Yu stiffened. He was sure he had covered A'Huan's ears...","Deng Xian looked towards the source of the voice. It was an exquisitely beautiful girl, with almond-shaped eyes, a delicate nose, and skin as white as snow—completely out of place among the rough men filling the tent.","A young girl whom the Crown Prince of Daqi would protect so closely... Deng Xian's eyes widened in shock.","\"I was the one who devised the formation. What of it?\"","\"God of War of Dayue, this was our first encounter. You lost.\"","Stunned, Deng Xian turned to look at Gu Zheng, who nodded in confirmation.","Old friend, such a meticulously calculated plan... this old brother of yours truly couldn't have come up with it, Gu Zheng felt wronged.","\"You... how old are you?\"","\"Thirteen.\"","Deng Xian suddenly let out a strange laugh. \"The tactics of this battle will surely be recorded in military manuals.\"","\"To have crossed strategies with a genius like you, Princess, my life has not been in vain. I lost fair and square.\"","Deng Xian took a deep look at Song Shihuan. \"Deng Xian is defeated, but our vast Dayue is not. If the Princess wishes to swallow Dayue whole, she should first consider whether her appetite is large enough.\"","With that, Deng Xian rushed out of the tent.","He charged headlong into a giant boulder, clearly intent on death.","No one tried to stop Deng Xian throughout the entire process, as if suicide was the universally accepted outcome for him.","A God of War could not become a prisoner.","Song Shihuan stared blankly at Deng Xian's corpse. Gu Zheng and the others, thinking she was frightened, hurriedly moved to block her view.","\"Princess, we will go and bury him at once.\"","The Princess was young; she must be soft-hearted and unable to bear such a bloody scene.","But the next moment, Song Shihuan's voice rang out:","\"Hang his corpse from the city gate tower. Consider it a greeting gift for Prince Rui.\"","Gu Zheng and the generals: ???","Where had the imagined delicate and adorable young Princess gone?","But Song Yu showed no sign of finding this problematic. Instead, he said, \"Hurry up and hang it. The smell will start bothering people soon.\"","Indeed.","Like daughter, like father."]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: Thinking of Using Song Yanzheng to Blackmail Da Qi into Withdrawing Troops","paragraphs":["Capital City, Shen Residence.","\"Third Master, Chief Shen is here.\"","Upon hearing Nian'an's words, Shen Qingping finally set down the book in his hand. Since the war began at the front, the court had fallen quiet. Even the censors, who usually would argue over the smallest matters, had shut their mouths.","Shen Qingping had found himself some leisure time.","\"Brew tea, receive the guest.\"","He said only this, but Shen Qingping made no move to rise.","When Shen Xiao entered, he carried an air of stern killing intent. Lifting his gaze, he saw the young Lord Shen, once dubbed the 'God of Slaughter', casually flipping through a book, not a trace of a smile on his face, exuding an aloofness that kept others at a distance.","\"Two taels of gold.\"","Shen Xiao's words caused the person on the soft chair to change expression. \"Shen Xiao, wasn't it agreed upon for one tael of gold? You are being dishonorable.\"","\"I'm telling you the result of the Emperor's assignment first. I'm risking my head doing this.\"","Shen Xiao's face was also cold. Nian'an just felt so cold, truly.","He missed His Highness the Crown Prince, missed the Princess, missed Liu Xi, missed Baoxia.","\"Nian'an, fetch two taels of gold for him,\" Shen Qingping said through gritted teeth, vowing to swindle this man out of a sum one day.","\"That person is indeed a member of the imperial clan.\"","With only that sentence thrown down, Shen Xiao rose and used qinggong (lightness skill) to swiftly disappear from Shen Qingping's sight.","\"What? Just one sentence, for two taels of my gold?\"","Shen Qingping was so angry he completely lost his mood for reading. He paced around the room like a headless fly, muttering incessantly:","Two taels of gold, two taels of gold...","\"Third Master!\"","Nian'an suddenly spoke up, \"You sought this information for His Highness the Crown Prince. In the future, His Highness will surely reimburse you for these two taels of gold.\"","\"Perhaps the Princess, with her soft heart, will reimburse you too.\"","\"That's true.\"","The young Lord Shen, who had always deeply understood the value of money, finally regained a sparkle in his eyes.","He could be scolded a few times, but taking his silver was unacceptable.","Shen Qingping nestled back into the soft chair. After a long while, he murmured:","\"A member of the imperial clan...\"","I wonder what princely title he'll be granted?","And who knows if this person's intentions are good or bad. He must take advantage of the Prince and Princess being away to test this suddenly appearing imperial relative.","...","Song Yu was completely unaware he had suddenly gained a cousin, and Song Shihuan was completely unaware she had gained a pair of twin cousins, one male and one female.","At this moment, the father and daughter had just received intelligence from Yu Fan: Prince Rui was about to arrive at the battlefield.","Emperor Mingde had used the position of Crown Prince of Dayue as bait, which would naturally make the fierce beast that was Prince Rui unleash his strongest combat power.","\"Princess, what do you plan to do?\"","Gu Zheng asked. The other deputy generals also looked at Song Shihuan in unison. Unconsciously, everyone had begun to regard the young Princess before them as their pillar of support.","\"Cold-tossed.\"","Song Shihuan innocently curved her almond-shaped eyes. \"I feel like having a cold-tossed dish.\"","Gu Zheng's gaze, however, softened. At this moment, the Princess was strikingly similar to Mingzhu. When it came down to it, they were both still children.","\"I know very little about Prince Rui. The only thing I know is that he is treacherous, cunning, and acts like a petty villain. With such a person, it's best to wait for him to make the first move.\"","Song Shihuan sighed. Unknowingly, it had been a month since leaving the capital.","\"How is Yu Fan?\"","Song Shihuan's question obviously jumped topics quite a bit.","\"He's fine. He and a group of his men have set themselves up as kings of the mountain. The entire village is full of his informants. He's quite impressive.\"","Song Shihuan nodded, then called Gu Zheng over to instruct the cook to make her a cold-tossed dish.","Only Song Yu smiled and shook his head. Gu Mingliu's belly was growing bigger day by day, and A'Huan was even more concerned about it than Mingzhu, her own blood sister.","Such a little person, worrying about everything all day long.","Thinking of this, Song Yu got up again to prepare tonic soup for Song Shihuan. He was genuinely worried the child wouldn't grow tall.","The old father was quite troubled.","Prince Rui arrived at the border city the day after Song Shihuan received the intelligence.","Well... this border city was not the border city of old.","Seeing the city filled with wounded soldiers, Prince Rui was furious. \"Didn't Deng Xian win battle after battle? How did he stumble here against Daqi, losing forty thousand out of a hundred thousand troops, with half of the remaining being wounded?\"","\"Your Highness, please calm your anger.\"","The deputy general who had served under Deng Xian could only hold his nose and accept the blame.","\"Any other situations?\" Prince Rui continued to ask.","Then came the sound of knees hitting the ground. The deputy general, who had been hanging his head like a quail moments before, was now crying, tears and snot running down his face. \"Your Highness, we beg you to seek justice for our General.\"","\"Daqi hung the General's corpse on the city gate, with Daqi's war banner planted beside it. This is a clear sign they hold no regard for our Dayue.\"","\"It's simply... simply too insolent!\"","Prince Rui's chest heaved with rage. Before coming, he had been confident and proud, thinking Deng Xian would have won a victory, and he could simply take credit for the achievement.","He never expected such a mess.","After a few breaths, Prince Rui's eyes were filled with malice. \"Since Daqi shows no mercy, then we need not hold back either.\"","That afternoon, war drums were beaten.","But Dayue showed no signs of sending out troops.","Left with no choice, Song Yu and Song Shihuan, along with a group of generals, ascended the city gate tower.","They saw on the opposite city wall, Prince Rui dressed in gray robes, standing next to a person who was bound tightly and gagged.","\"Huh? We shouldn't have any captured officers or soldiers,\" Li Laoba wondered aloud.","The next second, he received a sharp knock on the head from Gu Zheng. \"Are your eyes on the back of your head? That's the Grand Imperial Grandson.\"","Oh, so it's...","It's actually the Grand Imperial Grandson!","The faces of all the generals grew heavy. Clearly, that treacherous villain Prince Rui intended to use the Grand Imperial Grandson as leverage to force them to withdraw their troops.","And they would indeed be held hostage by this.","In less than half the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, a faint sorrow appeared on the faces of several generals.","\"If you do not wish your Grand Imperial Grandson to be separated from his head, then withdraw your troops and return the cities of our Dayue that you have occupied.\"","Prince Rui grabbed Song Yanzheng by the back of his neck, forcing him to lift his head so the people opposite could see clearly.","A strong light simultaneously burst forth in the eyes of Song Yu and Song Shihuan. It really was Song Yanzheng!","How should they make Song Yanzheng die?","\"I will count to three. If you do not remove your Daqi war banner next to Deng Xian's corpse, I will immediately push Song Yanzheng off this city wall.\"","\"The height of this wall is enough to kill him by the fall.\"","Prince Rui wore a smile of certain victory, but he did not notice that Song Shihuan had already, under the stunned gazes of several generals, slowly drawn her longbow.","\"Three.\"","\"Two.\"","Seeing no reaction from Daqi, the smile on Prince Rui's face changed. Could it be that the Crown Prince of Daqi could watch his own nephew die before his eyes?","Wasn't he afraid that the censors' saliva spray would bury him?","Thinking of this, Prince Rui removed the rag from Song Yanzheng's mouth and threatened:","\"You, say a few last words.\""]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: Song Yanzheng Died Just Like That","paragraphs":["Last words?","A flicker of confusion passed through Song Yanzheng's eyes. If before, Great Yue could still treat him as a human, ever since the Yu Fan incident caused Great Yue to lose face completely, the Great Yue imperial family had vented their full fury onto him, a royal grandson of Great Qi.","He went hungry, wore only thin clothes in the dead of winter, and suffered endless bullying.","He was used as a living target for the imperial descendants' archery practice, and even the lowest servants could insult him at will.","And also...","The fingers of Song Yanzheng's hands, bound behind his back, were already mutilated.","From the moment his fingers were cut off, Song Yanzheng knew he could never go back.","Great Yue could never let Great Qi know their royal grandson was being abused like this; it would harm diplomatic relations between the two nations.","So, from some unknown point on, Song Yanzheng's wish had been... simply to die.","But he had never thought about last words, or rather... had never imagined he would have a chance to speak last words to \"his own people.\"","\"If you don't speak now, you know my methods...\"","Prince Rui's voice rang out, and Song Yanzheng shuddered violently.","Prince Rui was a man with a heart as venomous as a snake's, possessing countless methods of torture.","Lifting his eyes to look across the way, a great army was pressing forward—the soldiers of his Great Qi.","The man at the forefront wore the distinctive python robe of the Crown Prince. It was his eldest uncle, also the Crown Prince of Great Qi.","It had been over half a year since they parted; his uncle had indeed become Crown Prince after all.","And also... Ah Huan.","Song Yanzheng suddenly felt a sharp pain in his heart, so intense it forced him to double over uncontrollably.","\"Go beg Great Qi to withdraw their troops like a dog. Aren't you best at playing the dog?\"","It was Prince Rui's voice again.","After a few more moments, Song Yanzheng let out a long sigh.","Summoning every ounce of strength in his body, he roared towards the Great Qi banners that were so close yet impossibly far:","\"Soldiers of Great Qi! Do not concern yourselves with my life or death! Charge forward! One day, trample Great Yue flat and display our Great Qi's might! I can die in peace!\"","To act for these beasts who had humiliated him to this extent—he could not do it.","Behind him, Prince Rui's face suddenly turned grim.","A gust of wind blew, making the Great Qi banners flutter sharply.","An arrow pierced through the air, but its target was not Song Yanzheng—it was Prince Rui.","Driven by the instinct to survive, Prince Rui subconsciously pulled Song Yanzheng in front of him, using him as a shield against the arrow shot by Song Shihuan.","This arrow, shot personally by Song Shihuan, ultimately struck Song Yanzheng squarely between the brows, killing him instantly.","The wheel of karma turns.","...","\"Soldiers! Great Yue has killed a royal grandson of Great Qi, scorned our national might! Their crimes are intolerable to both heaven and reason! If we cannot win this battle, will we have any face left to return home and see our parents?\"","Song Shihuan's voice rose, accompanied by the stirring beat of war drums, making Prince Rui's expression turn utterly foul.","He had calculated many possibilities, even considered that Great Qi might actively kill Song Yanzheng to save face. The only thing he hadn't calculated was that the arrow would be aimed at him.","Openly forcing him to use Song Yanzheng as a shield.","One arrow, two targets.","This Commandery Princess of Great Qi, her cunning and capability were not to be underestimated.","\"Victory! Victory! Victory!\"","The roars of the Great Qi soldiers pierced the sky, forcefully suppressing the morale of Great Yue.","As a commander, one knows that a moment's delay in seizing the opportunity can be fatal.","Gu Zheng's eyes gleamed, and he directly led the soldiers behind him into battle.","For no other reason than this: the fury ignited in the Great Qi soldiers at this moment was the most invincible weapon.","This time, Song Shihuan did not arrange any battle formations. The Great Qi soldiers fought based on their most familiar formations, relying purely on primal killing intent.","Song Shihuan wanted precisely to use this method to instill fear in Great Yue.","From dawn till dusk, Great Qi captured another city.","\"Do not pursue further.\"","Song Shihuan spoke slowly, ordering the drums to sound the retreat.","\"Clear the battlefield. We've pushed Great Yue to desperation this time. They will likely make a desperate, all-out counterattack. Have everyone rest and regroup where they are.\"","After speaking, Song Shihuan lifted her gaze to the city wall, where Song Yanzheng's body lay.","A quarter of an hour later, several people ascended the wall.","\"Showed some spine before he died,\" Gu Zheng couldn't help but mutter.","Song Shihuan, however, knelt down and carefully examined Song Yanzheng's body.","\"General Gu, send a message to the capital immediately. Say that the Eldest Royal Grandson suffered inhuman abuse in Great Yue: four of his ten fingers were severed, his body is covered in wounds, and the injuries have festered,\" Song Shihuan said with an abnormally calm demeanor. \"His Majesty will know how to make good use of this.\"","This matter was enough to place Great Qi firmly on the moral high ground.","Gu Zheng left hastily, leaving only Song Yu and Song Shihuan.","\"Ah Huan, are you saddened by his death?\"","Song Yu stared at the wound on Song Yanzheng's brow, his hands clenched into tight fists beneath his sleeves.","\"No. He once tried to kill me.\"","Instantly, the clenched fists loosened.","\"When I first arrived at the Prince of Qin's residence, he poisoned me for Song Xiyan's sake. Father, I am not a magnanimous person.\"","Song Shihuan had already stood up, her whole person resembling a prickly little hedgehog.","Song Yu simply placed his hand on the hedgehog's spines. \"It's fine. 'A crooked beam produces a warped rafter.' I'm not a magnanimous person either.\"","It was better not to be magnanimous. The torment Song Yanzheng suffered in Great Yue was not half of what Ah Huan endured in her past life.","To maintain the moral high ground for condemning Great Yue using Song Yanzheng, his remains were properly collected and encoffined. The coffin would soon be transported to the capital.","That night, Song Yu got up from his tent and came to the open ground where Song Yanzheng's coffin was temporarily placed.","His first words were:","\"Your death was still too easy.\"","\"My coming here now is not to see you off. It's to ensure you don't get reborn into a good life.\"","Song Yu sat on the ground, his hair dancing in the wind, holding three sticks of sandalwood incense in his hand.","Lighting the incense, Song Yu glanced up at the sky. Behind him, a dense, intense purple aura seemed to shimmer faintly.","\"Heaven and Earth bear witness.\"","\"Song Yanzheng harmed my daughter; his crimes are too numerous to record.\"","\"He abandoned Ah Huan like worthless trash because of the absurd talk of a 'lucky star' and a 'disaster star.' As an elder brother, he harbored malicious intent, making multiple murderous attempts against her across two lifetimes. He also used Ah Huan's knowledge to pass off as his own talent, causing my daughter to suffer unbearable pain in her past life.\"","\"Since Heaven and Earth took pity on my daughter, allowing her to live again through fate's chance, I beg you, do not let such a heartless, ungrateful wretch go unpunished.\"","After learning of the past life's events, what Song Yu hated most was not Song Ling, his incompetent and cruel father, nor the jealousy-filled Song Xiyan, but Song Yanzheng.","A Song Yanzheng who helped Song Xiyan commit evil without any bottom line. Whenever Song Xiyan took a dislike to Ah Huan, Song Yanzheng would immediately offer hundreds of ways to harm her.","Thus, most of the suffering that befell Ah Huan originated from Song Yanzheng.","He wanted Song Yanzheng to have no peace even in death.","The three sticks of sandalwood incense burned out. Some incense ash, carried by the wind, landed on Song Yu's jade-white hands. A searing, stinging pain came, yet Song Yu smiled.","Incense ash adhering to the body signifies the spirits have accepted the plea."]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: Enforcing Justice on Behalf of Heaven, Never Fought Such an Abundant Battle","paragraphs":["At the same time, within the Li Garden of the Pingwang Manor in the capital.","The cup in Lady Chang's hand fell to the ground with a crisp sound.","\"Aunt.\" Chang Ling'er immediately put down the embroidery in her hands.","\"I'm fine.\"","Lady Chang's sickly face forced out a few more traces of a smile, \"I was just a bit distracted for a moment.\"","For that brief moment, Lady Chang had felt as if something was being pulled away from her body.","And then... her entire being felt lighter.","\"Aunt, your health is getting worse and worse.\"","Chang Ling'er knelt before Lady Chang, reaching out to tightly hold her hands. Though not yet forty, the white hairs on her head were increasing more and more, making her seem like an old woman.","\"The manor physician says you have a burden on your heart, but what burden could be more important than life itself?\" Chang Ling'er's eyes were already brimming with tears. In this world, her aunt was her only family left.","\"Ling'er, although you used to be quick-tempered, you've never done anything bad. If one day I am no longer here, the Crown Prince should spare your life.\" Lady Chang looked at Chang Ling'er with loving pity. \"At that time, you can tend to some flowers and plants to pass the time. Don't let yourself suffer.\"","\"Aunt, what are you saying? If one day you are gone, I will go with you.\"","Chang Ling'er always felt her aunt harbored a secret, one profound enough to make her indifferent to life and death.","\"Don't talk nonsense, Ling'er. Aunt has a matter to entrust to you.\"","An hour later, Chang Ling'er emerged from Li Garden, her face blank and her steps somewhat unsteady.","Her aunt told her she must live well, no matter what.","To watch over Princess Fu'an for her aunt.","If one day Princess Fu'an was no longer under the protection of His Highness the Crown Prince, she was to bring Princess Fu'an back to Pingwang Manor in her aunt's name.","Her aunt also said... before she died, she would clean up Pingwang Manor...","Why would her aunt say such strange things?","...","News of Da Qi's successive victories reached the capital, stirring excitement among the common people.","Also gaining fame from a single battle was Song Shihuan's \"Crane Wing Formation.\"","\"Princess Fu'an, so young, yet able to conceive such an ingenious battle formation.\"","\"I heard the frontline casualties this time were much lower than before.\"","Whether on main streets or in back alleys, rumors about Song Shihuan were spreading everywhere.","Commoners who had seen Song Shihuan before even described her as a celestial maiden descended from the heavens, even romanticizing her time living outside the palace as a period of receiving guidance from immortals.","\"Lord Shen, why do these people's talk sound so mystical?\"","Inside a private room, two bored individuals had gathered.","Shen Qingping deftly flicked Gu Mingzhu on the forehead, showing not a hint of elder-like demeanor. \"Little ancestor, then you tell me, why would the Princess possess such astonishing ability in troop formation and strategy?\"","\"Naturally, she learned it from the military books my elder sister gave her.\"","Shen Qingping glanced at Gu Mingzhu, who was burying her head in eating, and revealed a look as if regarding a fool, too complex for words.","How did General Gu raise his daughter, managing to teach her into such a naively innocent, simple-minded state?","It was perfectly clear the Princess had some other opportunity, she just hadn't spoken of it yet.","\"How is your elder sister?\"","Remembering Song Shihuan's instructions before leaving, Shen Qingping patiently asked.","\"She's very well, just her belly is getting bigger and bigger like a leather ball.\"","Great, the little ancestor had killed the conversation again.","\"What about the painting of His Highness riding in the parade that day?\"","A voice tinged with mischief sounded. Gu Mingzhu's swallowing movement halted. Oh no, it wasn't finished yet.","\"Lord Shen, you must surely be burdened with miscellaneous affairs. I won't disturb you further, farewell.\"","On the way back to the manor, Gu Mingzhu even gave herself a smack.","Why was she so unreliable, insisting on inviting Lord Shen out for leisure?","Thinking of this, Gu Mingzhu's smiling face completely fell.","When would the Princess return? She was utterly bored.","...","No sooner had Gu Mingzhu left than Shen Qingping was summoned to the palace by Emperor Yuanyou.","\"How are those new palace examination graduates?\"","Emperor Yuanyou asked first, referring to Zheng Fang and the others.","\"They've already started getting their hands on the work.\" Shen Qingping now appeared quite at ease before Emperor Yuanyou.","Otherwise, how could he be so idle?","If you don't know how to lead a team, you'll have to work yourself to death.","Emperor Yuanyou nodded, then suddenly dropped a line on Shen Qingping. \"Song Yanzheng is dead.\"","\"Ah?\"","Emperor Yuanyou glanced at Shen Qingping; this expression was probably feigned shock.","Emperor Yuanyou guessed correctly.","Shen Qingping even added in his heart: Serves him right.","After Emperor Yuanyou described the manner of Song Yanzheng's death, Shen Qingping's eyes lit up. \"Your Majesty, this truly shows Heaven is protecting our Da Qi.\"","A marvelous death.","\"At tomorrow's morning court, I will announce this matter, and also announce Song Heng's true origins.\"","Mu Heng had already become Song Heng.","Hearing this, Shen Qingping merely lowered his head. The men he had sent to investigate Song Heng's family these past few days reported back that they were an honest, simple family.","But he didn't fully believe it. Even someone as foolish as Prince Qi wasn't truly simple.","What honest, simple people exist among the royal family?","Early the next morning, at court.","Emperor Yuanyou announced the cause of Song Yanzheng's death with a pained expression. Shen Qingping immediately stepped forward, holding his official tablet.","\"Your Majesty, Da Yue harming a royal grandson of Da Qi shows they have no regard for our Da Qi whatsoever. Moreover, their prince is still being well-fed and cared for in Da Qi.\"","Shen Mingwen, who knew the inside story of this 'care': His old face stiffened.","\"This subject believes Da Qi should take up the banner of carrying out Heaven's will, to bring divine punishment upon the Da Yue imperial family.\"","\"This subject concurs.\"","The entire court agreed with Shen Qingping's proposal.","Zheng Fang and the others, newly entered court and standing at the very back, watched Shen Qingping's impassioned speech, much like Shen Qingping himself in his early days at court.","\"I have another matter to announce.\"","Emperor Yuanyou paused. \"My third brother had a son who was lost. Now that he has been found, I specially enfeoff him as Prince Heng. His son, Song Liu, is named Heir of Prince Heng, and his daughter, Song Hui, is named Princess Yale.\"","\"They are a pair of twins,\" Emperor Yuanyou said with a smile.","“Heaven sending down this auspicious sign at this very moment further confirms Lord Shen's words earlier. Our Da Qi's dispatch of troops this time is an action in accordance with Heaven's will.”","After morning court, two pieces of news quickly spread.","Shen Qingping, being quite bored to begin with, simply rolled up his sleeves and began vigorously promoting and pushing the righteousness of this war. Unexpectedly, he may have overdone it a bit.","Commoners from various regions began voluntarily donating grain to support the front line...","The frontline, where granaries could hold no more: ...","\"I had only heard of Lord Shen's reputation as a fierce god, never imagined... he had such skill as well.\" Gu Zheng swallowed hard with effort.","He had never fought a war with such abundance...","Song Yu also wore a complex expression, turning to order: \"Tell the cooks not to worry about provisions when preparing meals. Let the soldiers eat their fill.\"","Only Song Shihuan stared at Gu Zheng for a long time before quietly speaking.","\"General Gu, will the Young General Gu die of anger?\"","After all, the northern deserts were short on grain!"]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: Suspecting Prince Rui, Yu Fan Investigates Personally","paragraphs":["\"So much grain?\"","The army cook stood before the granary, a spatula in each hand, his eyes vacant.","Seeing this, Gu Zheng hurried forward and addressed the soldier behind the cook, \"What's going on? Why did you bring the cook here?\"","\"General, the cook didn't believe what I said. He insisted on coming to see for himself.\"","The cook had been like a charging goose, utterly impossible to stop.","After a full incense stick's worth of time had passed, the cook finally freed one hand to wipe his face.","That night, every soldier held a bowl of exceptionally thick white congee.","Their expressions were identically dazed.","Was this the last meal before a final, desperate mission?","\"Eat up, eat up.\"","Song Yu also held a bowl with several chips on its rim, sitting right on the ground, embracing the local customs wholeheartedly.","Slurp—","Song Yu ate with hearty relish.","\"Why aren't you eating? Is the congee too thin?\"","Song Yu's words nearly made Gu Zheng and several lieutenants' eyes pop out of their heads. This congee was thicker than what their wives had when giving birth!","Even Gu Zheng was puzzled. What scheme was the Prince brewing now?","Only Song Shihuan rubbed her ears slightly. The show was about to begin.","\"This food is all saved mouthful by mouthful from the rations of the common people. If you don't eat it properly, you are rejecting their goodwill.\"","As soon as Song Yu said this, the soldiers became even more afraid to eat.","\"Song Yanzheng was killed by Dayue. When the news reached the capital, the Emperor was furious, declaring that our expedition is to uphold justice. The people, filled with righteous anger, are supporting us in this way so we have no worries on the home front.\"","After speaking, Song Yu gulped down another mouthful of congee. \"So this congee, we must drink it.\"","\"Drink it well, so we can win the battle.\"","Gulp—","The sound of drinking congee arose from all around.","Unlike the usual lively chatter during meals, this time, everyone was eerily quiet while drinking.","Their eyes held the ultimate thirst for victory.","Gu Zheng shuddered inwardly. Since when did His Highness possess such skill in swaying hearts and minds?","After finishing the congee, Li Laoba, with a sheepish look, brought a cup of wine to Song Shihuan and knelt straight down before her.","\"Commandery Princess, it was I, Li Laoba, who spoke disrespectfully before. Now we all know your capabilities. Whether you wish to beat or punish me, I, Li Laoba, have no complaints.\"","The wine cup was offered up with both hands, but his head remained bowed low.","This fierce general, notorious for his ferocity in the military camp, was kneeling before a young maiden.","The maiden took the cup of fine wine and drank it in one go.","Placing the cup casually on the ground, Song Shihuan curved her eyes at Li Laoba:","\"Stand up.\"","Li Laoba rose like a simpleton.","Her next words were, \"Watch out.\"","The two actually began to fight. The expressions of the surrounding soldiers had shifted from shock to numbness.","Li Laoba, a man built like a brick, was actually trading blows evenly with the Commandery Princess.","Was this right?","\"I can't beat Vice General Li anymore.\"","Song Shihuan smiled as she withdrew her hands, yet her composure did not suggest she was at a disadvantage in the slightest.","Li Laoba, shocked, ran ten circles on the spot right then and there.","His gaze towards Song Shihuan instantly became fervent. The Commandery Princess's strength...","He, Li Laoba, would pledge his life to support the Commandery Princess!","\"Everyone's full. Since you're full, we continue the fight tomorrow.\" Song Shihuan deliberately raised her voice slightly. \"This time, we fight all the way to Dayue's lair.\"","Later records stated: Commandery Princess Fu'an competed in martial arts with soldiers in the military camp. Though she claimed she could not defeat him, she matched him. From then on, no soldier in the army did not revere her.","......","Elsewhere, on a mountain in some remote, out-of-the-way corner.","\"Boss.\"","Yu Fan's heart trembled slightly. No matter how many times he heard it, he couldn't get used to this title.","\"Any unusual activity lately?\"","The mountain Yu Fan had chosen was near a strategic location of Dayue, where troop movements had to pass by. His band of bandits, under the guise of going out to rob for survival, were perfectly suited for gathering intelligence.","\"Prince Rui has started fleeing towards the capital. This time, Dayue is probably finished.\"","The speaking bandit looked mournful.","\"Fleeing at this time?\" Yu Fan's eyes held mockery. He then asked casually, \"Any changes in troop movements recently?\"","\"We bandits need to keep a constant eye on army movements.\"","Yu Fan provided a reasonable explanation.","The bandit saw no reason to doubt him. \"Speaking of troops, it's strange. With fighting at the front, most troops should be there to respond. But recently, several waves of soldiers have been heading towards the capital along with Prince Rui.\"","Yu Fan's brow furrowed almost imperceptibly.","\"And recently, a few people seem to have disappeared from the city. The common folk say we kidnapped them.\" Another bandit chuckled. It seemed they still held quite a fearsome reputation among the people.","\"Fool.\"","Yu Fan's words were like poison. \"You're happy even when a black pot is dumped on your head? Go find out exactly who disappeared.\"","It was common for people to occasionally disappear during wartime, but for some reason, Yu Fan felt something was off.","By the time the bandits brought back more news, Dayue had captured another city.","The bandits on the mountain were all like frost-bitten eggplants.","\"Boss, ten strong men disappeared, all full of vigor. Probably pressed into military service. Also, a craftsman disappeared, the scholarly kind, I heard...\"","A craftsman, one who designs architectural plans.","Yu Fan's brow was now tightly knitted.","For Prince Rui, the commander-in-chief, fleeing before battle was a capital offense. The only plausible explanation was that Prince Rui had devised a plan to turn the tide of war.","He had to find out what Prince Rui was planning.","\"It looks like the war is about to reach us here. I won't keep you all. Everyone should seek their own fortune.\"","Yu Fan's words left all the bandits stunned.","\"Boss, where are you planning to go?\"","They were all people who should have died long ago. If not for the boss saving them, they would have been reincarnated already.","\"Fleeing to the capital.\"","Prince Rui had returned to the capital, so he had to go investigate.","\"Then we'll go with the boss.\"","Seeing this, Yu Fan flew into a great rage, saying every harsh word he could to drive them away. The journey ahead was fraught with danger; he couldn't let these men follow him to their deaths.","Before leaving, Yu Fan wrote two letters. One contained his speculations about Prince Rui, the other was for Gu Mingliu.","He hid both letters in the highest tree on the mountain. Yu Fan took a deep look in the direction of the Great Qi capital, disguised himself as a strong laborer, and left the mountain under cover of darkness.","......","Ever since the soldiers had eaten their fill, their momentum in battle grew fiercer.","They only stopped to rest after capturing three cities in a row.","Now, only two cities stood between them and the Dayue capital.","Following the map, Song Yu and Song Shihuan found the mountain where Yu Fan had been, but it was already deserted.","\"What happened?\"","A slight tremor entered Gu Zheng's voice."]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: Her Mouth, Gu Mingzhu's, Is Sealed Tight","paragraphs":["\"Don't rush. Send men to surround the mountain and search inward layer by layer.\"","At this moment, Song Shihuan was actually calmer than the old man Gu Zheng.","\"That boy Yu Fan is blessed with great fortune and a strong life. He'll be fine.\" Song Yu also noticed Gu Zheng's distress and, thinking of Gu Mingliu back in the capital with her swollen belly, offered words of comfort.","Meanwhile, Song Shihuan's mind had already begun racing.","There were no signs of a struggle in the mountains, which meant Yu Fan had left voluntarily. What... could have made Yu Fan so anxious that he dismissed everyone and hurried away?","Song Shihuan looked towards the tallest tree on the mountain and spoke:","\"Li Laoba, is there a bird's nest in that tree?\"","\"There's a big one.\"","\"Go check if there are any bird eggs. I'm a bit hungry.\"","Hearing Song Shihuan's words, Song Yu's eyes widened. Since when did his daughter like eating bird eggs?","He had no idea.","On this campaign, Song Yu felt he was really opening his eyes. He even wanted to pull A-Huan over right now and ask:","What other surprises do you have that your father doesn't know about?","Not long after, Li Laoba's voice exploded above everyone's heads, \"No bird eggs, but there are two letters.\"","Excellent. Song Shihuan's restless heart settled down.","For now, it seemed the child in Sister Gu's belly still had a father.","After reading one of the letters, everyone fell silent.","\"No wonder we haven't seen Prince Rui in the last few battles. Thought he was turtling up in the city.\" Li Laoba was a character with an exceptionally thick skin, completely failing to notice Gu Zheng's trembling hands holding the other letter.","\"It seems Prince Rui has kept a trick up his sleeve.\"","Song Shihuan spoke slowly, \"In that case, after we take Stone City, we'll rest and regroup there.\"","Once Stone City fell, only Fog City would remain between them and the capital of Dayue.","The letter stated Prince Rui had returned to the capital, so they would wait in Stone City to receive Prince Rui's next move.","\"Yu Fan... you absolutely must not come to harm.\"","Gu Zheng suddenly let out a wail.","If he hadn't sensed grave danger, why would he have prepared a letter for Mingliu?","\"General Gu, immediately dispatch a team of men disguised as Dayue civilians towards the capital to rendezvous with Yu Fan.\"","Seeing Gu Zheng in this state, Song Shihuan thought for a moment and handed over her handkerchief, \"General Gu, things haven't deteriorated to the extent you imagine. If you really can't hold it in, use this to wipe your tears.\"","Gu Zheng: \"...\"","The stifling-laughter deputy generals nearby: \"...\"","How bizarre.","...","While Song Shihuan was preparing to take Stone City, back in the capital of Daqi, all the nobility were sizing up the freshly emerged Prince Heng.","Emperor Yuanyou also held a palace banquet to welcome the return of Prince Heng and his family.","However, apart from Emperor Yuanyou, the only imperial clan members present at the banquet were Prince Heng's family.","The scene was extremely awkward.","\"This is Prince Heng.\" Emperor Yuanyou introduced Song Heng to the assembled ministers with a beaming smile, quickly taking a sip of wine at the same time.","Not easy. Only on such occasions could he taste a few drops.","\"Gentlemen, no need for formalities. I will have much to learn from you all in the future.\"","Having grown up outside the palace, his temperament was much more polished.","That was the first label Shen Qingping attached to Prince Heng: polished temperament.","After Prince Heng and the ministers exchanged greetings, Emperor Yuanyou smiled and spoke again, \"Your eldest brother is currently fighting at the front. When he returns victorious, the two of you must share a good drink.\"","\"As for your second brother, he passed away young.\"","\"Your third brother is now reflecting at the Imperial Awareness Temple.\"","\"Your fourth brother has already reached the Northern Desert.\"","Emperor Yuanyou said this without changing expression, but Prince Heng felt the pressure multiply. Aside from the Crown Prince, it seemed the fates of these princes were rather unfortunate.","Especially the one who passed away young.","\"I must certainly share a drink with His Highness the Crown Prince in the future.\" Prince Heng's face still wore a standard smile. \"I've heard His Highness's daughter, Princess Fu'an, is clever and quick-witted. My son specifically instructed Hui'er to study more with the Princess in the future.\"","Mentioning Song Shihuan, the smile on Emperor Yuanyou's face deepened a little.","\"Probably won't be back for another month or two.\"","At this moment, Emperor Yuanyou looked exactly like a grandfather eagerly awaiting his grandchild's return, which secretly surprised Prince Heng. The rumors that Princess Fu'an enjoyed immense imperial favor were indeed true.","\"Girl Mingzhu.\"","At the sound of Emperor Yuanyou's voice, Gu Mingzhu, who had been dozing off, nearly hit her chin on the table.","\"Your Majesty, your subject's daughter is here.\"","\"In the coming days, you take Princess Yale around the capital, let her get familiar with the place.\"","\"Alright.\"","Gu Mingzhu's large eyes, which usually only seemed to hold food, glinted slightly. This was a perfect chance to test whether this Princess Yale was easy to get along with. If not, she, Gu Mingzhu, would not give any bad person a chance to get close to her Princess.","Shen Qingping caught the fleeting dark glint in Gu Mingzhu's eyes.","He thought to himself, indeed, the Gu family also had no pushovers.","After three rounds of drinks, Prince Heng actually brought Prince Heng's heir, Song Hui, before Shen Mingwen and Shen Qingping.","\"I have long heard of the esteemed reputations of Grand Tutor Shen and Young Lord Shen. Meeting you today fills me with admiration. This is my son. Come, offer a toast to these two gentlemen.\"","Watching Prince Heng's mouth open and close incessantly, Shen Qingping mentally assigned him a second label: terribly long-winded.","Shen Mingwen noticed Shen Qingping's impatience and engaged in conversation with Prince Heng and his son himself.","Shen Qingping downed a few cups of wine on his own.","The front lines...","I wonder how things are at the front.","...","The next day, Gu Mingzhu took Song Hui for a stroll through the streets.","\"Mingzhu younger sister, may I call you that?\"","Gu Mingzhu nodded, \"The Princess is of noble status. You may call me whatever you like.\"","Passing by a candied hawthorn stall, Gu Mingzhu's eyes fixed intently. Just as she was about to pull out some silver, she heard Song Hui speak: \"Mingzhu younger sister, does the Princess like candied hawthorn?\"","\"She does not.\"","Gu Mingzhu's hand, reaching for the silver, fell back to her side.","\"What kind of clothes does the Princess like to wear? I heard the Princess often wears red.\"","Gu Mingzhu's baby-faced cheeks began to darken. \"The Princess's clothes are all arranged by her matrons. The Princess doesn't usually pay much attention to such things.\"","Really, how could this person so blatantly wear the words 'probing for information' on his face?","Could he possibly be even more foolish than her?","\"Mingzhu younger sister, what food does the Princess like?\"","\"I don't know.\" Gu Mingzhu had already begun to fake-smile.","\"I heard the Princess is immensely talented, composing verses effortlessly.\" Song Hui still hadn't noticed Gu Mingzhu's odd behavior.","\"Yes.\"","Gu Mingzhu gave a rare direct answer.","But for other questions, Gu Mingzhu either shook her head or said she didn't know.","That evening, Song Hui returned to Prince Heng's mansion.","\"Father, is that Gu Mingzhu truly Princess Fu'an's close friend? Why did she know nothing about the Princess no matter what I asked?\"","Prince Heng was also somewhat puzzled, questioning the source of their information.","Meanwhile, Gu Mingzhu trotted happily to the Shen residence and chattered away nonstop. It wasn't until the renowned Grand Tutor Shen, Shen Mingwen, smilingly handed Gu Mingzhu a few pieces of cube sugar that she finally stopped talking.","\"Well done.\" Shen Mingwen gently tapped the little girl's pretty nose.","Little girls were still more endearing, much better than stinky boys.","With her mouth full of candy, Gu Mingzhu's words were a bit slurred:","\"Trying to get information about the Princess from my mouth? No chance.\"","Her mouth was sealed tight!"]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: Danger Danger Danger, Yu Fan Danger","paragraphs":["The Gu Residence.","\"Elder Sister, I brought you pastries from the south of the city.\"","The young girl shot towards Gu Mingliu like a cannonball, yet stopped a few feet away. \"Was the little baby good today?\"","\"The baby is very good. I just wonder if the baby's auntie was good.\"","Hearing Gu Mingliu's words, Gu Mingzhu tossed her head proudly and recounted her day's interactions with Song Hui in detail.","\"You're certainly visiting the Shen family quite frequently these days.\"","\"Father said before he left that I should behave. If I really got too restless, I could go play at the Shen family,\" Gu Mingzhu mumbled. Gu Mingliu, however, laughed until she was bent over.","Their father's original intention was for Mingzhu to stay quietly at home. Thinking that Mingzhu had always been afraid of Third Young Master Shen, he figured adding that extra line wouldn't make a difference.","Who would have thought this little girl would get so bored she actually went and sought out the Shen family.","\"If you're truly bored, write a letter to the Commandery Princess.\"","\"Write a letter?\" Gu Mingzhu tilted her head. \"But the Commandery Princess is busy with troop deployments and battle formations now. It's very mentally taxing. My letter would disturb her.\"","\"It won't.\"","In the candlelight, Gu Mingliu's face took on a hint of the serenity unique to a mother-to-be. \"Letting the Commandery Princess know that Mingzhu misses her will make her happy too.\"","Any string kept taut for too long will snap.","She hoped Mingzhu's letter could bring the Commandery Princess a moment of relaxation and peace.","Gu Mingzhu nodded upon hearing this and scampered off towards the study.","......","When Song Shihuan received Gu Mingzhu's letter, the army had just captured Stone City and was facing the Great Yue capital across the expanse of Mist City.","\"Commandery Princess, a letter from the capital.\"","At first, everyone thought it was just an ordinary letter.","Until...","Song Shihuan accidentally shook the letter open, fully unfurling it. Its total length... was about as long as Song Yu was tall.","It was actually a letter written on a scroll.","Everyone looked at Gu Zheng. Was the youngest daughter of General Gu's family this... bold?","Even Song Yu looked on with disdain. He and A-Huan had already agreed she would explain the battle formations to him later. This \"letter\" would likely take A-Huan a full hour to read.","Only Song Shihuan wore a rare, almost childlike expression of delight. She dismissed everyone, even her own father, Song Yu, who was unceremoniously pushed out of the command tent.","Outside the tent, Song Yu tilted his head back at a perfect angle, refusing to let his tears fall.","Inside the tent, Song Shihuan began to read the letter with great relish.","In the letter, Gu Mingzhu talked about everyone. She mentioned how boring Shen Qingping was, how he ruthlessly exploited Zheng Fang and the others, and recounted the events surrounding the newly minted Prince Heng, emphasizing what a principled confidante she was.","It made Song Shihuan laugh out loud.","At the end of the letter, there were clearly a few drops of ink, evidence of hesitation when writing.","Song Shihuan's gaze fell upon it, and her breathing softened.","\"Elder Sister has been spacing out a lot lately. The nursemaid says she could give birth at any time. I think Elder Sister misses Brother-in-Law. She always says he wants a daughter.\"","A quarter of an hour later, Song Shihuan emerged from the tent.","\"Commandery Princess, did Mingzhu mention me in the letter?\"","Song Shihuan shook her head.","Gu Zheng's heart shattered.","\"Has the team we sent out reported back?\"","Seeing no one answer, the color in Song Shihuan's eyes deepened inch by inch. It seemed the matter was indeed tricky.","......","The matter was indeed tricky, so tricky that even Yu Fan took a good while to digest the reality before his eyes.","Prince Rui was actually digging an underground tunnel from the Great Yue capital to Mist City.","“What are you staring at? Prince Rui has given the order. The tunnel must be completed within half a month, or it’s execution of the nine familial generations.”","A whip lashed towards a sickly-looking man among the laborers. Yu Fan's figure flashed, blocking the whip for the man.","The whip-wielding overseer sneered at the sight, seemingly mocking Yu Fan's overestimation of his own strength.","Yu Fan, holding a shovel, mimicked the others and dug, his mind racing on how to get a message to Great Qi.","Prince Rui's scheme was utterly vicious.","Knowing that Great Qi was now unstoppable and Great Yue powerless to resist, he was abandoning cities to set up this underground tunnel.","If the advancing Great Qi forces, having captured cities one after another, remained unaware, they would attack and take Mist City as before, then deploy troops to besiege the Great Yue capital.","If at that moment, Great Yue's divine troops suddenly descended from the heavens into Mist City via the tunnel, striking Great Qi from behind...","The veins on Yu Fan's arm bulged.","But the tunnel diggers were under extremely tight guard, with no chance to escape.","Thus, a stalemate ensued.","Great Qi, after capturing Stone City, rested and regrouped there, showing no intention to advance further. Great Yue also did not take the initiative to attack.","Until the tunnel was completed.","\"Your Highness, how should we deal with these workers?\"","Prince Rui held a wine cup. \"Conscript them. Next time we go to battle, have these men charge at the very front.\"","Clearly, Prince Rui intended for them to die.","\"Have the archers on the city walls aim at these men when the time comes. Leave no survivors.\"","The secret of the tunnel must not get out.","\"Yes.\"","Prince Rui's subordinate showed no surprise at the order and continued, \"Great Qi currently shows no intention to continue their attack. What should we do?\"","\"If they don't want to fight, then we'll take the initiative and fight them.\" A ruthless glint flashed in Prince Rui's eyes. No matter what, he had to force Great Qi into his trap.","The Crane Wing formation?","Let's see how it fares against this prince's Tunnel formation.","Meanwhile, the people Song Shihuan had sent out finally made contact with Yu Fan.","\"Young Master Yu.\"","Yu Fan looked at the four men before him, also disguised as diggers, his eyes wide with shock.","\"The Commandery Princess sent a team to find you. The four of us managed to infiltrate here,\" the leader said, glancing around to ensure safety before speaking. \"One more is blending in with the army. He will find a way to get you out.\"","Hearing this, a strong hope ignited in Yu Fan's eyes. It seemed the Commandery Princess had found the message he left.","\"Great Yue will initiate battle tomorrow. They plan to have us tunnel diggers charge at the front, then have us shot and killed. So we must escape tonight.\"","Upon hearing this, Yu Fan's pupils contracted sharply, but he did not respond.","Night fell. Yu Fan was stopped by the overseer who had whipped him before.","\"If it isn't 'Tiger Head,' who loves taking whips for the weak and sick.\"","The overseer held his long whip. \"I heard you're going to the battlefield tomorrow. I came tonight specifically to... see you off.\"","He emphasized the last few words deliberately. The next second, the whip lashed towards Yu Fan.","\"Don't kill him. They need a headcount tomorrow,\" another man said with a laugh. \"Just vent your anger, that's enough.\"","\"Don't worry, I know my own strength. He enjoys the taste of the whip.\"","Lash after lash, Yu Fan dared not fight back, fearing he might reveal his capabilities.","In the shadows, the four men clenched their fists. Only when blood began to seep through the back of Yu Fan's clothes did the overseer reluctantly stop, seemingly unsatisfied.","\"Are you alright?\"","Yu Fan shook his head. \"I'm fine.\"","\"Young Master Yu, shall we proceed with the original plan?\"","But Yu Fan shook his head again:","\"You all go ahead with the original plan.\""]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: What I Want to Win for Da Qi Is the People's Support","paragraphs":["\"And what about you?\"","Facing the questioning from the four men, Yu Fan only smiled. Under the moonlight, his face was frighteningly pale.","\"I have more important matters to attend to.\"","\"After you return, tell the Princess that when the battle begins tomorrow, the soldiers charging at the front must hold shields to receive and protect the conscripted laborers forced to dig the trenches. We also need a dedicated team to disrupt the archers on the city walls who will be shooting at these laborers.\"","Shrouded in night, the four could barely make out Yu Fan's features, yet the scent of blood in the air grew increasingly thick.","\"Master Yu, our mission on this trip is to bring you back to Daqi.\"","That was the military order.","\"Thank you for your kindness, but I must stay. I am not a citizen of Dayue, but the other laborers are. As long as even one of them survives, they can stand up and denounce the Dayue imperial family's callous indifference. When that happens, what our Daqi will win is... the people's hearts.\"","What he wanted to win for Daqi was the people's hearts.","After capturing the city, if the common people revolt, should Daqi suppress them or not?","If they can smoothly make the people of Dayue submit, how many fewer Daqi soldiers would have to die?","Emotions flickered repeatedly in Yu Fan's eyes before settling back into calm.","\"If I ultimately do not return alive to Daqi, tell my wife for me... I've chosen a name for our unborn child: A'Tuan.\"","Whether a boy or a girl, they would be called A'Tuan—the 'Tuan' for reunion.","The eyes of the four Daqi soldiers were bloodshot. Seeing this, Yu Fan straightened his clothes and bowed deeply to them.","\"The journey ahead is fraught with peril. Please, by all means necessary, return alive to Daqi and deliver my message to the Princess.\"","Watching the four figures disappear into the distance, Yu Fan finally allowed his back to bend. Pain—a piercing, heart-wrenching pain—radiated from his back.","Yu Fan suddenly gave a wry smile.","During his time in Dayue, he had come to know simple, honest villagers and sworn brothers willing to lay down their lives for each other. So, he had arranged for the villagers' evacuation beforehand and urged his brothers to seek their own paths.","In any war, the ones at fault are never the common people.","Yu Fan rested on the spot for a quarter of an hour before heading towards the dilapidated hut. He needed to inform the laborers in advance, to prepare them for tomorrow.","......","Deep in the night, all was silent.","The gates of Stone City were pounded upon. As they opened, a soldier, looking like a man of blood, collapsed to the ground with a thud.","\"Your Highness... Princess...\"","Li Laoba rushed over, his eyes narrowing in shock. \"Mao Lin, how are you so badly wounded?\"","The young soldier called Mao Lin clutched Li Laoba's hand desperately. \"See His Highness... and the Princess...\"","Song Yu and Song Shihuan had run all the way there.","Upon seeing them, the young soldier swallowed the blood in his mouth. \"Dayue has dug tunnels from the capital to Fog City. They plan to lure our troops into Fog City today and trap us in their encirclement.\"","\"When the battle starts...\"","The young soldier's eyes were already beginning to glaze over. He bit the tip of his tongue to stay conscious.","\"...the front line of their charge will be the laborers who dug the tunnels. Master Yu is among them. The Dayue soldiers on the city walls will also shoot to kill these laborers... leaving no survivors.\"","\"Master Yu wants to save them, to win the people's hearts... Tomorrow, use shields to receive them, disrupt... disrupt the archers...\"","\"The child... the child's name is A'Tuan... the 'Tuan' for reunion.\"","With that, the young soldier breathed his last.","He was the youngest, so the other three had covered his escape. Although he hadn't fulfilled the mission of bringing Master Yu back, he probably still... served some purpose.","Thud—","Li Laoba's fist slammed hard into the ground. Beside him, Gu Zheng's temples throbbed with bulging veins.","\"He just got married this year... didn't even have a child yet.\"","Li Laoba's choked sob made the air grow even stiller. Song Shihuan reached out and closed the young soldier's eyes. \"Record his military merits.\"","\"Come with me to the command tent to arrange the battle formation.\"","It seemed Song Shihuan was the first to react.","But Song Yu, following behind her, clearly saw her hands trembling violently.","At this moment, only one thought filled Song Shihuan's mind: she must beat the Dayue imperial family down so thoroughly they could never stand straight again.","Avenge Daqi's brave sons.","It wasn't until the first light of dawn that everyone finally emerged from Song Shihuan's command tent.","\"Everyone, go get some rest.\"","Gu Zheng, who had walked out, wiped his face and let the cool morning breeze wash over him. He wandered aimlessly. How could he possibly sleep?","They had just strategized so many ways to rescue the laborers, each one perilous and risky.","And Yu Fan, who insisted on protecting the laborers under such circumstances... did he still have any chance of survival?","Gu Zheng suddenly felt a terrible tightness in his throat.","If the worst really happened, how could he ever face Ming Liu?","\"General Gu, the Princess summons you urgently.\"","Gu Zheng was taken aback. It hadn't even been a quarter of an hour. Why was the Princess summoning him?","......","The laborers arrived at Fog City amidst the ranks of soldiers. Seizing a lull while the army adjusted its formation, Yu Fan reminded everyone once more:","\"Remember the posture I described last night?\"","\"Remember. We must bend low and stick close to the person behind us,\" one laborer spoke up. \"And quickly take cover behind the Daqi soldiers' shields.\"","\"But we are Dayue citizens. Why should Daqi protect us?\"","Yu Fan smiled. \"Survival is what matters.\"","\"You always looked out for us while digging the tunnels, taking the lashes meant for us. You walk at the very front later. We'll protect you as we move.\"","Seeing everyone begin to agree, the smile on Yu Fan's face widened again. \"The younger ones and those who are nimble, stand at the front. I'll bring up the rear.\"","\"Those in the very last row must stay close to the Dayue soldiers, making it hard for those on the wall to take aim.\"","Seeing the worried looks directed at him, Yu Fan appeared rather nonchalant. \"Don't worry. A master once told my fortune. My fate is exceptionally hardy.\"","Noon, the time when the sun was fiercest.","The Dayue soldiers in Fog City awaited Prince Rui's command. But suddenly, war drums sounded—it was Daqi choosing to take the initiative and attack at this very moment.","\"Excellent! To think they'd deliver themselves to our doorstep. Proceed according to the original plan,\" Prince Rui laughed, as the beauty beside him fed a peeled grape into his mouth.","The gates of Fog City slowly opened. Just as Yu Fan had said, standing at the very front were laborers without even a scrap of armor.","Through the spyglass, Song Shihuan spotted Yu Fan at once, standing in the very last row of laborers.","Instantly, tears welled up in Song Shihuan's eyes.","At the very moment the battle horn sounded, a cry of pain also echoed from the Gu residence in the capital.","\"Elder Sister, what's wrong?\"","Gu Mingliu rushed in frantically, tripping over a chair and falling to the floor.","Gu Mingzhu's face was deathly pale and covered in sweat, yet she managed a reassuring smile for Gu Mingliu.","\"I think... I think the baby is coming.\""]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: Dawn and New Life: The Delivery of Gu Mingliu","paragraphs":["\"My good child, how is your elder sister doing?\"","Gu Mingzhu, who had been standing outside the house utterly distraught, immediately burst into tears upon hearing this voice, her tears falling like broken strings of pearls.","\"Lady Shen, the midwife is inside. Elder sister seems to be in great pain.\"","Listening to Gu Mingliu's cries of pain, Lady Shen steadied her own nerves. \"Don't be afraid, Mingzhu. I'll go in and stay with your elder sister. I gave birth to three children, all safe and sound. Your sister will surely be fine.\"","Seeing Lady Shen enter the room, Gu Mingzhu finally relaxed her tense body. As if remembering something, she darted off towards the Gu family's armory.","A quarter of an hour later, Gu Mingzhu returned to Gu Mingliu's courtyard carrying the long spear Yu Fan always used.","Thud—","The spear was planted firmly on the ground.","It seemed to be standing guard over the courtyard in its master's stead.","With the spear here, evil spirits would keep their distance.","Not long after, Yingchun arrived, and with her came Mei Zhilin, who had rushed over in haste.","\"Second Young Lady, don't be afraid. The Commandery Princess gave instructions beforehand. Once Lady Gu went into labor, we were to immediately summon Physician Mei from the palace.\"","Yingchun also entered the room, while Mei Zhilin stood outside listening to her describe Gu Mingliu's condition before prescribing a formula.","The last trace of fear in Gu Mingzhu's heart gradually faded away.","Bathed in sunlight, the little girl holding the spear, her face streaked with tears and sniffles, cried until her eyes were swollen red like walnuts.","So, before leaving, the Commandery Princess had also made arrangements for the Gu family's affairs.","......","Meanwhile, on the battlefields near Stone City and Mist City.","The two armies faced each other. Gu Zheng wore a rare look of solemnity, even skipping the usual pre-battle exchange of taunts.","As the war banner was waved, the Daqi formation shifted into a configuration never before seen by the Dayue forces. The soldiers at the front held not swords or blades for charging, but shields.","This left the Dayue side utterly bewildered.","\"Attack!\"","Gu Zheng's voice rang out, announcing the start of the battle.","The conscripted laborers at the front of the Dayue ranks were forced into the fray. These men, who had never seen battle before, felt their legs go weak, advancing with unusual slowness.","\"Move forward. Don't look back.\"","Yu Fan's voice suddenly boomed, exploding in the ears of the conscripts like a bomb. All of them mustered every ounce of strength to press forward, charging straight towards the Daqi soldiers' shields.","Seeing the first conscript successfully received, the Dayue general sensed something was wrong.","\"There's a traitor! Seize the traitor! Kill all the conscripts on sight!\"","At the same moment, the Dayue soldiers on the city wall received the order to loose their arrows.","Immediately, many blades and arrows were aimed at Yu Fan.","Just then, the beat of the Daqi war drums suddenly grew rapid and dense. The front-line Daqi soldiers each produced something utterly unexpected.","Large bronze mirrors.","It was high noon, the time of the fiercest sunlight. The light reflected off the bronze mirrors, blinding the Dayue archers on the walls. Their vision filled with glaring beams, they could only shoot based on instinct.","Gu Zheng galloped over on horseback and tossed a sword to Yu Fan:","\"Catch.\"","The appearance of the bronze mirrors ignited a fierce will to survive in Yu Fan's eyes. He gripped the sword and charged towards the Dayue soldiers.","Yu Fan fought with a blood-red fury.","Li Laoba and the other officers also fought with a blood-red fury.","Dayue wanted to flee.","To be precise, they weren't fleeing because they had prepared escape tunnels in Mist City in advance; they were being scared away by the sheer momentum of the Daqi forces.","But there was no escape.","The Dayue general who had sensed something amiss had his throat slit by Yu Fan's sword.","On the battlefield, the Dayue soldiers were all killed to the last man, except for those who surrendered.","Only upon hearing the Daqi signal to retreat did Yu Fan, covered in wounds, collapse heavily to the ground.","Before falling, Yu Fan saw Gu Zheng rushing towards him with a look of horror.","Yu Fan thought to himself.","This time, he had fulfilled his mission without dishonor.","......","\"All sixty thousand Dayue soldiers have been captured by us. Ten of the conscripted laborers were rescued.\"","Listening to the battle report, Song Shihuan nodded. \"Have the troops rest where they are. At dawn tomorrow, we launch another attack—a retaliatory one.\"","In this life, Song Shihuan never considered herself a good person.","Those who struck her people, she would repay a thousandfold.","\"If not for the Commandery Princess devising the plan with the bronze mirrors and ordering the attack at high noon when the light was strongest, we certainly wouldn't have succeeded so smoothly.\"","Li Laoba's wounds had been hastily bandaged. He had now become one of Song Shihuan's most devoted supporters.","What kind of celestial being could conceive such a method to turn the tide?","He couldn't have thought of it even if he lived to two hundred!","The Commandery Princess was born to be a commander.","At that moment, a commotion arose outside the tent. A soldier entered and reported:","\"Commandery Princess, it's those conscripts outside. They wish to see Young Master Yu.\"","At the mention of Yu Fan, everyone present fell silent for a moment.","Song Shihuan took several deep breaths, steadying her expression, before stepping out of the tent:","\"He is gravely wounded. There are clear marks of severe whipping on his back. Also, likely while protecting one of you, he took an arrow to the back of his arm.\"","\"The arrowhead was hastily removed. His left chest and both legs sustained various injuries. He has fractured ribs and is now unconscious from exhaustion.\"","As Song Shihuan's words fell, the conscripts began to wail loudly.","\"Will... will Tiger-Head be in mortal danger?\" one of the conscripts choked out between sobs.","\"The army physicians' skills are limited. I have already sent for a renowned doctor from the capital to treat him. Whether he lives or dies depends entirely on his own fortune.\"","\"And also, his name is not Tiger-Head.\"","Song Shihuan felt a sharp, dense pain in her heart. \"His name is Yu Fan. He is a son of the Gu family of Daqi.\"","If you are truly grateful to him, then tell the world how the Dayue royal family treated you. As long as the Dayue common people harbor no thoughts of rebellion, we will treat them with kindness as well.","With that, Song Shihuan strode towards the tent where Yu Fan lay.","She left behind a crowd of conscripts weeping uncontrollably.","Inside the tent, Song Yu had been keeping watch. Seeing Song Shihuan arrive, he gave a slight, strained smile. \"Already sent a letter to that old fellow Mei.\"","“To survive so many wounds and still cling to life... truly blessed with great fortune. He could have just hidden in the shield formation to be rescued, but he had to charge in and kill the enemy general.”","Resignedly, Song Yu took a damp cloth and wiped Yu Fan's face.","That young man who once knelt before him, pledging his service, had grown with such astonishing speed into this towering tree.","His Song family was deeply grateful for the Gu family's loyalty and righteousness.","\"We're using ginseng to sustain his life for now. Don't worry, Ah-Huan.\"","Song Shihuan sat by the bedside, remaining in quiet vigil.","Outside the tent, Gu Zheng sat on the ground, staring blankly at Yu Fan's sword, stained with blood.","Suddenly, Gu Zheng grinned.","Ancestors of the Gu family, behold. The son-in-law he had chosen had not brought shame upon the Gu name."]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: Retribution from Song Shihuan, the Gu Family Gains a Daughter","paragraphs":["The Gu Family Residence in the capital.","Gu Mingliu was having her first child, and after a long labor, the baby still hadn't arrived.","The commotion even reached Emperor Yuanyou in the Zichen Hall.","\"How is that girl from the Gu family doing?\" Emperor Yuanyou couldn't help but ask. Gu Zheng was fighting at the front, and Gu Mingning was guarding the northern frontier. He had to show some concern for the two young women of the Gu family.","Your Majesty, Physician Mei is attending to her. Lady Shen and Yingchun from the princess's side are also there. Physician Mei says it's Lady Gu's first child, and first births are usually slow for women.","Hearing Wu Qi's words, Emperor Yuanyou relaxed slightly. \"Alright, inform me as soon as there is news.\"","The baby in that Gu family girl's belly... Ah Huan was extremely fond of it.","Medicines and tonics flowed like water to the Gu residence, with Ah Huan saying this was her first junior.","Thinking of Ah Huan, Emperor Yuanyou's gaze softened unconsciously.","Victory reports kept arriving from the border. He had never imagined that the one commanding the central army wasn't Gu Zheng, but his own young granddaughter, merely thirteen years old.","With a force like crashing waves, she pressed Dayue into retreat step by step, and even perfectly handled the public opinion crisis regarding Song Yanzheng.","Emperor Yuanyou admitted to himself that at that age, he couldn't have done it so flawlessly.","How far would Ah Huan's future reach?","Even Emperor Yuanyou felt he couldn't see it clearly now.","Meanwhile, Gu Mingliu was drenched in sweat from head to toe, as if fished out of water.","\"Young Lady, you must follow the rhythm to breathe.\"","Seeing Gu Mingliu gradually losing strength, the midwife pinched her thigh hard. Gu Mingliu struggled to keep her eyelids open. \"Yingchun, I have no strength left.\"","\"Young Lady, news came from the border. Shicheng has been taken. Presumably, the capital of Dayue will fall soon. Then General Gu and Young Master Yu will both return in triumph.\" Yingchun was also witnessing childbirth for the first time, her voice trembling. \"They are all waiting to see if it's a young master or a young lady in your belly.\"","Mention of the border brought a glimmer of light to Gu Mingliu's eyes:","\"A victory... a great victory...\"","\"Mingliu, my third son said if this battle is won, Yu Fan will earn considerable military merit. Push a few more times, and your family will be reunited soon.\" Lady Shen's eyes also held tears; she knew the feeling of giving birth without one's husband by her side.","\"And the princess!\" Yingchun wiped her tears. \"The princess has been looking forward to holding the baby herself!\"","\"I see the head! I see the baby's head!\"","The midwife's excited voice helped Gu Mingliu gather her strength once more. She pushed again and again as instructed by the midwife.","The labor lasted a full day and night.","At dawn the next day, as the sky lightened, Gu Mingliu's heart-wrenching cry pierced the air:","\"Yu Fan—\"","Then, an infant's cry resounded throughout the Gu residence.","After more than a decade of quiet, the Gu family welcomed a new life.","\"Congratulations, Young Lady. The joy of a daughter.\"","Exhausted, Gu Mingliu fell into a deep sleep. Gu Mingzhu rushed into the room and saw Lady Shen, looking somewhat disheveled but smiling gently, holding the swaddled infant.","\"Mingzhu, your elder sister gave birth to a beautiful little girl.\"","Gu Mingzhu's little mouth quivered, and she began to cry, her wails even louder than the newborn's.","The two cries seemed to compete over which was louder.","Lady Shen felt a moment of dizziness, her eyes stinging again.","The master was right. Loyal and heroic families like the Gu's sacrificed far more than common people could imagine. Mingzhu, who had held strong outside for so long, was still just a child herself.","...","Shicheng.","“Princess, the advance team, based on the laborers' accounts, has found the entrance to the tunnel.”","Song Shihuan nodded upon hearing this. \"Prince Rui still doesn't know the tunnel is exposed. Proceed according to plan. Divide the troops into two groups. One attacks the capital, the other guards the tunnel entrance.\"","Song Shihuan paused here, then a faint, knowing smile appeared on her face. \"Prepare some dried chili peppers. Burn them and throw them into the tunnel, then block the entrance.\"","Everyone present felt a sympathetic sting in their noses upon hearing this.","Dried chilies were pungent and potent—quite effective.","\"This time, our attack will be in two steps.\"","Under fluttering banners, Song Shihuan's words reached everyone clearly.","\"First, prevent Dayue from emerging behind us via the tunnel. Second, use the tunnel to get behind Dayue's lines.\" Song Shihuan raised her voice. \"The tunnel Prince Rui painstakingly dug must serve us. This time, we will fight our way to the gates of Dayue's imperial palace, make their old emperor open the palace doors for us, and avenge our fallen soldiers.\"","\"Do you have confidence?\"","\"Yes! Yes! Yes!\"","Hearing this sky-rending roar, Song Yu sighed softly. Well, now he couldn't even serve to stabilize morale.","He could only express the court's concern to the wounded in the rear.","What made Song Yu even more indignant was overhearing Li Laoba whispering to the soldiers beside him:","\"The princess's mind works incredibly fast; she can think of any method, and she's bold too. I thought just taking Wucheng would be an achievement, but the princess wants to fight all the way to Dayue's palace.\"","\"Doesn't feel like the Crown Prince's offspring.\"","\"More like a celestial spirit born from the heavens. That's how it's written in the storybooks.\"","Passing by the dazed Song Yu: ...","War drums sounded. Daqi caught Dayue completely off guard.","\"Your Highness, Daqi is attacking from Wucheng!\"","Hearing the news, Prince Rui revealed a confident smile. \"Send the troops through the tunnel. Let Daqi witness the might of our Great Yue!\"","In less than fifteen minutes, the soldiers who entered the tunnel came out red-faced, with runny noses, coughing uncontrollably.","\"Your Highness, we've been exposed! Daqi is burning dried chilies at the other end of the tunnel. Our men simply cannot get through.\"","Covering their noses was useless; it burned their eyes.","Prince Rui was thunderstruck. How did Daqi learn such a top-secret piece of information?","\"How should we respond now? We await Your Highness's instructions.\"","Prince Rui began to panic and spoke hurriedly, \"Since the tunnel is useless, transfer all forces to defend the city gates. The capital must not fall!\"","As he spoke, Prince Rui personally headed for the capital's city walls. If this battle was lost... he couldn't bear his father's wrath.","Just as the two sides fought fiercely outside the city, a group of Daqi soldiers quietly passed through the tunnel beneath the battlefield and emerged within Dayue's capital.","After counting the men, Li Laoba gripped his weapon tightly. \"Brothers, the time to earn glory and merit has come.\"","Next, a spectacular scene unfolded.","The Dayue soldiers who were diligently shooting arrows at the Daqi forces suddenly began falling to the ground one by one, as if punished by heaven.","Prince Rui was both shocked and terrified. He looked towards Song Shihuan on the opposite city wall.","He saw Song Shihuan slowly raise her hand towards Prince Rui...","and gave him the middle finger."]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: Capture Prince Rui Alive and Breach the Capital of Da Yue","paragraphs":["This battle was fought differently from the previous ones.","The soldiers of Great Qi seemed to be deliberately toying with Great Yue, using the very methods Great Yue intended to use against Great Qi to counterattack them. Every move and strategy originated from Prince Rui's hand.","Also, due to Yu Fan's severe injury, Great Qi's attacks carried a hint of vengeance.","Caught in a pincer attack, more and more Great Yue soldiers in the center fell.","Song Shihuan stood on the city wall of Wu City, quietly watching Prince Rui's desperate last stand.","After a long while, Gu Zheng returned on horseback.","His tied-up hair had become disheveled, and it was impossible to tell whose blood stained his armor. Gu Zheng knelt on one knee, \"Commandery Princess, the capital of Great Yue has been breached.\"","In an instant, crows cawed, circling above Wu City.","\"Great Yue abandoned the capital's gates, recalling all their forces to defend the imperial palace,\" Gu Zheng's eyes flashed with a trace of mockery. \"Prince Rui has also been abandoned.\"","They had captured Prince Rui alive, yet the tightly shut palace gates never opened for him.","In wars between nations, the fight is for every inch of land.","A single retreat means the battle is lost.","\"A brilliant victory!\"","Song Shihuan did not stint in her praise for the soldiers. Beneath her deliberately raised tone, the eyes of the soldiers below the wall shone brightly.","They showed no sign of exhaustion.","\"Our vast Great Qi, our mighty army, has remained undefeated since the campaign began, conquering all the way to the Great Yue capital. On behalf of Great Qi, I thank you all for your valor.\"","\"Gentlemen.\"","\"Let us advance together into the capital of Great Yue.\"","As Song Shihuan's voice faded, thunderous cries of \"Long live!\" and \"A thousand years!\" soared to the clouds. Song Yu and Song Shihuan descended the watchtower and surged into the Great Yue capital with the soldiers, pulling down the Great Yue banner that had stood for centuries.","Song Shihuan stared intently at the Great Yue banner fallen on the ground.","She had been reborn, initially seeking revenge.","As her hatred gradually subsided, she began to seek the warmth of close family, something she had longed for but never obtained in her previous life.","And now, Song Shihuan felt she sought one more thing: protection.","As a commandery princess of Great Qi, supported by its people, she should protect the people of Great Qi, allowing them to live peaceful and stable lives.","If one day the people on Great Yue's land became her subjects, she would protect them just the same.","Perhaps... this was also her mission in this rebirth.","\"Commandery Princess, Prince Rui has been brought forward.\"","A voice snapped Song Shihuan out of her reverie. Before she could speak, Song Yu delivered a fierce kick to Prince Rui.","This kick perfectly embodied the true teachings of Emperor Yuanyou.","Prince Rui glared furiously at Song Yu after being struck.","\"Where did this beast crawl out from, daring to glare at this prince?\" Song Yu looked down at Prince Rui. \"So, you're the one who came up with that despicable plan of digging tunnels, right?\"","\"Are your Great Qi's tactics any less underhanded?\"","\"A righteous army employs the art of war's deception. How is that underhanded?\"","Seeing Song Yu's righteous and confident manner, Prince Rui felt a surge of bloody sweetness rise in his throat.","\"We wouldn't kill conscripted laborers after using them,\" Song Yu kicked him again, venting his anger. \"In your eyes, the common people are like ants. Clearly, heaven does not wish someone like you to sit on the dragon throne.\"","\"And you? An overachieving Crown Prince overshadowing the Emperor, can you sit on the dragon throne? Don't forget what happened to your Great Qi's former Crown Prince?\"","Another kick.","Gu Zheng and several deputy generals watched wide-eyed. The moment it involved a prince, the style changed abruptly, but... it was very satisfying to watch.","Then Song Yu suddenly shook his head. \"This prince might have a bit of a talent—specifically for severing people's imperial aura.\"","Song Ling was like that, and so was Prince Rui.","\"Ahem—\"","Song Shihuan, who had been silent until now, cleared her throat. Song Yu immediately fell silent and, with practiced ease, handed her a cup of water.","To moisten her throat first.","\"I'm thinking of hanging Prince Rui up. When we attack the palace later, we can ask the Great Yue emperor whether he wants Prince Rui's life or the palace. What do you think?\"","Gu Zheng was so excited he nearly rolled his eyes.","He had never fought such a satisfying battle!","Not long ago, Great Yue used Song Yanzheng to force Great Qi to retreat. And now, they could hang up Prince Rui to force Great Yue's surrender.","\"Good, very, very good.\"","As soon as Li Laoba finished speaking, he fell to the ground with a thud. Just as everyone moved to check on him, he raised a hand. \"Don't mind me. I'm just too thrilled. I need to lie down and calm down.\"","Otherwise, he felt like he was floating on clouds.","A quarter of an hour later, Gu Zheng and several deputy generals were all lying on the ground.","The corner of Song Shihuan's mouth twitched. Under Prince Rui's terrified gaze, she gave the order:","\"Tie him up. We're going to fish for a big one.\"","...","Great Qi capital.","After Gu Mingliu gave birth, to help her recuperate, Mei Zhilin visited the Gu residence daily, transforming from an elegant physician with a neat beard into a disheveled old man.","But on this day, Mei Zhilin prescribed two months' worth of medicine all at once.","\"Physician Mei, won't you be coming anymore?\" Gu Mingzhu asked, tilting her head.","Mei Zhilin paused. \"These old bones of mine can't run around anymore.\"","\"You're lying to a child. Last night, you didn't get on the carriage, but whoosh—you ran several meters and jumped into it.\"","Gu Mingzhu's eyelashes trembled almost imperceptibly. She walked to Mei Zhilin's side and tugged at his sleeve.","\"Is it... someone at the front line severely injured?\"","Mei Zhilin took a deep breath. This little ancestor was indeed sharp, too sharp... He didn't know how to answer.","In those few seconds of Mei Zhilin's hesitation, Gu Mingzhu understood.","She curtsied to Mei Zhilin. \"I entrust this to you, Physician Mei.\"","Her father and brother-in-law were on the battlefield, as were her close friend and the Crown Prince.","She couldn't bear it if anything happened to any of them.","Seeing Gu Mingzhu like this, Mei Zhilin fumbled in his pouch for a while, pulled out a cube of sugar, and handed it to her.","\"Second Young Lady Gu, has the Gu family's new little miss been given a pet name?\"","\"Not yet. Physician Mei, you have saved countless lives and accumulated immense merit. Would you like to give her one?\" Gu Mingzhu said with a smile, the sugar cube in her mouth.","Seeing that Gu Mingzhu didn't seem suspicious, Mei Zhilin secretly sighed in relief.","\"This old man presumes to suggest: how about 'Atuan'?\"","\"Atuan is good. Let's call her Atuan.\"","Without a moment's hesitation, Gu Mingzhu immediately agreed to the name Atuan.","After Mei Zhilin left, Gu Mingzhu ran all the way back to her own courtyard. Only after closing the door did her eyes turn red.","Atuan...","Most likely, it was her brother-in-law who was injured.","What about her elder sister?","Gu Mingzhu stayed alone like this for a long time. Not until almost dinnertime did she push open her door, a smile already back on her face.","\"Elder sister! Freshly simmered chicken soup is ready!\"","Gu Mingzhu's voice rang out. \"Drink up quickly, so you can feed our beautiful, lovely little Atuan.\"","\"Atuan?\" Gu Mingliu paused.","\"Isn't 'Atuan' a good pet name? I think it sounds wonderful.\"","Gu Mingliu simply thought Gu Mingzhu was being childish and smiled, tapping her sister's head playfully.","\"Alright, we'll listen to her aunt. Let's call her Atuan.\""]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: We have won, a resounding victory.","paragraphs":["Just a few days after her birth, Tuan had transformed from a little red, wrinkled baby into a plump and fair-skinned infant. She was a very quiet baby, sleeping as soon as she was full. Now, hearing Gu Mingliu murmur the name \"Tuan,\" the little one seemed to sense it and smiled in her sleep, the corners of her mouth curling upwards.","\"Mingzhu, she likes the name Tuan.\"","Gu Mingzhu struggled to suppress her tight lips, forcing a difficult smile onto her face. \"Little Tuan, may you have a happy and complete family.\"","In the end, Gu Mingzhu couldn't hold back and ran outside.","She had made up her mind: if her brother-in-law truly abandoned her elder sister like this...","She would find a new husband for her elder sister and then let Tuan take another man's surname!","After all, it wasn't uncommon in Great Qi for widowed women to remarry.","Wiping away her tears, Gu Mingzhu thought fiercely to herself.","If her brother-in-law truly cared for his wife and child, even if he had to fight the King of Hell at the gates of the underworld, he should beat him up and come back alive.","...","Elsewhere, outside the palace of Great Yue.","Gu Zheng had found skilled craftsmen among the military ranks and had Prince Rui hoisted up. The height was just right for him to face the people on the palace wall.","When the soldier guarding the wall came face-to-face with the captured Prince Rui,","his legs trembled with fear.","Good heavens, why was Prince Rui dangling right in front of him?","\"Listen up, you on the wall! If you don't want your Prince Rui to lose his head, tell Emperor Mingde to open the palace gates and welcome our Great Qi's mighty army inside.\"","Gu Zheng followed the example set just last month when Prince Rui had grabbed Song Yanzheng to shout threats. The imitation made Prince Rui's face flush red with anger.","\"Prince Rui, care to share some last words?\"","Song Yu's voice rang out, but only his voice was heard, not the man himself.","Hidden archers had been aiming for a while, but seeing Song Yu completely shielded by six protective shields, they could only twitch their lips in frustration.","What was there to aim at?","Behind the shields, Song Yu grinned widely. A'huan had instructed that as long as three people moved together, each holding one shield high and one low, guarding the front, left, and right, those archers would be rendered useless.","\"If you don't speak now, you'll never get another chance.\"","\"I'll speak!\" Prince Rui's voice cracked with desperation. \"Go quickly and tell my father to save me! I am a prince of Great Yue, you cannot just watch me die!\"","As soon as he finished, the Great Qi soldiers burst into loud laughter.","Their laughter was full of mockery, making the Great Yue soldiers blush with shame.","Although the Great Qi Crown Prince's eldest son also had a notorious record, compared to this spineless Prince Rui, he was practically a general among dwarfs.","A few moments later, an arrow shot towards Prince Rui, killing him instantly.","The archer was none other than Great Yue's Second Prince, King Duan, who declared, \"By the Emperor's order, defend the palace to the death.\"","Song Shihuan narrowed her eyes, watching King Duan on the city wall.","Gu Zheng spoke slowly, \"This man is shallow and cannot bear provocation.\"","Remembering Gu Zheng's earlier assessment of Prince Rui, Song Shihuan and Song Yu exchanged a glance, feeling assured. This battle was as good as won.","\"You have seized so many of Great Yue's cities in such a short time. Aren't you afraid of a backlash from the people?\" King Duan, who had somehow acquired a torch, continued, \"When civil unrest erupts, all of you will be trapped here in Great Yue, giving the surrounding nations a chance to attack you.\"","\"If you are willing to negotiate peace with Great Yue, I will not light this signal beacon.\"","Once the beacon was lit, it would be an urgent summons from the sovereign, calling all military forces, including militia, to come to the emperor's aid.","\"King Duan, is it?\"","\"Go ahead and light it. If you don't light it today, you're my grandson.\"","Song Yu extended a single finger from behind the shields, gave an extremely sarcastic waggle, and retracted it at lightning speed.","He almost had an intimate encounter with an arrow shot from Great Yue.","Song Yu's heart was pounding with fear, but he mustered all his courage. \"Scared now? Call me Grandpa.\"","\"Open the gates for your Grandpa, good grandson.\"","The signal beacon was lit, the sudden surge of heat into the sky momentarily stunning King Duan.","Why had he lit it?","His father had specifically instructed him to use this as leverage to negotiate carefully with Great Qi.","Down below the wall, Song Yu swaggered back to safety:","\"A'huan, I performed quite well today, didn't I?\"","He, the illustrious Crown Prince of Great Qi, had finally found his moment to shine!","...","\"It's time for us to take the stage.\"","Due to the war, the people of Great Yue were hiding in villages. A group of strong laborers specifically sought out villages with the most refugees. Dressed in tattered clothes, their eyes were already seven-tenths red before they even began to speak.","\"We were captured to dig tunnels as forced laborers.\"","\"We dug day and night, beaten if we worked even slightly slower.\"","\"It was Young Master Yu Fan who risked his life to save us...\"","Mentioning Yu Fan, who was still bedridden and hanging onto life, a group of grown men had reddened eyes. \"Fellow villagers, the Great Yue royal family does not care about us at all. The people of Great Qi live in peace and prosperity under a wise ruler. We should also abandon the darkness for the light...\"","The laborers spoke with such heartfelt tears that the effect was astonishingly good.","Inside the command tent.","\"Commander, the news about the laborers is spreading faster than anticipated. Not a single relief force has been sighted yet.\"","As soon as Gu Zheng's voice fell, Li Laoba burst into laughter. \"The villagers convinced by the laborers are spontaneously spreading out. Whenever they encounter troops, they start telling the story. According to scouts, seven waves of troops have already been persuaded to turn back.\"","\"Those retreating troops then carried the message to other places. The effect is superb.\"","At this point, Li Laoba couldn't help but glance at Song Shihuan.","So that was why the Commander had the Crown Prince provoke King Duan into lighting the beacon.","Turns out she was using King Duan as their unpaid laborer.","\"Now Great Yue has lost the hearts of its people and is at the end of its strength,\" Song Shihuan said slowly. \"At dawn tomorrow, we storm the palace.\"","Seeing the excited expressions on the soldiers' faces, Song Shihuan paused:","\"Let me be perfectly clear. After taking the palace, there will be no acts of defilement, especially towards the consorts and princesses.\"","Military texts also record that in ancient times, after King Cheng conquered Zhao, he defiled the wives and daughters of the King of Zhao, completely losing the people's support.","Sometimes, in the heat of battle, after victory, impulsive actions are hard to avoid.","\"Commander, rest assured. Great Qi's military discipline is strict.\"","At dawn the next day, war drums once again shook the heavens.","Great Qi's final battle was fought just as brilliantly. Emperor Mingde, sitting withered on his dragon throne, still hadn't figured out why not a single relief force had come for Great Yue, even as he was surrounded.","All the princes and princesses were herded into an open square. The imperial consorts wept softly, unsure whether they were crying for their own uncertain futures or for the impending fall of Great Yue.","The Prime Minister, Cheng Guang, held a vial filled with poison in his hand. Looking at Gu Zheng before him, Cheng Guang laughed foolishly.","So, in the end, he still hadn't been able to best the Gu family.","\"A'huan.\"","Song Yu suddenly spoke. Song Shihuan turned to look at him.","She saw his eyes shining like stars:","\"We've won. A complete victory.\""]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: Losers Should Act Like Losers","paragraphs":["\"A bunch of useless fools, you have failed me!\"","Emperor Mingde suddenly roared, glaring at the ministers who had all taken refuge in the palace the moment the capital fell. \"Your spines should all be broken.\"","Hearing Emperor Mingde's words, Cheng Guang's hand, holding the poison vial, paused.","Emperor Mingde, however, seemed possessed. \"Why does Great Qi keep producing fine generals, while you cannot?\"","A bunch of spineless cowards, who only know how to hide when trouble comes.","\"And you all, why does a mere commandery princess of Great Qi have the talent to lead troops, while you only know how to weep here? What are you crying for? A funeral dirge?\"","Seeing Emperor Mingde like this, a sense of shared despair settled in everyone's hearts.","\"Your Majesty, this subject is bold.\"","Cheng Guang's clouded eyes were filled with sorrow. \"That day, Prince Rui abandoned the city and returned, saying he had another strategy for victory. I pleaded with him three times, saying we could not just hand the city over. And what was the result?\"","\"Later, you sent Prince Duan to guard the palace gates. I also advised you to let me go in his stead, but you did not consent. The signal beacon was lit, and Prince Duan was captured.\"","Cheng Guang couldn't help but look up at the sky.","Why did heaven never favor him?","He had finally achieved the merit of supporting the emperor's rise, and before he could even help select a truly virtuous and capable crown prince, Great Yue was about to fall.","\"Cheng Guang, the chief culprit among the guilty ministers is you, the Prime Minister. How will you account for yourself to the Great Yue imperial clan after your death? How will you account to my imperial father?\"","Mentioning the old emperor, Cheng Guang's emotions instantly grew agitated.","\"Your Majesty, this subject cannot account to the late emperor. But what about you? Can you give a proper account either?\"","Seeing the sovereign and his minister actually begin to bicker, Song Yu couldn't help but roll his eyes dramatically.","He kicked each of them once.","Neither would be at a disadvantage.","\"How dare you! You dare show such disrespect to me!\" Emperor Mingde bellowed.","What greeted Emperor Mingde was a straight punch from Song Yu. \"I'm hitting you precisely.\"","\"This prince is the Crown Prince of Great Qi. And who are you?\"","Looking at Song Yu's half-smiling expression, Emperor Mingde's breath caught.","He was the Emperor of Great Yue... but with Great Yue in such a state now, he couldn't bring himself to say it.","\"Losers should act like losers.\"","Having said that, Song Yu walked up to Cheng Guang and directly kicked over the poison vial in his hand with his foot. \"Holding a poison vial and striking a pose here? If you don't want to die, then don't die.\"","He hated these pretentious types the most!","Song Yu's thin lips moved, cursing Great Yue from top to bottom in a thorough and satisfying manner.","The feeling of winning a war was just this exhilarating.","\"Your Highness, how should we deal with these people?\"","\"Tie them up and send them back to the capital in prisoner carts.\"","Song Shihuan silently watched the imposing Song Yu, her eyes full of amusement. Well, it was good to let Father have some sense of participation, wasn't it?","\"Commandery Princess Fuan.\"","Emperor Mingde's voice suddenly rang out, his gaze passing over the crowd to land on Song Shihuan.","This was the first time Emperor Mingde had seen his true adversary.","\"At such a young age, you carry so much bloodshed on your hands. Aren't you afraid of retribution?\"","\"Dare to disrespect our Commandery Princess? Beat the crap out of him!\"","Before Song Shihuan could even open her mouth, Li Laoba shot out like a tiger, charging towards Emperor Mingde.","Soon, other soldiers also threw down their weapons and began intimate, hand-to-hand contact with Emperor Mingde.","Pig-slaughter-like screams rang out. Song Shihuan blinked.","\"Father.\"","Song Yu was so angry smoke seemed to rise from the top of his head, his handsome face flushed red from holding back.","\"Why don't you go throw a few punches too.\"","Don't hold it in and get sick, really.","Upon hearing this, Song Yu charged forward like an unbridled wild horse.","...","The line of prisoner carts was long like a winding dragon, escorting the captives from all levels of Great Yue.","The Great Yue commoners they passed watched with cold indifference, even actively offering food and drink to the Great Qi soldiers.","\"Hey, why don't I see that one?\"","That one, meaning Emperor Mingde.","\"Yeah, I don't see him either. Could he already be dead?\"","The whispers reached the ears of a Great Qi soldier, whose mouth twitched uncontrollably.","Out of a kind heart, the soldier pointed to one particular person with a face swollen like a pig's head and said, \"That is Emperor Mingde.\"","\"Wh... what?\"","The speaking commoner nearly bit his tongue.","That person, beaten black and blue with a huge lump on his head, was their emperor?","Oh no, not anymore.","\"See that big lump? Our Crown Prince did that!\"","The soldier said proudly, his spine straightening.","Their Crown Prince could top the imperial examinations in literature and put a lump on an enemy emperor's head in martial prowess—accomplished in both, peerless in the world!","As for the Commandery Princess...","She was practically a celestial being!","The Great Qi soldiers grinned widely with simple joy, while the Great Yue captives looked as if they were mourning their own parents.","\"The Great Yue Imperial Seal?\"","In the Great Yue palace, Song Yu looked at the retrieved seal and shook his head with considerable disdain, then tossed it to Song Shihuan.","This seal looked ugly even to the eye.","Forced to catch it, Song Shihuan's little face scrunched up into a knot. What was she supposed to do with this thing? She wouldn't use it.","The next second, Song Yu's matter-of-fact voice rang out:","\"Ahuan, keep it to prop up a wobbly table leg.\"","Gu Zheng and a group of deputy generals all smiled at Song Shihuan as if collectively hard of hearing. They weren't censors; why should they care about propriety?","So what?","Couldn't their Commandery Princess play with an enemy nation's imperial seal?","She could probably play with the Great Qi imperial seal too!","...","Elsewhere.","Mei Zhilin's old bones had stubbornly endured the jolting journey, which nearly shook his guts out, finally allowing him to see Yu Fan, who lay unconscious on a bed, with great speed.","\"Physician Mei, you must save Young Master Yu.\"","Mei Zhilin glanced at the burly man, eight feet tall, crying with swollen, red eyes, and closed his own. \"You, get out.\"","Looking at him gave Mei Zhilin a headache and made his eyes hurt.","After taking Yu Fan's pulse, the small old man sighed repeatedly.","After further examining Yu Fan's injuries, Mei Zhilin was too worried to speak. How had he managed to get himself into such a state?","Yu Fan's life was hard, and Mei Zhilin's life was hard too.","Resigned to his fate, Mei Zhilin took out his silver needles, inserting one after another into Yu Fan's body.","\"Your wife has given birth. A beautiful baby girl, named Atuan as you wished.\"","\"The birth was not smooth. Your wife suffered greatly, nearly losing strength at the end, risking both their lives. Thankfully, heaven protected them, but she will need several years to recover.\"","\"Rest assured, she doesn't know about your critical injury. A woman in confinement must not grieve.\"","The usually taciturn Mei Zhilin uncharacteristically rambled on at length.","Looking at Yu Fan, now resembling a porcupine from his needles, Mei Zhilin wiped the sweat from his forehead. \"With injuries like this, the Prince and the Commandery Princess must have given you their own life-saving treasures.\"","Suddenly, Mei Zhilin saw Yu Fan's finger move with great effort.","\"This old man knows your will to live is strong. Don't worry, I will definitely let you hold your daughter.\""]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: Kissing up to the wrong person.","paragraphs":["The news of the great victory flew towards Daqi as if on wings. The soldier delivering the triumphant report, his face flushed with excitement, held the military dispatch aloft and sang out all the way:","\"A great victory! Daqi has won a great victory!\"","Zichen Hall.","Emperor Yuanyou sprang to his feet, his hands trembling as he took the military dispatch.","They had truly won.","And it was such a brilliant victory.","Emperor Yuanyou was so delighted he began pacing in circles on the spot. \"Go and summon Shen Mingwen.\"","In just a quarter of an hour, Shen Mingwen stood before Emperor Yuanyou.","\"Minister Shen, the Crown Prince's position is secure.\"","\"Everything is as Your Majesty foresaw.\"","Shen Mingwen let out a heavy sigh of relief. From this point on, His Highness's position as Crown Prince would be unshakable.","\"Excellent, I... I eagerly await their triumphant return.\" As he spoke these words, Emperor Yuanyou himself felt a pang of sorrow. Hadn't he suffered, not seeing his son and granddaughter for several months?","\"Regarding Young Master Yu's injuries...\"","A flicker of concern passed through Shen Mingwen's eyes.","\"The military dispatch states his wounds have begun to improve. This time, Mei Zhilin used all his secret skills.\" Emperor Yuanyou's fondness for Yu Fan had multiplied at this moment. \"When Yu Fan returns, I shall bestow generous rewards upon him. His contributions this time were not small.\"","\"In my humble opinion, the one with the greatest merit should be the Commandery Princess.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was pleased.","He nodded repeatedly with satisfaction.","Minister Shen indeed knew best what he wanted to hear, which was why he always enjoyed calling Minister Shen for a chat when something came up.","\"My granddaughter... she's just a bit cleverer, a bit stronger, a bit more talented, that's all, nothing much really.\"","Shen Mingwen could hardly hold back his laughter.","What difference was there between the Emperor's current demeanor and the Crown Prince's boastful manner?","\"The Commandery Princess's grace and bearing are unmatched.\"","\"Children shouldn't be praised too much.\"","Emperor Yuanyou waved his hand dismissively as he spoke, then pressed his fingers to his forehead with a wry smile.","His granddaughter was simply too outstanding. What was he to do?","...","At the court assembly the next morning, Emperor Yuanyou arrived earlier than usual and had even meticulously groomed his beard.","In the court, Emperor Yuanyou cleared his throat. \"What are your views, esteemed ministers, on Daqi's capture of the Dayue imperial palace?\"","The subtext was clear—","Alright, you may now begin your praises.","\"Your Majesty, the Crown Prince is accomplished in both civil and military affairs. With such an heir, Daqi can ensure prosperity for ten thousand years.\"","\"Commandery Princess Fu'an is truly a remarkable woman, a lucky star for our Daqi!\"","The civil and military officials lavished praise for a full half-hour, with Emperor Yuanyou showing no intention of stopping them.","The atmosphere began to grow slightly awkward.","Because everyone was starting to run out of words.","Just then, an official who hadn't had a chance to speak up until now boomed in a resonant voice, \"The royal family's newly acquired pair of dragon and phoenix children are indeed an auspicious sign, having blessed our Daqi with this great victory.\"","Instantly, Emperor Yuanyou's face fell.","His son and granddaughter had risked their lives fighting on the front lines. If heaven were to bestow blessings, it would be for their sake.","Song Heng's pair of twins were merely a convenient pretext, a justification for the campaign.","Emperor Yuanyou was displeased and was about to retort when he was interrupted by another voice.","\"The victory in this battle was achieved firstly by relying on Your Majesty's wisdom, secondly because His Highness and the Commandery Princess had brilliant strategies, and thirdly due to the soldiers' courageous charge,\" Song Heng hurriedly spoke up. \"My unworthy son and daughter do not deserve such praise from you, sir.\"","Seeing Song Heng's attitude, Emperor Yuanyou's expression improved slightly.","He ultimately didn't continue with what he had intended to say. He was the Son of Heaven; if he were to be so petty, wouldn't it invite ridicule?","\"The court is dismissed.\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt somewhat dispirited. He would return and write a letter urging Yu'er to lead the troops back to the capital soon.","Or perhaps send A'huan back to him first would be good too.","...","Shen Residence.","After returning from court, Shen Qingping didn't even take the time to remove his court robes. He directly ran to the old tree, took a shovel, and dug up a jar of wine.","\"Third Master, this is strong liquor, you...\"","Nian'an's voice grew softer under Shen Qingping's gaze, leaving him no choice but to watch helplessly as Shen Qingping walked away holding the wine jar.","Ever since Third Master fell seriously ill that year, he had rarely drunk alcohol, and when he did, it was usually wine of ordinary strength.","But this wine, buried for many years, was extremely potent.","Shen Qingping went straight to find Zheng Fang.","\"Care for a drink?\"","Looking at Shen Qingping before him, Zheng Fang inwardly remarked on his extraordinary, almost celestial appearance.","The man was clad in the crimson official robes of the second rank. His complexion was fair, his eyes and brows sharp. The gold threads on his robe shimmered faintly in the sunlight, and the jade belt cinched at his waist accentuated an air of cool detachment.","No wonder the world condemned his ruthless methods, yet never called his appearance plain.","\"I would be honored.\" Zheng Fang cupped his hands towards Shen Qingping.","Lifting the lid released an intense aroma of wine.","After one sip, Shen Qingping's expression remained unchanged.","\"His Highness has won the battle, the Eastern Palace's position is secure. Everyone outside is now praising His Highness. You can set your mind at ease, sir.\"","After Zheng Fang finished speaking, Shen Qingping actually laughed.","\"When His Highness first stood before the troops, his calves were trembling.\"","Zheng Fang's pupils shook with shock. Was this something he was allowed to hear?","Would he be silenced for this?","Was it still too late to call Ling Ming and Feng Kuizhi over?","Zheng Fang's mind raced, but then he heard Shen Qingping speak again:","\"Zheng Fang, human hearts are fickle.\"","\"Those who praise His Highness now are the same ones who looked down on him in the past.\"","Shen Qingping's Adam's apple bobbed. His Highness was straightforward by nature, something Shen Qingping knew he himself fell short of. He, Shen Qingping, held grudges.","\"At the peak of the criticism, they said His Highness was unfilial, uncultured, and unworthy of being a prince.\"","Shen Qingping was growing drunk.","\"On my way back to the residence today, I heard many words praising His Highness. Yet, I didn't feel as happy as I imagined. Instead, I kept thinking of the past.\" Shen Qingping drained the fine wine in his cup once more. \"So Zheng Fang, we cannot let our guard down. We cannot become complacent.\"","\"We must remain clear-headed.\"","Zheng Fang's expression suddenly turned serious. Looking at the man before him, whose drunkenness was now apparent, he stood up and bowed. \"Thank you for the reminder, Young Master Shen.\"","\"Enough. Keep me company while I drink.\"","An hour later, both men were slumped drunkenly over the table, with Shen Qingping still clutching his wine cup.","A while later, two maidservants carefully approached carrying sobering soup. One of them walked up to Shen Qingping, intending to take the wine cup from his hand.","The moment she drew near, Shen Qingping's eyes snapped open.","Killing intent was plain in his gaze.","The maidservant was so frightened she fell to the ground, spilling the sobering soup everywhere.","\"What happened?\" Zheng Fang was also startled back to awareness by the commotion.","\"This servant... this servant wanted to take the cup from your hand, sir. The kitchen prepared sobering soup for both gentlemen.\"","\"It's nothing. You may leave.\" Shen Qingping sat up straight.","Zheng Fang looked at Shen Qingping apologetically, a trace of something obscure in his eyes. Young Master Shen had never practiced martial arts. How could he possess such keen alertness...","Even in a drunken state, he could react so swiftly.","But then he saw Shen Qingping wave his hand and speak with an air of nonchalance:","\"Too many people in this world wish to kill this official.\"","It was merely a means of preserving his life."]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: Is a Loyal Minister Not to Serve Two Masters","paragraphs":["The Gu Residence.","\"Elder Sister, military reports have arrived from the frontier. We achieved a great victory.\"","Gu Mingzhu jumped for joy, planting kisses on Tuan, who was about to be a month old.","\"Tuan truly brings good fortune. You'll soon be reunited with your father.\"","Seeing Gu Mingzhu's delight, Gu Mingliu also smiled.","After being apart for several months, she too missed her father and her husband dearly, as well as that little princess who was now spoken of in almost mythical terms by the common folk.","\"The army will likely return in triumph any day now, Mingzhu. You should go to welcome them then.\"","Gu Mingliu, a new mother, spoke with exceptional gentleness. Gu Mingzhu nodded emphatically, then hesitated for a moment.","\"Elder Sister... do you resent Brother-in-Law?\"","Gu Mingliu seemed somewhat surprised and even flicked Gu Mingzhu's forehead. \"Gu Mingzhu, what on earth are you thinking? How could I blame your brother-in-law?\"","\"Without him, our Great Qi would have been one force weaker in this war. Fighting valiantly on the front lines is precisely what my husband should do.\"","\"Of course I wish he could have been by my side, especially during childbirth, a time hanging by a thread. But Mingzhu, one cannot live by love alone.\"","Gu Mingzhu understood, a shadow flickering in her eyes.","\"Thank you for your guidance, Elder Sister. I was mistaken.\"","After leaving the room, the smile completely vanished from Gu Mingzhu's face, replaced even by a sternness reminiscent of Gu Zheng's unsmiling demeanor.","\"Investigate that pastry shop I frequent. Someone is trying to drive a wedge between me and my brother-in-law.\"","If she hadn't asked her elder sister directly, those words would have become a thorn in her heart. After all, she knew best the immense suffering her sister endured during childbirth.","\"It seems like a bed of blooming flowers, but underneath, there are always some vermin crawling in the shadows.\"","Gu Mingzhu sighed like a little adult, then added,","\"If the pastry shop really is problematic, keep the chef who makes the pea flour cakes.\"","......","Elsewhere.","The journey back to the capital was much smoother than the march out. Everyone's faces were lit with joyful smiles, except for the dark-complexioned Li Laoba.","\"General, please put in a good word for me with His Highness. Let me return to the capital with the main army.\"","Why could everyone else leave, while he alone had to stay in Dayue?","His Highness was definitely getting his revenge!","\"His Highness singled you out because he trusts you,\" Gu Zheng said with a fatherly air that made Li Laoba uneasy. \"Although Dayue has been conquered, there may still be attempts to resurge. His Highness is leaving you in command of thirty thousand troops in Dayue to give you another chance to earn merit.\"","\"When the Emperor inevitably dispatches officials to govern Dayue, you'll be responsible for their protection. You have a future so bright it'll keep you up at night.\"","\"Really?\"","Li Laoba didn't believe it. He still felt His Highness was punishing him.","Seeing the deception fail, Gu Zheng's mind raced, and he spoke again, \"Yu Fan is still in Dayue. Don't you want to look after him?\"","Although Yu Fan was out of mortal danger, his injuries weren't suitable for travel, so he was temporarily staying in Dayue to recuperate.","\"I...\"","Li Laoba's face flushed with frustration. The General was Yu Fan's father-in-law, so why wasn't he staying to look after him?","\"You'll be credited with another merit. Farewell.\"","Gu Zheng patted Li Laoba's shoulder, suppressing a laugh.","Good lad, it's truly for your own good to let His Highness vent his anger.","Li Laoba stared blankly as the troops and horses grew farther and farther away, his heart sinking into icy despair.","I'll never shoot my mouth off again!","Gu Zheng scurried over to Song Yu's side, winking and making faces. \"Your Highness, the matter is settled as you wished.\"","Song Yu grinned in response, everything understood without words.","Song Shihuan, standing nearby, felt a flicker of confusion in her almond eyes. Why were Father and General Gu acting so strangely?","Before she could ask, she saw a soldier rushing over. Dismounting and bowing, he hastily reported,","\"Your Highness, Princess, Cheng Guang is on a hunger strike. He says he seeks only death.\"","\"That won't do!\"","Song Yu became immediately anxious. \"Cheng Guang is one of the rare clever minds in Dayue. He even managed to prop up a wretch like Emperor Mingde onto the throne. I was counting on him to be my workhorse.\"","Who would he order around if Cheng Guang died?","Seeing this, Gu Zheng suddenly thought that if he were Cheng Guang, he might prefer death.","But he wasn't... so it was better for Cheng Guang to hang on a while longer.","Inside a prison cart, Cheng Guang lay with his eyes tightly shut, the very picture of a man seeking death. The steamed bun placed beside him remained untouched.","\"Cheng Guang, you wish to die?\"","At Song Yu's voice, Cheng Guang opened his eyes and uttered only one phrase:","\"A loyal minister does not serve two masters.\"","\"Minister Cheng, you jest,\" Song Shihuan's childish voice chimed in, yet her words made Cheng Guang's eyes roll back, nearly fainting. \"You employed many underhanded tactics to secure Emperor Mingde's ascension, costing many their lives. Is that what you call loyalty?\"","\"With a 'master' like Emperor Mingde, is he even worthy of the title?\"","Song Yu looked at his daughter behind him with incredulous delight. Look at that! This sharp little tongue is a perfect inheritance from me!","Let anyone dare say Ah Huan isn't his daughter now!","\"I...\" Cheng Guang tried to defend himself further.","But Song Shihuan had no patience for it. Her goal wasn't merely to use Cheng Guang. If he starved himself to death, other Dayue officials would likely follow suit, potentially inciting unrest among the scholars... which was the last thing Song Shihuan wanted.","So this \"pillar of stability,\" Cheng Guang, absolutely had to be preserved.","\"Minister Cheng, the only way left for you to salvage your reputation now is to pledge loyalty to our Great Qi's Emperor and Crown Prince.\"","\"In the annals of history, you will then be recorded as a capable minister serving under wise rulers. If you die now... you'll be remembered as the treacherous minister of a tyrant, a fitting end.\"","Cheng Guang's hands trembled uncontrollably. He picked up the steamed bun and began devouring it.","Treacherous minister of a tyrant...","If he died like that, his ancestors from the Cheng family would surely drag him down to hell even from their graves...","As they drew closer to Great Qi's borders, Song Yu and Song Shihuan's moods visibly brightened.","After nearly four months, they finally set foot once more on Yongping County, the former border region between Great Qi and Dayue.","All the officials of Yongping County were gathered at the city gates to welcome them. Moreover, common folk spontaneously lined both sides of the streets, kneeling and shouting \"Long live!\" the moment they saw Song Yu and Song Shihuan.","The roar was deafening, echoing for a long time.","\"The Crown Prince has returned! The Princess has returned! Quick... quick, kneel and give thanks!\"","They didn't know what other commoners might think, but for the people of this borderland, this victory guaranteed them a century of peace, free from the harassment of Dayue's frontier troops.","Song Yu, clad in his Crown Prince's python robe, rode on horseback side-by-side with Song Shihuan, neither choosing to ride in a sedan chair.","Seeing the people's overwhelming excitement, father and daughter both had smiles in their eyes.","Especially Song Yu, who was struggling to maintain the dignified composure expected of a Crown Prince.","So, the joy of a triumphant return is a different feeling from the parade of a top scholar...","But then again...","I love them both! I want it all!"]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: He Relishes It","paragraphs":["The Mansion of King Heng.","\"Your Highness, the Crown Prince and the Princess have arrived in Yongping County.\"","Upon hearing the servant's words, King Heng's hand holding the brush paused. Looking at the less-than-elegant calligraphy before him, a sharp glint flashed in his Heng's eyes.","He had not been taught by renowned masters since childhood, so his handwriting was naturally not presentable.","But a prince... how could he not even write well?","\"Where are Liu'er and Huier?\"","\"Your Highness, the young master is studying diligently in the library as you instructed. The young princess went to the girls' school today and has not yet returned.\"","Hearing this, King Heng's expression improved slightly.","\"Prepare the carriage. This prince will enter the palace to see His Majesty.\"","Zichen Hall.","\"King Heng, what urgent matter brings you to see Us?\"","Emperor Yuanyou, though lacking deep affection for this nephew who appeared midway, had granted him ample status and position.","\"Imperial Uncle, your nephew has heard that the Crown Prince and the Princess have arrived in Yongping County. I wish to go personally to welcome them. I cannot wait to see my cousin and Ah Huan.\"","Hearing King Heng's words, a smile also appeared on Emperor Yuanyou's face.","\"We know you are eager to see them, but the local officials have never met you. We fear you might be slighted if you go rashly. Stay and wait with Us in the capital. Given your cousin's temperament, he will rush back within three days.\"","Emperor Yuanyou himself was far more anxious than King Heng.","\"Your nephew was thoughtless. I will follow Imperial Uncle's arrangements in all matters.\"","Seeing his scheme to familiarize himself with the local officials thwarted, King Heng showed no change in expression. Instead, he even stepped forward to actively grind ink for Emperor Yuanyou.","From time to time, he shared amusing anecdotes among the common people, eliciting constant laughter from the Emperor.","Outside the hall, Shen Qingping's eyes were inscrutable.","\"Lord Shen, this servant will announce you immediately.\" Wu Qi said and was about to enter the hall but was stopped by Shen Qingping.","\"No need. This official wished to report to His Majesty regarding the arrangements for welcoming back His Highness and the Princess. Since King Heng is inside, I will find another time.\"","Seeing this, Wu Qi bent his waist slightly, speaking as if casually:","\"Lord Shen, King Heng is very filial, and his character is simple and generous. Many officials praise him highly.\"","Upon hearing this, the smile on Shen Qingping's face widened, but the aura around him made Wu Qi secretly uneasy.","\"Indeed, this official also often hears court ministers praising King Heng. His Highness and the Princess will also be very fond of him when they return.\"","It wasn't until he passed through the palace gates that Shen Qingping's expression finally turned completely cold.","The Shen Residence.","\"Nian'an, who has upset your master?\"","Shen Mingwen's words made Nian'an's eyelid twitch. Why did it feel like the master was enjoying seeing the third master being thwarted?","\"Father, what do you think of King Heng?\"","Shen Qingping's question made Shen Mingwen pause. After holding back for a long while, Shen Mingwen managed to say:","\"He is not as simple as he appears on the surface.\"","A prince who seemed honest and generous, yet knew to request him, the Grand Tutor of the court, to instruct King Heng's son. If he hadn't been sharp-witted, he would have truly been deceived by King Heng's facade.","Princess Yale had not been at the girls' school for long. Though her knowledge was not extensive, she had won the praise of many noble ladies.","This was not a situation someone without any cunning could achieve.","Shen Qingping sighed. \"King Heng is much cleverer than His Majesty's own sons.\"","For a moment, Shen Mingwen wanted to jump up and cover Shen Qingping's mouth.","\"You... if you keep speaking such treasonous words, this old man will pin you down and give you a beating.\" Shen Mingwen pointed angrily at Shen Qingping's nose. Was it easy being this scoundrel's father?","\"Prince Ping was arrogant, hence his defeat and death.\"","\"Prince Chu was foolish, acting without considering the consequences, hence his house arrest.\"","\"Prince Qi was cowardly, valuing his life above all else, hence his departure to his fiefdom.\"","\"But this King Heng... is not easy to deal with.\"","Shen Qingping slumped into a soft chair, sitting improperly without a proper posture, making Shen Mingwen frown so deeply it could crush a fly.","\"A few days ago during the morning court, some ministers subconsciously praised the auspicious fortune of the royal twins. That was not without reason.\" Shen Qingping's sharp eyes seemed always able to see deeper than the surface. \"It's because the family of King Heng now enjoys great reputation in the court.\"","\"Third Son, His Majesty has stated explicitly that the position of the Crown Prince is unshakable.\"","Shen Mingwen sighed. \"You need not worry excessively.\"","Looking at a particularly prominent white hair at Shen Qingping's temple, Shen Mingwen felt a sharp pang of sorrow.","\"Father, you are the Grand Tutor of the court. Assisting His Majesty in governance is your duty.\" At this point, Shen Qingping curled the corner of his mouth. \"But I, your son, am an official of the Eastern Palace. I must keep a tight watch on anyone who could pose a threat to the Crown Prince.\"","His Highness and the Princess are facing danger and fighting wars at the front.","Yet in the rear, King Heng's family is gaining much good reputation.","That's right, he simply couldn't stand it.","After Shen Qingping left, Lady Shen entered the room from outside, carrying tea.","Shen Mingwen took a sip of tea. \"This old man is not as good as this son.\"","\"This humble wife dares to speak words behind closed doors: Your relationship with His Majesty, sir, is one that began midway.\" A hint of a smile appeared in Lady Shen's eyes. \"Even your relationship with the Crown Prince is that of a teacher and student who met midway.\"","\"But Ping'er and His Highness share a bond forged since childhood. If His Highness ascends the throne one day, no one among all the court officials will be more trusted by him than Ping'er.\"","\"If Ping'er did not act this way, that would truly be failing His Highness.\"","Shen Mingwen leaned back in his chair, wiping his face. \"He is not yet forty, yet his hair is already turning white prematurely.\"","\"Extreme intelligence brings harm. He cannot always be so tense.\"","Shen Mingwen genuinely ached for this son from the bottom of his heart.","Hearing this, the smile on Lady Shen's face gradually faded. Husband and wife looked at each other in silence.","...","King Heng did not get his wish, but that very night, Shen Qingping left the capital on horseback.","He happened to meet Song Yu and Song Shihuan, who were hastening their journey, in Laijin Prefecture.","\"Teacher!\"","Upon seeing Shen Qingping, Song Shihuan called out happily. \"Did Teacher come specially to welcome me because you heard of my victory?\"","During the months of war, even though praised by officers and soldiers from top to bottom, Song Shihuan had never shown a hint of pride or complacency.","Now, upon seeing Shen Qingping, she unconsciously revealed a bit.","\"I specially had someone write the Princess's heroic deeds into a storybook, along with Your Highness's. We'll have the opera troupe perform them well later.\"","\"Well done.\" Song Yu offered restrained praise.","Due to Shen Qingping's arrival, Song Yu ordered the main army to continue marching while he and Song Shihuan rested there for the night, catching up with the army the next day.","The three of them, wearing veiled hats, walked the streets of Laijin Prefecture.","\"Is this a school opened by the Shen family?\" Song Shihuan looked curiously several times. The sound of children reading aloud came from inside, refreshing to the heart.","The school was large, accommodating many children.","Shen Qingping nodded.","That year, when Shen Qinghui made a mistake, he promised on behalf of the Shen family to establish a school in Laijin Prefecture.","Since he promised, he would ensure it was done to the best of his ability.","\"Teacher, thank you.\"","\"My father and I thank you on behalf of the children of Laijin Prefecture.\"","Through the black gauze of the veiled hat, Shen Qingping saw the bright eyes of both Song Shihuan and Song Yu.","The world could not fathom why he would pour his heart and soul into it to such an extent.","For him, it was a labor of love."]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: When three people hang out together, there's always one... follower.","paragraphs":["The three of them found a private room in an inn and sat down.","It was a rare moment of relaxation for all.","\"So, how have things been?\"","Song Yu looked at Shen Qingping. \"I've been away from the capital for months. Why do you look like you've aged several years?\"","Shen Qingping paused while drinking his water. Could someone please come and shut His Highness's mouth?","\"I haven't had the chance to congratulate Your Highness yet...\"","Song Yu thought Shen Qingping was going to personally congratulate him once more on his great victory, but his expression froze the next second as Shen Qingping continued his lecture:","\"...on gaining a younger brother.\"","\"What is Song Heng like?\" Song Yu asked irritably, running a hand through his hair. He had finally swatted away a few flies, and now another one had appeared?","\"My father's assessment is that he is not as simple as he appears on the surface. He even wanted to leave the capital to personally welcome Your Highness, but the Emperor rejected it. You'll understand after interacting with him a few times after your return to the capital.\"","Shen Qingping took a slow sip of water. \"If Prince Heng harbors no improper ambitions, then it's fine. If he does, Your Highness will have your hands full.\"","\"No matter. We'll cross that bridge when we come to it.\"","Song Shihuan spoke up, having watched Shen Qingping for a while. She feared her teacher had been quite troubled by these matters lately; he did look rather haggard.","\"Teacher, let me tell you about our experiences on the battlefield.\"","Song Shihuan smiled, changing the subject. Shen Qingping listened as father and daughter chattered away about the war, sipping his tea.","He even refrained from rebutting when Song Yu boasted extravagantly about his own exploits.","When he heard that everyone in the army admired Song Shihuan, Shen Qingping laughed outright—a genuine, deeply relaxed laugh, unlike the faint smiles he wore in the capital.","\"No one could dislike the Junzhu.\"","Many years later, Shen Qingping would still fondly remember this day in Laijin Prefecture. It was as if he had shed all burdens and become that carefree, frivolous young master from years past, free of worldly worries.","Just as the three of them were engrossed in their lively conversation, Liuxi and Nian'an rushed into the private room.","\"Your Highness, someone has been following us!\"","Following?","The trio immediately grew alert.","\"Where are they?\"","As soon as the words were spoken, a person bundled up from head to toe was brought in. Song Shihuan looked at the pair of eyes revealed and felt as if struck by lightning.","\"They're one of us, don't attack.\"","\"Gu Mingzhu, is that you?\" Song Yu stepped forward and yanked off Gu Mingzhu's hood, then laughed in exasperation. \"Did you sneak here following Shen Qingping?\"","Gu Mingzhu, looking embarrassed, nodded.","Shen Qingping and Song Shihuan covered their eyes simultaneously. It was too much to bear.","\"Then why were you tailing us instead of just coming out to meet us?\"","\"What else? Afraid of running into her father, of course.\" Shen Qingping's remark made Gu Mingzhu grimace.","A few moments later, Gu Mingzhu got her wish and joined them at the table.","\"Junzhu—\"","To the surprise of Song Yu and Shen Qingping, Gu Mingzhu immediately threw her arms around Song Shihuan and began to cry.","She cried about being lonely at home, about Gu Mingliu's difficult childbirth, about Yu Fan being injured... In short, she cried so much that Song Yu and Shen Qingping wanted to plug their ears.","\"If you keep crying, I'll throw you out,\" threatened Song Yu.","The crying continued, even showing signs of rising in pitch.","\"If you keep crying, I'll summon Gu Zheng back.\"","The world fell silent.","\"Someone is trying to harm me,\" Gu Mingzhu said between sobs, sounding utterly wronged.","She gave a highly embellished account of someone trying to sow discord between her and Yu Fan.","\"Have you found out who it is?\" Shen Qingping asked, narrowing his eyes slightly.","\"No. We only know a servant from the shop has disappeared.\"","\"The waters of the capital truly never settle.\"","Shen Qingping murmured softly.","\"I was scared because we couldn't find anything. I went to the Shen residence and happened to see Young Master Shen on horseback, seemingly about to leave the capital. I thought he must be going to find Your Highness and the Junzhu, so I followed.\"","Gu Mingzhu kept talking, her hands never pausing as she picked up pastries.","\"But now that Your Highness and the Junzhu are returning to the capital, I feel at ease.\"","After all, if the sky falls, there are tall people like His Highness and Young Master Shen to hold it up. She was short, so she wasn't afraid.","Song Yu and Shen Qingping both rolled their eyes upon hearing this. Song Yu wearily called out to Liuxi:","\"Tell the waiter to bring more food.\"","Otherwise, it wouldn't be enough for this young lady alone.","Gu Mingzhu grinned happily upon hearing this. His Highness had changed quite a bit during his trip.","With Gu Mingzhu joining them, the conversation in the private room flowed endlessly, punctuated by bursts of laughter and friendly banter.","Outside the room, Liuxi and Nian'an exchanged a smile.","Such noisy liveliness was far better than cold silence.","......","Zichen Palace.","\"What? Shen the Third went directly to find Yu'er and Ah Huan?\"","\"What? The Gu family girl went too?\"","Emperor Yuanyou sighed to the heavens. They all can go, so why can't I!","\"Your Majesty, this is something Young Master Shen gave to this servant before he left. He said he drafted a protocol for welcoming His Highness and the Junzhu's triumphant return, and asks if Your Majesty would review it for suitability.\"","Taking the memorial, Emperor Yuanyou snorted.","Outrageous. Truly outrageous.","No matter what, he would find some fault with this memorial.","After reading it, however, the Emperor's expression turned peculiar. \"Just... just proceed as Shen the Third suggests.\"","It was arranged flawlessly, leaving no room for criticism.","\"And also...\" Wu Qi felt his scalp prickle. \"Young Master Shen also said that if there are to be rewards for His Highness or the Junzhu, he would persuade them to decline and let more of the rewards go to the soldiers.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's face shifted through several expressions, but in the end, he said nothing.","That scoundrel really has some luck with his ministers, to have a pillar like Shen the Third by his side.","After a few moments, Emperor Yuanyou spoke slowly, \"Reduce the rewards I originally planned for the soldiers by twenty percent. Then, let the Crown Prince and the Junzhu plead for additional imperial favor on the soldiers' behalf.\"","The rewards initially decided upon were already exceptionally generous. Even reduced by twenty percent, they would still be substantial.","Since Shen the Third had made arrangements, he was willing to go with the flow and let Yu'er and Ah Huan gain even better reputations.","Two days later, Song Yu and Song Shihuan personally led the main army to the outskirts of the capital.","When they departed, the army was led by Song Yu and Gu Zheng. Upon return... Gu Zheng had dutifully fallen back behind Song Yu and Song Shihuan.","Emperor Yuanyou, dressed in the Son of Heaven's dragon robes, led the civil and military officials to welcome them outside the capital.","All officials wore their court robes, standing in order of rank.","Imperial clan relatives stood behind Emperor Yuanyou. Even Lady Chang and Song Xiyan from the Ping Prince's household had been summoned.","The common people poured out of their homes, lining both sides of the streets within the capital to wait. The spectacle was grand and rare.","Song Yu was also momentarily stunned by the scene before him. He dismounted briskly and, with Song Shihuan, walked up to Emperor Yuanyou and knelt.","\"Your son has not failed your trust, Father. We achieved a great victory.\"","\"Your granddaughter has not failed your trust, Imperial Grandfather. We achieved a great victory.\"","A gust of wind blew, making the great Qi war banner flutter sharply. Gu Zheng held the banner high, and hundreds of thousands of soldiers knelt in unison, shouting:","\"We have not failed Your Majesty's trust. We achieved a great victory.\"","Even the gods in heaven should have been able to hear the sound of the Great Qi's victory."]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: Princess Fu'an......","paragraphs":["\"Everyone, rise.\"","Emperor Yuanyou personally helped Song Shihuan, who was next to Song Yu, to her feet.","Song Yu wore an expression that said he had expected this, and obediently stood up by himself.","\"Ah Huan, this time you have rendered a great service to Da Qi. Your imperial grandfather is proud of you.\" Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Shihuan, who had grown much thinner, his heart aching for her.","He automatically ignored his own grown son standing beside her.","\"Ahem—\" Song Yu couldn't help but clear his throat, trying to evoke the Emperor's rather scant paternal affection.","But when Emperor Yuanyou saw Song Yu, who hadn't lost an ounce of weight and instead had gained some flesh on his face, the old Emperor's expression immediately lost its smile.","Why hadn't this rascal lost weight, while his precious granddaughter had grown thin?","If Song Yu knew what Emperor Yuanyou was thinking, he would cry injustice. This extra weight was purely from being forced to drink rice porridge.","The granaries were overflowing, so they had to drink their fill.","He wasn't on the front lines fighting, nor did he have to devise battle tactics; his energy expenditure was low, so naturally, he gained weight.","\"You did well this time.\"","Emperor Yuanyou finally did say a word to Song Yu, who immediately flashed a wide, toothy grin.","\"Mind your decorum.\"","Emperor Yuanyou couldn't help but remind him.","So many eyes were watching; he mustn't disgrace his old father's face.","\"Wu Qi, announce the decree.\"","The edict of rewards took Wu Qi a full stick of incense's time to read aloud. By the time he finished, his mouth was parched, and everyone present was stunned into silence.","Crown Prince Song Yu was rewarded with a thousand pieces of gold.","Crown Prince's daughter, Song Shihuan... was enfeoffed as Princess Fu'an, with a stipend of ten thousand households?","According to ceremonial laws, the daughters of the Crown Prince and princes are titled Commandery Princesses. Only under special circumstances or by exceptional grace are they enfeoffed as Princesses.","Yet the civil officials and censors present, even the Minister of Rites himself, kept their mouths tightly shut.","To hold the foremost merit in a war that destroyed an enemy state—such an achievement was sufficient for exceptional grace and enfeoffment.","Song Shihuan clearly hadn't anticipated that Emperor Yuanyou would bestow such a reward upon her either, standing there rooted to the spot in surprise.","The first Princess of Da Qi...","It was Song Yu who remembered Shen Qingping's advice. Under the gaze of the crowd, he knelt once more. \"Father Emperor, your son does not want the gold. I beg Your Majesty to bestow these rewards upon the soldiers who fought valiantly on the battlefield.\"","\"Imperial Grandfather, your granddaughter also does not want rewards. The victory was carved out by the soldiers blade by blade, sword by sword. They are the ones most deserving of reward.\"","Thus, father and daughter nearly won over the entire army's loyalty in one fell swoop.","At this moment, even if the father and daughter ordered the soldiers to march to their deaths, they would not hesitate for a moment.","Those in high positions stepping down from their pedestals, patiently listening to their hardships—no one could resist such an allure.","\"Crown Prince, I can take back your thousand pieces of gold.\"","\"Ah Huan, I can also take back your stipend households, all to be exchanged for rewards for the soldiers. However, your title of Princess is not to be refused.\"","Emperor Yuanyou couldn't help but reach out and stroke Song Shihuan's cheek. This princess title was what his granddaughter deserved.","\"Thank you for your grace, Imperial Grandfather.\"","\"Congratulations, Princess.\" Wu Qi was also immensely pleased. Seeing this, the host of courtiers behind him chimed in unison, \"Congratulations, Princess Fu'an.\"","From then on, there was no more Commandery Princess Fu'an, only Princess Fu'an, who, as the daughter of the Crown Prince, was exceptionally enfeoffed as a Princess.","Lady Chang looked at Song Shihuan before her, her eyes rimmed red.","She had never imagined her daughter could possess such capability—top of the women's academy, devising strategies on the battlefield, she had actually become the most accomplished descendant of the Chang family.","That young girl witnessing slaughter on the battlefield—she wondered if she had been afraid?","Lady Chang longed to walk to Song Shihuan's side and hug her child, but she no longer had the right.","Song Xiyan kept her head lowered the entire time, making it impossible to tell what she was thinking.","The family of King Heng all wore gentle smiles on their faces, but the warmth did not reach their eyes.","\"Imperial Grandfather, I heard I have gained another uncle.\"","Song Shihuan tilted her head as she spoke. Emperor Yuanyou then remembered King Heng behind him and beckoned for him to come forward with his son and daughter.","\"According to age, this is your Third Uncle, now enfeoffed as King Heng.\"","\"Greetings, Third Uncle.\"","King Heng laughed upon hearing this and took out an exquisite box from his sleeve. \"Meeting for the first time, Ah Huan. Congratulations on your triumphant return.\"","\"This is your elder male cousin, Liu'er, and your elder female cousin, Hui'er.\"","Song Hui looked at the Song Shihuan before her, somewhat dazed.","Since returning to the imperial family, she had often heard about how favored and talented this cousin was. Now, seeing her in person... could someone like her ever stand shoulder to shoulder with her?","The minds of King Heng's family were turning a hundred times over, but their expressions gave no cause for fault.","Just as King Heng was about to step forward to pay his respects to Song Yu, Emperor Yuanyou's voice rang out:","\"Alright, there will be a palace banquet tonight. You can all get properly acquainted then.\"","Emperor Yuanyou took Song Shihuan's hand and entered the capital city gate. The cheers and bows of the common people rose one after another, all eager to catch a glimpse of Princess Fu'an's grace.","Behind them, Shen Mingwen glared at Shen Qingping—leaving without a word, that little rascal.","Shen Qingping, however, acted as if nothing had happened, cheerfully following behind Song Yu, completely ignoring Shen Mingwen's dagger-like stares.","Gu Zheng hurriedly returned to the Gu residence, anxious to hold his freshly 'produced' granddaughter.","In the crowd, King Heng spoke as if unintentionally, \"Earlier, His Majesty's expression when looking at His Highness the Crown Prince didn't seem too favorable?\"","It rather gave him the feeling that the father was honored because of the daughter.","An official smiled and said, \"His Majesty and His Highness have always interacted this way. In the future, you might even see His Majesty chasing His Highness around the Zichen Hall to beat him. In truth, His Majesty is most satisfied with His Highness.\"","\"Indeed, it's just the special affection for the next generation. His Majesty's satisfaction is simply expressed more through the Princess.\"","\"I see. Thank you for informing me, gentlemen.\"","Having gotten his answer, the boulder in King Heng's heart sank even heavier.","How should he deal with such a situation?","...","Gu Residence.","Gu Mingzhu was being punished, standing in the room holding a basin filled with water.","\"Gu Mingzhu, have you grown too bold for your boots? Slipping out of the capital without even a word? If the capital guards hadn't sent a message back in time, what was I supposed to do?\"","Gu Mingliu's eyes were red with anger. Even Gu Zheng stood to the side, not daring to plead for leniency.","When the eldest daughter was angry, the situation was serious.","\"I was wrong. The situation was urgent at the time, so I just told the guards to send a message back...\"","\"You still dare to argue!\"","\"I dare not.\" Gu Mingzhu obediently admitted defeat.","It took Gu Mingliu a long while to calm her emotions. Then, after staring at Gu Zheng for a long time, she finally realized something was amiss. Her voice began to tremble slightly:","\"Where is Yu Fan?\"","\"Didn't we win the war? Why hasn't Yu Fan returned?\"","Gu Zheng's old face stiffened. He made eyes at Gu Mingzhu, who signaled for him to speak. Father and daughter stared at each other, neither daring to speak first.","\"Has he... had an accident? Is he... gone?\"","\"No, no, no,\" Gu Zheng hurriedly said. \"He's alive, he's alive.\"","\"Then he's injured, wounded so severely he can't be moved, is that it?\"","Under Gu Mingliu's gaze, the excuses Gu Zheng had prepared beforehand—like Yu Fan needing to stay behind to guard the army—were completely unspeakable. He nodded weakly.","\"Imperial Physician Mei is already treating Yu Fan. He says the recovery is going well, and in another month, he can be moved back to the residence to recuperate.\"","\"Mingliu, this time Yu Fan has performed a great service. He was very brave, a son our Gu family can be proud of.\"","But Gu Mingliu only held the little one in the swaddling clothes tighter.","A tear fell on the infant's cheek. Suddenly, Gu Mingliu remembered what had happened on the day Mei Zhilin left. Then, she kissed the little one tenderly.","\"So, Tuan, this name was chosen by your father.\""]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: My... Younger Brother","paragraphs":["That evening, Emperor Yuanyou held a grand victory banquet in the palace.","Lady Chang and Song Xiyan were supposed to return to confinement in the Ping Prince's mansion, but Song Yu spoke up softly:","\"After all, Yan Zheng has brought great honor to Da Qi this time, Father. Perhaps the ban on the Ping Prince's mansion could be lifted?\"","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Yu several times. Had this scoundrel been possessed?","He usually gnashed his teeth at the mention of the Ping Prince's mansion, so why was he pleading for them today?","\"Your Majesty, the Crown Prince speaks reason. The matter of the Eldest Imperial Grandson is known to the people. Compensating the Ping Prince's mansion in this way is also fitting.\"","Shen Mingwen also voiced his agreement. Seeing this, the assembled ministers also began to plead for the Ping Prince's mansion.","Only one princess of a principality (junzhu) remains; she poses no threat.","\"If that is the case, then let the ban on the Ping Prince's mansion be lifted.\"","Hearing Emperor Yuanyou's words, Song Xiyan finally looked up in disbelief, her eyes filled with joy.","Seeing this, Shen Qingping curled the corner of his mouth slightly. Still joyful? The next target for His Highness will be this last remaining junzhu.","How can you beat a dog if you don't let it out?","At the palace banquet, Song Yu and Song Shihuan were clearly the center of attention.","Song Shihuan was directly summoned by Emperor Yuanyou to sit beside him, where he inquired in detail about the situation on the battlefield.","Seeing this, King Heng raised his wine cup and walked up to Song Yu. \"Elder Brother, let me offer you a toast.\"","This gave Song Yu a chance to scrutinize King Heng carefully before him.","After a few moments, Song Yu parted his thin lips. \"My... younger brother?\"","\"Unfortunately, my younger brothers usually don't come to good ends.\"","Instantly, the smile on King Heng's face nearly faltered.","\"Elder Brother, what are you saying? Having just returned to the royal family, there are many matters I am not yet familiar with. Once I am accustomed, I can help share Elder Brother's burdens.\" Song Heng wore an obedient and honest expression. \"Whenever Elder Brother has need, just give the order.\"","\"You are somewhat better than the Chu and Qi Princes.\"","Song Yu's gaze was inscrutable as he drained his cup.","\"Liu'er, come quickly and greet your Eldest Uncle.\" King Heng called out to Song Liu, who immediately stepped before Song Yu. The spirited youth was already up to Song Yu's shoulder in height and acted particularly affectionate towards him.","\"Liu'er pays his respects to Eldest Uncle.\"","\"Could Eldest Uncle tell Liu'er about the battles? Liu'er has dreamed since childhood of becoming a great general, but our family was poor and couldn't afford a martial arts tutor.\"","\"Gu Zheng knows more about battlefield matters than I do. Go ask him.\"","Song Yu felt he truly was still annoyed by children, just not by A'Huan.","Seeing he was refused, Song Liu wasn't angered. Instead, he clung to Song Yu's side, asking all sorts of questions.","The court officials watched this scene of \"harmony between uncle and nephew,\" each with their own thoughts.","The Crown Prince is now of age to marry.","How can it be acceptable for him to have only a princess at his knee?","...","\"Xiyan younger sister, may I call you that?\"","Song Xiyan looked up dazedly at Song Hui, who was showing her kindness, and gave a slight tug at the corner of her mouth. \"They all avoid me like the plague. Why have you come?\"","\"You are a royal junzhu, and also my younger sister. No matter what, I cannot stand by and watch you be isolated and bullied.\"","A warm current flowed through Song Xiyan's heart, and she actually felt an impulse to cry.","\"If you don't mind, you may call me A'Hui.\"","\"A'Hui elder sister.\"","Seeing Song Xiyan's expression soften, Song Hui patted the back of her hand. \"We are Da Qi's junzhu. Do not fear the gazes of others.\"","She had heard many stories about this Xiyan Junzhu in the women's academy. If used properly, she could be a sharp weapon.","Unaware that she had already become a chess piece on someone else's board, Song Xiyan was still greedily clinging to the warmth Song Hui doled out.","\"If only A'Hui elder sister were my blood sister.\"","\"But we are already sisters connected by blood.\"","Song Hui blinked at Song Xiyan.","Unbeknownst to them, it all fell into Song Yu's sight. He raised his wine cup, a smile curling at his lips.","If Song Hui was wicked, it would coincidentally allow Song Xiyan to taste the feeling of betrayal by a blood relative. A fortunate accident.","At the victory banquet, all parties were satisfied.","After Emperor Yuanyou returned to the Zichen Hall, everyone rose to leave.","Song Liu walked up to Song Shihuan. \"A'Huan younger sister, let me escort you back to the Eastern Palace.\"","A big question mark popped up in Song Shihuan's mind.","\"I'll go back with Father.\"","Did she need an escort?","\"I didn't get a chance to speak with you tonight, A'Huan younger sister.\" Song Liu put on an elder brother's demeanor. \"If you ever need help in the future, A'Huan, just tell me. Feel free to order me around like a real older brother.\"","An official nearby, seeing this, couldn't help but nod, whispering to his colleague, \"King Heng's heir and the Yalle Junzhu both seem kind-hearted, especially the heir. He seems more like the princess's elder brother than the previous few.\"","As the surrounding officials nodded in agreement, Shen Mingwen sensed something was amiss.","Shen Residence.","\"Could King Heng be planning to take advantage of His Highness having no sons, aiming to push his heir onto His Highness as a son?\"","Having said this, before Shen Qingping could speak, Shen Mingwen negated his own words. \"No, His Highness is in his prime. Once he marries a Crown Princess, he won't lack for legitimate heirs. I must be overthinking.\"","But Shen Qingping's expression did not improve as he slowly said,","\"What if His Highness is unwilling to marry, or if, after marrying, the Crown Princess fails to produce a legitimate heir for a long time?\"","If King Heng truly harbored such intentions, then it would indeed... be quite troublesome.","At least for now, King Heng's household conducted itself cautiously and properly. Coupled with the auspicious blessing of the dragon-phoenix twins, they had won considerable praise from the court officials.","\"Earlier, I noticed the Yalle Junzhu was constantly speaking with the Second Junzhu... oh no, the Third Junzhu. Perhaps we are overthinking.\" Shen Mingwen sighed, but his heart remained heavy.","To be honest, even Shen Mingwen himself didn't believe he was overthinking.","\"Nian'an, dispatch people to keep a close watch on King Heng's mansion.\"","Shen Qingping's face was full of cold intent. He had said it all along—King Heng's family was not honest.","As if remembering something, Shen Qingping strode out of the residence.","\"Where are you going so late?\"","Shen Mingwen's anxious voice followed from behind.","...","King Heng's Mansion.","\"Liu'er did very well today.\"","King Heng patted Song Liu's shoulder in approval.","\"Hui'er as well.\"","\"Father has said that as a male of the royal house, I must be especially mindful of my reputation.\" Song Liu spoke slowly. \"Your son keeps Father's teachings in mind at all times, advancing step by step with steady footing, not daring to take a single wrong step.\"","\"Your daughter does the same.\"","King Heng looked at his son and daughter, feeling even more resentment towards his father for deliberately concealing their identities. If not for that, why would the children have to be so cautious now?","\"Only strike when you are sure of a single, fatal blow. At all other times, remain calm and lie in wait.\" King Heng's eyes flashed with immense ambition. Being a leisurely, idle prince was certainly good.","But the Crown Prince had no sons. He could also strive for it.","\"Have the loose ends at the pastry shop been dealt with?\"","\"Father, they have been taken care of.\"","Song Hui lowered her head slightly, hiding the dark glint in her eyes."]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: Cheng Guang's Heated Debate with Prince Heng","paragraphs":["The Eastern Palace.","\"Father has released Song Xiyan.\"","Under the moonlight, Song Yu and Song Shihuan were strolling along a path in the Eastern Palace to aid their digestion.","\"I told you, none of those from Pingwang Manor who bullied you will come to a good end.\"","Song Yu's tone was light and casual, yet Song Shihuan's eyelashes fluttered slightly.","\"Now only Song Xiyan remains. Ah Huan, just watch her bring about her own destruction.\"","Song Yu was no longer the idle, pleasure-seeking prince who could be easily fooled. He had now learned to use leverage, manipulating people's hearts effortlessly.","\"But...\"","Song Shihuan wanted to say more, but Song Yu flicked her forehead. \"Starting tomorrow, you go keep your Imperial Grandfather company. Relax properly. On the battlefield, I couldn't help you and could only watch you toil. Now that we're in the capital, I can protect our Princess properly.\"","The words 'our Princess' made Song Shihuan blush.","\"Father, you're teasing me.\"","\"Ah Huan is utterly deserving of this princess title. The only regret is that the conferment did not come from me.\"","Song Yu smiled, looking at Song Shihuan whose features were becoming more defined. \"Rest early. Tomorrow, go visit the Gu residence and see that A'Tuan you've been pining for.\"","At the mention of A'Tuan, Song Shihuan's heart melted into a bubbly softness.","...","Early the next morning.","Song Shihuan arrived at the Gu residence and saw Gu Mingliu, who was still wearing a forehead band.","\"Sister Gu.\"","Instead of rushing to see A'Tuan first, Song Shihuan took Gu Mingliu's hand. \"Sister Gu, don't worry about Yu Fan. Imperial Grandfather has appointed him as a Deputy Fifth Rank Commander. To rise from a commoner to Deputy Fifth Rank is an unprecedented honor.\"","\"That's right. Even young Lord Shen is only a proper Seventh Rank,\" Gu Mingzhu immediately chimed in, taking a jab at Shen Qingping.","\"He earned his merits in battle, and I am happy for him,\" Gu Mingliu understood Song Shihuan's concern. \"Your Highness, rest assured. I know Physician Mei is treating his injuries, and I am at ease.\"","\"That's good then.\"","Only then did Song Shihuan look at A'Tuan in the swaddling clothes. The baby's skin was as white and tender as tofu, with grape-like eyes that were incredibly clear. Song Shihuan fell in love with little A'Tuan at first sight.","\"Truly a child this princess has been looking forward to since before its birth.\"","Song Shihuan hadn't cuddled with A'Tuan for long when a servant reported that Song Hui had arrived with Song Xiyan.","Gu Mingzhu immediately rolled her eyes.","Of all times, they had to come now.","\"Mingzhu, go welcome the two young mistresses in,\" Gu Mingliu, sensing the shift in atmosphere, instructed Gu Mingzhu with a smile.","Soon, Song Hui's laughter rang out.","\"It seems Sister Xiyan and I have come at just the right time, bumping into Sister Ah Huan.\"","Then, Song Hui turned to Gu Mingliu. \"I heard Sister Gu suffered greatly during childbirth, with Master Yu not by your side. It even scared Mingzhu to tears.\"","A seemingly ordinary sentence, yet the looks in Gu Mingzhu and Song Shihuan's eyes changed instantly.","The pastry shop...","Song Shihuan, who had just risen from her seat, sat back down. This is getting interesting...","At the same time, in the Zichen Hall.","\"How do you all think these newly acquired cities should be governed?\"","A group of senior ministers had been summoned to the palace. Faced with Emperor Yuanyou's question, each offered different answers.","Even King Heng, under the encouraging gazes of the ministers, boldly voiced his opinion.","Seeing this, Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Yu. \"Crown Prince, what are your thoughts?\"","\"Replying to Father Emperor, your son has no particular thoughts.\" As soon as Song Yu said this, joy surged within King Heng. The information he had gathered was correct; the Crown Prince was still a wastrel just a few years ago.","But the next moment, Song Yu spoke again:","\"However, there is one person who should know. This person is the former Prime Minister of Great Yue, Cheng Guang.\"","Cheng Guang was brought into the palace and scrutinized by the senior ministers of Great Qi for a good while.","Then, the Crown Prince walked up to Cheng Guang. \"Cheng Guang, we're troubled over how to govern those cities. Think of a solution for us.\"","Cheng Guang paused. To kill a man and condemn his heart.","\"If the solution is good, we might consider giving you an official post.\"","Song Yu acted as if he and Cheng Guang were the best of buddies. \"The solution must both stabilize the local populace and produce administrative achievements.\"","\"Elder Brother, Great Yue has been destroyed. What talent could their prime minister possibly have?\"","King Heng spoke without thinking, inexplicably wanting to appear superior to Song Yu before Emperor Yuanyou.","But it backfired.","Cheng Guang had been somewhat reluctant, but provoked by King Heng, he immediately said:","\"Isn't it simple? Just appoint two prefects in each city, with equal authority. One should be an old official from Great Yue, and one an official from Great Qi. They check and supervise each other. The Great Yue official stabilizes the populace, the Great Qi official is responsible for achievements. After a stable transition, reduce to one Great Qi official.\"","Cheng Guang's words left everyone present stunned.","This method was truly better than all the ones previously discussed.","Even Emperor Yuanyou couldn't help but take a few more looks at Cheng Guang. He remembered Ah Huan mentioning this person, saying he was capable.","Cheng Guang gave a cold snort and walked up to King Heng. \"And which prince might you be?\"","\"Minister Cheng, this is my cousin, the newly recognized King Heng,\" Song Yu kindly and thoughtfully added.","\"Not raised under the guidance of a great talent since childhood, no wonder your vision is so shortsighted.\"","Ignoring King Heng's stiff expression, Cheng Guang went all out:","\"Is the prime minister of a nation a position just anyone can hold? No matter how weak a country, one should not belittle its senior ministers. Your Highness's behavior makes me think Great Qi is nothing more than this.\"","Since being recognized, King Heng had been praised wherever he went. This was the first time he was pointed at and scolded, and his face turned pale.","\"You defeated foe, how dare you openly provoke a prince of our Great Qi!\" A senior minister, feeling Cheng Guang's act was provocative, rebuked him.","\"I am a defeated foe, but I was defeated by the Crown Prince and the Princess, not by you.\" Cheng Guang seemed to have unlocked some inner potential. \"The reason I stand before you is by the Crown Prince's will. I offered this strategy in response to the Crown Prince's request.\"","\"Yet your King Heng here constantly belittles me. Isn't he simultaneously belittling the Crown Prince?\"","Cheng Guang scoffed lightly. \"He must harbor some ill intentions.\"","\"Uncle, I absolutely have no such intention! This man's words are pure slander!\" King Heng anxiously knelt on the ground, his back soaked with sweat.","Seeing this, Cheng Guang snorted coldly:","\"Anyone with a bit of sense knows to say they have no ill intentions. Your Highness the Crown Prince, you'd better be more wary.\"","Song Yu struggled to suppress the corners of his mouth from turning up and immediately decided to send a pot of wine to Cheng Guang that evening."]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: Revisiting the Matter of the Crown Princess","paragraphs":["\"Are you willing to serve this prince?\"","Under the night sky, Cheng Guang looked at Song Yu, whose eyes held a smile before him, and then glanced at Song Shihuan, who was taking small sips of fruit wine beside them. He felt as if he were in a dream.","\"Last year... last year I nearly... nearly harmed Yu Fan.\"","Cheng Guang's speech was even stammering. He hadn't seen Gu Zheng look at him like a starving tiger pouncing on prey, practically wanting to devour him whole.","He had been avoiding Gu Zheng every time.","\"It's not too late to atone for your mistakes with merit.\"","Song Yu's slender fingers were curled, the knuckles flushed with a faint red, as he rhythmically tapped the table. \"As long as you serve this prince loyally, I can give you more than your old master ever could.\"","After a few moments, Cheng Guang knelt down with a pious expression.","\"I am willing to be driven by Your Highness.\"","\"Good.\" A slight smile tugged at Song Yu's lips. \"That Prince Heng is getting restless. He will surely make another move soon. Your sharp, venomous tongue is most suitable for dealing with such a hypocrite.\"","Upon hearing this, Cheng Guang was taken aback. Was he, with all his abilities, being sent to deal with some illegitimate, worthless prince?","Wasn't that a bit of a waste?","As if reading his thoughts, Song Shihuan spoke up with a light laugh. \"Father must first test how sharp this blade of yours is.\"","Cheng Guang nodded.","Then, gathering his courage, he asked, \"If in the future... would I still have a chance to become Chancellor?\"","\"No chance.\"","Song Yu didn't hesitate for even a moment. \"The position of Chancellor was decided by this prince back when I was still a wastrel.\"","Cheng Guang was disappointed. Cheng Guang sighed. Cheng Guang shed a tear.","Who had acted so early?","......","With Song Yu's support, Cheng Guang transformed from the chancellor of an enemy state into the largely ceremonial and powerless Vice Minister of the Court of Imperial Entertainments in Great Qi.","Since it was a titular position without real authority, there weren't many voices of opposition in the court. The only one suffering was Prince Heng, whose demeanor from princely etiquette to his handling of affairs was criticized thoroughly by Cheng Guang.","Originally, Prince Heng could rely on his reputation for generosity and benevolence to win the favor of court officials. But when someone started crowing like a goose all day long about his ordinary origins, some noble families also began to look down on him.","The worst part was he couldn't easily retort.","It infuriated Prince Heng to the point that his complexion grew noticeably paler.","Prince Heng's Mansion.","\"Perhaps... the matter of the Crown Princess should be put on the agenda.\"","Prince Heng looked at his eldest son before him. \"I've inquired. Back then, the Crown Prince was harmed by traitors and had an unborn child with a palace maid. That's why the Crown Prince is unwilling to marry.\"","\"If forced to do something he dislikes, given the Crown Prince's temperament, he's likely to cause a major uproar.\"","\"Father, what if the Crown Prince is willing to marry?\"","Song Liu was somewhat puzzled. If that were truly the case, wouldn't they be helping the Crown Prince?","\"Princess Fuan is exceedingly clever, almost unnaturally so. She and the Crown Prince are not truly father and daughter. She won't stand by and watch the Crown Prince take a Crown Princess.\"","Prince Heng, convinced he had seen through everything, felt his expression improve.","\"No rush. Their good days are about to come to an end.\"","......","The proposal Cheng Guang had previously put forward was ultimately adopted by Emperor Yuanyou. In the Zichen Hall, Cheng Guang held his head high, like a rooster brimming with fighting spirit.","\"His Highness Prince Heng initially rejected this official's proposal. It seems his political acumen isn't very high.\"","Cheng Guang clicked his tongue twice. Wanting to hold power in the court? Dream on.","Prince Heng's face stiffened slightly, then quickly adjusted back to a gentle smile. \"It seems I still have much to learn.\"","\"Yes, enough for you to learn until old age.\"","As soon as Cheng Guang's lips moved, Prince Heng felt an impulse to sew them shut with a needle.","Prince Heng steadied himself and walked towards Song Yu with an extremely considerate demeanor, causing Song Yu's right eyelid to twitch immediately.","A dogskin plaster! (A nuisance that sticks to you.)","\"Now that Elder Brother presides over the Eastern Palace and has the people's hearts, shouldn't he also consider taking a Crown Princess?\"","Silence.","Everyone involuntarily quieted for a moment. The next second, overwhelming joy surged in the hearts of the important ministers.","Finally, someone had brought this up!","Since ancient times, the court and the inner palace have been inseparable. Emperor Yuanyou was advanced in years and his harem was nearly empty, so the only target everyone could set their sights on was the Crown Prince, who was in the prime of his life.","\"No need for you to trouble yourself.\" Song Yu spoke with a smile that didn't reach his eyes.","\"I am many years younger than Elder Brother and already have Liu'er by my side. Elder Brother should also soon father a royal grandson, so that His Majesty the Emperor can personally nurture the third-generation ruler of Great Qi.\"","Prince Heng's words were flawless, painting a perfect picture of a younger brother concerned for his elder brother.","Song Yu gritted his teeth in anger and looked at Cheng Guang.","Go on!","Cheng Guang immediately understood.","\"Your Highness Prince Heng's words are rather inappropriate. This official believes the princess is superior to the heir in countless ways, yet Your Highness's words seem to deliberately overlook the princess.\"","\"Could it be that in Your Highness's heart, because the princess is female, she is less noble than the heir?\"","Emperor Yuanyou's expression changed instantly.","\"I absolutely have no such intention.\"","Prince Heng's face flushed red. \"The Crown Prince has simply reached the age when he should marry.\"","\"Prince Heng is right. Now that His Highness the Crown Prince has returned victorious, it is time to select a noble lady from a prominent family to be Crown Princess and continue the royal line.\"","\"Indeed, the selection of a Crown Princess should be decided soon.\"","\"Once a legitimate grandson is born, Great Qi will truly have a successor.\"","Court officials chimed in one after another to support Prince Heng, mentally running through the eligible young ladies from their own families.","Seeing this, Cheng Guang paused. How had this gone from dealing with Prince Heng alone to dealing with so many people?","What should he do?","Emperor Yuanyou remained silent throughout.","After the debate subsided, Emperor Yuanyou finally looked up at Song Yu. \"Crown Prince, what are your thoughts?\"","\"This son currently has no intention of taking a wife.\"","Hearing the expected reply, Prince Heng couldn't help but reveal a hint of a smile in his eyes.","Would the important ministers let such a coveted position as Crown Princess remain empty?","Sure enough.","As soon as the news of Song Yu refusing to take a Crown Princess spread, it immediately affected the interests of a large group of people.","During the morning court, memorials petitioning for Song Yu to take a Crown Princess piled up almost as high as a small hill.","Zichen Hall.","Emperor Yuanyou let out a heavy sigh. \"How about you marry in a couple of years instead?\"","Song Yu, who had long prepared ten thousand reasons to refuse marriage in his heart, looked up, his mouth slightly agape in surprise. Could his ears be playing tricks on him?","The old man was advising him to marry in a couple of years?","Emperor Yuanyou wore a troubled expression. \"I know this isn't entirely fair to you. Just two years. In two years, Ahuan will be of age and can establish her own residence. After that, you can marry whomever you please.\"","\"However, this time, you should first take two consorts.\"","Emperor Yuanyou added. If this scoundrel didn't let a single person into his rear courtyard this time, the memorials would only pile higher, and the one suffering would be him, this old man in his sixties.","Besides, children born to consorts could never be more noble than Ahuan anyway. Bringing them in wouldn't cause any real harm.","Song Yu was utterly shocked.","Wait...","Was this right?","His father wasn't pressuring him to get a wife anymore?"]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: The Crown Prince's Demands Are... Complicated to Explain.","paragraphs":["The next day.","Faced with the urging of the court officials, Song Yu no longer wore a cold expression as he had in previous days. Instead, he nodded cheerfully, \"Thank you all for your concern regarding this prince's marriage.\"","\"However, this prince currently has no intention of taking a Crown Princess. This prince plans to take two consorts first.\"","As Song Yu spoke halfway through his statement, the officials frowned; after he finished, their expressions brightened.","Consorts are fine too! As long as someone can enter the Eastern Palace's rear courtyard!","Upon hearing this, Prince Heng's expression turned somewhat unnatural. He hadn't expected Song Yu to choose a compromise, relenting to take consorts.","\"May I ask what kind of woman Your Highness prefers? Your servants can seek them out for you,\" one courtier eagerly spoke up. He would scour his family's genealogy register until it fell apart to find a maiden meeting the Crown Prince's standards!","The other court officials also pricked up their ears, afraid to miss a single word.","\"This prince has already relayed the requirements to Cheng Guang.\"","Having said that, Song Yu found a chair to sit in, preparing to watch the show.","Seeing this, Cheng Guang cleared his throat.","\"Although they are consorts, the consorts of the Eastern Palace are equivalent to the principal wives of a prince; they cannot be chosen rashly.\"","Cheng Guang took a subtle jab at Prince Heng, mixing in a personal dig.","The officials nodded. This was true.","If His Highness ascends the throne in the future, a consort would at least hold the rank of an imperial consort. It truly should be considered carefully.","\"The consorts His Highness wishes to wed must match His Highness in talent and learning. Otherwise, it would be quite a letdown if His Highness recited a line of poetry and the consort couldn't understand it.\"","A woman whose talent and learning matched that of the top scholar...","Even Emperor Yuanyou's beard twitched. Cheng Guang really dared to say it.","\"This... Your Highness has already achieved the highest rank in the imperial examinations. Under heaven, a woman whose talent and learning are on par with Your Highness... I'm afraid there is none.\"","\"Who says so? Ah Huan is one,\" Song Yu began to perform, putting on a look of deep distress. \"Ah Huan is only thirteen this year and has already achieved such accomplishments. Could it be that you want this prince to marry someone whose learning is far inferior to Ah Huan's?\"","\"Your servants will certainly search diligently for Your Highness.\"","The officials' faces all grew troubled. His Highness's requirements were a bit high, but not impossible to fulfill.","But the next second, Cheng Guang's annoyingly smug voice rang out again, \"Apart from talent and learning, they must also have some proficiency in martial arts. The kind who faints at any moment, even if they bear a royal grandson, probably wouldn't be very bright.\"","Song Yu nodded emphatically.","That Lady Chang from the Chang family before, fainting at the drop of a hat, was terribly unlucky.","The officials' already burdened spines were weighed down a few degrees more.","\"This... Few women in Great Qi dabble in martial arts.\"","\"Ah Huan does! She can even deploy troops and arrange battle formations,\" Song Yu chimed in at just the right moment, with a proud expression.","But as he looked up, Song Yu met Gu Zheng's horrified gaze.","Both talent and martial arts? Could His Highness have taken a fancy to his family's Mingzhu?","After all, Mingzhu is the top female scholar in learning and knows many martial arts techniques...","Song Yu eerily deciphered Gu Zheng's expression.","Resolutely, he shook his head at Gu Zheng!","He didn't want to marry a little ancestor who would make him spend a fortune on pea flour cakes!","Gu Zheng let out a sigh of relief, his heart still pounding. He had been scared to death too!","By now, the officials' gazes had begun to grow somewhat vacant.","Song Yu was satisfied.","“Since Prince Heng is so concerned about His Highness the Crown Prince's lifelong affairs, Your Majesty, perhaps this matter should be entrusted primarily to Prince Heng?” Cheng Guang suggested with a smile, tossing this hot potato to Prince Heng with a clear conscience.","\"Prince Heng is thoughtful and thorough, most suitable for the task.\"","Whoever's daughter is chosen will inevitably offend the other families.","Prince Heng, understanding the intricacies, clenched his fists tightly beneath his sleeves.","...","\"Does Your Highness truly intend to take two consorts?\" In the Eastern Palace study, Zheng Fang asked hesitantly, feeling something was off about the whole affair.","With the requirements His Highness had thrown out, they were more than sufficient for selecting a Crown Princess.","\"This prince merely has such an intention.\"","Zheng Fang and Shen Qingping exchanged a glance. Sure enough, His Highness was just toying with the officials.","They wondered when His Highness had picked up this mischievous habit.","Shen Qingping, however, offered a few pointed remarks, \"If you push the officials too far, they will organize a selection banquet. When the time comes, with beauties of all shapes and sizes present, Your Highness will have to choose at least one, or else everyone will be left in an awkward position.\"","\"A selection banquet? This prince has already considered that.\"","\"Since Zheng Fang and the others aren't married either, when the time comes, this prince will simply assign them virtuous wives.\"","Zheng Fang's eyes widened.","Why? On what grounds?","\"What? This prince wouldn't harm you. Or would you rather matchmakers continue to wear down your mansion's doorstep?\"","With a few words, Song Yu managed to intimidate Zheng Fang.","It wasn't until Zheng Fang left and only Shen Qingping remained in the room that Song Yu finally picked up the book from the table and began to read.","\"Does Your Highness truly not intend to marry?\"","\"In my past life, this prince remained unmarried until death. It seems there is no marital fate for me.\"","Song Yu seemed to be speaking casually, but Shen Qingping instinctively frowned.","He felt there was something... he wasn't aware of.","\"Of course, this prince has no idea if you were married in your past life. If there is a selection banquet, you should also keep your eyes open and choose carefully.\" The upright book blocked Song Yu's gaze.","After returning to the Eastern Palace, he had that dream again.","The end of the dream was his own death; he hadn't seen the others.","Shen Qingping raised an eyebrow. \"With a reputation like mine, who would dare marry me?\"","\"Pfft, don't be so pessimistic. There's always a suitable woman for you.\" Song Yu simply placed the book over his face. \"This prince is different. This prince was born in this life to protect Ah Huan.\"","Song Yu suddenly felt a bit curious about the cause of Shen Qingping's death in the past life.","\"Shen San, if Ah Huan died, and this prince also died, what would you do?\"","\"Fight with my life.\"","Upon hearing this, Song Yu clicked his tongue. It seemed Shen San's fate in the previous life wasn't good either.","\"If you take a fancy to any maiden at the selection banquet, this prince will personally act as your matchmaker and have His Majesty bestow a marriage upon you.\"","Consider it repayment for the brotherly bond of fighting with your life in the past life.","Shen Qingping was taken aback. Marriage? He really hadn't thought about getting married either.","...","News spread that Song Yu intended to take two consorts, and Song Shihuan felt that everyone's gazes towards her had become somewhat complicated.","One day, while Song Shihuan and Gu Mingzhu were inspecting shops, they encountered Song Hui and Song Xiyan again.","\"Ouch, my father infuriated me yesterday. He has an old injury on his waist. I told him to apply a medicated plaster, but he refused, saying it makes his whole body uncomfortable.\"","Gu Mingzhu deliberately raised her voice. Song Hui could still maintain a smile, but Song Xiyan couldn't hold back.","\"Ah Huan, do you know that Uncle intends to take consorts?\" Song Xiyan wore a smug expression. \"Once the consorts enter the Eastern Palace and bear royal grandsons for Uncle, you'll have a brother who can support you.\"","\"Her Highness the Princess already has His Majesty and His Highness the Crown Prince for support,\" Gu Mingzhu retorted boldly.","\"A royal grandson and a princess... are not the same.\" Song Xiyan spoke like someone with experience. \"I understand the difference better than you.\"","\"Her Highness the Princess is different from you. The royal grandson born of a consort is an illegitimate royal grandson, the same status as you.\" Gu Mingzhu blinked and slowly said:","\"Whereas the Princess is the legitimate eldest daughter of the Eastern Palace.\""]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: Sorry, the Heaven Restrains the Eternal King","paragraphs":["\"Sister Hui, she...\" Song Xiyan was so enraged by Song Shihuan that a coppery, bloody taste began to spread in her mouth. She never knew Gu Mingzhu could be so sharp-tongued before.","Seeing this, Gu Mingzhu made a face. \"Even if a consort is taken, the Princess is still the legitimate eldest daughter. And until a consort bears a child, the Princess remains the Crown Prince's only child.\"","\"Not like you, Princess, who gets to enjoy the fortune of having elder brothers' care.\"","These words almost directly stabbed Song Xiyan in her sore spot.","After all, everyone knew how coldly Song Yanzheng and the other two brothers later treated Song Xiyan.","Song Xiyan ran off in a huff. Song Hui said a few polite words and hurriedly chased after her.","Seeing this, Gu Mingzhu scoffed. \"Looks like a good person, but her heart is actually black.\"","Her elder sister had already told her: anyone who wants His Highness to take a wife now is just trying to climb the social ladder and doesn't have the Princess's best interests at heart!","\"Don't be angry, Mingzhu. Come on, let's get you some treats first, then go look at the shops.\" Song Shihuan pinched Gu Mingzhu's little cheek.","Hooray!","Gu Mingzhu's gloomy expression vanished instantly, and she skipped along happily after Song Shihuan.","In all the world, the Princess and food matter most!","On the other side.","\"Xiyan, don't cry. Your makeup will be ruined.\"","\"Sister Hui, she clearly looks down on both of us. Aren't you angry at all?\" Song Xiyan looked at Song Hui with tearful eyes. Having been confined in the Ping Manor for so long, her disposition had unconsciously become much more timid.","\"The Princess is the Princess. How would I dare to be angry?\"","Song Hui's willow-leaf brows furrowed slightly. \"His Highness entrusted this task to my father. I only hope nothing goes wrong.\"","Seeing this, Song Xiyan hated Song Shihuan even more.","Sister Hui treated her like a real sister, sharing everything with her, while Song Shihuan utterly despised her...","Noticing the hatred in Song Xiyan's eyes, the corner of Song Hui's mouth unconsciously lifted.","What a fool.","......","King Heng was utterly aggrieved, yet he had no choice but to run himself ragged selecting suitable candidates for Song Yu's consort. After several sleepless days and nights, King Heng finally settled on three noble ladies.","Zichen Palace.","\"Your Majesty, His Highness's requirements were truly demanding. Your nephew practically scoured all the suitable families in the capital and consulted many court officials before selecting these three.\"","Not only had things not gone according to his plan, but he had also exhausted himself and offended many people in the process.","The only silver lining was that the fathers and brothers of these three ladies were now exceedingly attentive to him.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at the portraits of the three women on the register, his expression shockingly stern.","After a long while, Emperor Yuanyou finally spoke. \"Have the Crown Prince come and take a look.\"","A quarter of an hour later, Zichen Palace welcomed not only the Crown Prince, but also Shen Qingping, and... Cheng Guang.","The last person King Heng ever wished to see.","\"I heard King Heng has already selected consorts for me?\"","Song Yu spoke cheerfully, reaching out to take the register. But in the next second, his expression changed, and he handed it to Shen Qingping.","After reading it, Shen Qingping also looked astonished and passed it to Cheng Guang.","\"Wh-what's wrong?\" King Heng suddenly had a foreboding feeling.","\"Your Highness, King Heng, even if you don't wish for His Highness the Crown Prince to take a consort, you needn't resort to such a foolish scheme to harm him, right?\"","Cheng Guang, like a master of facial transformations, knelt down. \"Your Majesty, Junior Minister Shen has recently been discreetly investigating the personal conduct of officials. This investigation uncovered several with moral failings. Coincidentally, the families of these three ladies are all... unclean.\"","\"With improper family morals, if they became consorts of the Eastern Palace, they would surely bring chaos.\"","Shen Qingping promptly presented the evidence as well. Their coordinated performance was seamless, catching King Heng completely off guard.","\"King Heng.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's voice carried clear traces of anger.","\"Your Majesty, your nephew truly knew nothing of this.\"","King Heng was both shocked and terrified. \"Your nephew had limited contact with these people and failed to detect their moral shortcomings in such a short time. It was negligence on my part, but I absolutely harbor no intent to harm the Crown Prince.\"","A cold sneer rang out. Cheng Guang stared at King Heng, detesting such hypocrites the most.","\"Nowadays, everyone knows His Highness is selecting a consort. You took on the task but botched it. What were your intentions? Acting like this, how could His Majesty ever dare to entrust important state affairs to you in the future?\"","\"And if something were to happen to the Eastern Palace because of this, the one who stands to gain the most would be you, Your Highness, wouldn't it?\"","Even Shen Qingping couldn't help but glance at Cheng Guang. How could this man's words be so venomous?","King Heng kowtowed, begging for mercy, repeatedly pleading his innocence.","Emperor Yuanyou stared at King Heng for a moment before his voice sounded again. \"In that case, you shall continue to familiarize yourself with the court affairs for now.\"","King Heng's kowtowing halted abruptly.","He had exhausted all his efforts to grasp a bit of real power, finally seeing a glimmer of hope, only to have it brutally crushed. Moreover, he had almost thoroughly offended everyone.","The Crown Prince was satisfied.","Junior Minister Shen was also satisfied.","Minister Cheng was even more satisfied.","The three left Zichen Palace wearing expressions of grief and shock. It wasn't until they returned to the Eastern Palace that they laughed heartily without restraint. Song Yu reclined lazily in his chair, laughing with wild abandon.","Shen Qingping leaned against a pillar, chuckling with his head lowered.","As for Cheng Guang... his fox-like eyes fixed on Shen Qingping. Could it be that this Junior Minister Shen has already secured the position of Chancellor?","The next day.","News spread that King Heng had been reprimanded by Emperor Yuanyou. The families of the three selected consort candidates were also dealt with one after another.","In an instant, King Heng lost all face and credibility.","......","Before the officials could enjoy peace for a few days, they began proposing to hold a consort selection banquet.","As expected, Song Yu naturally agreed immediately.","It was a perfect opportunity handed to him on a silver platter to help Zheng Fang and the others settle their lifelong affairs. He was almost grateful to these court officials.","Song Yu even showed a bit of enthusiasm, which delighted the officials to no end.","Only Zheng Fang and his group wore worried expressions.","\"Brother Zheng, I actually think it's a good thing for you and Brother Ling,\" Feng Kuizhi said, fanning himself. \"Otherwise, with so many demons and monsters eyeing your households, you'd be schemed against sooner or later.\"","\"His Highness has excellent taste. He's sure to pick ideal wives for both of you.\"","Zheng Fang's mouth twitched. Thanks, but no thanks—he had only ever heard of an \"ideal husband.\"","\"Feng Kuizhi, if you think it's such a good thing, you join in too.\"","\"No, no, no.\" Feng Kuizhi shook his head like a rattle-drum. \"I'm almost at the stage of discussing marriage with the Coroner. I can't mess around at this critical juncture.\"","This was a marriage alliance he had worked so hard to obtain.","Upon hearing this, Zheng Fang and Ling Ming rolled their eyes in unison. Men with wives really don't fit in.","In mid-September, the consort selection banquet, held under the guise of a Chrysanthemum Appreciation Banquet, commenced grandly.","Zheng Fang and Ling Ming were dressed up like handsome young gentlemen, following behind Song Yu, though both wore rather unnatural expressions.","\"Keep your eyes wide open. If you see a young lady from any family you like, just speak up and tell me.\"","Song Yu adopted a tone of earnest persuasion. \"If you dawdle, you'll never get a wife.\"","He said this as if he already had a family of his own.","\"It's a rare opportunity. Choose someone you truly fancy.\"","Shen Qingping also chimed in from the side, only to be met with a glare from Song Yu the next second. \"Shen San, you too. Open your eyes and look carefully.\"","Thus, Song Yu cooperated exceptionally well throughout this consort selection banquet, strolling through the imperial gardens for several rounds.","The noble ladies were all bashful and demure, outshining the very flowers meant for admiration.","The day after the banquet, Song Yu had already settled on two candidates.","\"You wish to take these two as your consorts?\" Emperor Yuanyou looked up several times. These two choices had rather divergent styles.","Could it be that this scoundrel's tastes were quite eclectic?","\"It's not for me to marry.\"","Song Yu spoke mysteriously. \"It's for Zheng Fang and Ling Ming to marry.\"","A few moments later, heart-wrenching cries echoed through the Zichen Hall.","\"Your son is already the Crown Prince, and you're still hitting him with your shoe sole?\"","\"I'm hitting precisely you, you wretched scoundrel!\""]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: Xu Family's Great Victory, Could Xu Yayu Become the Crown Princess","paragraphs":["Emperor Yuanyou vented his anger for a full quarter of an hour before finally stopping, panting with fury.","\"So you had this scheme in mind from the very beginning. How do you expect me to face the court officials with any dignity?\" Emperor Yuanyou tightened his grip on the shoe sole in his hand. This debt-collecting ghost should go back to wherever he came from!","\"The highest-ranking father or brother among these two young women holds a fourth-grade official post. Although Zheng Fang and Ling Ming might be considered as marrying above their station for now, given time, their own ranks will surely surpass the fourth grade.\"","Song Yu spoke while twisting his sore arm, his face scrunched up in pain.","\"Furthermore, both men are upright and honorable, genuine gentlemen. Their households also have no parents-in-law to serve, which, for a woman, constitutes a very good marriage.\"","Ling Ming's parents were both deceased, and Zheng Fang's... might as well not exist.","\"Father, why not send someone to inquire? If the young ladies are unwilling, then let it be. But if they are willing, why not facilitate two happy unions?\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt he must be going mad, because he actually found some sense in this scoundrel's words.","\"Get out!\"","\"Right away.\"","Song Yu swiftly made his exit from the Zichen Hall, only then patting his chest with lingering fear.","The old man's temper was really getting worse lately; his backside had suffered for it.","The next day, palace eunuchs were sent to the homes of the two young women to make inquiries, and both families gave their consent.","East Palace, Song Yu's residence.","\"Pick an auspicious date. I'll be sitting at the head table when the time comes.\" Song Yu adopted a lordly manner, while Zheng Fang and Ling Ming both blushed, not daring to contradict him in the slightest.","\"Shen the Third, your standards are too high.\" Song Yu glanced at Shen Qingping. \"Next time there's a chance, we'll hold another one for you, and you can choose carefully then.\"","There would be plenty of future banquets for selecting consorts anyway.","Shen Qingping helplessly used his fan to cover his eyes and brows. Since when had His Highness developed a fondness for playing matchmaker?","Heng Wang's Mansion.","\"I truly underestimated the Crown Prince after all.\" Heng Wang's eyes churned with dark thoughts as he sat entirely in shadow, appearing particularly intimidating.","\"Father, anyone who can reduce his other brothers to such states is no benevolent soul. He actually pushed his own subordinates out to shield himself from the consort selection banquet. How much genuine loyalty can such a person command?\"","Song Liu finished speaking and received a deep, penetrating look from Heng Wang.","\"Liu'er, you are the one who will become the Crown Prince's adopted son. From now on, not a single word detrimental to the Crown Prince shall pass your lips.\"","\"I understand, Father.\" Song Liu also realized the impropriety in his words and lowered his head.","\"Your sister now spends more time with Song Xiyan and is already treated dismissively by the princess. You must work hard to build a good relationship with the East Palace and seek the Crown Prince's guidance frequently.\" Heng Wang tightened his grip on the armrest of his chair. Ultimately, his imperial cousin still refused to select a consort.","No legitimate heir... then the only option left was... adoption.","...","The officials enjoyed a rare period of calm, as none were sure what new pitfall Song Yu might dig for them next.","Just as the follow-up matters of conquering Dayue were being settled, good news arrived from Xu Jinruo's front.","\"Victory report!\"","“Lord Xu has defeated the Japanese pirates, also achieving a great victory!”","The military dispatch was delivered to the capital, thrilling the common people. They had just taken Dayue, and now Japan was defeated as well.","Heaven protects Great Qi!","Emperor Yuanyou was also delighted, his very eyebrows seeming to smile. Reading the dispatch, he found himself viewing the Xu family in a favorable light for once. \"Xu Jinruo does indeed have some strategic sense in that head of his.\"","\"The troops returning from Dayue had barely arrived at the Japanese battlefield for a month before securing this victory.\" As he spoke, Emperor Yuanyou's voice grew low.","Just as Song Yu thought the old man might be dozing off, Emperor Yuanyou finally let out a soft sigh. \"The Xu descendants are all clever; it's a blessed family.\" Fen'er was like that.","Ah Huan was also like that.","\"Father is right. I also believe I inherited a small portion of the Xu family's intelligence.\" Emperor Yuanyou's face darkened. There was no point in saying more.","“But this Xu fellow's methods are truly severe. All the Japanese who refused to submit were killed outright, without even going through a persuasion to surrender process.” Song Yu clicked his tongue. Who would have thought?","\"The Japanese are treacherous and cunning. Xu Jinruo's approach was correct.\"","The very thought of Japan's deceitful ways made Emperor Yuanyou feel a blockage in his heart.","\"When Xu Jinruo returns in triumph, I shall reward him handsomely.\"","Strange.","Why did defeating Japan feel even more satisfying than defeating the Great Yue?","The previously quiet Xu residence suddenly became bustling, with visitors arriving one after another, yet none managed to cross the threshold of the main gate.","Xu Residence.","\"Young Miss, that's the seventh group of visitors today.\"","\"See none of them.\" Xu Yayu continued copying texts by herself, not even looking up. Fragmented sunlight filtered through the window paper, dusting her hair, making her seem as if gilded with a golden light.","\"When my father and brother departed for Japan, no one came to see them off. Now that they are victorious, everyone wants to befriend the Xu family. Relationships between people should not be so mercenary.\" Over these past few months, Xu Yayu had truly lived up to her name, being polished into a piece of jade that was even more composed and gentle.","“Young Miss, since the day of the Crown Prince's top scholar parade, you haven't left the mansion. This servant worries you've been alone for too long.”","\"I am still in mourning. Staying within the mansion is most proper.\" She had thought her father and brother would spend the latter half of their lives battling Japan abroad, but now they had achieved a complete victory. Xu Yayu was already filled with gratitude.","At the thought that the Xu family would no longer be guarded by her alone, her hand holding the brush trembled slightly.","She missed her father and brother.","She missed her grandmother too.","Just as the entire court awaited Xu Jinruo's triumphant return, a discordant voice suddenly arose:","\"Your Majesty, this subject believes the daughter of the Xu family is suitable to be Crown Princess.\" King Heng watched the official who spoke, lowering his head to conceal the smile in his eyes.","The Xu family was at the peak of its influence. If the Crown Prince refused to marry the Xu daughter now, he would make an enemy of the Xu family and lose a major source of support.","Sometimes, King Heng even thought that Great Qi having a Crown Prince unwilling to marry was Heaven clearly presenting him with an opportunity.","This statement was like a stone breaking the surface of seemingly calm water, with court officials emerging one after another to echo the sentiment.","After all, whether in status or talent, the Xu daughter was fully qualified to be Crown Princess.","Song Yu's face darkened once more.","Not because he felt pressured.","But because the candidate for Crown Princess mentioned by the hundred officials was someone with whom he had shared some rather unpleasant past experiences.","\"What is the Crown Prince's view?\"","\"I have no particular view. You may continue your discussion.\" Song Yu adopted a detached demeanor, which made the court officials frown repeatedly.","This news also quickly reached the Xu residence.","\"Young Miss, do you wish to become the Crown Princess?\" Hearing her maid's words, a rare flicker of emotion stirred in Xu Yayu's eyes. Countless noble families would fight tooth and nail for the position of Crown Princess; how could it simply fall into her lap?","Most likely, promoting her was just a pretext; testing the Crown Prince was the real aim.","Considering this, Xu Yayu slowly spoke:","\"I once thought about becoming Madam Guo, but I never thought about becoming the Crown Princess.\""]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: A Noble Daughter Should Strategize for Her Family","paragraphs":["\"What is the difference between being a consort and being the Crown Princess?\"","The maidservant was clearly somewhat confused. Aren't they both just becoming the Crown Prince's wife?","But she saw Xu Yayu shake her head with a smile, then, as if thinking of something, the smile on her face faded slightly.","Now that the calls for her to become Crown Princess were so loud... could she smoothly weather this storm?","Would those court officials be willing to let her off?","On the sixth day after the great victory, Xu Jinruo led the triumphant army back to the capital. Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu, along with all the officials, went to the city gates to welcome them.","At this moment, Xu Jinruo had visibly lost a great deal of weight, his entire bearing having gained a certain steadiness. He dismounted and immediately kowtowed in obeisance to Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu.","You have defeated the Japanese pirates. I must reward you handsomely. I hereby confer upon you the title of Marquis of Anding.","The merit of vanquishing a foe, coupled with the Xu family having produced a former Empress, was enough for Emperor Yuanyou to be generous this once.","\"Thank you, Your Majesty.\"","Xu Jinruo's voice trembled slightly as he gave his thanks. Before his mother passed, her greatest worry had been the decline of the Xu family. Now that he was being enfeoffed as a Marquis, his mother could rest in peace in the netherworld.","\"Come, accompany me into the palace.\"","Emperor Yuanyou led the large crowd into the palace in a bustling procession. Song Yu intentionally slowed his steps to walk beside Gu Zheng. \"For the Da Yue campaign, Father did not confer a marquis title upon you. You...\"","Upon hearing this, Gu Zheng even looked at Song Yu with a guarded expression. \"No, this subject does not need it.\"","If the price of becoming a Marquis was to relinquish command of troops...","Then he would rather remain a simple, unadorned general who held military power.","Seeing that Gu Zheng understood the situation more clearly than anyone, Song Yu nodded with satisfaction. \"General Gu, this prince has high hopes for you.\"","As the Crown Prince's right-hand man, how could he not hold military power?","That evening, at the palace banquet.","From the moment Xu Yayu appeared, she became the focus of the entire gathering.","Upon seeing his daughter, Xu Jinruo forgot about everything else, circling around Xu Yayu for a long while, inquiring about every detail of her food, clothing, shelter, and travel.","It was only belatedly that he noticed the unusual looks everyone was giving his daughter.","\"What has happened?\"","\"They believe your daughter is suited to be the Crown Princess.\"","With this one sentence from Xu Yayu, Xu Jinruo's face flushed with suppressed anger. These shameless people wanted to harm his Xu family!","Back then, when Grandmother tried to arrange a match, one was unwilling to marry and the other unwilling to wed, nearly causing a rift between the Xu family and the Crown Prince.","Now who has dug all this up again?","Just as Xu Jinruo's mind was racing, Cheng Guang approached. \"Does the Marquis intend to select a husband for Miss Xu?\"","Such blunt words caused the surroundings to fall quiet.","Everyone wanted to hear Xu Jinruo's reply.","\"Everything will be according to Yayu's wishes. I have only this one daughter.\"","After speaking, Xu Jinruo frowned slightly. \"And you are?\"","\"The former Prime Minister of Da Yue, Cheng Guang.\"","The corner of Xu Jinruo's mouth twitched. What a fine rebel and traitor.","\"Marquis, you may not know, but currently all the court officials believe Miss Xu could be the Crown Princess, especially those few ministers over there, clamoring louder than dogs. The Crown Prince also wishes to know your thoughts.\"","Xu Jinruo's gaze swept over the men Cheng Guang pointed out, a flash of killing intent in his eyes.","\"If the Marquis says so, then this humble official understands.\"","Unwilling to marry, then.","......","\"Miss Xu, the Crown Prince invites you for a word.\"","After several rounds of wine, Xu Yayu looked at Liu Xi standing before her and tightened her grip on the handkerchief in her hand.","The last time she saw the Crown Prince was during the top scholar's parade, which was also when she learned that the Crown Prince was Guo Feng.","The palace at night held a slight chill. A breeze blew past, carrying away some of the stifling feeling from inside the hall.","\"Your subject's daughter pays her respects to the Crown Prince.\"","\"No need for such formality.\" Song Yu also looked at Xu Yayu. \"Given the current situation at court, if I directly refuse to marry Miss Xu, it would be tantamount to trampling the Xu family's face underfoot.\"","Xu Jinruo is a Marquis with military achievements. I cannot do that.","\"Thank you, Your Highness, for considering the Xu family.\"","Misunderstanding Song Yu's meaning, Xu Yayu gave a graceful bow, her eyes clear. \"Does Your Highness need a Crown Princess?\"","\"A Crown Princess who merely holds the position in name, one who will not disturb Your Highness's normal life, nor mistreat the Princess?\"","Song Yu looked at Xu Yayu with some surprise.","\"If this act can ensure the Xu family's prosperity for a hundred years, Yayu is willing to become such a Crown Princess.\"","A Crown Princess living in widowhood while her husband lives.","As a daughter of a noble family, protecting the family and preventing it from being dishonored when necessary was her duty.","\"Although this situation is difficult to resolve, I do not need you to sacrifice yourself to solve it. You are now the legitimate daughter of a Marquis's household; you can live a better life.\"","Song Yu straightened his expression. In the night, Xu Yayu actually felt she was seeing Guo Feng's face again.","\"I called Miss Xu here today to ask Miss Xu to be the one to refuse me.\"","Song Yu was deeply aware of the harshness of the world towards women. If he were to refuse the Xu family, not only would it slight the Xu family, but it was likely that Xu Yayu's future marriage prospects... would not be smooth.","\"If Miss Xu is willing, you can refuse using the reason of observing mourning for your grandmother.\"","\"When Miss Xu meets someone you truly care for, I will personally request His Majesty to issue an edict bestowing the marriage upon you.\"","After finishing his words, Song Yu made to rise and leave. Watching his retreating figure, Xu Yayu suddenly spoke:","\"Your Highness need not be bound by the past. Cause in a previous life, effect in the next. Grandmother once told me that Your Highness's handling of that fetus back then was the most correct choice.\"","\"Today, Your Highness schemes for my Xu family. The matters of Your Highness teasing and deceiving me several times in the past are now written off.\"","Song Yu's footsteps paused for a moment, then he strode away.","Only after Song Yu's figure had completely disappeared did Xu Yayu lower her head. His Highness said she could live a better life.","\"Miss...\"","\"Let's go, back.\"","......","The next day, news spread from the Xu family that Xu Yayu would observe a three-year mourning period for the late Madame Xu.","The Great Qi Dynasty placed the highest importance on filial piety. Naturally, someone in mourning could not hold a grand wedding.","The entire court of civil and military officials also ceased mentioning the matter of Xu Yayu being suitable as Crown Princess. The clamorous issue of selecting a consort ultimately failed to bring one or two new women into the Eastern Palace's rear courtyard.","Prince Heng's Mansion.","\"Father, Marquis Anding has gone to the Eastern Palace again.\"","Song Yu had given the Xu family ample face, so Xu Jinruo naturally was willing to stick to the Eastern Palace like a plaster.","Prince Heng only felt a sharp pain at his temples and pressed the spot with his fingers.","Ever since the Crown Prince returned to the capital, none of his schemes had succeeded, giving him a deep sense of powerlessness.","But he had a pair of dragon and phoenix twins hailed as an auspicious sign, and the Eastern Palace had no legitimate heir. These two facts seemed to push him forward.","\"Hui'er, it is time to move the piece that is Song Xiyan.\"","Prince Heng sighed. Consider it a final gamble. If it failed, he would accept his fate.","Upon hearing this, Song Hui slowly rose. \"Your daughter understands. Song Xiyan is now quite dependent on me and also believes our Prince Heng's Mansion is constantly being bullied by the Eastern Palace.\"","\"With just a little guidance from me, Song Xiyan will certainly speak up for us.\"","After all, that person's mind is not very sharp.","She was born to be used as a tool."]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Song Xiyan Used as a Pawn, Ahuan Becomes the Target of Public Criticism","paragraphs":["\"Sister Hui, why are you crying?\"","Song Xiyan looked at Song Hui, who was crying her heart out in the room, and quickly took out a handkerchief to wipe her tears.","\"Father has been in a bad mood lately, and I've upset him again.\"","\"Sister Xiyan, my father kindly took charge of the Crown Prince's consort selection for the Eastern Palace, but in the end, not only did the Eastern Palace not appreciate it, he also offended other court officials. My father... he's already walking on thin ice at court.\"","Song Hui cried as she looked at Song Xiyan. \"Could there be a day when the Heng Prince's household also becomes like the former Ping Prince's household, and I become like you once were, Sister Xiyan?\"","\"That won't happen!\"","Song Xiyan's eyes narrowed, and she spoke without thinking.","\"Why wouldn't it? The Crown Prince only has eyes for Princess Fu'an. If I ever anger the Princess, I'm afraid I'll be disposed of by the Crown Prince immediately...\"","Song Hui guided Song Xiyan sentence by sentence, stirring up the hatred for Song Shihuan buried deep in Song Xiyan's heart.","\"Sister Hui, don't worry. Others may not know what Song Shihuan's true character is, but I understand perfectly. I will definitely expose Song Shihuan's real face.\"","Hearing Song Xiyan's words, Song Hui almost laughed out loud, but her expression grew even more pitiful. \"But if it would affect you, Sister Xiyan, I couldn't bear to let you take the risk.\"","\"Sister Hui, you needn't worry.\"","Song Xiyan left resolutely, as if she had made up her mind.","That very day, the Eastern Palace received news passed on by Liu'er.","\"Song Xiyan plans to expose Ah Huan's true colors at the palace banquet three days from now?\"","Song Yu pinched Song Shihuan's cheek. \"My Ah Huan's little face is perfectly genuine. Does it need her to expose it?\"","\"Song Xiyan has been let loose for so long, it's rare for her to make a move. I'm delighted, if anything.\" Song Shihuan broke free from Song Yu's \"clutches.\" \"Liuxi, remember to bring Consort Chang into the palace on the day of the banquet.\"","It's about time the truth of what happened back then is made clear before all the civil and military officials.","Seeing that their masters weren't the least bit worried, Liuxi lit three metaphorical candles in his heart for Song Xiyan. Rest in peace.","...","Three days later, at the palace banquet.","Song Xiyan attended in full regalia. Although the fabric of her dress was somewhat outdated, she held her head high as she entered the hall, as if she had already won.","Lady Chang beside her glanced at Song Xiyan, feeling she was acting rather strangely today.","Today's banquet was to reward the soldiers who fought in the war against the Wa Kingdom. Wu Qi recited the long list of rewards, feeling out of breath several times.","The Da Qi soldiers were brave and skilled in battle, they just tended to wear out his voice.","The military officers all wore smiles. Da Qi hadn't fought a war in decades, and those civil officials had almost come to think they were useless good-for-nothings. Now, in one campaign, they had conquered two countries!","So satisfying!","After three rounds of drinks, the atmosphere in the hall was exceptionally lively. The military officers rose one after another to toast all around, these drunkards almost dancing before the civil officials.","It was at this moment that Song Xiyan made her move.","Standing before Song Shihuan, she accused:","\"Song Shihuan, do you know your crime?\"","At that moment, Song Shihuan was eating crab meat that a palace maid had shelled for her. The plump crab meat and roe made Song Shihuan's eyes light up, so much so that upon hearing Song Xiyan's words, she instinctively chewed and swallowed the food in her mouth first.","Then she looked up, her face full of question marks.","\"Did I steal your crab to eat?\"","That one sentence caused the momentum Song Xiyan had painstakingly built up to instantly collapse.","\"It's because you won't let the Crown Prince take a wife that the Eastern Palace's rear courtyard remains empty to this day. You just want to prevent the Crown Prince from having a legitimate heir, so you can maintain your status as the Crown Prince's only daughter.\"","The entire hall fell so silent you could hear a pin drop.","Emperor Yuanyou, seated in the place of honor, had a face as dark as the bottom of a pot.","\"Evidence?\"","Song Shihuan spoke unhurriedly, completely unaffected by Song Xiyan's words, though she thought to herself, so there really is something about a 'lucky star'!","\"The fact that the Eastern Palace's rear courtyard is still empty is the evidence!\"","Song Xiyan turned to face the hundred officials. \"Your Excellencies may not know this. Before my mother gave birth, a master made a prophecy, saying that of the twins in her womb, only one would be a lucky star, while the other would inevitably be a calamity star.\"","\"Song Shihuan was lost at birth. What is that if not a calamity star?\"","\"Ever since Song Shihuan was recognized and brought back, our family has suffered one misfortune after another. Now Song Shihuan is trying to drain the Crown Prince's fortune. It is utterly detestable.\"","\"If we let her continue like this, disaster will befall Da Qi!\"","Song Xiyan's long, impassioned speech was met with utter silence.","Song Shihuan even found it amusing. \"I feel like the calamity star the master spoke of is you, Song Xiyan.\"","Boom—","A hint of crimson flashed in Song Xiyan's eyes. \"Song Shihuan, don't you dare quibble.\"","The next second, Song Xiyan felt a sharp slap land on her cheek, the force so strong her head snapped to one side.","Looking up, the one who had struck her... was actually her own mother.","\"Mother, why did you hit me? You clearly know about the lucky star matter too?\"","Song Xiyan had thought it through smoothly. Those who suspected she was the calamity star were all dead now, except for Song Yanming who was half-dead. So, as long as she preemptively pinned the label of calamity star on Song Shihuan, Song Shihuan would be finished.","But she never expected Lady Chang would strike to push her towards death.","Another slap.","Lady Chang trembled with anger. \"How dare you say Ah Huan is the calamity star?\"","\"When Ah Huan was first recognized and brought back, you and Song Yanzheng conspired to drug her, trying to kill her. Is that the act of a lucky star?\"","\"Later, when Ah Huan entered the girls' school, you tried every method to trip her up. Is that the act of a lucky star?\"","\"And later...\"","\"Enough!\" Song Xiyan covered her ears. \"You are my mother. Why do you always take her side in everything?\"","\"I am only stating facts. The fact is, Song Xiyan, you are the calamity star.\"","Lady Chang laughed, a bit wildly. \"Why do you think your brothers later kept their distance from you? It's because they all found out you weren't the lucky star.\"","Lady Chang looked at Song Shihuan. \"Back then, the master who read the fate said the lucky star was Ah Huan.\"","Hearing this, a light unconsciously brightened in Song Yu's eyes. Sure enough, his judgment was excellent. He had spotted Song Ling's lucky star at first glance and taken her away.","Seeing this, Song Hui clenched her fists tightly under her sleeves. Useless thing.","Can't even handle such a simple matter.","\"Attendants.\" Emperor Yuanyou, who had been dark-faced all along, slowly spoke. \"Slap her face.\"","Hearing this, the court officials were shocked.","No matter what, she was a royal junzhu (princess/duchess). To have her face slapped in front of all of them...","Wu Qi stepped forward and began slapping, one after another. Soon, Song Xiyan's face swelled up like a pig's head.","But as long as Emperor Yuanyou didn't call for it to stop, Wu Qi didn't dare to cease.","Finally, just as Song Xiyan was about to faint, Emperor Yuanyou's voice rang out again:","\"For speaking insolently, she is to receive fifty face slaps daily outside the Ping Prince's former residence, for thirty days. Afterwards, she is to be demoted to commoner status.\"","\"The royal family cannot tolerate someone so vicious, cruel, and stupid as a pig!\"","What dreadful luck. His old face has been utterly shamed!"]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: The Ending of Song Xiyan: You Owe Me a Life","paragraphs":["October.","Outside the Prince Ping's mansion, a crowd of commoners had gathered, an unprecedented sight. The guards surrounding the area showed no intention of driving them away, as if deliberately wanting more people to witness the scene.","All eyes were fixed on Song Xiyan, kneeling at the mansion's entrance.","Song Xiyan knelt on the ground, her eyes vacant, her face still swollen.","\"His Majesty has shown grace. Shouldn't the County Princess express her gratitude?\"","Wu Qi's voice rang out. Song Xiyan tried to curl her lips into a semblance of a smile, but the movement sent sharp pain shooting across her face.","\"I thank my Imperial Grandfather for his... kindness.\"","This was the final punishment. After today, she would no longer even have the right to call him 'Imperial Grandfather'.","Wu Qi's sharp palm strike swept towards Song Xiyan, showing not a hint of mercy.","Song Xiyan's screams grew increasingly hoarse. As her body slumped over several times, Wu Qi ordered two young eunuchs to hold Song Xiyan firmly on either side, forcing her to endure all fifty slaps.","The surrounding commoners were so terrified they dared not even breathe loudly.","After the punishment was over, Song Xiyan was tossed back into the Prince Ping's mansion like a ragged cloth doll. Liu'er let Song Xiyan burn with high fever, not once moving to call the mansion's physician for her.","In her feverish delirium, Song Xiyan saw Song Shihuan's face.","Song Xiyan immediately began to struggle. \"Just because I said a few words, I have to suffer such torment? Song Shihuan, don't you feel even the slightest bit of unease in your heart?\"","Outside the room, Lady Chang's hand, poised to push the door open, froze.","\"Not only do I feel no unease, I am exceedingly pleased.\"","Song Shihuan reached out and pressed down on Song Xiyan's cheek, eliciting another scream.","\"Song Hui used you. You should have figured that out by now.\" Song Shihuan's lips curled into a slight smile. \"How does it feel to be betrayed by so-called family?\"","\"Song Hui, I curse her to die a horrible death!\"","Mentioning Song Hui made Song Xiyan's emotions flare even more intensely. Thirty full days, fifteen hundred slaps—it was more than enough time to piece together the whole story.","\"But Song Shihuan, you deliberately pleaded for my release from the Eastern Palace, didn't you? Just so I would make a mistake. May you all die horrible deaths too.\"","Song Xiyan's words did not anger Song Shihuan in the slightest. Instead, Song Shihuan nodded. \"Not completely stupid after all.\"","\"Then, do you know why I came here today?\"","Without waiting for an answer, Song Shihuan continued on her own:","\"I came to take your life.\"","\"Song Xiyan, you owe me a life.\"","......","Outside the room, Lady Chang instantly covered her mouth, forcing herself not to make a sound.","Inside, clear fear surfaced in Song Xiyan's eyes. She could tell... Song Shihuan's words were not false.","\"You are standing alive before me now. How could I possibly owe you a life?\" Song Xiyan tried hard to swallow. \"I can testify that Song Hui incited me... if you are willing to spare my life.\"","\"You are no longer useful.\"","Song Shihuan let out a long sigh. \"Song Xiyan, have you ever had dreams?\"","\"Dreams where I was a worthless county princess living worse than a servant, whom you could hit and scold as you pleased, just like... your venting doll.\"","Mentioning the events of her past life, Song Shihuan actually felt a sense of relief.","If she killed Song Xiyan today, her vengeance from that past life would be complete.","\"I struggled to survive under your hands, willing to risk my life just to earn your favor. But what happened later? Song Xiyan, you killed me.\"","\"You pushed me, with my limbs broken, into the lake of the Imperial Garden. The water was so cold, it chilled me to the bone. I swore in my heart that I would make you all pay.\"","Song Xiyan shook her head incessantly.","\"Song Shihuan, I've never even heard of these things you speak of. Why are you slandering me?\"","Hearing this, Song Shihuan stared fixedly at Song Xiyan for a long moment, then suddenly laughed. \"Then consider it as me killing you for a crime that never happened.\"","Song Shihuan slowly drew out a short blade, its edge glinting coldly.","\"Five stabs in total. Four for the hands and feet, one for the heart. By then, Imperial Grandfather will only know you committed suicide, unable to bear your current situation. No need to trouble his elderly heart with anything else.\"","Song Shihuan tightened her grip on the short blade and raised her right hand.","Before she left the palace, her father had called out to stop her several times, seemingly not wanting her to come to the Prince Ping's mansion. But she had come anyway.","If it was Song Xiyan's blood, she was willing to stain her hands with it.","Just as the blade was about to touch Song Xiyan, the door was suddenly pushed open. Lady Chang rushed in and wrapped her arms around Song Shihuan from behind, so tightly that Song Shihuan could feel the trembling of Lady Chang's body.","\"A-Huan, be good. Put the knife down.\"","......","\"Let go.\" Song Shihuan's face turned completely cold.","On the bed, Song Xiyan's tears streamed down her face. \"Mother Consort, save me, quickly!\"","But Lady Chang, looking at the veins standing out on the back of Song Shihuan's hand, gently coaxed her again. \"Don't dirty your hands.\"","\"Those things you spoke of... I know about them.\"","Song Shihuan was stunned.","\"She was born from me. For committing such evil deeds, it should be me who ends her.\" Lady Chang took the short blade from Song Shihuan's hand and threw it to the ground. \"You are a Princess. You already stand high, watched by many. Don't give anyone a reason to harm you.\"","\"I will help you kill her.\"","Looking at Lady Chang before her, Song Shihuan felt a rare sense of absurdity.","Did Lady Chang... have memories of the past life?","Lady Chang wiped the tears from the corner of her eye and called out loudly to Liu'er in the courtyard. \"Liu'er, escort the Princess away from the Prince Ping's mansion.\"","\"Princess, please.\"","Song Shihuan pressed her lips together and followed Liu'er out. When she reached the courtyard gate, she suddenly stopped and looked back.","In her line of sight, Lady Chang's hair was completely white, aged like a woman in her fifties. Seeing Song Shihuan look back, she raised a smile on her face and waved at Song Shihuan.","The lingering warmth from Lady Chang's embrace still seemed to cling to her body. This was, astonishingly, the first time in both her lifetimes combined that she had felt the warmth of Lady Chang's embrace.","How laughable.","Song Shihuan left. Lady Chang stared in the direction she had gone for a long time before slowly bending down to pick up the short blade from the ground.","\"Mother Consort...\"","Song Xiyan called out to Lady Chang with panic in her voice.","\"Xiyan, we all have to die. Not just you.\"","A flash of madness passed through Lady Chang's eyes. \"These are the debts we owe A-Huan from our past life. That's why the people of Prince Ping's mansion are dying one after another. Today, I will send you on your way. Remember on the road to the Yellow Springs, do not drink the Meng Po soup. For life after life, do not forget our sins.\"","\"After you die, Mother Consort will follow you. Don't be afraid.\"","Lady Chang used her other hand to gently stroke Song Xiyan's forehead, her tone almost coaxing. \"But before that, tell Mother Consort, how did Song Hui use you?\"","Song Xiyan was utterly terrified by now.","She answered whatever Lady Chang asked, terrified that the next second the short blade in Lady Chang's hand would pierce her flesh.","After hearing the full account of how Song Xiyan had been used by Song Hui, Lady Chang finally smiled.","Let this be the final gift from her, as a mother, to A-Huan."]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: In the Next Life, I Still Want to Be Your Mother","paragraphs":["Elsewhere.","The carriage carrying Song Shihuan was nearing the palace gates when her voice suddenly rang out:","\"Turn around. Go to the Pingwang Residence.\"","A sudden, intense premonition struck her: if Lady Chang had truly killed Song Xiyan, then Lady Chang herself would not choose to live on either.","The palace servant driving the carriage immediately turned the vehicle around, speeding towards the Pingwang Residence. Meanwhile, Song Yu, upon receiving news that Song Shihuan was heading there again, grew concerned and rode out from the palace on horseback.","Standing once more before the gates of the Pingwang Residence, the previous bustle had vanished, replaced by a desolate and lonely courtyard.","Song Shihuan strode towards Song Xiyan's courtyard. The closer she got, the stronger the smell of blood became.","When Song Shihuan pushed open the door to the room, Song Xiyan had already ceased breathing. Lady Chang had covered her eyes with white cloth and arranged her body in a dignified, proper posture.","Only the blood seeping from the five wounds on her body remained starkly, glaringly visible.","At that very moment, Lady Chang was raising a short blade towards her own abdomen. Hearing the door open, she looked up at Song Shihuan with an expression of disbelief, and a smile instantly spread across her face.","In the next second, the short blade plunged into her abdomen, producing the sound of metal piercing flesh.","Baoxia, who was behind Song Shihuan, quickly instructed Liu'er to send word to the palace. Song Shihuan herself stood frozen, staring blankly at Lady Chang, whose abdomen had already begun to bleed.","The person before her, whose life was fading, was her birth mother, and also the person she had hated for two lifetimes.","In Song Shihuan's plans, people like Song Yanzheng and Song Xiyan were to pay with their lives, even including Song Ling. As for Lady Chang, Song Shihuan's plan was for her to live out her days in lonely, bitter regret.","\"Ahuan...\"","Lady Chang's voice was extremely weak. Lacking the strength to support herself, she slumped against the bedside, only managing to stay upright by leaning on the bed.","\"In our past life... it was I who wronged you. I shouldn't have... shouldn't have looked down on you from the start, nor should I have... allowed you to be bullied.\"","\"But it's useless to say any of that now.\"","Blood-tinged tears began to seep from the corners of Lady Chang's eyes as she let out a long, sorrowful sigh.","After realizing her mistakes, she had tried countless times to make amends. Yet, every time she saw Ahuang's face, she knew that only the price of her own life could atone for this sin.","So from the very beginning, it was destined that she had no face to live on.","\"Come... come closer to your mother.\"","Lady Chang's speech was becoming fragmented. Continuous blood loss rapidly drained the color from her face, turning it deathly pale. She waved away the arriving physician, her eyes seeing only Song Shihuan now.","Beneath her sleeves, Song Shihuan's hands clenched tightly into fists. She walked towards Lady Chang.","Finally stopping before her, Song Shihuan knelt down.","Lady Chang struggled to raise her hand, as if wanting to touch Song Shihuan's face. \"So beautiful... It's good that you look like Empress Yuan. It's good to look like Empress Yuan.\"","\"The Crown Prince treats you as his own. When you come of age... I fear he may be unwilling for you to live separately in your own residence. If the Crown Prince takes a wife then, Ahuang... you must not panic. Do not resort to foolish schemes. The Crown Prince is a man of noble character; he will not treat you poorly.\"","At this moment, Lady Chang was like any ordinary mother, desperately planning for her child's future in the final moments of her life.","\"The Great Qi's national power is unprecedentedly prosperous. There is no need for you to marry for political alliance. In the future, you are free to find a suitable husband... find someone... like the Crown Prince...\" Lady Chang's eyes were beginning to lose focus. Her hand ultimately lacked the strength to lift any higher.","In the end, she never managed to touch Song Shihuan's face.","\"And also... your coming-of-age ceremony gift... it's prepared. In the wooden box on the highest shelf... Inside is also... the recipe for almond tea. From now on, Ahuang will have to brew it for her own children.\"","\"In the next life... I still want to be your mother.\"","This was her only selfish wish.","In this life, she was willing to atone with her life. Could she be Ahuang's mother again in the next life?","The sound of hurried footsteps arose, and Song Yu's figure appeared before Lady Chang's eyes. Seeing him, she smiled even more contentedly.","With His Highness protecting Ahuang so, she could die in peace.","If the Chang family hadn't been ensnared by the deposed Empress's schemes, if she had married Song Yu as her father had arranged in the bloom of her youth, would everything have been different?","What a true pity...","With her last ounce of strength, Lady Chang whispered softly:","\"Ahuang... could you... call me 'Mother' once?\"","Song Shihuan lowered her eyes, but her lips remained firmly shut.","Lady Chang seemed to let out a faint sigh of regret. Then, her eyes slowly closed, and her body slumped forward uncontrollably, leaning against Song Shihuan.","Feeling the sudden weight, Song Shihuan's kneeling legs slowly gave way, and she knelt fully, feeling the warmth gradually fade from Lady Chang's body.","After a long while, Song Yu finally stepped forward. \"Ahuang, let's lay the consort on the bed.\"","Song Shihuan nodded somewhat numbly, watching as Song Yu and Liuxi together lifted Lady Chang's body onto another bed.","A wail of grief erupted.","Chang Ling'er stumbled and rushed towards Lady Chang's body, weeping as if her heart would break.","\"Ahuang, this was her own choice.\"","Song Yu took Song Shihuan's hand. The warmth from his touch slowly eased the stiffness from her body.","\"Father, I know.\"","\"Let's return to the Eastern Palace.\"","...","Before leaving, Song Yu noticed a piece of paper on the desk in the room, a corner fluttering in the breeze. Walking over to look, even Song Yu was momentarily dazed.","\"She has written down the entire process of how Song Hui used Song Xiyan.\"","Song Shihuan also looked at the paper. The handwriting was not the delicate, floral style common among young women of good families, but rather carried a sharp, forceful quality.","Song Shihuan suddenly remembered Lady Chang saying she also loved reading history books.","Perhaps those who love history mostly share a stubborn nature, insisting on settling accounts clearly, even if the cost is their own life.","\"Take it. It will be useful against Prince Heng and his faction.\"","Hearing Song Yu's words, Song Shihuan nodded and stored the paper away.","\"I want to go to her courtyard.\"","Arriving at Li Garden, Song Shihuan went straight to the wooden box on the highest shelf. Opening it, she found a hairpin lying quietly inside, along with a sheet of paper that had already yellowed with age.","Small characters were inscribed at the base of the hairpin. Song Shihuan looked closely.","'For my daughter, Ahuang.'","Song Yu reached out and ruffled Song Shihuan's hair. Seeing the little one's obvious, yet stubbornly suppressed, sorrow, he simply reached out with a large hand, closed the box, and handed it to Liuxi.","\"Come, accompany your father to the palace to see your Imperial Grandfather.\"","Seeing Song Shihuan look at him with some confusion, Song Yu curved the corner of his mouth into a slight smile:","\"For our Ahuang's sake, I will personally request an imperial favor for Lady Chang—to have her buried with the rites of a principal consort.\"","A daughter of the Chang family, raised in utmost privilege and honor, should depart this world with dignity and grandeur.","And she had also rid Ahuang of Song Xiyan.","This was Song Yu's gesture of gratitude."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: Prince Heng's Mansion I Don't Want to Play with Them Anymore.","paragraphs":["Lady Chang was ultimately granted permission to be buried with the honors due to a Princess of Ping.","Furthermore, the incident of Lady Chang killing her daughter was given an extremely plausible justification: Song Xiyan, unable to bear being demoted to commoner status, had sought an opportunity to kill Song Shihuan, and Lady Chang had acted only to prevent Song Xiyan from committing this crime.","Thus, in the mouths of the common people, all of Lady Chang's crimes were whitewashed.","Zichen Palace.","\"Wu Qi, has A-Huan's appetite been unusual these past couple of days?\"","Upon hearing this, Wu Qi immediately bowed. Just look at the imperial favor the Princess enjoys! Even matters of food and drink were something the Emperor found time to inquire about.","\"Your Majesty, the Princess's appetite is as usual. It's just that she has remained in the Eastern Palace these past few days and hasn't come out.\"","Emperor Yuanyou sighed softly upon hearing this. He hoped Lady Chang's death would not affect A-Huan.","During these days when the Pingwang Residence had set up the mourning hall, A-Huan had not gone either.","Today was the final day the coffin would remain...","Outside the palace, the common people were also paying attention to Song Shihuan's movements, speculating whether she would come on this last day to see Lady Chang off on her final journey.","Eastern Palace.","\"A-Huan, I plan to go to the Pingwang Residence. Are you coming?\"","Song Yu spoke as if casually, wanting to gauge Song Shihuan's current mood.","\"I'll go.\"","By the window, the young girl propped her head in her hands. Her usually lively eyes seemed somewhat pensive, as if she was brewing something.","\"Father, I don't want to play along with King Heng's family anymore.\"","Song Yu was momentarily taken aback.","Then, Song Shihuan's voice sounded again, \"The people of the Pingwang Residence have received their due retribution. From now on, I only want to live happily with you, Father. I don't want to play this cat-and-mouse game with King Heng's family anymore.\"","With her vengeance from her past life now fulfilled, she had no patience left to wait for King Heng to make a mistake.","So, she would force King Heng to err.","\"We'll do as A-Huan says.\"","Song Yu was also thoroughly disgusted by King Heng's family, especially after realizing that even a young girl like Song Hui could use Song Xiyan without batting an eye.","Song Yu put on a profound air and sighed, \"It seems the Song family's fortune has all landed on us.\"","Hadn't he noticed how the others were as foolish as pigs, lacking even half the bearing befitting imperial descendants?","\"It's just that this family is too good at putting on appearances, and with the auspicious omen associated with them, Lady Chang's testimony lacks concrete evidence. I'm afraid they'll argue their way out of it.\"","\"Isn't it enough as long as Grandfather believes it?\"","Song Shihuan lowered her eyes. \"Let Grandfather see the true nature of King Heng's family, force them to make a move, just like we forced Song Xiyan.\"","Just as Song Yu was about to say something more, Song Shihuan stood up. She was wearing a plain, pale yellow dress, with only a single jade hairpin in her hair. \"Father, let's go.\"","If they didn't leave now... they would miss King Heng's family.","Seeing that Song Shihuan was not overly affected by Lady Chang's death, Song Yu felt relieved.","Then another thought occurred to him, filling his heart with sweetness.","Did this mean that A-Huan regarded only him as family?","That Lady Chang was nothing more than an ordinary person to A-Huan?","As they were leaving, Song Yu, rather excitedly, ordered a palace attendant to present the paper written by Lady Chang to Emperor Yuanyou.","Completely disregarding the likely outburst of rage Emperor Yuanyou would have in the Zichen Palace.","...","Pingwang Residence.","Song Yu and Song Shihuan happened to run into King Heng's family as they were leaving.","\"Princess Ping's righteous act of severing ties for justice is truly admirable,\" King Heng said hypocritically. Song Yu merely smiled and did not respond.","\"Did you know about Song Hui using Song Xiyan to target me?\"","Song Shihuan's direct words froze the expression on King Heng's face, making him look utterly ridiculous.","\"What Your Highness is saying... I don't understand.\"","\"Your daughter, Song Hui, instigated Song Xiyan to publicly insult me at the palace banquet. Before her death, Lady Chang wrote down Song Xiyan's testimony. It has already been delivered to Grandfather.\" Song Shihuan's face was cold. \"You should think about how to explain yourselves to Grandfather, not tell me you don't understand.\"","Seeing Song Shihuan, who seemed like a completely different person, Song Hui, standing behind King Heng, took a fearful step back.","Seeing this, Song Shihuan brushed past King Heng and walked towards the mourning hall.","Feeling panicked?","Panic leads to mistakes, to acting on one's most genuine impulses.","Thoughts raced through Song Shihuan's mind, but upon entering the mourning hall, she set aside all distractions and solemnly offered three sticks of incense to Lady Chang.","The grudges of her past life were now settled.","Meanwhile, before King Heng's party could even return to their residence, they were summoned to the palace.","All their pre-prepared excuses and arguments were useless in the Zichen Palace.","\"Scoundrel! Is this the fine daughter you've raised?\"","Emperor Yuanyou had no desire to listen to King Heng's defense. Furious, he threw the paper in Song Hui's face. \"Such malicious intent at such a young age! You have disgraced the imperial family's name.\"","Song Hui had never experienced such a scene before and was scared into tears.","\"It... it was Hui'er who harbored impure thoughts. Imperial Uncle, your nephew will return and discipline Hui'er properly.\"","King Heng made his choice almost instantly, pushing Song Hui forward to take the blame.","Seeing this, Song Hui cried until she was gasping for breath.","Emperor Yuanyou snorted coldly at the sight. \"Song Heng, I know you suffered hardships outside, which is why I enfeoffed you as a prince upon your return. But do not take me for a fool.\"","\"Song Hui shall copy the 'Admonitions for Women' ten times daily and is confined to the Hengwang Residence.\"","\"I do not wish to see such a thing happen again.\"","A touch of sorrow inevitably welled up in Emperor Yuanyou's heart. Of all his brothers, only he remained. He had originally wanted to treat his brothers' descendants well, yet it had led to his own granddaughter being wronged.","Thinking of this, Emperor Yuanyou spoke again, \"King Heng, from now on, you shall be an idle prince with no official duties.\"","King Heng trembled, choking back a sob as he accepted the decree.","This was cutting off any possibility of him handling court affairs.","...","The Hengwang Residence became unusually quiet, a quiet that brought a sense of peace to the court as well.","At least Cheng Guang's honking was no longer heard.","Eastern Palace.","\"King Heng is truly someone who can endure humiliation and bear heavy burdens. After being reprimanded by the Emperor, he personally invited tutors to his residence to teach Song Liu and Song Hui. He's putting on a very good show of reforming himself.\"","Shen Qingping spoke slowly, a chill evident behind his words to anyone listening.","\"But our goal isn't to make them afraid. It's to crush them completely.\"","A sharpness appeared between Song Shihuan's brows. \"Master, regarding King Heng's true objective, do you have any conjecture?\"","Shen Qingping paused upon hearing this. \"He likely wants Song Liu to become the Crown Prince's son.\"","That would mean adoption.","Song Yu practically jumped three feet in the air.","\"Become my son? Song Heng really has the audacity of a door-sized face.\"","If he died and it was Song Liu holding the spirit tablet and breaking the funeral bowl, he would be so angry he'd come back to life.","Song Shihuan's face showed no surprise. \"Master's thoughts align with mine. Otherwise, King Heng wouldn't have set his sights on the Crown Princess position.\"","Hearing this, Song Yu looked left at Song Shihuan, then right at Shen Qingping.","Wait...","How come he hadn't noticed King Heng was so petty-minded and sinister?"]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: Prince Heng Enters the Game, No Path Ahead","paragraphs":["\"No wonder they've been pushing me to marry all along.\"","Song Yu suddenly understood.","\"If you, Father, stubbornly refuse to marry, it will inevitably provoke discontent among all the court officials. At that time, as the only royal grandson of suitable age and... sound mind, Song Liu would naturally become the most suitable candidate to be your heir.\"","Sound mind...","Shen Qingping couldn't help but cover her mouth slightly.","This was the conclusion Song Shihuan had reached after observing the Heng Prince's residence for a long time.","Because Song Liu's affection for the Eastern Palace was simply a bit too enthusiastic.","\"My child is not a position just anyone can take.\" Song Yu sneered. \"They'd be more fitting as my grandson.\"","The corners of Shen Qingping and Song Shihuan's mouths twitched simultaneously. If these words reached the Purple Sun Palace, the man before them was sure to get a beating.","\"What if we proceed exactly according to Prince Heng's expectations?\"","Song Shihuan spoke again, a complex glint flashing in her eyes.","They could create the perfect environment for Prince Heng.","\"Liuxi, instruct the palace servants in advance. Let Prince Heng have a good taste of how fickle people can be. Let him know that once you offend His Majesty, even the palace servants will look down on them.\"","This was meant to force Prince Heng to abandon the option of simply being an ordinary prince.","\"Also, Father will have to endure some hardship for a while. Spread the word that my father has no intention of marrying in this lifetime.\"","Song Yu, standing to the side, nodded eagerly, a genuine nod from the heart.","He wasn't the least bit aggrieved!","\"And one more thing...\"","Song Shihuan frowned slightly. \"Teacher, please investigate Song Heng's father again. I have a feeling there must be a reason why his father hasn't come to the capital to claim kinship all this time.\"","To reject such overwhelming wealth and status, there must be a thunderbolt hanging over his head that could lead to utter ruin.","Hearing this, Shen Qingping looked at Song Shihuan, a few more traces of amusement in his eyes. \"Rest assured, Princess.\"","\"As for me...\"","Song Shihuan's little face scrunched up into a knot, pondering how to add more pressure on Prince Heng.","\"Got it!\"","\"Baoxia, start a rumor. Say that it's because of me that Father won't marry. Let everyone come and criticize me.\"","A criticized princess and a heir with the reputation of being an auspicious sign—if Prince Heng doesn't make a move, he'd be letting down this chess game.","Baoxia's small head was filled with big question marks.","Song Shihuan, however, was extremely pleased with her own idea and even clapped her hands lightly. \"This way, not only can we force Prince Heng to reveal himself, but we can also help Father see which court officials have ulterior motives.\"","\"No.\"","Song Yu's answer was resolute. \"Ahuan cannot be criticized.\"","\"Father, it won't just be me who gets criticized. You will be too.\"","Song Shihuan instantly became cheerful. \"When the time comes, His Majesty can pretend to be ill from anger to avoid it. Teacher will be criticized for helping me, and General Gu and the others will all be criticized too.\"","Song Shihuan used the happiest tone to say the most sorrowful things, and like a little adult, she patted Song Yu's shoulder. \"Don't worry, Father, we'll all be criticized.\"","Not a single one will be spared.","Shen Qingping was taken aback for a moment, rarely beginning to doubt whether the educational influence their group had on the princess was perhaps a bit off track.","Otherwise, why would his sweet, soft little princess turn into such a schemer?","After a moment's thought, Shen Qingping decided it was the Crown Prince's fault.","If the upper beam is not straight, the lower ones will go askew.","And the \"not straight upper beam\" at that moment had a face flushed red with suppressed emotion. He said to Song Shihuan, \"Isn't the price we're paying this time a bit too high?\"","\"Not high at all. It's the last fly.\"","Song Shihuan nestled in the lounge chair, feeling a bit cold, and pulled the cloak tighter over herself.","\"Father, I only have you now.\"","Song Yu's heart instantly softened. He wrapped Song Yu's cloak even tighter around her.","\"Everything will be as Ahan wishes.\"","\"The princess of Great Qi possesses the wealth of the four seas; all the people under heaven are her subjects. Ahan is not only mine.\"","\"I will always be by your side.\"","Song Shihuan had fallen asleep, her little face rosy, looking unbearably cute.","Recalling the dream of his past life, Song Yu finally revealed a satisfied smile.","Finished killing them, finished killing them all.","......","In November, the chill arrived, and people donned thick cotton clothes.","Yet, the Heng Prince's residence only received shoddy garments passed off as good, and even the charcoal for burning was of the smoky kind, making people cough incessantly.","\"Father, these people are going too far. They think our Heng Prince's residence has fallen out of imperial favor, so they fob us off with this stuff.\"","Song Liu was furious. Although these things would have been considered excellent for them in the past, times were different now. They were now members of the imperial clan!","Prince Heng's face was also extremely grim. \"I originally thought that even if our schemes failed, we could still live a good life. The palace... has too many people who fawn on those in power and bully the weak. We cannot retreat. Otherwise, we won't even get this meager share.\"","No wonder the previous few princes didn't rest content with their situation either.","\"We'll wait for an opportunity. There will be a chance...\"","A few days later, Song Yu publicly declared at a court assembly his unwillingness to marry, instantly provoking questions from all the officials.","Even rumors spread outside that it was because the princess was unwilling that the Crown Prince refused to marry.","The rumors grew increasingly fierce, yet the Eastern Palace remained silent and did not explain, further confirming the rumors.","Prince Heng laughed heartily in his residence for a full quarter of an hour, then looked at Song Liu with ecstatic joy. \"Liu'er, our opportunity has come.\"","It truly seemed heaven was helping him!","His two children were indeed auspicious signs!","Purple Sun Palace.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Yu kneeling on the ground. Thinking of this scoundrel's speech at the court assembly, Emperor Yuanyou felt his heart and liver aching with anger.","Hearing Wu Qi report how people outside were speaking about Ahan, the Emperor was so enraged he kicked Song Yu.","Song Yu felt he was getting the short end of the stick—not only criticized but also beaten.","\"Father, this is a strategy.\"","\"A strategy?\"","Emperor Yuanyou narrowed his old eyes. This scoundrel's idea of a... strategy?","Only after Song Yu explained at length did Emperor Yuanyou's anger subside. \"This time Ahan is being criticized. I am not pleased.\"","Hearing this, Song Yu pouted. If Ahan were to pitifully say in front of the old man, \"I only have you,\" the old man would probably also willingly do as Ahan said.","\"Therefore, to prevent you from being criticized, your son suggests you fall seriously ill—ill from anger.\"","Emperor Yuanyou wasn't made ill from anger; instead, he laughed in exasperation.","\"Very well.\"","After Song Yu left the Purple Sun Palace, Emperor Yuanyou fell gravely ill and did not rise from his bed. Mei Zhilin took up permanent residence in the Purple Sun Palace, dutifully feeling the pulse of the Emperor, whose complexion was ruddy and healthy.","When news of Emperor Yuanyou's illness spread beyond the palace, public opinion against the Eastern Palace grew even stronger.","Everyone aligned with the Eastern Palace was being criticized equally; none escaped.","Liuxi's most arduous daily task was stopping Song Yu, who wanted to go out and argue with those people.","\"These court officials, are they throwing a fit because they couldn't marry their daughters off to me?\"","Just as Song Yu was so angry smoke seemed about to rise from his head,","Prince Heng made his move.","Prince Heng led Song Liu out of the Heng Prince's residence and, under the gaze of all the civil and military officials, had Song Liu kowtow to Song Yu.","\"Liu'er is willing to be your son, to take care of you and Ahan younger sister.\"","Song Yu felt the world spin and vomited all over Prince Heng.","What a disgusting mess."]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: How Could Someone Look Proud While Being Scolded","paragraphs":["\"Sorry, I had something too salty for lunch.\"","Song Yu's expression was utterly sincere, leaving King Heng and his son unable to voice their bitterness.","\"By the way, what was Song Liu saying earlier? This prince didn't quite catch it.\"","Hearing Song Yu's words, Song Liu's mouth twitched violently. On his honor, he dared not repeat what he had just said a second time.","He was afraid the man before him would vomit again.","King Heng's face was livid as he pulled Song Liu away from the Eastern Palace. The Crown Prince's unwillingness was plain, but what did it matter if only the Crown Prince objected?","As long as the civil and military officials were willing, the Crown Prince would have to accept Liu'er as his son, even if it made him vomit.","Soon, all the officials learned of Song Liu's intention to become the Eastern Palace's adopted heir.","Song Liu spoke earnestly. At a young age, he displayed the makings of a fine jade to be polished—gentle and courteous. For a time, the officials approved of King Heng's plan.","If the Crown Prince was unwilling to marry, then why not just acknowledge a son!","Currently, the only royal of suitable age was King Heng's heir. Coupled with the fact that the heir showed potential for cultivation, the voices in the court petitioning for the Crown Prince to adopt King Heng's heir grew louder and louder.","Zichen Palace.","\"I will have them killed!\"","Emperor Yuanyou's eyes were red with rage. \"How dare they covet my throne.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was willing to treat his brother's descendants well, but that did not mean he was willing to hand over the throne. The mere thought of Song Liu ascending in the future, and even Ah Huan having to bow and scrape before him...","His own line reduced completely to subjects...","Made Emperor Yuanyou want to kill.","In matters of such grave principle, those so-called bonds of brotherhood were tossed to the back of Emperor Yuanyou's mind.","\"Your Majesty, the Princess instructed you not to anger yourself.\"","Wu Qi hung his head. \"Now that King Heng's ambition is exposed, the Princess wishes you to use this opportunity to observe the distribution of power in the court.\"","The factions in the court were in constant flux.","Although the position of heir was settled, the ministers below had their own factions and pursued their own interests.","\"Also, regarding the cause of King Heng's father's death, Young Master Shen says he has found some clues and has left the capital to verify them.\"","Hearing this, Emperor Yuanyou took a long moment to calm down before speaking.","\"Then let them live a few more days.\"","Wu Qi's eyes trembled. These words... meant that even if a great immortal came, King Heng and his lot were doomed to die clean.","Faced with the officials' support, the Eastern Palace had only one retort:","\"Whoever wants to acknowledge this son can go ahead.\"","This statement instantly pushed the already tense atmosphere to a new height. Those courtiers who felt their good intentions were met with disdain immediately turned their criticism back towards the Eastern Palace.","And in the Eastern Palace at this moment...","\"They are truly hilarious. They scold me for being arrogant and looking down on everyone except the Princess.\"","Gu Mingzhu \"gesticulated wildly\" describing how she was being criticized, her face showing not a hint of sadness, only delight at realizing the court officials were binding her and the Eastern Palace together.","\"This isn't scolding me at all; it's clearly helping me declare my devotion to the Princess.\"","As she spoke, Gu Mingzhu threw a rather clumsy, flirtatious glance at Song Shihuan.","Gu Zheng shuddered, covering his eyes with both hands.","Out of sight, out of mind.","\"I got scolded too,\" Cheng Guang said, chest puffed out. \"They say I support the Eastern Palace without any bottom line, right or wrong, just to gain a foothold in Da Qi.\"","Quite right. He accepted it all.","\"And me...\" Zheng Fang also timidly raised his hand. \"My wife was so indignant she had our servants go argue with them, and they actually made a Censor's wife cry with their scolding.\"","What a heroine!","They all looked at each other and burst into laughter.","Only Gu Zheng's expression grew worse and worse.","Why were the criticisms against these others inconsequential, but when it came to him, they dialed up the intensity?","Thinking of this, Gu Zheng's voice dropped unusually low, like the buzzing of a fly. \"I was scolded too. They say I rely on my military power, am unwilling for the Crown Prince to adopt an heir, and fear... fear I have rebellious intentions.\"","\"Old pal, that's indeed not something to be happy about.\"","Cheng Guang patted Gu Zheng's shoulder in a comradely manner, only to have it shrugged off unfeelingly.","\"This shows General Gu genuinely makes them feel threatened,\"","Song Shihuan blinked, \"That's why they want to drive a wedge between the Eastern Palace and General Gu.\"","Exactly!","Seeing that the Crown Prince and Princess showed no sign of doubt, Gu Zheng raised his head high and cast a contemptuous look at Cheng Guang.","\"The Princess is right. Let them scold if they love to.\"","The matron arranged for everyone to dine together in the Eastern Palace, and sounds of laughter and joy continuously drifted out.","\"Yingchun, it's the first time I've seen people look so proud after being scolded.\"","Yingchun smiled upon hearing this. \"Indeed, a rare sight.\"","The Eastern Palace's disregard made King Heng and his son somewhat panicked.","\"Have you found out the situation in the palace?\"","\"Your Highness, His Majesty is likely truly gravely ill. It's said that recently, Eunuch Wu Qi from Zichen Palace has been running to the Eastern Palace frequently.\"","Hearing his subordinate's words, King Heng's eyes turned inscrutable. If His Imperial Uncle was truly failing, they must solidify Liu'er's status before that happened.","Otherwise, once the Crown Prince ascended, everything would be useless.","\"Send word, notify those several ministers. It's time to act.\"","A few days later.","A court official dashed himself against a pillar at the palace gate and died. Before his death, he shouted loudly:","\"The Eastern Palace cannot be without an heir! King Heng's heir can be the Eastern Palace's adopted son!\"","On the same day, another court official slit his own throat with a knife on the busiest street in the capital, uttering the same words before dying.","Instantly, the common people were drawn into this court of public opinion, though the direction was somewhat strange.","\"His Highness the Crown Prince is in the prime of his life. Why must he acknowledge someone else's son when he can have his own?\"","\"I heard it's because His Highness doesn't want to marry.\"","\"Even if he doesn't marry, he can take concubines. Concubines can bear children too.\"","The common people were very puzzled. If the Crown Prince were old and frail, adoption might make sense. But a man in his prime, who would want to adopt another's child?","However, the emotions of the officials had clearly been thoroughly stirred.","They saw far more complexity than the common folk. The Eastern Palace was giving a warning to them all, cutting off their path to becoming the imperial in-laws. Ultimately, it was a lack of trust in any of their aristocratic families.","Throughout history, a delicate balance existed between ruler and ministers. Often, the Son of Heaven had no choice but to endure the constraints of his officials.","But if the Eastern Palace were allowed to continue like this, in the future, all their interests would be judged solely by the word of the Eastern Palace.","This was a situation the aristocratic families of every dynasty were unwilling to be reduced to.","Thus, in the latter half of the eleventh month, some emotionally charged officials surrounded the homes of the Eastern Palace's allies like the Gu and Shen families.","Shen Mingwen was so angry he was huffing and puffing.","\"Have these people gone mad? Drunk King Heng's bewitching soup?\"","Were they taking advantage of his son being away from the capital to bully an old man living alone?","\"Those standing outside are all court officials, right?\"","Seeing the servant nod, Shen Mingwen took a deep breath. \"Go find some rotten vegetable leaves and rotten eggs, and throw them over the wall.\"","Smother those blind fools!","Now I can't even buy the braised duck my wife wanted to eat!"]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: Oops... I think I might have gone a bit too far.","paragraphs":["The ministers waiting outside the Shen Manor were not met by a yielding Shen Mingwen, but by rotten vegetable leaves raining down from above.","And stinking eggs bursting open over their heads.","\"My Grand Preceptor has said: His Highness the Crown Prince was personally instructed by him. He is a man of noble character and upright temperament. His decisions are never made without cause. If you do not return, you are making an enemy of the Shen family!\"","Shen Mingwen's declaration left the ministers outside the Shen Manor momentarily stunned. Feeling the sudden stench, each one left with a face ashen with anger.","Meanwhile, the Ye Manor was not besieged at the same time. Ye Shijie had not been remembered by the court ministers in this turmoil and thus avoided any scolding.","Mainly because Ye Shijie was accustomed to acting alone, so the ministers also believed he wouldn't take a clear stance in support of the Eastern Palace.","But...","\"What? Shen Mingwen said that when his manor was surrounded?\" Ye Shijie put down the book in his hand. The Emperor had been ill for several days with no morning court, so he was at home reading in casual clothes.","Regarding the restless King Heng, Ye Shijie merely scoffed, calling him a clown.","\"Yes, Grand Preceptor Shen's words... If the Crown Prince does not object, wouldn't that solidify Grand Preceptor Shen's position as the Emperor's tutor?\"","The servant naturally knew what Ye Shijie cared about most. Upon hearing this, Ye Shijie's expression changed instantly.","\"Spread the word that I, Ye Shijie, have always supported His Highness the Crown Prince.\"","Ye Shijie immediately sat up straight. \"Let them come and scold me too.\"","Otherwise, his chance at the position of Emperor's tutor would fly away.","The servant swallowed hard with effort, nodding vigorously. \"You are right, my lord. Being scolded at this time is the right thing to do!\"","Hadn't he seen that the Gu Manor even specially bought wine, clearly overjoyed!","And so, the entire situation began to develop in an extremely bizarre direction.","Those criticizing the Eastern Palace grew more and more vehement, while those speaking up for it yielded not an inch. The two factions argued fiercely, locked in a stalemate.","It was at this precise moment that Yu Fan returned.","The court fell briefly silent.","......","King Heng's Manor.","\"Your Highness, this humble official believes that when Minister Yu returns to the capital tomorrow, we should take the initiative to greet him at the city gates.\"","\"Indeed, Minister Yu has made great contributions in the battle to annihilate Da Yue. If we do not go... it could affect our official reputations.\"","Upon hearing this, the smile on King Heng's face became strained. \"Gentlemen, this prince has no intention of stopping you. Not only that, tomorrow this prince will bring Liu'er along to welcome him.\"","\"Your Highness and the heir are truly broad-minded.\"","After flattering King Heng a few more times, the officials left one by one.","Leaving King Heng behind, his eyes filled with malice.","\"Father, isn't it enough for the Eastern Palace to greet him tomorrow... If they go, won't it be with the Eastern Palace leading again?\" Song Liu was somewhat unwilling, feeling this would put them at a disadvantage.","\"What can we do about it?\"","King Heng took several deep breaths. \"Not returning early or late, but precisely at this time!\"","\"After tomorrow, pretend to fall ill because of this matter. Let those court ministers argue even more fiercely on your behalf.\"","\"Understood.\"","At the same time.","\"Minister Yu, your injuries are not fully healed yet. There's no need to be in such a hurry...\"","The army medic's words died in his throat under Yu Fan's fierce gaze.","Stubborn old man.","\"The Crown Prince is in trouble. I must return.\"","Yu Fan's movements were still somewhat inconvenient, and the jolting of the carriage made his wounds ache dully.","\"I carry great military merit. To speak a treasonous truth, even the Emperor would greet me at the palace gates upon my return to the capital. Now that the Emperor is gravely ill, it will be His Highness the Crown Prince who greets me.\"","Yu Fan's lips were parched. \"Naturally, others must go too. The more I honor the Crown Prince, the more directly they will feel the distinction between superior and subordinate. That worthless beast is utterly unworthy of coveting the Eastern Palace's lineage.\"","Hearing Yu Fan speak like this, the army medic also fell silent.","Indeed, the Crown Prince and Princess, with their illustrious military achievements, were revered as deities by the soldiers in the army. Why was it that upon returning to the official court, those officials dared to be so treasonous?","The next day.","Yu Fan arrived at the capital.","Civil and military officials unanimously gathered outside the capital's city gates, clearly forming ranks behind Song Yu and Song Shihuan.","Supported by the army medic, Yu Fan stepped down from the carriage.","He walked directly up to Song Yu and Song Shihuan.","\"Your subject, Yu Fan, pays his respects to Your Highness the Crown Prince, to Your Highness the Princess.\"","Then, there was silence.","With an extremely arrogant attitude, he completely ignored King Heng and the heir, Song Liu, who stood by with forced smiles.","All were shrewd individuals and instantly understood Yu Fan's stance.","\"This prince has been waiting for you for a long time.\"","Song Yu personally helped Yu Fan up. \"Your child, A Tuan, is very adorable, quite beautiful.\"","A glimmer of tears seemed to flash in Yu Fan's eyes.","He knelt down once more.","\"Without Your Highness the Crown Prince and Your Highness the Princess, there would be no Yu Fan today. My very life belongs to the Eastern Palace. If anyone dares to wrong the Eastern Palace by even a fraction, I, Yu Fan, will resist unto death.\"","Silence.","Complete silence filled the scene.","Gu Zheng held military power and dared not speak so recklessly.","But Yu Fan... this newcomer who had just risen to prominence in the court, speaking under the shadow of the Gu family, had uttered such words, leaving others unable to find the slightest fault.","After all, everyone knew the Eastern Palace's grace in recognizing Yu Fan's talent.","That very night, news spread from King Heng's Manor that Song Liu had fallen ill. This time, it was not feigned; he was truly angered into sickness.","\"I only wanted to become Crown Prince Uncle's son, to take care of A Huan for him. Did I do wrong?\"","Song Liu's single sentence once again ignited the fervor in the hearts of the court ministers.","It seemed to return to the state of a few days prior, though hindered by Yu Fan's presence, the ministers were somewhat restrained in their actions, after all, not daring to scold a newly meritorious hero.","At this time, a group of people quietly arrived in the capital.","Their leader was a frail, gray-haired old man.","\"Sect Leader, are you certain the person you're looking for is the Princess of Da Qi?\"","The head disciple, Qingling, spoke cautiously. After all, the Sect Leader had been unconscious for years and, upon waking, immediately wanted to investigate the situation in Da Qi to find a girl now thirteen years old.","The entire sect had searched for a full half-month, and the result actually pointed to the Princess of Da Qi.","\"There is no mistake.\"","The old man glanced at the somewhat crumpled portrait in his hand. \"How could one not recognize one's own child?\"","The other disciples also widened their eyes in shock.","The Sect Leader, at such an age, had suddenly produced a teenage daughter?","This was practically going to be explosive headline news in the Qingyun Realm!","\"The Princess is truly pitiful.\"","In the inn, guests at a nearby table spoke up. \"If the Crown Prince really recognizes King Heng's heir as his adoptive son, the Princess's situation will become extremely difficult.\"","\"Yes, many people are cursing the Princess. If it were before, the Crown Prince would surely be furious and have the Imperial Guards patrol everywhere to prevent the Princess from being insulted. But this time, the Eastern Palace hasn't stepped in to protect her as before. I'm afraid it's...\"","Qingling walked over expressionlessly. \"You two gentlemen, how is the Princess being cursed? I love to join in the excitement and listen to all sorts of gossip.\"","Half an hour later.","The old man was so angry his breathing became rapid. The urge to go to the Eastern Palace to seek his relative was forcefully suppressed.","\"Take A Huan directly back to the Qingyun Realm.\"","The Great Qi Imperial Family doesn't know how to raise a child, but his Qingyun Sect does!"]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: The Prince Lowered His Proud Head","paragraphs":["\"Master, you must not agitate yourself in your condition.\"","Not just Qingling, but all the disciples nearby grew tense. Seeing the old man leaning weakly in his chair, Qingling made a quick decision and had him taken upstairs to a room in the inn.","\"You all go, go and... bring Ah Huan out.\"","The journey had been bumpy, and the old man's body simply couldn't bear it anymore.","He patted the quilt sadly with his hand. This wretched body of his didn't even have the strength left for him to stand before Ah Huan and personally bring her home.","\"Don't worry, Master. We'll go right away.\"","Qingling looked at the youngest junior brother. \"Qingchi, you stay here and look after Master.\"","The youth called Qingchi nodded, but his expression dimmed. It wasn't that he was unwilling to care for the master; he just also wanted to be among the first to see the little girl who was about to become the first in the Qingyun Realm.","A whole bunch of men—he was truly sick of the sight!","\"Behave, or after we find her, we'll talk nonstop about how awful Qingchi is.\"","Qingchi nearly jumped out of his skin. These people always bullied him, the young and handsome one!","...","One hour later, the guards at the palace gate stared wide-eyed at the five exceptionally handsome young men before them, each with his own distinct charm.","Where had these distinguished guests come from? Their bearing and aura were extraordinary at first glance.","The leader appeared mature and steady, yet an aura of sharp, sword-like energy surrounded him, making the guards hesitant to move.","\"Please inform the Eastern Palace that the princess's family has come to take her home.\"","The guards felt their heads buzzing. They immediately turned and sprinted toward the Eastern Palace.","Heavens above! Where had these so-called relatives of the princess sprung from?","Eastern Palace.","\"What?\"","Song Yu shot to his feet. \"This prince is Ah Huan's family. Ah Huan said she has no one else in this world but me.\"","\"Where did these damned relatives come from?\"","Liuxi, standing nearby, felt his eyelid twitch.","\"Your Highness, perhaps we should first send someone to investigate the identities of these men?\"","What if they really were connected to the princess... His Highness's sharp tongue would have already offended them irreparably.","\"This prince will go personally!\"","Song Yu strode away, leaving Liuxi with a resolute and determined back.","Outside the palace gate.","\"Qingling, eldest disciple of the Qingyun Sect.\"","Qingling did not bow to Song Yu. Instead, he stood facing him as an equal.","During the many years the old master was unconscious, Qingling single-handedly managed the entire Qingyun Sect. His reputation as Young Master Qingling was known throughout all the kingdoms.","\"Song Yu, Crown Prince of Great Qi.\"","Song Yu looked at Qingling, his heart sinking slightly. \"Ah Huan is this prince's daughter.\"","\"Does the Crown Prince know from where Ah Huan's name originates?\"","Qingling seemed certain Song Yu wouldn't know and continued, \"'Constant joy, born to be happy.' Our master only wished for Ah Huan a life of happiness and carefree joy.\"","Master...","Connecting this to the 'master' Ah Huan had mentioned in the past, Song Yu felt his breath catch.","What in the world was this? The renowned Qingyun Sect was here to snatch his child away?","The world had gone mad.","\"This prince will not allow anyone to take Ah Huan from my side.\"","Song Yu stared fixedly at Qingling. \"No matter who it is.\"","\"What a coincidence. By our master's command, we are to take Ah Huan back no matter what.\"","The two stood in confrontation, the air between them seeming ready to spark at any moment.","At the same time, in the Eastern Palace.","\"Princess, something terrible has happened!\"","...","\"If you truly cherish Ah Huan, why did you allow her to be criticized by Great Qi's ministers and common people?\"","\"Our Qingyun Sect may be entirely male, but if Ah Huan returns, she could even become the future sect leader. Why can't she hold a position of succession here in your Great Qi?\"","The four men behind Qingling also began chattering, but their core purpose was singular: even if they had to use a sack, they would carry the little girl back.","Song Yu felt even more wronged than if it had snowed in June.","Just as Song Yu was at a loss for how to defend himself, a clear voice rang out:","\"What's happening?\"","\"Ah Huan.\" Song Yu looked at Song Shihuan, his eyes lighting up. The savior had arrived!","The eyes of the five men opposite also lit up simultaneously.","Song Yu was shoved aside.","\"I am your eldest senior brother, Qingling.\"","\"I am your second senior brother, Qingfan.\"","\"And me...\"","\"The sixth is the most mischievous, so we specifically left him with Master to avoid scaring you.\"","The five men tightly encircled Song Shihuan. Song Yu couldn't even see a strand of her hair.","\"Little junior sister, you're amazing! To use the battle formations Master taught you so masterfully, sending Great Yue running with their tails between their legs.\"","\"As soon as Master woke up, he said he wanted to find you. But upon arriving in Great Qi, we heard you were being criticized by so many. Don't be afraid, little junior sister. Your senior brothers will get justice for you.\"","From their eager, overlapping words, Song Shihuan pieced together the complete story.","\"Master... is here too?\"","Song Shihuan's heart ached terribly. So the old man had been in trouble; he hadn't abandoned her.","\"He's here, but he's too weak to get up. Otherwise, he would have come to fetch you himself.\"","\"Little junior sister, come with us.\"","Song Yu immediately grew wary.","Hearing this, Song Shihuan was stunned for a moment. Then, with effort, she made her way to Song Yu. \"Father, I want to go see Master.\"","\"Of course, of course.\" Song Yu forced a smile that was uglier than a grimace.","Watching Ah Huan's figure surrounded and escorted by her five senior brothers, the Crown Prince of Great Qi lowered his proud head.","Would Ah Huan... not come back?","But thinking of the criticism Ah Huan had faced recently, Song Yu felt a wave of helplessness. The Qingyun Sect's anger... was justified.","When it came down to it, Ah Huan had devised such a strategy for his sake.","Dejected, Song Yu made his way to the Zichen Hall.","\"Didn't I say you shouldn't come to the Zichen Hall while I am gravely ill?\"","\"Ah Huan has been taken away.\"","Song Yu spoke listlessly.","\"What? My granddaughter has been kidnapped?\" Emperor Yuanyou's voice boomed, startling even Mei Zhilin, who trembled.","Who could understand a gravely ill man producing such a sound?","\"Not kidnapped, taken away.\"","Song Yu looked at Emperor Yuanyou. \"Her master, the one who taught her all those battle formations, is the leader of the Qingyun Sect.\"","\"Now that the leader has regained consciousness, he's come to the capital with his disciples to find her.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was also dumbfounded.","\"No, we absolutely cannot let them take my granddaughter away.\" Emperor Yuanyou grew anxious. \"I will go see this sect leader myself.\"","Seeing this, Song Yu sighed softly. \"Father, you are currently gravely ill in bed. If you appear before everyone hale and hearty...\"","\"Then what should we do? Just watch as Ah Huan is taken away?\"","\"Let's leave it all to Ah Huan's decision.\"","Song Yu's eyes suddenly reddened. \"Father, her name was given by that man. If not for him in those first ten years, Ah Huan might not have survived to return.\"","\"If Ah Huan wishes to return to the Qingyun Realm, I... I won't stop her.\"","Plop—","A tear slid from the corner of Song Yu's eye."]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: Father and Daughter, Each Other's Light","paragraphs":["Standing outside the door, Song Shihuan felt a mix of apprehension and nostalgia.","During the time after her master went missing, she would often cry secretly at night. As Granny's cough grew heavier, she resented her master for abandoning her and Granny.","But it turned out her master had gone alone to the perilous Tianshan Mountains to find the life-saving snow lotus for Granny.","After being unconscious for nearly a decade, the first words he uttered upon waking were her name.","Thinking of the stories her Imperial Grandfather had told about the Qingyun Realm, Song Shihuan's eyes reddened. No wonder the old man always said she made his heart ache—it was because his heart meridian had been damaged all along.","In an instant, Song Shihuan felt an ache throughout her entire body.","In her past life, when her master woke and learned of her death, was he utterly heartbroken?","\"Little Junior Sister, Master has missed you for a long time.\"","With a creak, the old man inside the room seemed to sense something and instinctively looked towards the door. Upon seeing Song Shihuan, he froze.","\"Master.\"","Song Shihuan strode to the bedside and kowtowed three times.","\"Qingchi, help me up.\"","The old man, sitting on the bed, beckoned to the young girl, his cloudy eyes also welling with tears.","\"Good child, it's enough that you're alive. It's enough that you're alive.\"","The moment he woke, his greatest fear had been hearing news of A'Huan's death.","\"Come here, all of you. This is the granddaughter I adopted during my travels in recent years. She is your junior sister.\"","The old man addressed several young men, \"A'Huan, these are all your senior brothers.\"","The previous generation of the Qingyun Sect had perished or been injured in that great war. When he left the Qingyun Realm, the eldest, Qingling, was only eighteen, yet he had shouldered the entire Qingyun Sect alone.","With the old man's words, the group immediately swarmed around Song Shihuan again, all eager to talk to this excessively adorable junior sister.","The old man watched from the side, smiling.","While also wiping away tears.","From this single meeting, he could tell that Great Qi had not mistreated A'Huan in terms of food, clothing, shelter, or travel.","As for other matters, A'Huan would speak of them when she was ready.","Thinking of the rumors outside, the old man narrowed his eyes, suspecting things were not as simple as they seemed on the surface.","......","Song Shihuan had always considered herself a child with weak bonds of sibling and family affection.","Now, looking at the faces before her, each eagerly awaiting her to call them 'senior brother,' Song Shihuan felt a strange and wonderful sensation in her heart.","\"Enough, all of you, go investigate who has been slandering A'Huan the most fiercely. Make a list for settling accounts.\"","\"Master is right,\" Qingling said, adopting a serious expression. \"Although our Qingyun Sect does not interfere with the affairs of various kingdoms, now that they've slandered our junior sister, we must show them the means of our Qingyun Sect.\"","The group swiftly left the room, their demeanor one of sworn determination to avenge Song Shihuan.","Seeing this, Song Shihuan pursed her lips and sat down by the bed. \"Master, Father treats me very, very well.\"","\"He even specially went to Granny's grave to speak with her, thanking her for raising me.\"","\"This recent incident was my idea. Father was also very saddened that I was being slandered.\"","Song Shihuan grasped the old man's hand. \"Master, please don't be angry with Father.\"","After a long while, the old man sighed and pulled Song Shihuan into his embrace. He was very thin, so thin that Song Shihuan could feel his bones pressing against her.","\"It was my fault, leaving A'Huan alone in Great Qi, letting her suffer so much.\"","\"Master, I suffered a great deal.\"","Song Shihuan looked up at the old man. She was raised by her master; from major skills like martial arts and formations to minor details like character and rules, everything was taught to her bit by bit by her master.","\"Song Ling abandoned me. Song Yanzheng and others repeatedly tried to poison and harm me. At first, I was foolish enough to think everyone in the world was as good as you, so I suffered greatly.\"","Song Shihuan knew that the more she said she hadn't suffered, the sadder her master would feel.","\"Don't be afraid. Master will avenge you.\"","\"They're already dead. They all died by my schemes.\"","\"Not enough,\" the old man gently stroked Song Shihuan's face. \"Silly child, far from enough.\"","\"Tell Master in detail about what happened in Great Qi, alright?\"","Song Shihuan nodded vigorously.","......","The Eastern Palace.","Looking at the completely untouched lunch, Liuxi was so worried he felt he was losing hair.","To make matters worse, Young Master Shen was not in the capital at this time. Having no other recourse, Liuxi summoned Cheng Guang.","This man had a devious mind, so he surely had plenty of cunning ideas.","\"Your Highness, are you troubled by the current situation?\" Cheng Guang asked, looking bewildered. \"We have already assessed the court's situation. Those who need dealing with are being handled according to plan. Everything is proceeding as scheduled.\"","\"A'Huan might be taken away.\"","Upon hearing this, Cheng Guang's eyes widened. What? The most valuable treasure of the Eastern Palace was going to be taken?","After Song Yu finished explaining about the Qingyun Sect, Cheng Guang fell silent.","\"Your Highness, no matter what, the Princess cannot leave Great Qi. If we lose the Princess...\"","Both you and His Majesty would go mad...","\"But I don't want to force A'Huan to do anything she dislikes.\"","Song Yu felt terribly conflicted, torn between his reluctance to part with A'Huan and his unwillingness to cause her distress.","Cheng Guang imagined the days without the Princess and shuddered. Absolutely not.","\"Your Highness, why not sit down and negotiate with the Qingyun Sect? It's all for the Princess's sake. Wouldn't it be better to join forces against Prince Heng? The Princess could then take turns residing in both places.\"","Song Yu sent Cheng Guang away.","He shut himself in his study.","The sky gradually darkened. The sweet voice that usually filled his ears was gone, replaced by endless silence and chill.","Song Yu even began to wonder: if he took up a blade now, killed Prince Heng, and became universally condemned, would A'Huan rush back to advise him?","Just as Song Yu was starting to select a blade,","a knock sounded at the door.","\"Didn't I say I have no appetite for a meal?\"","Song Yu thought it was Liuxi.","But the door opened anyway. Just as Song Yu frowned, about to reprimand the intruder, he saw the face he had missed intensely all day.","\"A'Huan?\"","Song Shihuan bounded in lightly and threw herself towards him. \"Father, I'm back!\"","\"You... you're not leaving with your master?\"","\"Master said he'll stay in the capital for a while first, to avenge me.\"","Song Shihuan smiled, revealing two dimples. \"But Master is very angry. He asks you to relay three demands to Imperial Grandfather. If they are not agreed to, he will take me away immediately.\"","\"What demands?\" Song Yu asked eagerly.","\"First, the bodies of Song Ling and his family are to be handed over to the Qingyun Sect for full disposal.\"","\"Second, Prince Heng's body, once the matter is concluded, will also go to the Qingyun Sect.\"","Master said that even death would not quell the hatred in his heart.","\"Third, the court officials who slandered me this time will be taught a lesson by the Qingyun Sect.\"","\"I will speak to your Imperial Grandfather tomorrow.\" Song Yu was even somewhat stunned upon hearing this.","The three matters were stated, but what about the bad news?","At that moment, Song Shihuan gently tugged at Song Yu's sleeve and looked up at him with eyes like dewy apricots:","\"No matter what, I will never be separated from you, Father.\""]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: Congratulations, you've kicked an iron plate.","paragraphs":["\"I thought... Ah Huan would miss that old man from the Qingyun Sect terribly.\"","Song Yu's words carried a tinge of jealousy. The man who had been despondent all day still looked somewhat unshaven, yet his chest was filled to bursting.","His Ah Huan, the brightest light in his life, had returned.","\"I do miss my Master very much,\"","Song Shihuan tilted her head, \"but I can't do without my Royal Father anymore.\"","Song Yu felt as if he had just tasted the sweetest candy in the world, so cloyingly sweet it made his whole being feel like floating.","\"Royal Father, I will go see Master tomorrow morning.\"","Plop—","Half of his beautiful fantasy shattered, replaced by a palpable sense of crisis.","His Ah Huan's heart was with him, but those disciples from the Qingyun Sect didn't look like honest folk at all. What if they sweet-talked Ah Huan into leaving?","Thinking of this, Song Yu grew somewhat anxious. \"Ah Huan, regarding King Heng's side, can we close the net soon? News from the Shen Manor says Shen Qingping has already found a clue and will return to the capital shortly.\"","Upon hearing this, Song Shihuan nodded, then smiled even more happily. \"Royal Father, there's no hurry. Master said they want to vent some anger for me first.\"","Song Yu smiled bitterly.","He was in a hurry.","Truly.","If he didn't hurry, he was afraid he'd lose standing in his daughter's eyes.","Early the next morning, Emperor Yuanyou attended the morning court session wearing a look of \"frailty,\" because he too feared that if he remained ill any longer, his granddaughter might just waste away from worry.","Once Emperor Yuanyou took his seat on the dragon throne, the court officials who had been arguing fiercely quieted down considerably.","\"Those with matters to report may speak; if none, court is dismissed.\"","As Wu Qi's voice rang out, not a single civil or military official in the full court dared to bring up the matter of the Eastern Palace.","It was at this moment that someone moved.","Cheng Guang shot a fierce glare in a certain direction. \"Your Majesty, during this recent period of your ailing health, the Eastern Palace has been thoroughly vilified by certain ministers.\"","\"Forcing the Crown Prince of a nation to adopt the son of a prince is utterly preposterous, and it has even implicated the Princess with slander. I believe these individuals should be charged with disrespect towards the heir apparent.\"","\"Your Majesty, I second the motion.\" Shen Mingwen also stepped forward. \"My residence, along with those of several other ministers, has been surrounded. This shows these people have gone mad.\"","Only then did the courtiers whose names were mentioned begin to feel fear.","Given the Emperor's obvious favoritism towards the Eastern Palace...","In an instant, King Heng received many pleading looks.","Just as King Heng was about to step forward to defend these people, he saw Emperor Yuanyou wave his hand. \"The Crown Prince is in the prime of his life. The matter of adoption is somewhat absurd.\"","King Heng's face instantly turned ashen.","\"We are weary. Court is dismissed for now.\"","As he left, Emperor Yuanyou paused in his steps. \"We may be old, but We will never allow anyone to casually slander Our son and granddaughter.\"","His tiger-like eyes swept the surroundings, and the entire hall fell so silent one could hear a pin drop.","It was only long after Emperor Yuanyou had left that King Heng moved his somewhat stiffened body. The Emperor's words just now...","They seemed to carry a great deal of killing intent.","Now, even the few remaining unruly court officials became compliant.","Had they not heard the Emperor's golden words, stating he did not support the adoption?","The winds at court changed swiftly. Those courtiers who had cursed the Eastern Palace most vehemently now began to huddle in their mansions, hoping to ride out this storm.","But they hadn't expected that this time, they had kicked an iron plate.","A few days later, a group of vibrant young men supporting an old man arrived outside the palace gates. The guards, seeing the familiar figures, instinctively wanted to run to the Eastern Palace.","But they saw the young men stop, and the leader, Qingling, produced a jade token from his waist.","\"The Sect Leader of the Qingyun Sect is here. Please quickly inform your Emperor.\"","Qingyun Sect?","Sect Leader?","One of the guards took off running again, though this time his destination was not the Eastern Palace, but the Zichen Hall.","He hadn't run far before he was suddenly grabbed by the collar by Shen Xiao, who appeared out of nowhere.","\"Without even asking the reason, you run to the Zichen Hall to deliver your death warrant?\"","Shen Xiao frowned. Where did this youngster come from, treating a report to the Emperor like passing a secret message?","\"Shen Xiao, Commander of the Great Qi Imperial Guards, pays his respects to Sect Leader Qing Shan.\"","Shen Xiao clasped his fist towards the old man. There was no martial artist under heaven who did not revere Qing Shan, the Sect Leader of Qingyun Sect, and Shen Xiao was no exception.","\"Might I ask why Sect Leader Qing Shan wishes to see our Emperor?\"","\"To settle accounts.\"","The old man's voice carried a natural, oppressive force that made it difficult for Shen Xiao to even stand straight:","\"My youngest disciple has been bullied by your Great Qi. I have come in person to demand justice for her!\"","\"A bunch of grown men bullying my little junior sister, a young girl. Your Great Qi courtiers are utterly shameless. In my opinion, if they rubbed their faces against tree bark, it's probably the bark that would get hurt.\"","The youngest of the youths opened his mouth, and the words that came out left Shen Xiao, for once, somewhat speechless.","And for the first time, the Qingyun Sect members felt that the youngest brother could actually produce something decent from his mouth.","\"Might I ask... who is the youngest disciple the Sect Leader speaks of?\"","\"You call her Princess.\"","Instantly, a flash of intense shock passed through Shen Xiao's eyes.","The guard Shen Xiao had stopped began to feel his legs go weak. The Princess was actually... a disciple of the Qingyun Sect!","Then the 'settling accounts' the Qingyun Sect spoke of...","Surely meant settling accounts with those ministers?","Heavens above!","...","One hour later.","The old man looked at the energetic Emperor Yuanyou before him and gave a slight, wry smile. \"I heard the Great Qi Emperor was gravely ill. It seems rumors are just rumors after all.\"","\"Feigning illness yourself while allowing your granddaughter to be slandered doesn't seem like the act of a proper gentleman.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's smile stiffened.","This Qing Shan actually called him an improper old man!","\"Sect Leader Qing Shan, you are not aware. This time, my illness was part of the strategy, a pretense to move the situation forward.\"","Emperor Yuanyou offered a dry explanation, wishing he could grab Qing Shan and pour out his affection for Ah Huan.","His heart for Ah Huan could be witnessed by heaven and earth.","Sect Leader Qing Shan smiled a thin, unamused smile. \"It seems you also intend to deal with King Heng.\"","\"Naturally.\"","\"And what about those useless followers who went with the flow? How do you plan to handle them?\"","\"Ah Huan told me, let the Qingyun Sect teach them a lesson first.\" Emperor Yuanyou immediately replied.","Wu Qi, watching from the side, secretly marveled at this almost fantastical scene. It was rare to see the Emperor so... obedient?","The old man seemed satisfied, his expression softening considerably. \"In that case, my thanks in advance.\"","\"I wish to meet the officials of Great Qi, so my disciples here can properly observe the dignified bearing of your court ministers.\"","Upon hearing this, Emperor Yuanyou actually felt his old face flush with embarrassment.","Dignified bearing...","These courtiers who had utterly disgraced his old face—he would definitely settle accounts with them later!"]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: Backing: Ah Huan Has a Powerful Backer Behind Him","paragraphs":["All civil and military officials received an urgent summons to the palace.","At the palace gate.","\"Your Highness King Heng, do you know the urgent matter for which the palace has summoned us?\" Some court officials with guilty consciences whispered to King Heng.","\"This prince does not know either. Perhaps His Majesty the Emperor wishes to handle court affairs.\"","Meanwhile, officials aligned with the Crown Prince's faction all entered the palace with their heads bowed, eyes fixed on their own noses and hearts. It certainly wouldn't be bad news.","If it were bad news, His Highness the Crown Prince would already be jumping up and down in the Zichen Hall by now.","Especially Cheng Guang, who looked utterly smug, making King Heng's teeth itch with irritation. How did a person with such an appearance climb to the position of a nation's Prime Minister?","One hour later, everyone had gradually arrived at the Zichen Hall.","Yet, Emperor Yuanyou's figure was conspicuously absent.","\"His Majesty is with an esteemed guest. Please wait, all of you,\" Wu Qi announced, holding a horsetail whisk, then signaled to the young eunuchs standing by. Each young eunuch was holding a chair.","Soon, a chair was placed behind Shen Mingwen.","Then behind Gu Zheng, Ye Shijie, Cheng Guang...","Gradually, everyone realized something was amiss. Only the court officials of the Crown Prince's faction had chairs!","Those who had spoken against the Crown Prince could only stand foolishly in place.","They stood like that for over an hour.","The legs of the standing officials were trembling, and they struggled to maintain their composure.","\"General Gu, this chair is making my back ache a bit. Do you feel the same?\" Cheng Guang asked with a smile, causing the standing officials to shudder.","Deliberate. That scoundrel Cheng Guang was absolutely doing it on purpose.","\"A little,\" Gu Zheng surprisingly took up Cheng Guang's remark, even stretching his back. \"Probably standing is more comfortable.\"","This tone of feigned envy made King Heng, who was standing, turn livid.","His resentment towards Emperor Yuanyou had reached its peak. To think he would use such an undignified method to punish them.","\"My, why is everyone standing?\"","Song Yu arrived late, wearing an expression of feigned surprise. \"Wu Qi, why hasn't a seat been provided for King Heng?\"","\"Your Highness, this is all His Majesty's intention.\"","\"Oh—\"","Song Yu deliberately drew out the syllable, then leisurely made his way towards the inner chamber.","Satisfied.","It seems the Qingyun Sect has no shortage of methods for dealing with people.","......","\"Master Qingshan, this is my good-for-nothing son.\"","Hearing Emperor Yuanyou's voice, Song Yu immediately wiped the playful smile from his face. He stepped forward swiftly and solemnly, bowing respectfully to Master Qingshan.","Emperor Yuanyou, standing to the side, felt a sour taste in his heart. This rascal was rarely this well-behaved in front of him.","Meanwhile, the old man slowly rose with the support of those beside him. \"Over these years, thank you, Your Highness the Crown Prince, for taking care of Ah Huan.\"","He had heard Ah Huan recount her experiences over the years, so he felt grateful towards the man before him.","\"It was... it was only right.\"","Emperor Yuanyou, watching Song Yu stammering before him, snorted coldly.","This old sect master hadn't even thanked him!","\"Ah Huan has a kind heart. If you show her three parts kindness, she wishes to repay you with seven.\" The old man looked steadily at Song Yu. \"Regarding this matter, I do not blame you.\"","I do not blame you, so I will administer the punishment to those in the hall on your behalf.","Then, the old man glanced at the sky outside and spoke to Qingling, \"The time has come.\"","Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu both shivered simultaneously. Was another spectacle about to unfold?","A quarter of an hour later.","A young eunuch hurried into the hall, walking up to one of the standing officials. \"My lord, your wife has been found guilty of privately lending money at usurious interest. Upon verification, not only your wife, but your elderly mother has also been engaging in this explicitly forbidden practice. They have been imprisoned.\"","Shocked by the terrible news, the official swayed on his feet, breaking out in a cold sweat.","Another quarter of an hour later.","The familiar young eunuch entered the hall again, this time approaching a different official. \"My lord, your youngest son, while intoxicated, recklessly discussed court affairs and even incited others at his table to disrespect the Crown Prince. This is a grave offense. He has also been imprisoned.\"","Thereafter, every quarter of an hour, one of the standing officials would receive devastating news from home.","Those who hadn't yet received bad news were all on edge, some even collapsing to the ground.","But the punishment was far from over.","The households of these individuals were thoroughly investigated. Even the crimes of some collateral branches of their clans were brought to light. The one behind this was clearly aiming to end their official careers.","Finally, when the young eunuch brought yet another piece of bad news, King Heng could no longer bear it and stopped him:","\"Might we inquire when we can see His Majesty? Could you convey a message for this prince?\"","By now, King Heng's back was soaked with sweat, and his voice sounded weak.","\"Your Highness King Heng, this servant is merely a messenger.\"","Upon hearing this, King Heng nearly slumped in defeat, lowering his head. This feeling of being slowly cut by a blunt knife was truly agonizing...","......","On the other side.","The expressions on Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu's faces shifted from initial calmness to later astonishment.","So this is how the Qingyun Sect operates!","A lesson learned!","Those fools in the hall still didn't know who was behind their punishment.","Meanwhile, the old man sipped his tea in small, confident gulps, as if holding all the cards.","This was just the beginning.","Their Qingyun Sect excelled at gathering information. Failure to tell the truth meant a beating.","\"Might I ask, when will your young Lord Shen return?\"","Qingling asked with a smile. \"Now we're just waiting for him.\"","\"You intend to...\" Song Yu realized something and suppressed the urge to applaud in admiration.","\"Since the punishment has begun, it must be carried out fully before it ends.\"","Qingling revealed a seemingly benign yet murderously intent smile. \"How could we possibly leave out your King Heng?\"","\"This prince will send someone to urge him immediately.\"","Meanwhile, at the Eastern Palace.","Liu Xi was like a restless melon-field rodent, constantly running back and forth between the Zichen Hall and the Eastern Palace, recounting the thrilling events unfolding in the Zichen Hall to Song Shihuan.","\"The Qingyun Sect is backing the Princess! This is the way to vent our anger properly!\"","Baoxia exhaled heavily, as if expelling all the pent-up frustration accumulated recently. \"This will teach those court officials who overestimate themselves and dare to criticize the Princess.\"","Even the usually steady Yingchun laughed aloud, her face clearly lit with relief.","The corners of Song Shihuan's mouth lifted, her eyebrows tinged with joy. Her current backers were probably unique in all the world.","This feeling... was truly wonderful.","The people in the Zichen Hall waited for nearly another hour, until those seated had started on their fifth cup of tea, when movement was heard outside again.","By now, among those standing, only King Heng had not received any bad news.","Everyone couldn't help but look at King Heng. Even he could hear the violent pounding of his own heart.","But this time, it was not the previous young eunuch who entered.","It was Shen Qingping, who had returned, covered in the chill of distant travels and dust from the journey.","\"King Heng, it's been a while.\""]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443: The One You Bully Is a Member of My Qingyun Sect","paragraphs":["Looking at the smiling Shen Qingping before him, King Heng had a feeling of impending doom.","\"Eunuch Wu Qi, please inform His Majesty that this official has returned, having fulfilled the mission without disgrace.\"","Wu Qi's demeanor towards Shen Qingping and King Heng was like night and day. Upon hearing Shen Qingping's words, he immediately scurried off.","A short while later, Emperor Yuanyou emerged.","Unlike his previous sickly appearance, Emperor Yuanyou now had a ruddy complexion, and his steps were firm and steady.","King Heng finally realized a terrifying possibility.","Perhaps the Emperor... had never been seriously ill from the start?","Seeing the old man beside Emperor Yuanyou, the court officials present were momentarily stunned, unable to make sense of the situation.","\"This is Master Qingshan, the leader of the Qingyun Sect.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's words caused everyone's eyes to widen in shock. The Qingyun Sect had always had no dealings with them, so why would they suddenly appear in the Great Qi imperial palace?","The old man walked straight towards King Heng, who instantly felt an oppressive aura.","\"You are King Heng?\"","\"You are the one who incited the Great Qi officials to support the Crown Prince adopting your son?\"","The so-called Qingyun Sect leader pressed forward step by step, forcing King Heng to defend himself:","\"What? Is the Qingyun Sect now meddling in the internal affairs of a nation?\"","A burst of mocking laughter rang out. A shadow seemed to flash behind the old man as Qingling's hand clamped down tightly on King Heng's neck.","\"What? Do you think my little disciple is unworthy of being an heir to the Crown Prince?\"","Boom—","The old man's words were like a massive rock thrown into water, instantly stirring up towering waves.","\"Not only that, but you deliberately sent people to find fault with my disciple. My disciple, a princess of noble status, is she someone you can casually criticize?\"","King Heng's face began to turn a purplish-blue from suffocation.","The surrounding court officials stood dumbfounded, each one forgetting they should try to save King Heng.","A single thought echoed in everyone's mind... The princess is actually the Qingyun Sect leader's little disciple!","\"My Qingyun Sect has always kept to its own affairs, but now you have bullied someone from our sect. I stand here today to demand an explanation from all of you standing here!\"","After saying this, the old man's face paled slightly. A disciple behind him silently stepped forward to support his arm.","\"My little disciple is only thirteen this year. She learned martial arts and battle formations at my knee since childhood, and just half a year ago, she led Great Qi to conquer Great Yue. Such monumental achievements were actually forgotten because of a damned King Heng and his son?\"","His forceful words made the standing officials lower their heads in fear.","\"The earlier misfortunes were just an appetizer.\"","With that, the old man signaled Qingling to release his grip. King Heng fell to the ground like a ragdoll, his violent coughing filling many hearts with terror.","So it wasn't the Emperor who acted, but the Qingyun Sect.","And the Emperor actually condoned the Qingyun Sect's actions!","The Crown Prince's faction, on the other hand, could barely contain their joy. With the Qingyun Sect now as the princess's shield, the Crown Prince's position was... as solid as a rock.","\"You are Ah Huan's tutor?\"","\"Greetings, Master Qingshan.\"","Shen Qingping was also startled by the sudden turn of events, his pupils contracting. \"I just heard the Qingyun Sect has already meted out some punishment. Regarding the remaining matter of King Heng, could you first hand him over to me?\"","\"Very well.\"","Shen Qingping glanced at Emperor Yuanyou, who also nodded, before turning to face the assembly.","Shen Qingping parted his thin lips slightly:","\"How can the descendant of a deserter defile the bloodline of the Crown Prince?\"","...","\"Shen Qingping! How dare you insult the imperial ancestors before so many people? You are courting death!\"","Seeing King Heng's furious and flustered expression, Shen Qingping's lips curved slightly. \"The deserter I speak of is precisely your father, Your Highness King Heng.\"","With that, Shen Qingping clapped his hands. Those waiting outside the hall immediately escorted the witness they had found into the chamber.","\"I have always wondered why your father, Your Highness, refused to come forward and acknowledge His Majesty, only revealing his true identity on his deathbed.\"","\"If I guess correctly, he must have also instructed you that if you were recognized by His Majesty, you must remain content as a mere imperial clansman, am I right?\"","King Heng's eyes darted about, but he vehemently denied it.","Shen Qingping was in no hurry. He turned his attention to the witness.","\"Your Majesty, this man also participated in that founding war of yours. He witnessed with his own eyes how King Heng's father, cowardly and timid, fled under the pretext of scouting enemy positions before the battle began.\" Shen Qingping's words left everyone dumbfounded. \"I have also found other witnesses. Here are their testimonies.\"","\"You lie! My father was seriously wounded, fell unconscious, was rescued, lost his memory, and only then ended up drifting abroad!\"","King Heng's eyes were bloodshot. If the desertion charge was confirmed, then they... they would have no chance of turning the tables.","\"Back then, we were ordered to protect King Heng's father.\" The witness, who had remained silent, finally spoke, his voice filled with unmistakable hatred. \"There were twenty of us. He lied, saying he would lead us to scout the enemy, but instead led us into a pre-set animal trap pit, staging it as an unfortunate accident to cover up his desertion.\"","\"I struggled to climb out, wanting to continue protecting him, but I saw him run away by himself! He deserted!\"","\"Scoundrel!\"","Emperor Yuanyou roared, rushing before King Heng and pointing a finger at his nose. \"Your father dared to desert back then, and now you try to confuse my bloodline!\"","\"Imperial Uncle, it's impossible... this is impossible...\"","\"Oh, right.\" The old man suddenly spoke up. \"If you don't believe it, our sect's Ghost Doctor can exhume that man's remains and deduce the injuries he suffered based on the bones.\"","Probably didn't have a single wound on him.","The atmosphere in the hall grew still. The standing officials wished they could slap their own faces. The descendant of a deserter could never, under any circumstances, become part of the Crown Prince's bloodline.","Then all their previous actions... were they no different from fools?","\"Gu Zheng, according to military law, how should one who flees the battlefield be dealt with?\"","\"Beaten to death with clubs.\"","Gu Zheng cast a deep look at King Heng, whose legs had begun to tremble.","\"If the father is no longer here, then let the son bear the punishment in his stead.\"","Emperor Yuanyou said this and then looked at the old man. \"I wonder if such handling satisfies Master Qingshan?\"","\"Have all other relatives of the Hengwang Residence come to witness the punishment.\"","The old man added with a smile, looking quite pleased with Shen Qingping.","This man acted decisively, striking straight at the enemy's vital point with a single blow.","Upon hearing this, Emperor Yuanyou went to instruct Wu Qi. Gu Zheng also began to roll up his sleeves, preparing to personally carry out the punishment on King Heng.","\"Should we invite Little Junior Sister?\"","\"Such a bloody scene might scare Little Junior Sister.\"","Over on the Qingyun Sect side, they had already started discussing their sect's one-and-only little junior sister."]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444: Prince Heng Beaten to Death with Sticks, Like a Dog Driven into a Dead End","paragraphs":["\"Father—\"","As soon as Song Liu and Song Hui arrived at the Purple Palace Hall, they saw Prince Heng already pressed down on the punishment bench. He had been stripped of his princely robes, leaving only his undergarments.","Song Yu, who had been trying to stay unnoticed, shuffled over to the old man. \"Didn't the Sect Leader prepare any other methods to deal with Prince Heng?\"","\"A-Huan mentioned earlier that her tutor was investigating.\"","The old man was rather terse, but the coldness in his eyes made Song Yu feel things were definitely not that simple.","This old man had chosen the ruthless method of destroying families and wiping out lineages to deal with those court officials. Merely taking Prince Heng's life seemed somewhat out of place.","Song Yu decided to wait and see.","\"Song Liu, Song Hui, do you object to Our decision?\"","At the sound of Emperor Yuanyou's voice, Prince Heng... oh no, Song Heng's struggling movements halted abruptly. He looked at his son and daughter. \"I am suffering punishment in your grandfather's stead. You two are auspicious signs, blessed with good fortune. Do not let your fate be damaged because of me.\"","With that, he spoke to a young eunuch nearby, \"Hold them back.\"","Seeing this, Emperor Yuanyou snorted coldly. \"Carry out the punishment.\"","Auspicious signs indeed, pah.","Gu Zheng personally carried out the punishment, using ten-tenths of his strength. With the first strike of the rod, Song Heng felt as if his internal organs had been displaced.","A military execution by rod did not have a set number of strikes; it continued until death.","At first, Song Heng could endure without making a sound, but gradually, the intense pain blurred his reason, and screams began to escape his lips.","It was at this moment that Song Shihuan arrived at the Purple Palace Hall.","As soon as she entered, everyone saw their Emperor squeezing his way through to run up to the Crown Prince. He took the Princess's hand with one hand and covered her eyes with the other.","The Crown Prince, a step too slow, stamped his foot in annoyance, then used both hands to cover the Princess's ears instead.","The assembled ministers: \"...\"","That wasn't all. Several disciples of the Qingyun Sect, reacting quickly, also ran over to surround the Princess, seemingly competing in a subtle contest of wills. Within moments, their Crown Prince was squeezed out of the circle.","His expression was one of shame and irritation.","Heavens, if the Princess wanted a star from the sky, these people would probably start climbing without a second thought.","It was rare for everyone's thoughts to wander at such a moment.","In the entire hall, only Song Liu and Song Hui were weeping bitterly for Song Heng.","...","Just as Song Heng was beaten to his last breath, the old man's voice slowly rang out.","\"Wait.\"","The punishment rod in Gu Zheng's hand stopped mid-air. Everyone's gaze turned towards the source.","They saw the old man walk up to Song Shihuan and gently pat her head. \"Master taught you, 'to drive a dog into a dead-end alley...'\"","\"'...is to invite a desperate counter-attack.'\"","Song Shihuan answered almost without hesitation.","\"Today, Master will teach you something more. If your strength is such that you can regard your opponent as an ant, then you may indeed drive the dog into the dead-end alley, to eradicate the threat forever.\"","\"Qingling.\"","\"Your disciple is here.\"","Qingling put away his gentle smile and took out a small booklet from his sleeve.","\"Our Qingyun Sect has also investigated the Prince Heng residence. We discovered that Song Heng has made many covert moves, using both favors and threats to grasp the weaknesses of several individuals, forcing them to do his bidding.\" Qingling looked at Song Liu. \"Surprisingly, Song Liu and Song Hui were also involved.\"","\"Using their age advantage to interact with peers from noble families, extracting secrets and leverage. We reasonably suspect this family harbors intentions of rebellion.\"","Song Heng, with only one breath left, tried to speak upon hearing these words but found he could no longer utter a sound.","Song Liu, terrified, turned and tried to run outside, only to be stopped by the guards at the hall's entrance.","After reading the small booklet in Qingling's hand, Emperor Yuanyou's face turned as dark as the bottom of a pot.","\"Song Liu, have you been to a blacksmith's shop?\"","\"I... I just wanted to forge a suitable weapon.\"","Song Liu suddenly felt tongue-tied, unable to explain himself clearly.","His visit to the blacksmith's shop... indeed wasn't solely for forging a weapon.","\"Song Hui, have you made contact with the pastry shop frequented by the Gu family's pearl?\"","Song Hui's face turned deathly pale, stammering, unable to speak.","\"Song Liu and Song Hui harbor impure intentions, damaging the royal family's reputation. They are granted the privilege of taking their own lives.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's voice, crystal clear, reached Song Heng's ears. Song Heng felt his eyes were about to burst from their sockets.","His son and daughter... his only two blood descendants...","\"Continue the punishment.\"","Hearing this, Gu Zheng raised the punishment rod even higher than before. Remembering the mention of the pastry shop, a look of utter contempt, as if viewing the dead, flashed in his eyes. He mustered all the strength in his body and brought the rod down heavily upon Song Heng.","Life was extinguished.","Only then did Gu Zheng let out a heavy sigh. Daring to set his sights on his daughter? He would find a Taoist priest later to ensure Song Heng was reborn in the animal realm.","May he never be human again.","\"Your Majesty, the man is thoroughly dead.\"","Wu Qi's voice sent a shiver through the hearts of all present.","\"All of you, disperse.\"","The words were like a great pardon. One by one, they eagerly scrambled out of the Purple Palace Hall.","Too terrifying. Upon returning home, they must write 'do not offend the Princess' into the family rules.","...","Song Liu and Song Hui were taken to the imperial prison. That very night, eunuchs arrived at their cell holding white silk and poisoned wine.","\"His Majesty is benevolent and kind, granting you the privilege of choosing your manner of departure.\"","Song Liu and Song Hui's teeth were chattering. \"Beating my father to death, and now wiping us out as well—this is called benevolent and kind?\"","\"How dare you!\"","\"Just based on your grandfather who deserted, it would be enough to send you both on your way. Yet you were not content, insisting on offending those you should not have. His Majesty has already granted you ample dignity.\"","\"Choose quickly.\"","Seeing their prolonged hesitation, the young eunuch began to grow impatient.","\"I can't die. I haven't even had my coming-of-age ceremony yet.\"","Song Hui suddenly broke down. \"If only we hadn't come to the capital. If only we hadn't come to the capital.\"","The eunuch wore a look of accustomed indifference. The will to live is human instinct. Usually, in such situations, they simply chose for them.","\"You two, force the poisoned wine down their throats.\"","With that, two more young eunuchs approached Song Liu and Song Hui.","As the poisoned wine was forced into their mouths, they heard the eunuch's shrill voice once more:","\"Blame your own greed. You offended the Princess—the heart and soul of the Emperor and the Crown Prince, the only female disciple of the Qingyun Sect.\"","\"One should revere such a person, not cross her.\"","Under the moonlight, the breaths of Song Liu and Song Hui gradually ceased.","The farce concerning the royal recognition came to a complete end.","And the auspicious reputation they had once been so proud of vanished without a trace.","Meanwhile, back in the Purple Palace Hall...","\"No, A-Huan must stay in the side chamber tonight. We haven't had a chance to talk with A-Huan for a long time.\"","\"No, A-Huan must return to the Eastern Palace tonight. Why stay in someone else's place when she has her own courtyard?\"","\"No, tonight our Qingyun Sect is taking A-Huan out to enjoy the sights of the capital.\"","The three parties glared at each other, then turned their gazes towards...","Song Shihuan, who was trying to sneak away quietly while pulling Shen Qingping along.","Heh heh.","Song Shihuan offered an awkward yet polite smile."]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445: Good and evil will eventually be repaid in the end.","paragraphs":["\"According to the agreement we reached earlier, the bodies of Song Ling's family will be handed over to our Qingyun Sect for full disposal.\"","Inside the Zichen Hall, the Qingyun Sect Leader and Emperor Yuanyou sat facing each other.","The two old men almost simultaneously picked up their teacups, taking a light sip to ease the tension.","Of course, we will proceed with this process in secret, so as not to damage the dignity of the Great Qi imperial family.","The old man felt he was being quite considerate. Given how Song Ling's family had treated Ah Huan, it wouldn't be excessive for him to go blow up their coffins directly.","Emperor Yuanyou was conflicted. In his heart, he wanted to agree, but he also felt they were, after all, his own bloodline. Would handing them over so casually lead to condemnation by his ancestors a hundred years later?","Seeing Emperor Yuanyou silent, the old man's face darkened.","\"In that case, I will take Ah Huan back to Qingyun Realm.\"","\"Then... you'd better take the bodies.\"","Emperor Yuanyou hastily spoke up, afraid that a second's delay would mean losing his precious granddaughter.","Let the ancestors condemn him if they must; he had his reasons for doing this!","\"Good. We will go dig up the corpses tomorrow night.\"","\"Oh, and don't forget Song Heng's body,\" Emperor Yuanyou even added, as if afraid the old man might forget.","The corner of the old man's mouth twitched.","This Great Qi Emperor truly despised Song Heng.","\"Don't worry. We'll help you clean up the trash while we're at it.\"","At the same time, in the Eastern Palace.","\"What do you want the bodies for?\" The full contingent of the Eastern Palace's wings had gathered, a rare occurrence, to celebrate the belated arrival of \"peace.\"","With fine wine in his belly, Cheng Guang couldn't help but ask the Qingyun Sect disciples.","\"I know! The Qingyun Sect has very high requirements for sword techniques. Their bones can be used to test the sharpness of sword energy.\"","Ugh—","Cheng Guang felt like vomiting.","Wrong. Master probably wants to test the keenness of weapons.","Zheng Fang began to feel aches all over his body.","\"You're both wrong. Master will definitely send them to the Mystic Physician, to see if they can be ground into powder for medicine.\"","Gu Zheng also started to feel a chill.","If Ping Wang (Prince Ping) had known his bones would end up in the hands of the Qingyun Sect after death, one wonders if he would have regretted being born into this world.","\"Regardless, it's nothing more than they deserve.\"","It was already the twelfth lunar month, bitterly cold, and Shen Qingping's complexion seemed especially pale.","His voice, as he spoke, seemed to carry a hint of cold air.","You are very suited to join our Qingyun Sect. Although you have no martial arts foundation, you would surely be a prodigy in learning formation arrays.","\"Master likes you very much too.\"","Qingling walked over to Shen Qingping and spoke in a low voice.","He could see that although this man before him was physically weaker than others, his temperament was the most unyielding, just like... a wolf in the snow.","Hearing this, Song Yu shot to his feet. Poaching his people right in front of him? The Qingyun Sect had no shame!","But then he saw Shen Qingping rise with a smile, meeting Qingling's gaze. \"No, thank you.\"","Several years ago, I already signed an indenture contract.","What a pity.","Qingling's expression dimmed.","He had still wanted to lure this man back to the Qingyun Sect to be the next sect leader. The young lady's tutor, with such ruthless methods, was most capable of commanding the respect of the entire sect.","He really didn't want to be burdened with sect affairs anymore!","Song Yu breathed a sigh of relief, and the others also relaxed slightly.","Only Cheng Guang stared dumbfounded at Shen Qingping. The 'indenture contract' this person just mentioned...","Could it be the position of Prime Minister?","If it were anyone else, he might still have a chance to compete, but if it were this one...","Cheng Guang felt extremely wronged. Was the order of appearance really that important?","......","As the year-end approached, Emperor Yuanyou, with thunderous methods, punished the many court ministers who had sided with Song Heng. Edicts flowed continuously, stained with blood, yet Emperor Yuanyou showed not a hint of softness.","He was old, and he wanted to use his remaining time to clear all obstacles for his child.","No one pleaded for mercy, and no one dared to.","Ping Wang's Mansion.","\"Is it almost New Year?\"","Now, the vast Ping Wang's Mansion held only Chang Ling'er. After Lady Chang's death, Chang Ling'er seemed to have been forgotten by everyone, staying in the Li Garden every day.","\"Soon.\"","Only one old maid was ordered to watch over Chang Ling'er.","The sound of footsteps approached. Chang Ling'er looked at the guard before her.","\"Second Miss Chang.\"","Hearing this address, Chang Ling'er was taken aback.","The bodies of Prince Ping's family have been secretly exhumed and handed over to the Qingyun Sect for disposal. The Crown Prince has ordered Princess Consort Ping's body to be moved to the Chang family ancestral graves. You may go pay your respects.","\"Qingyun Sect?\"","The maid on the side carefully explained the recent events to Chang Ling'er.","Chang Ling'er listened, crying and laughing by turns, finally looking up at the sky. \"Aunt, the princess has the Qingyun Sect protecting her. You can rest at ease.\"","That night, Chang Ling'er changed into her favorite clothes.","Snow began to fall from the sky, the first snow of the year.","\"Nanny, personally take this letter and give it to the guard outside the mansion gates.\"","Watching the nanny walk away, Chang Ling'er foolishly laughed. The princess now had a powerful backer, so she could go to the underworld to find her aunt.","Not just her aunt, but also her father and mother.","She had clung to life for so long in this world, missing them terribly.","A candle was knocked over. The flame caught the fabric in an instant and began to burn. In less than a quarter of an hour, the Li Garden was engulfed in raging flames.","In the moment before losing consciousness, Chang Ling'er's vision was completely blurred.","Yet within that blur, she seemed to see that year again. She was sitting on the swing in the courtyard, her father pushing her gently yet firmly from behind. She swung very high.","A young man suddenly barged into her sight like that, a smile on his lips, calling her 'Ling'er, cousin.'","From then on, her heart was lost.","And she began walking towards a bottomless abyss.","The greatest mistake of Chang Ling'er's life was falling in love with Song Yanzheng.","Outside Ping Wang's Mansion, the nanny's legs felt as heavy as if filled with lead. Trembling, she opened the letter in her hand—it was blank paper.","Clearly, it was just to send her away...","The nanny wept uncontrollably.","The fire burned for a full two hours, consuming the entire Ping Wang's Mansion.","The once splendid Ping Wang's Mansion was now left with even its walls blackened. Passersby dared not linger, afraid of being haunted by something sinister.","Upon hearing of Chang Ling'er's death, Emperor Yuanyou merely ordered her to be buried in the Chang family ancestral graves.","\"Yu'er, I feel that place, Ping Wang's Mansion, is inauspicious,\" Emperor Yuanyou frowned. \"Why not demolish it?\"","\"It is indeed inauspicious,\"","Song Yu agreed. \"Tomorrow, I will have the Ministry of Works start demolishing it. In my opinion, Chang Ling'er's fire actually burned well.\"","\"It burned away all the filthy things hidden within Ping Wang's Mansion.\"","Denied proper burial after death, their dwelling burned to ruin.","Such vengeful ghosts, how could they possibly re-enter the cycle of rebirth?","Song Yu raised his eyes to look at the snowflakes outside the window, his heart trembling slightly.","If only... if only he could also have a chance to start over, a chance to protect Ah Huan anew.","How wonderful that would be..."]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446: Who Said I Was Going Back to the Azure Cloud Realm","paragraphs":["On the day before New Year's Eve, Song Shihuan brought the old man to a place.","\"This is where Grandma is buried. Father has had it repaired; it looks much nicer than before.\"","Over the years, Song Shihuan had grown quite a bit in height, now blossoming into a graceful young woman.","The old man behind her cracked a smile, but it didn't quite reach his eyes. Holding a roast goose, he stood there foolishly, unsure what to do.","\"Grandma, Master is back. He remembers you loved roast goose best and specially went to buy it for you.\"","\"Master, why aren't you saying anything?\"","Song Shihuan turned her head to look at the old man. He wiped his eyes with his hand, then placed the roast goose before the grave, along with a single red plum blossom.","The white of the snow and the red of the plum complemented each other.","\"Don't eat too much roast goose; it's not good for your health.\"","Hearing the old man's words, Song Shihuan couldn't help but pout. That line again.","Grandma would definitely be covering her ears if she heard it.","\"I was too late. I couldn't save you, and I couldn't protect Ah Huan either.\"","The old man rambled on in front of the grave for a long time. Song Shihuan wasn't in a hurry, just waited patiently by his side.","It wasn't until dusk began to fall that the old man finally pushed himself up. \"Tomorrow is New Year's Eve. We'll save a seat for you at the table, so remember to come and have the reunion dinner with us.\"","Hearing the words \"reunion dinner,\" Song Shihuan couldn't help but smile.","Yes.","This was the true reunion.","Everyone she loved, and everyone who loved her, was by her side.","......","Everyone had a wonderful New Year this year.","They had won the war and stabilized the court. Even the common people on the streets wore joyful smiles. With the Great Qi nation prosperous and strong, their lives were naturally happy and fulfilling.","At the Gu residence.","Gu Zheng was playing with his little granddaughter. Tuan was now at that delightful age where she could babble in response to adults, understanding speech but not yet able to talk properly.","Seizing a moment when no one was watching, Gu Zheng quickly planted a kiss on Tuan's little cheek. The next second, he was met with a roar worthy of a lioness:","\"Father! You kissed Tuan again!\"","Gu Mingzhu looked like a mother hen protecting her chick. \"Your beard is so rough! Tuan's skin is delicate; it will hurt her.\"","\"Unless you shave that beard off, you can't kiss Tuan.\"","\"How could I possibly do that?\" Gu Zheng's voice rose several notches. \"What kind of man doesn't keep a beard?\"","\"Fine, no kisses then!\"","Gu Zheng stomped off in a huff.","The next day, at the New Year's Eve palace banquet.","Emperor Yuanyou stared at Gu Zheng, whose beard had been shaved completely clean, and for a moment couldn't quite process it.","Where was his burly, bearded general?","\"Gu Zheng, where is your beard?\"","Emperor Yuanyou voiced the question on everyone's mind in the hall.","\"The beard was inconvenient, so I shaved it off,\" Gu Zheng said with an awkward laugh. He had tossed and turned all night, ultimately deciding that cuddling with his granddaughter was more important.","So, he had shaved it off first thing in the morning.","Yu Fan, who knew the inside story, stifled a laugh.","Everyone else felt a bit uncomfortable. A general without a beard... looked like a tiger stripped of its fur.","An eyesore.","After three rounds of drinks, the free-toasting session began.","Yu Fan picked up his wine cup and headed straight for Song Shihuan.","\"Minister Yu, have you fully recovered?\"","\"Thanks to Your Highness's blessings, I am completely well now.\" Yu Fan's eyes were full of respect for Song Shihuan. \"You saved my life. Today, I offer you this toast.\"","During that great battle, if the princess hadn't thought of using mirrors to reflect sunlight, he... would have found it very hard to keep his life.","\"It's good that you're fully recovered. That way, Sister Gu can rest easy too.\"","As she spoke, Song Shihuan raised the cup of goat's milk in front of her and gulped it down.","In the past, she could still drink some fruit wine, but now that the old man was here, she was only allowed goat's milk.","Song Shihuan felt a bit deflated. This really hindered her journey to adulthood.","\"I remember back when you married Sister Gu, you said you wouldn't return to the Northern Desert until you had achieved military merit. It's been so many years, and you and Sister Gu haven't seen your parents since. Now that you are covered in glory, when do you plan to go back to the Northern Desert to see them?\"","Song Shihuan's eyes darted around mischievously. If they were planning to go to the Northern Desert, they should take her along!","The palace nowadays was a minefield everywhere.","Of course, the minefield was only for her.","\"We should go back for a visit.\"","Mentioning his family brought a touch of longing to Yu Fan's eyes. \"I've discussed it with Ming Liu. We plan to go to the Northern Desert together after the New Year celebrations. Mingzhu wants to go too once she heard, to see her elder brother.\"","I want to go too!","Song Shihuan screamed internally.","\"It's good to have a plan. Remember to inform His Majesty in advance when the time comes,\" Song Shihuan said with a smile.","That would give her enough time to win over her grandfather.","\"Of course.\"","Seeing Song Shihuan and Yu Fan chatting happily, Emperor Yuanyou cleared his throat several times, failing to attract Song Shihuan's attention. Just as he was about to make more noise, a light laugh sounded beside him.","\"How old are you, still acting like a child?\"","Master Qingshan was leaning back in his chair. As he hadn't fully recovered from his illness, he was wrapped in a blanket, and his cup contained only tea.","For decades, no one had dared speak to him with such disregard for the boundaries between ruler and subject. Emperor Yuanyou felt both embarrassed and annoyed, yet also found it somewhat novel.","\"You should worry about yourself first. Don't let a gust of wind blow you away.\"","\"Thank you for your concern. I still have some weight to me; the wind won't blow me away.\"","And so, the two old men began trading barbs.","Song Yu and Qingling exchanged a look, both clearly finding the situation ridiculous.","Had these two old men eaten something wrong today?","......","The New Year holiday was Emperor Yuanyou's only break all year—no court sessions, no reviewing memorials. He wished every day could be spent in the blissful joy of doting on his grandchildren.","But it seemed the people from the Qingyun Sect had decided to overstay their welcome.","They kept taking Ah Huan out of the palace for day trips and bringing her back.","One day, the imperial father and son were fuming in the Zichen Hall, nursing their grievances.","\"Yu, isn't it about time the Qingyun Sect people left?\"","\"Should we hold a farewell banquet for them?\"","\"Reasonable.\"","Song Yu agreed without a second thought. Although this move was somewhat rude, it could win back custody of Ah Huan.","The next day, Song Yu began preparing the farewell banquet.","When the Qingyun Sect members heard about it, they didn't object, allowing the banquet to be arranged.","The elaborate banquet preparation process was forcefully compressed into three days.","The seventh day of the New Year, an auspicious day for moving.","At the farewell banquet, Master Qingshan looked perfectly normal, even cheerful, showing no sign of displeasure whatsoever.","Seeing this, Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu breathed a huge sigh of relief.","Getting rid of unwanted guests was hard.","As the farewell banquet was drawing to a close, Emperor Yuanyou asked with a smile, \"Might I ask when the Master plans to return to the Qingyun Realm with your disciples?\"","The old man looked at him with a puzzled expression.","Emperor Yuanyou instantly had a foreboding feeling.","\"Who said I'm returning to the Qingyun Realm?\"","\"But today is the farewell banquet...\" Emperor Yuanyou said, practically biting off each word.","\"Indeed. My disciples will set off for the Qingyun Realm tomorrow.\"","The old man leaned back in his chair. \"But I'm old, and my health isn't good. I'll stay in the capital to recuperate for now, and keep Ah Huan company.\"","Then the old man looked straight at Emperor Yuanyou:","\"Great Qi won't turn me away, will it?\""]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447: The old man wants to throw in the towel and quit","paragraphs":["The Qing Mountain Sect Leader successfully managed to stay on at the Great Qi Imperial Palace, infuriating Emperor Yuanyou so much that smoke practically billowed from the top of his head.","On this day, Shen Mingwen and Ye Shijie once again brought their dispute to the Purple Dawn Hall.","When scholars 'fight', it means they debate.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at the two faces flushed red with anger before him and sighed for the hundred and first time. What was so great about being emperor, anyway?","That old man from Qing Mountain could get Ah Huan to accompany him sightseeing all over the capital, but he, the emperor, could not.","Because whenever he left the palace, it had to be a grand production with countless eyes watching him.","Even that good-for-nothing from the Eastern Palace was now trotting happily behind the old Qing Mountain man, under the pretext of protection, but in reality, it was just a father who couldn't bear to be apart from his daughter. How pathetic!","Emperor Yuanyou's heart trembled slightly. What if he... stopped being this emperor?","\"Your Majesty, I wish to impeach Ye Shijie!\"","Shen Mingwen's voice abruptly yanked Emperor Yuanyou out of his beautiful daydream. Looking at the two men who had already come to him for a ruling no less than three times, Emperor Yuanyou pulled a long face.","\"You two are fighting over the future position of Imperial Tutor to this extent. Is it really worth it?\"","Shen Mingwen nearly choked on his own saliva. What did he mean... 'Is it worth it'?","It absolutely was!","\"Your Majesty, Ye Shijie's temperament is as cold and hard as a stinking rock. How could such a person properly instruct His Highness the Crown Prince?\"","\"Your Majesty, Grand Tutor Shen has more schemes than a honeycomb briquette. He would surely lead His Highness astray.\"","Emperor Yuanyou pressed his temples, feeling a headache coming on.","Finally, after the two continued attacking each other for another quarter of an hour, Emperor Yuanyou spoke. \"Who said the Imperial Tutor can only be one person?\"","Upon hearing this, the two men glanced at each other and promptly slipped out of the Purple Dawn Hall.","Dual Imperial Tutors was exactly what they wanted!","\"Hmph!\"","\"Hmph!\"","Once outside the hall, they snorted at each other again in mutual disdain, leaving Emperor Yuanyou inside staring out the window in a daze for a long time.","\"Go, summon the Crown Prince back to me.\"","......","And so.","Song Yu, who had been having a grand time playing outside, entered the palace utterly bewildered.","\"Father, instead of reviewing memorials in your hall, why have you summoned me to the Imperial Garden?\" Song Yu wrapped his cloak tighter around himself. \"It's bitterly cold in the middle of winter.\"","He saw Emperor Yuanyou wearing a look of paternal kindness, which only made Song Yu feel uneasy.","\"Yu'er, you are my most outstanding son.\"","\"You only have four sons in total. One died, one was deposed, one is a fool, so that just leaves me.\"","The emotion Emperor Yuanyou had painstakingly built up was shattered by Song Yu's words. Giving up the pretense, the Emperor laid his cards on the table:","\"I intend to abdicate the throne to you.\"","Song Yu immediately jumped up. \"No.\"","\"Why not?\" Emperor Yuanyou was exasperated. \"A Crown Prince who doesn't want to be emperor is not a good Crown Prince.\"","\"Being emperor is too exhausting, even more tiring than preparing for the imperial examinations.\" Song Yu waved his hand dismissively. \"You hardly get a few days off all year, and you have to play judge settling disputes. Father, you are still in the prime of your life for striving. What's all this talk of abdication?\"","\"I'm over sixty!\"","Emperor Yuanyou roared in anger. Over sixty and still in his 'prime for striving'?","\"But your son needs to spend time with Ah Huan now. If I become emperor, I won't have as much time for her.\" Song Yu grew somewhat sorrowful at the thought. \"When Ah Huan gets a little older, she'll have places she wants to go and people she wants to see. Then I'll only be able to watch her back as she leaves.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's lips trembled with rage. He wanted to spend time with his granddaughter too.","But before Emperor Yuanyou could say anything, Song Yu whooshed away.","As he left, he tossed back a line, \"Father, you are hale and hearty. Take good care of yourself, and you might even father another princess.\"","He ran faster than a rabbit.","But that very night, Song Yu sat facing Song Shihuan with a grave expression.","\"Ah Huan, the old man wants to shirk his duties and quit.\"","\"What should we do?\" Song Shihuan had no experience in this either.","\"Run.\"","Song Yu's thin lips parted slightly. \"Didn't you say Yu Fan and the others want to go to the Northern Frontier? We've been sending grain and silver there for years. It's perfectly reasonable to go see the people of the Northern Frontier. The situation is urgent. We'll set off first thing tomorrow morning.\"","Song Shihuan felt conflicted. Would this make Grandfather so angry he might faint?","\"Ah Huan, if I become emperor, I'll be tethered to the palace. Shen San, Zheng Fang, and the others would also be stuck in the capital. Then no one would be able to accompany you on trips outside the city anymore.\"","\"I think Grandfather is still in the prime of his life. It wouldn't be too late for Father to share his burdens in a couple of years.\"","Song Shihuan spoke against her conscience, her mind racing to figure out how to placate the old man after running off like this.","She did love her grandfather very much.","Just two years. In two years, she'd let her father become emperor.","......","At the same time, in the Northern Frontier.","Snowflakes fluttered, the north wind howled.","Gu Mingning, clad in armor, sat on the ground holding a roasted lamb leg, but a trace of loneliness, not easily shown to others, flickered in his eyes.","Another New Year had come.","He could scarcely remember how long it had been since he celebrated the New Year with his father and sisters.","Though young, he stood like a stone stele planted in the land of the Northern Frontier.","\"General, a letter for you.\"","The soldier's words were like a beam of light falling upon Gu Mingning. He finished the lamb leg in a few quick bites, carefully washed his hands, and only then accepted the letter.","Looking closely, Gu Mingning's hands trembled.","It was a letter from Mingzhu.","The letter said all the Gu family members were safe and well, that Yu Fan had received honors and rewards, and also described the turmoil at court.","Of course, the longest part was about little Tuan.","The corners of Gu Mingning's stern mouth turned up slightly, a rare sight that the surrounding soldiers witnessed with curiosity.","Having suppressed the naturally belligerent Northern Di tribe for so many years that they dared not provoke easily, Gu Mingning was regarded by the soldiers as a brilliantly talented young general.","\"My Tuan is truly beautiful.\"","Through the words, Gu Mingning seemed to traverse time and space, seeing the tiny figure in swaddling clothes.","When his gaze reached the last line, Gu Mingning froze completely. They... they were coming to the Northern Frontier?","A heart long dormant instantly began to pound wildly.","Just at that moment, another urgent voice sounded.","\"General, Prince Qi has led troops to patrol the border line.\"","The border line, mere steps away from the Northern Di territory, was fraught with danger. Surface patrols were actually demonstrations and warnings, usually completed swiftly by seasoned veterans.","Hearing this, Gu Mingning cursed under his breath. \"Why didn't you stop him?\"","\"Prince Qi said the Northern Frontier is his domain, and he has a duty to protect its people,\" the soldier reported woodenly. \"He also said that if he patrols, the people living near the border will feel at ease.\"","Gu Mingning was taken aback. Had Prince Qi taken the wrong medicine?","Just yesterday he was complaining that the Northern Frontier people trusted Gu Mingning more than they did Prince Qi, a royal scion, and today he was nobly risking his life?","As it turned out.","Prince Qi had miscalculated.","Walking along the border line, on one side were the Northern Frontier subjects looking at him with admiration in their eyes, on the other were the Northern Di people, weapons in hand, watching him like a tiger eyeing its prey.","Prince Qi swallowed hard, his legs feeling weak.","He shouldn't have listened to that damned advisor's suggestion to win over the people's hearts using such a dangerous method!"]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448: Being early is not as good as being timely; watch the King of Qi make a fool of himself.","paragraphs":["The Great Qi Imperial Palace.","Song Yu had slipped away with Song Shihuan, leaving Emperor Yuanyou with a letter and an equally resentful old man.","The letter contained only one sentence:","\"Gone to the northern deserts. Will return swiftly. Do not worry.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was so angry he could barely speak coherently. Pointing at the pitiful letter lying on the desk, he sputtered, \"That scoundrel! He left the capital without a word, and even took my granddaughter with him!\"","Master Qingshan, for once, found himself on the same side as the Emperor.","\"The Crown Prince's actions are indeed excessive.\"","\"He clearly could have taken me along too...\"","\"I wonder if we could still catch up if we set out now...\"","Each sentence was like rubbing salt in Emperor Yuanyou's wounds.","The Emperor grew even angrier. Just because he was the Emperor, he couldn't leave the palace at will!","\"My own flesh and blood, my own flesh and blood...\" Emperor Yuanyou repeated silently to himself, forcing himself to calm down. When he looked up again, a faint smile had appeared on his face, which inexplicably made Master Qingshan's heart tremble.","\"Tell me,\" the Emperor said, \"where would be a good place for me to build a princess manor for Ahuan?\"","Master Qingshan's eyes shifted thoughtfully. If a manor were built for Ahuan, they could directly set aside a courtyard for him, and he wouldn't have to go to the Eastern Palace to find her every day.","Thinking this, the two old men immediately reached an agreement.","They began planning the location for Song Shihuan's princess manor.","This time, Emperor Yuanyou's wrath was more \"ferocious\" than ever, and even Shen Qingping felt its effects.","\"Third Master, so many memorials...\" Nian'an stared, dumbfounded. Sorting through this many memorials... was the Emperor trying to work his Third Master to death?","\"Yes, so many memorials,\" Shen Qingping said through gritted teeth. \"It's fine. We'll tackle them one by one. If I can't finish reading them, we'll just wait for His Highness to return and read them together.\"","He emphasized the words \"His Highness\" heavily.","So, he runs off to enjoy himself, leaving me here in the capital to do the hard labor, is that it?","Meanwhile, Song Yu, who was merrily on his journey, suddenly sneezed.","\"Who's grumbling about me behind my back again?\"","......","Due to Gu Mingliu's incomplete recovery and Tuan being too young, their travel speed could only be described as snail-like.","Back in the capital, the resentment from the two old men could have filled the entire Eastern Palace, while their party still had a three-day journey to reach the northern deserts.","It was at this moment they encountered a soldier urgently dispatched from the northern deserts, heading to the capital to deliver a message.","\"What happened?\"","Yu Fan's face was full of worry, fearing something had gone wrong in the northern deserts.","Upon seeing Song Shihuan, the soldier visibly relaxed, as if seeing a savior. \"Prince Qi has been captured by the Northern Di!\"","\"Prince Qi led troops to patrol the border, his legs gave way, he fell into Northern Di territory, and was taken away by the Northern Di people...\"","Everyone present was stunned, feeling an absurd sense that while this was outrageous, if it involved Prince Qi, it somehow made perfect sense.","\"You continue to the capital to report this matter. This prince will go to the northern deserts to rescue him,\" Song Yu said slowly. Did this old fool think he could just shirk his duties?","He even has to clean up the mess for the useless son he himself produced.","Meanwhile, at the Northern Di military camp.","\"Why is the patrol this time some green recruit?\" The Northern Di generals roared with laughter. \"Judging by his attire, he might be from a noble family. We've hit the jackpot this time.\"","\"Release me, or our General Gu will not let this matter rest.\"","Speaking these words, Prince Qi felt utterly humiliated. To save his own skin, he not only had to conceal his identity but also refer to that fox, Gu Mingning, as 'General'!","\"You fell into our Northern Di territory yourself; we didn't snatch you.\"","One of the Northern Di generals spoke up. \"I wonder how much grain the Great Qi is willing to pay for your ransom.\"","The northern deserts lacked grain, but the Northern Di lacked it even more.","This gift of grain delivered right to their doorstep delighted the Northern Di immensely.","\"Hey, man from Great Qi, bark like a dog for us.\"","Prince Qi turned his face away, putting on an air of unyielding defiance.","\"Stubborn temper? Then cut off one of his fingers. If he still doesn't bark, keep cutting.\"","\"Woof woof—\"","A sound Prince Qi himself couldn't believe he made escaped his lips.","The laughter grew even louder. Prince Qi was humiliated and furious enough to die, but he didn't actually want to die.","Thus, by the time Song Yu and his party arrived in the northern deserts, Prince Qi had already mimicked every animal sound he knew in his lifetime.","The Northern Di people affectionately called Prince Qi... the Songbird.","......","Reuniting with long-separated family, Gu Mingning saluted and then picked up Tuan. Looking at the exhausted, sleeping child, Gu Mingning lovingly stroked Tuan's little face.","\"She looks like her mother.\"","\"Everyone says Tuan looks like eldest sister,\" Gu Mingzhu ran to Gu Mingning's side, rubbing her head against his armor. She had missed her eldest brother terribly.","Gu Mingning handed Tuan to Yu Fan, then turned to Gu Mingzhu. \"Mingzhu has grown again. Have you been listening to Father and Mingliu?\"","Gu Mingzhu nodded emphatically.","A familiar large hand landed on her head. Gu Mingzhu narrowed her eyes contentedly. She liked her eldest brother's hand, and her father's hand too.","Gu Mingning asked in detail about Gu Mingliu's health. Seeing that she was fine, he finally looked at Yu Fan, clenched his fist, and lightly punched Yu Fan's chest. \"Well done!\"","Yu Fan immediately broke into a wide grin.","No words sounded better than these.","\"Come, let me take you to see your parents. I didn't know when you'd arrive and was afraid they'd wait anxiously, so I didn't tell them in advance.\"","Yu Fan smiled and shook his head. \"Let's rescue Prince Qi first. I'll go see them after we save him. There's no rush.\"","After all, Prince Qi was a royal prince. If something happened to him in the northern deserts, it would be bad for the region.","Gu Mingning clearly understood Yu Fan's concern and nodded.","Song Yu, however, seemed to have a sudden realization. \"This prince wondered what I'd forgotten. So it was that blockhead Prince Qi.\"","The border line.","\"Go tell your general that the Crown Prince of Great Qi has arrived in the northern deserts. We heard you captured one of our northern desert civilians and demand an explanation!\"","The murderous aura emanating from Yu Fan made the Northern Di soldiers a few meters away somewhat timid. \"We didn't capture anyone.\"","\"A few days ago. Right here.\"","Song Shihuan also stood to the side. The Northern Di soldiers didn't know her identity and couldn't help but glance a few extra times at this unfamiliar young girl.","\"Are you talking about the Songbird?\"","Gu Mingning and Song Shihuan both exclaimed in unison. What Songbird?","Another, more lively Northern Di soldier spoke up excitedly. \"We didn't capture the Songbird; he fell into Northern Di himself.\"","\"To exchange for him, it'll cost a thousand dan of grain.\"","\"So expensive?\" The more experienced Gu Mingning frowned. Could it be that Prince Qi's identity had been discovered?","\"The Songbird can imitate all kinds of animal sounds—chickens, ducks, dogs, geese, you name it. Our general is especially amused by him every day,\" the Northern Di soldier glanced at the two of them.","To be honest, they all thought keeping the Songbird was more interesting.","\"If you think it's too expensive, you don't have to make the exchange.\""]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449: We're not swapping, let's fight.","paragraphs":["In the camp of the Northern Di, Prince Qi was enduring humiliation to carry out a heavy task.","At that moment, a soldier hurried in, shattering the camp's cheerful atmosphere. Seeing this, the Northern Di general Lang Qing lifted his eyelids. \"Well? How much grain is the Mo Bei willing to pay for his ransom?\"","Prince Qi's ears perked up secretly. He was, after all, a prince. That fellow Gu Mingning should know what to do, right?","But the next second, the soldier stammered, \"The Great Qi Crown Prince has arrived at Mo Bei. They said... they said...\"","\"Spit it out! What did they say?\" The deputy generals nearby lost their patience.","\"They said it's too expensive. They won't make the exchange!\"","Instantly, the entire tent fell silent. General Lang Qing of the Northern Di suddenly stood up and delivered a kick straight to Prince Qi's solar plexus.","\"In the past, even if we captured ordinary civilians, Mo Bei would exchange grain for them. But this time, they refuse. What a useless waste you are!\"","\"General, it seems the Great Qi Crown Prince is nothing special after all. Where is the famed love for his people as if they were his own children?\"","Everyone began cursing and complaining, one after another. Only Prince Qi, upon hearing that Song Yu had reached Mo Bei, revealed a look of utter despair in his eyes.","It's over.","Song Yu would probably prefer him dead in Mo Bei.","\"Go find out why the Great Qi Crown Prince has suddenly come to Mo Bei,\" Lang Qing's tone shifted. \"Also, have all the soldiers stay alert.\"","\"You worry too much, General. Great Qi just fought wars against Da Yue and the Wo Kingdom. Although they won both, their own national strength has been significantly depleted. Attacking the Northern Di now would not be wise,\" a deputy general said with a laugh. \"It's likely the Crown Prince can't swallow his pride to ransom him. If that's the case, let the 'Lark' stay with the Northern Di. He'll make a fine amusement.\"","The soldiers were all quite fond of the Lark.","Lang Qing's eyes flickered slightly, but he said nothing more.","Prince Qi's mind raced frantically. No, he had to save himself. He couldn't be the Northern Di's Lark forever!","...","Great Qi Imperial Palace.","\"Your son is a 'Lark'?\" Master Qingshan looked at Emperor Yuanyou several times before finally blurting out.","\"Your son is the Lark!\" The already irritated Emperor Yuanyou snapped back instantly.","\"I don't have a son.\"","Master Qingshan stood up and patted his backside. \"Better think carefully about how to deal with this Lark.\"","A loud thump sounded from behind. Master Qingshan quickly said to Wu Qi, \"Hurry and find some cooling remedies for your Emperor. Don't let him work himself into an illness.\"","Having said that, Master Qingshan couldn't help but laugh again.","So hilarious.","Mo Bei.","Gu Mingning still seemed somewhat hesitant. \"Your Highness, are we really not going to do anything about Prince Qi?\"","After all, he is a prince of the kingdom. Prince Qi's life might be a small matter, but if his identity is exposed someday, the damage to Great Qi's prestige would be a major issue.","\"We are going to deal with it.\"","Song Yu crossed his legs. \"We don't have that much grain to exchange. So we'll fight.\"","Wipe out the Northern Di, and the person will naturally come back.","\"Your Highness, how many elite troops do you plan to request from His Majesty?\" Hearing there was a battle to fight, Gu Zheng's eyes lit up, and even Yu Fan straightened his posture.","\"None.\"","Huh?","Facing several stunned faces, Song Yu snapped his fingers. \"Mo Bei has a permanent garrison of fifty thousand soldiers. These fifty thousand are each as fierce as tigers. That's enough.\"","\"Yes, it's enough.\"","Song Shihuan also spoke with a smile.","Once Song Shihuan spoke, Gu Zheng and Yu Fan simultaneously sighed in relief.","This left Song Yu somewhat dissatisfied.","Why did he feel his words didn't carry much authority in the ears of Gu Zheng and Yu Fan?","...","\"Your Highness, Princess, how should we proceed with our arrangements now?\"","Gu Mingning was somewhat anxious. Conquering Mo Bei was his lifelong wish.","Now that it seemed within reach, he wished he could mount his horse and charge with his spear immediately.","\"Don't rush.\"","Song Shihuan shook her head with a smile. \"Let's wait for Prince Qi to make his move first, then we'll formulate our tactics.\"","Gu Mingning grew even more anxious, scratching his head and ears. What should he do if he didn't quite understand the Princess's words?","Seeing this, Song Shihuan kindly explained, \"Prince Qi knows my father has arrived in Mo Bei. Given his petty and vindictive nature, he's certainly convinced Great Qi won't save him. Therefore, he will desperately try to save himself.\"","\"To save himself, he must create chaos within the Northern Di. The Northern Di people are brave and skilled in battle but simple-minded. Prince Qi actually has a chance of succeeding.\"","\"Let's patiently wait and see what my Third Uncle is capable of.\"","Come to think of it, if he really succeeds, we might even have to credit the Lark with an achievement!","The night was late, but the Northern Di people had no habit of sleeping early. This was the time for them to dance around the bonfire. No one paid any attention to Prince Qi.","Prince Qi was so tired he could barely keep his eyes open, yet he forced himself to stay awake.","A sound came from behind. Prince Qi took a deep breath. Success or failure hinged on this move!","\"That damned Crown Prince, how could he be unwilling to save the life of an ordinary soldier like me? How sad my old father at home must be right now.\"","\"And to think I even devised a method to deal with Lang Qing. Although Lang Qing is highly vigilant, he is also arrogant and conceited. He's surrounded by beautiful concubines. The nightly bonfire gatherings are when he's most relaxed, making it the perfect time for an assassination.\"","\"If that fails, one could secretly poison the concubines' lip rouge.\"","\"If it fails again, one could falsely claim to have spotted a ferocious beast to lure Lang Qing...\"","\"If it fails yet again...\"","Prince Qi talked until his mouth was dry. A certain deputy general who had stepped out to relieve himself listened, utterly stunned, a strange light flashing in his eyes.","\"Ah, what a pity they won't ransom me. I'll never tell Great Qi about this excellent method!\"","With that, Prince Qi scurried back into his tent, his heart pounding like thunder.","Would that deputy general directly report him and have Lang Qing kill him? This was the deputy general he had observed to be most at odds with Lang Qing.","That night, Prince Qi didn't dare close his eyes, fearing Lang Qing would burst in and kill him the next second.","But by daybreak, Prince Qi's head was still securely on his shoulders.","Prince Qi stood up, somewhat incredulous. \"Could it be... it's working?\"","\"Lark! The General wants you!\"","A familiar voice called from outside the tent. For once, Prince Qi rushed out eagerly:","\"Coming, coming!\"","...","A few days later, chaos erupted in the Northern Di.","The spies Great Qi had secretly infiltrated into the Northern Di also sent back messages.","Yes, spies had been placed after Prince Qi's capture, but they weren't wasted on a reckless rescue attempt.","\"Prince Qi's childish methods didn't lead to a successful assassination by the deputy generals, but they successfully angered Lang Qing. Now, the Northern Di commanders are all living in fear. Lang Qing has already executed quite a few deputy generals he suspected of disloyalty.\"","\"This actually worked?\" Song Yu felt somewhat disillusioned. \"Lang Qing has controlled the Northern Di for so long. How could he not have contingencies in place? Prince Qi has been a prince for many years, after all...\"","\"He didn't have any contingencies when he was a prince either.\"","Song Yu suddenly understood.","Prince Qi was like an unkillable cockroach, always managing to get back up and make another foolish move.","It turns out a rotten apple spoils the barrel wherever it goes. Even in the Northern Di, he could muddy the waters.","Impressive.","\"Alright, it's time for us to make our move.\"","Song Shihuan's face wore a smile of certain victory."]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450: Let's Appreciate the King of Qi's Wonderful Cooperation","paragraphs":["\"General, the soldiers of Da Qi have crossed the border line.\"","Lang Qing had just finished killing a deputy general. The successive betrayals had somewhat unhinged the usually arrogant Lang Qing. By his count, he had already killed nearly a third of his deputy generals.","The subordinates of these slain deputies within the army were all living in fear.","And right at this moment, Da Qi made its move.","Lang Qing wiped the blood from his longsword, his expression grave. \"Is it an attack formation?\"","Hearing Lang Qing's question, the officer shook his head. \"It doesn't seem like it. They only crossed by one meter, then retreated. Also, judging by the troop deployments, Da Qi hasn't sent any additional forces to the northern frontier.\"","Hearing this, Lang Qing felt a slight relief in his heart. Clashing with Da Qi at this time would not be a good thing.","It was then that Prince Qi raised his hand. \"I... I know Gu Mingning's military tactics, General Lang Qing. Allow me to serve you!\"","\"Then tell me, what is the meaning of Da Qi's action?\"","\"The Crown Prince has arrived at the northern frontier. He must do something to demonstrate his capability. Pay it no mind.\"","Lang Qing nodded.","It made perfect sense.","\"Alright, you are now one of the new deputy generals. You have a clever mind. Go with the others to guard the border line.\"","Upon hearing this, Prince Qi scurried off eagerly.","Behind him, Lang Qing's eyes were inscrutable. An attendant nearby spoke up, \"General, he is an outsider after all. He cannot be trusted.\"","\"This general knows. That is why I did not send him to guard the border line alone. Once battle commences, we will use him as a sacrifice. I wonder what Da Qi will think when they see an outsider guarding their border line?\"","In truth, Da Qi was overjoyed.","Prince Qi's mind had never been so sharp. Why only cross the border by one meter... Song Yu might be a fool, but his daughter was not.","After much deliberation, Prince Qi felt that the one-meter distance they had crossed was of crucial importance.","He had to cooperate with Da Qi!","Several days later, Da Qi crossed the border line again. This time, it was two meters.","Prince Qi was ordered to personally inspect that two-meter area to prevent Da Qi from setting any traps that could cause losses for the Northern Di.","Prince Qi examined it meticulously. At the same time, Song Yu and Song Shihuan were watching Prince Qi through a telescope.","\"Father, do you think Prince Qi will find what we left?\"","It was only after discovering that Prince Qi had been inexplicably sent to guard the border line that they initiated this second crossing action, leaving behind a... minuscule clue.","Da Qi was certain the Northern Di would assign dangerous tasks to Prince Qi.","\"That's hard to say. His eyesight has always been poor.\"","Song Yu pursed his lips. Nothing was surprising when it came to Prince Qi.","Prince Qi had never been so focused, not even when Emperor Yuanyou quizzed him on his studies as a child.","Just then, Prince Qi's eyes narrowed. He spotted a tiny, almost negligible patch of white—lime powder, unique to Da Qi.","Prince Qi was ecstatic!","He stepped on it, and the white instantly mixed with the soil, disappearing.","He could state with the authority of a prince: Da Qi intended to annihilate the Northern Di!","And these few meters crossed each time would be the site of a trap on the final occasion.","He was bursting to tell Song Yu that the Northern Di's internal affairs were in chaos, but he had no way to do so. He could only argue with the other deputy generals near the border line every day.","Hoping Song Yu would understand his hints.","Song Yu: ...","...","\"Is he still arguing today?\" Song Yu asked expressionlessly.","\"Yes. The arguments are all about suspecting the deputy generals of disloyalty to Lang Qing.\" Gu Mingning's mouth twitched. A prince, acting like a gossip, criticizing the deputy generals' families inside and out.","\"Cross the line again in three days, by three meters this time.\"","Song Shihuan's voice rang out. Gu Mingning promptly scurried over to Song Shihuan's side, leaving Song Yu standing alone.","It looked quite desolate.","\"This time, Lang Qing will not let it go no matter what.\"","\"When Lang Qing leads his troops to attack, we will proceed with the original plan: face the Northern Di head-on!\"","Everyone stood straight. This time, they hadn't devised many complex formations for fighting the Northern Di. What Song Shihuan chose for the frontier soldiers was a direct assault.","\"The soldiers have been guarding the northern frontier for too long, separated from their families. They must be holding in a lot of pent-up frustration. Fight directly, let that frustration out! After the fight, go home and reunite with your parents!\"","Even Gu Mingning, upon hearing Song Shihuan's words, felt an urge to immediately go kill a few hundred enemies.","Their soldiers stationed at the northern frontier... had suffered too much.","Just as Song Shihuan predicted, after this three-meter crossing, Lang Qing began mobilizing his troops.","\"Da Qi insults us too gravely! We must take the initiative and strike once ourselves!\"","Hearing Lang Qing's words, Prince Qi's heart skipped a beat.","Finally, the wait was over.","Even though the areas crossed in the first two instances had proven safe, Lang Qing, ever cautious, still ordered Prince Qi to investigate again.","Three meters. Prince Qi looked tense.","Two meters. Prince Qi's palms were already sweating. Could he have been wrong? Was there no ambush here? Did Da Qi not plan to destroy the Northern Di?","One meter...","A sharp pain shot through the sole of his foot, but Prince Qi broke into a grin.","Prince Qi took many more steps across the two- and three-meter distances before returning to the command tent. \"General, it's the same as the previous two times—no issues. Da Qi probably just wants to bolster their Crown Prince's reputation. When you lead the troops tonight and catch them by surprise, Da Qi will surely regret it deeply.\"","Lang Qing laughed heartily upon hearing this.","\"Well done, my little lark.\"","Prince Qi's lips moved slightly, but he ultimately said nothing. Leaving Lang Qing's tent, Prince Qi's face remained as pale as paper.","The sole of his foot hurt so much...","And he was no lark...","That night.","Lang Qing led all the Northern Di troops, intending to cross the border line and teach Da Qi a lesson.","But as they approached the border line, they found themselves face-to-face with the Da Qi soldiers on the other side.","\"It seems we had the same idea.\"","A bloodthirsty smile appeared on Gu Mingning's face. \"In that case, Lang Qing, let us have a satisfying, all-out battle.\"","\"Fine. I've long wanted to fight you as well.\"","Now with the two armies confronting each other, although Lang Qing sensed something amiss, he had no retreat.","The battle flags of both sides fluttered in the wind. As the war drums sounded, Lang Qing curled the corner of his mouth and raised his longsword high:","\"Before the armies engage, I, Lang Qing, will kill someone to consecrate our banners.\"","As soon as Lang Qing finished speaking, Prince Qi, bound tightly, was brought to the front of the formation.","\"Fine by us. That man is just an ordinary soldier to us. On the contrary, your Northern Di soldiers seem quite fond of him, even calling him 'the lark'.\" Gu Mingning's eyes were dark. \"But haven't you, Lang Qing, killed enough people already? Your banners must be inauspicious from all that consecration.\"","This single sentence made the Northern Di soldiers stiffen, reminding them of the many slain deputy generals.","The lark... had indeed brought them much joy.","Lang Qing realized something. The sword that should have fallen on Prince Qi's head instead struck the ropes binding him.","\"This general is not one who mistreats his men. Capture Gu Mingning alive to consecrate our banners, and I will personally reward you.\"","With a formidable enemy before them, morale could not afford the slightest damage.","Prince Qi's face was deathly pale, clearly frightened nearly to death...","I almost thought I was going to meet a heroic end just like Song Yanzheng."]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451: Fortune Favors Fools","paragraphs":["Three meters.","Two meters.","One meter...","When the Northern Di soldiers stepped into the area one meter from the border, screams instantly filled the ground.","Cavalry were thrown from their startled horses, infantry writhed in pain from their feet.","The soldiers behind, unable to stop their momentum, uncontrollably tumbled forward. In just a few breaths, the pre-buried \"ghost arrows\" took effect.","Small in size, easy to scatter quickly and hard to detect, ghost arrows were chosen by Great Qi as the key to breaking the Northern Di's morale.","In battle between two armies, the first drumbeat fuels courage, the second weakens it, and the third exhausts it.","Seeing their comrades screaming ahead, the Northern Di soldiers couldn't help but hesitate and wonder: what had Great Qi done to this one-meter strip of land?","Lang Qing finally realized what was happening and immediately moved to seize the Prince of Qi.","This \"Nightingale\" must have deceived them, conspiring with Great Qi from within!","At this critical moment, Great Qi's pre-positioned covert agents sprang into action. Archers provided covering fire with their arrows, and together they rescued the Prince of Qi to the other side of the border.","\"You actually conspired to trick the Northern Di! I, Lang Qing, vow not to be human if I don't kill you today!\"","As a Northern Di general known to devour raw flesh, Lang Qing felt he had suffered a profound humiliation.","But now, fear had begun to creep into the hearts of the Northern Di soldiers, while the Great Qi troops stood with fierce determination in their eyes, weapons in hand, eager to engage the Northern Di in a fierce and satisfying battle.","Since the campaign against Great Yue began, they had dreamed of the day they could utterly destroy the Northern Di!","To let the northern frontiers never again be harassed by the Northern Di.","\"Soldiers, for this battle, we have a reason for certain victory.\"","Song Shihuan's voice rang out. \"If we win, Great Qi's territory will expand northward for a thousand miles. You will be heroes whose achievements benefit the present and whose legacy benefits future generations!\"","\"For me, kill! Fight for a life of peace and happiness for the people of the northern frontiers!\"","\"Kill! Kill! Kill!\"","Lang Qing thought the Great Qi people were insane.","Bewitched by the words of a mere girl.","The light in these Great Qi soldiers' eyes was familiar to Lang Qing—it was the unconscious craving of a predator looking at its prey.","For the first time, Lang Qing felt threatened.","The two armies instantly clashed, soldiers falling one after another.","The Northern Di's national strength was inherently weaker than Great Qi's. It was only because the Northern Di were skilled in horseback archery, adept at fighting from the saddle, agile and hard to catch, that they had secured a place north of Great Qi.","But now...","Lang Qing discovered in despair that Great Qi had deliberately lured them across the border. On the other side of the line were countless tangled threads on the ground, easily tripping their horses and forcing them to fight on foot.","When they began to retreat, the Great Qi soldiers would cross the border line, able to advance or retreat, attack or defend at will.","The first battle between Great Qi and the Northern Di ended with the Northern Di's defeat. Lang Qing led the remnants of his forces in a rout, and Great Qi successfully pushed the border approximately thirty kilometers north.","Song Shihuan and the others headed towards the command tent.","\"Ouch, ouch—\"","A familiar cry of pain sounded. Song Shihuan paused mid-step, then forcefully changed direction. \"I just remembered I have something else to attend to...\"","Half an incense stick's time later, only Gu Mingning remained outside the tent.","Gu Mingning resigned himself with a bitter smile and entered the tent.","\"Your Highness, Prince of Qi.\"","\"General Gu, my foot... is it going to be crippled?\"","The Prince of Qi now bore no resemblance to his previously imposing self. His eyes were red and swollen from crying, his face pale with pain, sweat beading continuously on his forehead.","Gu Mingning glanced at the Prince's utterly mangled sole and felt a tremor in his heart. \"Your Highness, have you been walking normally all this time?\"","\"Of course. Otherwise, if they saw my foot was injured, your plan would have failed.\"","So he had secretly pulled out the ghost arrow and used dirt to staunch the bleeding.","Enduring the pain for an entire day.","Gu Mingning's long-accumulated resentment towards the Prince of Qi instantly dissipated. Forget it, he thought, he is, after all, a prince of Great Qi.","\"Medic, how is His Highness's foot?\"","The medic's expression was clearly grave. \"The ghost arrow was unclean. Fortunately, His Highness pulled it out promptly himself. However, due to the crude subsequent treatment, I dare not guarantee the foot can be saved. If he passes the next month without complication, it can be preserved.\"","Otherwise, if anything goes wrong during that time, the foot must be... sacrificed.","The Prince of Qi felt like crying but held back, looking at Gu Mingning. \"Can I see the Crown Prince?\"","...","A quarter of an hour later, Song Yu stood before the Prince of Qi, his face as sour as if he'd been owed a hundred taels of silver.","\"Elder Brother, wu wu wu wu.\"","As soon as the Prince of Qi spoke, Song Yu took several steps back, eyeing him warily.","What is this fool up to now?","\"Elder Brother, my foot is going to be crippled.\" With only the two of them in the tent, the Prince of Qi cried without restraint. \"Elder Brother, I know you're good to me. You went to great lengths, even planning to destroy the Northern Di, just to rescue me... so I... I couldn't hold you back.\"","\"I treated you so poorly before, yet you were still willing to save me... I really was a scoundrel before. I was too stupid to tell friend from foe.\"","Looking at the Prince of Qi, a mess of snot and tears, Song Yu twitched the corner of his mouth:","\"Quite stupid indeed.\"","He never intended to save this idiot.","Song Yu prepared to tell the Prince this harsh truth, to let him understand the dangers of the world.","But after a moment's thought, what came out of Song Yu's mouth changed: \"You are Father Emperor's son. How could I not save you?\"","The Prince of Qi cried even louder.","\"I've heard all about how you bravely patrolled the border for the people of the northern frontiers. The Northern Di soldiers also seemed quite fond of you. In the future, when we conquer the Northern Di, you will be the most suitable person to garrison there. I believe you can govern the Northern Di well, correct?\"","The Prince of Qi nodded vigorously.","He could never repay his elder brother's kindness in saving him.","Song Yu was satisfied. In the future, he could just dump this fool in the Northern Di territory, and the Northern Di problem would be solved.","After all, the Northern Di people weren't that clever either; they'd be a good match for this idiot.","\"Your foot...\"","Song Yu glanced at the Prince's foot and said leisurely, \"Who knows if it isn't a blessing in disguise?\"","Given the \"Nightingale\" identity, the old man (the Emperor) probably wanted to kill the Prince of Qi.","This foot injury would be enough to appease the old man's anger, preserve the dignity of the Great Qi royal family, and spare the Prince of Qi's life.","The Prince of Qi didn't quite understand Song Yu's words, but Song Yu had already left the tent.","\"Rest well. If you have time, read more books.\"","Outside the tent, Song Shihuan wore an indescribable expression.","\"Father, does the Prince of Qi think we launched the campaign to rescue him?\"","Song Yu paused. \"His face is quite large, and his heart is too.\"","But this misunderstanding was wonderful; it would save him a lot of effort.","Song Shihuan finally couldn't hold back a laugh.","If the Prince of Qi truly reformed in the future and guarded this Northern Di territory well, his descendants would also live comfortably.","Perhaps this was another case of \"fools have fortune\"?"]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452: I'm No Lark","paragraphs":["The capital, Zichen Hall.","Emperor Yuanyou was in a rare good mood and felt like chatting with Master Qingshan.","But when he saw Master Qingshan, Emperor Yuanyou's heart gave a frightened jolt. \"It's only been a few days. How has your complexion worsened so much?\"","Master Qingshan merely waved a hand. \"For this old body of mine, having the chance to see Ahuan again is already a great fortune. As for anything else... I seek nothing more.\"","Emperor Yuanyou fell silent. Of those who had been to the Tianshan Mountains and returned alive, only this old man before him remained.","\"Later, I'll have Mei Zhilin come to examine your pulse,\" Emperor Yuanyou said, still somewhat uneasy.","\"The Mystic Physician from the Qingyun Sect has already seen me. There's no need to trouble him.\"","The Mystic Physician of the Qingyun Sect was not only highly skilled in medicine but also proficient in fortune-telling.","Seeing this, Emperor Yuanyou did not insist further and changed the subject. \"My worthless, rebellious son has finally done one decent thing. Otherwise, I was considering not letting him keep the surname Song.\"","He handed a memorial over to Master Qingshan. After reading it, Master Qingshan smiled. \"Good. Leaving behind a brother to rule a fiefdom will prevent the Crown Prince and the Princess from being labeled cold-blooded and ruthless in the future.\"","\"You!\"","Emperor Yuanyou rolled his eyes. Couldn't this man speak a little less directly?","Master Qingshan carefully read the strategy for attacking the Northern Di written in the memorial and nodded after finishing. \"The Northern Di are finished.\"","\"I'll take that as your auspicious words.\"","\"The young lady I personally taught knows best what kind of tactics are most effective.\"","A flicker of interest passed through Emperor Yuanyou's eyes. \"What was Ahuan like... when she was little?\"","He very much wanted to know.","\"Obedient to the point of being heartbreaking, and intelligent to the point of being startling.\"","A trace of reminiscence also appeared in Master Qingshan's eyes.","\"She recognized characters at three, could discern the crux of problems at four, and had a nearly photographic memory for books she read. Emperor of Great Qi, if such a child were in your arms, you too would pour all your efforts into nurturing her.\"","That's why Master Qingshan had imparted everything he knew to her without reservation.","\"Ahuan was far more intelligent than her peers, yet she never grew arrogant because of it. Instead, she helped others within her power and was filial to her elders. She could remember every one of my habits and preferences, so no matter how much I gave her, it was never too much.\"","Emperor Yuanyou opened his mouth, wanting to say something, but swallowed his words.","Then, Master Qingshan spoke again, \"Yet it was precisely this child who, at her own birthday banquet, was despised and called a jinx by her own birth parents.\"","Afterward, Master Qingshan murmured softly, as if talking to himself:","\"You know, I've always felt I shouldn't be this calm about it.\"","Master Qingshan staggered to his feet and walked towards the hall's exit. After waking up, he had clung stubbornly to life just to see Ahuan. Now that he was sure Ahuan was safe and sound, he could feel the flow of his life ebbing away even more clearly.","That's why he had shamelessly stayed on in Great Qi.","Outside the hall, Master Qingshan saw Shen Qingping, who was waiting for an audience with Emperor Yuanyou.","\"Master Qingshan.\"","\"This old man was just thinking of looking for you.\"","Master Qingshan looked at Shen Qingping, then pulled out a small booklet from his sleeve.","\"Your constitution once suffered a depletion, affecting your lifespan. Recently, I specially wrote a set of fist techniques for you. Practice them once every day, and I guarantee you'll live to a hundred.\"","Shen Qingping rarely showed an expression of being overwhelmed by favor.","A fist technique personally written by Master Qingshan would be fiercely sought after anywhere in the world.","\"This...\" He was somewhat at a loss for how to thank Master Qingshan.","\"If you were willing to go to the Qingyun Sect, the Mystic Physician could cure your ailment with a single dose of medicine. But you refuse to go, so this old man can only do this,\" Master Qingshan said, looking at Shen Qingping with the expression of one regarding an unreliable junior.","\"Remember to practice. If there are any movements you don't understand, go ask your little disciple.\"","Watching Master Qingshan's retreating back, Shen Qingping smiled wordlessly. So it was thanks to the Princess that he had obtained this fist technique manual.","Shen Qingping carefully tucked the booklet into his chest and proceeded into Zichen Hall.","......","The Northern Frontier.","\"Princess, the Northern Di are cunning and skilled in horseback archery. Wiping them out completely won't be easy.\"","Gu Zheng gazed at the endless desert to the north, somewhat troubled.","\"We need to force them into a corner, force them out to engage our army in a frontal battle.\"","Song Shihuan spoke slowly. The reason for Great Qi's great victory in the first battle was precisely because of the frontal engagement, which curbed the Northern Di's advantages and amplified Great Qi's.","\"It seems the Princess already has a brilliant plan.\"","Yu Fan spoke with a smile, the edges of his features seeming even sharper. Fighting a victorious battle in his homeland brought Yu Fan an unprecedented sense of fulfillment.","\"Use regular troops to drive them, and surprise troops to block their retreat.\"","\"Deploy all our soldiers, spreading them out to search inch by inch. Once Northern Di traces are found, have the cavalry, traveling light, block their escape routes.\"","Gu Zheng couldn't help but stand up. \"Does the Princess intend to eliminate the Northern Di piece by piece?\"","\"Aren't the Northern Di currently fleeing in scattered pieces?\"","Song Shihuan answered his question with one of her own, making Gu Zheng's eyes suddenly brighten.","Even though what the Princess described was a familiar tactic from military texts, the way she applied it always managed to pleasantly surprise them.","\"This kind of warfare is usually a protracted one, but I want the Northern Di completely annihilated within a month.\"","\"We guarantee completion of the mission!\"","As he was leaving, Gu Mingning couldn't help but take another look at Song Shihuan.","Now he understood why his father and Yu Fan held the Princess in such high esteem, having witnessed it firsthand.","The Princess truly was like the bright moon in the sky, radiant and dazzling.","......","The soldiers, having been pent up in the Northern Frontier for years, already harbored pent-up frustration.","Now, fully deployed across the former Northern Di territory, everyone fought like madmen. Whenever they spotted traces of the Northern Di, they would find a way to eliminate them no matter what.","They weren't willing to let a single Northern Di person escape.","And so, with three days still left before the month's deadline, Gu Mingning dragged Lang Qing before Song Shihuan.","Gu Mingning had jogged the whole way and was still slightly out of breath as he came to a stop.","The young man in his early twenties had bloodstains all over his armor, and several smudges of grime on his face. He looked utterly disheveled, yet he still smiled, revealing a row of white teeth.","His raised eyebrows seemed to be seeking credit on behalf of their owner.","\"We have not failed the Princess's expectations. Lang Qing has been captured alive.\"","Lang Qing was in an even more wretched state, his thigh bandaged, clearly wounded by a weapon.","Song Shihuan stared at Lang Qing for a while.","Before she could speak, an urgent voice rang out from behind. Prince Qi was carried over on a stretcher.","\"Lang Qing, you dog! You've finally fallen into this prince's hands!\"","This prince...","Something seemed to shatter in Lang Qing's eyes.","\"Lark, weren't you just an ordinary Great Qi soldier?\"","A cowardly, ordinary soldier.","\"Bah!\"","Prince Qi was furious, forgetting all decorum as he spat several times in Lang Qing's direction.","\"This prince is no Lark!\"","\"This prince is the Prince Qi of Great Qi!\""]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453: Subduing the Northern Barbarians Once More, the Northern Desert Henceforth Pacified","paragraphs":["\"Impossible...\"","Lang Qing looked at the man before him, one foot bundled up like a pig's trotter, and shook his head repeatedly. \"Don't try to fool this general. Looking like this, how could you be a prince of Da Qi?\"","If this were a prince of Da Qi, then it would be too ridiculous.","They, the Northern Di, would be a complete joke.","They had captured a Da Qi prince alive but mistakenly thought he was just a common soldier. They had been collectively deceived, ending up in this predicament.","\"This is indeed our Prince Qi.\"","Though they were reluctant to admit it.","Hearing this, Lang Qing seemed to suffer a tremendous blow, his whole body swaying as if about to collapse.","\"Your Northern Di has few soldiers left now. I imagine it will only take a few days for our Da Qi to round you all up,\" Prince Qi said fiercely, glaring at Lang Qing. \"From then on, the Northern Di will cease to exist.\"","\"Silence!\"","\"Why should this prince be silent? Not only that, but in the future, my fiefdom will likely encompass the Northern Di lands. The place you take such pride in will soon be mine. History will record you as a defeated general.\"","Watching Prince Qi's demeanor, Song Shihuan felt that no further torture was needed for Lang Qing; Prince Qi's words were torture enough.","\"If you have any conscience left, send the signal for the remaining Northern Di soldiers to surrender. Only then can you protect your people.\"","Lang Qing looked up sharply at these words. \"You want the Northern Di to surrender? In your dreams.\"","\"Our mission as Northern Di people is to kill the people of Da Qi. As long as one of our soldiers lives, we will fight with all our might to kill your soldiers and your people.\"","Instantly, Lang Qing's head was separated from his body.","Prince Qi jumped in fright.","Even Gu Mingning was somewhat caught off guard, staring blankly at the empty scabbard at her waist.","Song Shihuan was holding Gu Mingning's sword, the blade still stained with Lang Qing's blood, faint steam rising from it in the cold air.","\"Hang Lang Qing's head up.\"","\"Ah Huan.\" Song Yu's voice suddenly rang out. He first took the sword from Song Shihuan's hand and handed it back to Gu Mingning. \"Don't be angry.\"","Song Yu patted Song Shihuan's shoulder, calming the bristling young woman down, before turning his gaze back to the pool of crimson on the ground.","\"By my command: all Northern Di soldiers are to be killed. No surrender is to be accepted.\"","\"If any Northern Di civilians resist, they are also to be killed.\"","Gu Mingning accepted the order and left.","Song Shihuan seemed somewhat deflated, her cheeks puffed out as she squatted to the side.","\"Are you angry?\"","Song Yu pinched Song Shihuan's cheek.","\"I know Father did that to protect my reputation, so you didn't let me give those orders.\"","She understood everything.","\"Silly child, I am the Crown Prince of Da Qi. Those words should come from my mouth.\"","The karma should also fall upon him.","Song Shihuan simply sat on the ground, mimicking Gu Mingning and the soldiers in the army, chewing on a blade of foxtail grass.","\"Father, did I fight well in this battle?\"","Song Yu nodded without hesitation.","\"Then will Master be satisfied?\"","Last time, during the campaign against Da Yue, her master wasn't by her side.","But this time, she knew her master would be in the capital, following every command she gave.","\"Master of Qing Shan will be very proud.\"","Song Yu finally said so.","On the vast northern plains, the princess in military attire bit down hard on the foxtail grass, a bold and unrestrained smile spreading across her face.","\"After we defeat the Northern Di and return to the capital, Father, will you help me host a formal apprenticeship banquet? Invite all the aspiring talents from across the land, okay?\"","\"I want the whole world to know that the Master of Qing Shan is my teacher.\"","So much of what she knew now originated from her master.","She wanted the world to know of this legacy.","\"Alright.\"","...","One month later, the last Northern Di soldier was pierced through the heart.","Faced with Da Qi's rare display of unwavering resolve, the Northern Di civilians could muster no will to resist, all bowing their heads in submission.","The people of the northern frontier crossed the former border for the first time.","This time, they were greeted not by fierce Northern Di warriors, but by the banners of Da Qi.","The northern frontier, which had endured centuries of raids, was finally at peace.","The army held a rare victory celebration, feasting on roasted lamb and beef, a stark contrast to the coarse bread and thin rice porridge of the past.","\"Does this mean we won't have to fight anymore from now on?\"","\"Then what will we do?\"","After a few rounds of drinks, the soldiers began to speak up one after another.","Hearing this, Gu Mingning looked at her father, only to find Gu Zheng looking at Song Shihuan.","Song Shihuan was staring absently at the fruit wine before her. After a long while, she slowly said, \"Change this to goat's milk for me.\"","Her master had said she couldn't drink fruit wine until after her coming-of-age ceremony.","Gulping down the goat's milk, she looked at the soldiers beside her.","\"His Majesty will surely make proper arrangements for everyone. Don't worry about that. You should first think about reuniting with your families.\"","At the mention of reunion, everyone's eyes lit up.","\"Lord Yu should be the first among us to reunite with his family, right?\"","\"Yes, I'll head back soon.\"","Yu Fan wore a contented smile. Hearing this, the soldiers' laughter grew even louder.","Yu Fan was very restrained today, drinking only two cups of wine.","As the victory banquet drew to a close, Yu Fan left his seat to fetch Gu Mingliu and Tuan.","\"It's improper that I haven't met them since marrying you.\"","Holding Tuan, Gu Mingliu felt somewhat apprehensive.","Hearing this, Yu Fan planted a kiss on Gu Mingliu's forehead. \"My wife endured all this for my sake. My parents understand that in their hearts.\"","\"My wife is beautiful as a flower and gentle and wise. They are happy for me that I married such a wife and will only treat you even better.\"","Yu Fan's words eased Gu Mingliu's heart a little. The family of three made their way toward a village.","The village under the night sky was not as quiet as before; children were playing and laughing on the paths outside.","With the victory over the Northern Di, the adults no longer insisted the children stay strictly indoors.","Suddenly, the children saw a tall, somewhat familiar man.","\"It's Brother Fan! Brother Fan is back!\"","\"Go tell Uncle Yu and Aunt Yu!\"","In less than half the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, heads were peeking out from every household in the village.","Yu Fan and Gu Mingliu stopped before a house and knocked on the door.","\"Your unfilial son, Yu Fan.\"","\"Your daughter-in-law, Gu Mingliu.\"","\"We kowtow to Father and Mother.\"","Uncle Yu and Aunt Yu looked at the beautiful couple before them, their eyes reddening.","\"Get up, please get up.\"","But Yu Fan did not rise. Instead, he looked up at Uncle Yu and Aunt Yu, his face already streaked with tears.","\"Father, Mother, your son has not failed your expectations. On the battlefield, I slew over a hundred enemies and protected the people of Da Qi.\"","He had become the man he had always wanted to be.","Hearing this, Aunt Yu choked back a sob as she helped Gu Mingliu up.","\"Good child, you've suffered.\"","They knew. They knew their son had repeatedly distinguished himself in battle, and they knew their daughter-in-law had risked giving birth alone and endured her postnatal confinement in grief.","\"Father, Mother, from now on, only good days lie ahead.\"","Gu Mingliu's heart settled, and she wiped the moisture from the corner of her eye."]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454: Young Master Shen Practices Boxing, Limbs Stiff and Immobile","paragraphs":["Yu Fan had thought there would be endless conversation between his father, his mother, and himself. He had even worried that his parents might neglect Gu Mingliu and had prepared himself mentally in advance.","He must steer the topic to Mingliu in time.","But...","Yu Fan looked at the two people before him, one holding Tuan and the other playing with Tuan, feeling somewhat bewildered.","This was not the scenario he had envisioned.","\"What a lovely little girl, so fair and tender, she looks just like her mother. She's clearly blessed with good fortune.\"","\"Little Tuan wants to talk to me, don't you, little Tuan?\"","The couple exchanged a glance. Well then, both of them were thoroughly ignored.","Gu Mingliu was slightly better off than Yu Fan; Aunt Yu gave Gu Mingliu the bracelet passed down through the generations of the Yu family.","As for Yu Fan... he only received a few kind words.","Indeed, the saying about grandparents doting on their grandchildren holds true.","Gu Mingliu tugged at Yu Fan's sleeve, signaling him to look outside.","Many villagers were gathered outside the courtyard, their eyes fixed intently on Yu Fan. He had left as a youth and returned a general with illustrious military achievements.","Seeing this, Yu Fan composed himself and led Gu Mingliu out of the courtyard.","\"Uncles and aunts, it was you who helped me leave the Northern Frontier back then. Today, Yu Fan returns with his wife and daughter, never forgetting your kindness. Please accept our bow.\"","With that, Yu Fan and Gu Mingliu bowed together.","In those days, the Yu family was poor. It was the entire village who pooled together the silver and grain for Yu Fan to leave the Northern Frontier.","\"Now that the Northern Di have been vanquished, everyone can sleep soundly from now on.\"","\"Well done, Fan!\"","\"We always knew that boy Yu Fan would make something of himself.\"","All the villagers were both crying and laughing.","At Gu Mingliu's signal, Yu Fan took out a heavy bag from his pack, filled with gold ingots.","It was enough for the people of the Northern Frontier to live in prosperity for decades.","\"You gathered silver for me back then. Now that I have military honors and rewards from the Emperor, I've come to repay the debt!\"","Yu Fan's voice was full of emotion:","\"At the village entrance, cooking smoke once wrapped scant silver; I now return to the villagers ten thousand taels of gold.\"","\"Every year from now on, I will come to bring you gold ingots. Please, uncles and aunts, you must accept them.\"","The village fell silent for a moment. Everyone took a few steps back, shaking their heads.","This was too valuable; they could not accept it.","\"This is Yu Fan's sincere wish. Please accept it, so your children can eat well, dress well, go to study, and build careers.\"","Gu Mingliu's voice also rang out, \"If you ever come to the capital in the future, remember to look for us. A drop of kindness deserves a fountain of repayment. You are all the benefactors of the Gu and Yu families.\"","That night.","Not a single household in the entire village could sleep.","They all stared wide-eyed at the gold ingots on their tables, afraid they might vanish the next second.","\"Husband, our village... seems to be about to prosper...\"","...","The Northern Frontier was immersed in the joy of victory. When the news of the triumph reached the capital, Emperor Yuanyou was overjoyed.","\"With the Northern Frontier pacified, only Miaojiang remains.\"","\"Miaojiang is a peculiar place. It's better left alone,\" Master Qingshan said with a smile. \"Let it follow its own course. It might even prove useful at critical times.\"","For instance, if there were some hard-to-cure illness, perhaps Miaojiang could use poison to attack poison and cure it.","\"Reasonable.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was already very satisfied. Now, almost all under heaven belonged to Great Qi. The Qingyun Realm was governed by the Qingyun Sect, all familiar faces, so naturally there would be no conflicts.","Thus, Emperor Yuanyou sighed with feeling, \"The world is finally about to settle into peace.\"","\"We should credit Ah Huan with another merit.\"","Master Qingshan quietly fought and bargained for Song Shihuan.","\"Ah Huan... I have nothing left to bestow upon her,\" Emperor Yuanyou fretted. \"I have no rare treasures left in my hands.\"","\"Well, there might be something.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was taken aback. Had this old man secretly peeked into his private treasury?","Seeing his expression, Master Qingshan's gaze turned inscrutable. \"In the future, if you or the Crown Prince wish to grant Ah Huan anything, you should first ask if Ah Huan wants it.\"","What Ah Huan wants is what is best.","\"Naturally.\"","The Shen Residence.","As soon as Shen Mingwen entered the manor, he asked the servant beside him, \"Where is your Third Master?\"","\"In the courtyard practicing boxing.\"","\"What?\"","Shen Mingwen couldn't believe his ears. His son, who had never practiced martial arts, was now practicing boxing?","This joke was not funny at all.","When Shen Mingwen arrived at Shen Qingping's courtyard, he found Lady Shen had already been secretly watching from the courtyard gate for quite some time.","A few moments later, two heads peeked out together.","They saw the usually aloof and noble Young Master Shen moving as if his limbs were uncoordinated, while Baoxia beside him frowned so hard her face scrunched up like a bun.","\"Young Master Shen, you're moving the same hand and foot together again.\"","\"Young Master Shen, your hands shouldn't be so stiff.\"","Shen Qingping had only completed half a set of the boxing routine and was already sweating profusely.","Who would believe that the ever-intelligent and wise Young Master Shen had been practicing for nearly a month and still hadn't managed to learn this set of boxing.","Young Master Shen was troubled.","Baoxia was also troubled.","The Princess had forgotten to take her to the Northern Frontier, so she ended up being tasked with teaching Young Master Shen boxing.","\"Miss Baoxia, please demonstrate it once more for me to see.\"","Shen Qingping spoke stiffly.","Baoxia nodded upon hearing this and executed a complete set of the boxing routine cleanly and efficiently, taking only the time it takes for one incense stick to burn.","When it was Shen Qingping's turn.","Right from the start, he moved the same hand and foot together again.","Baoxia facepalmed.","The two heads outside the room couldn't help but laugh out loud.","A few moments later, the two were caught and stood before their son, whose face was livid with anger.","\"Boxing is good. Learn slowly, no rush.\"","Shen Mingwen was beside himself with glee; he had finally caught his son being bad at something.","\"The boxing manual Master Qingshan gave is a good thing. Son, you must learn it.\"","Lady Shen's eyes, however, were full of concern.","\"Father, have you finished handling all your court affairs?\"","\"Mother, isn't it time to collect the earnings from your shops?\"","In other words, you both have too much free time.","The two were successfully shooed away. Only then did Shen Qingping let out an almost imperceptible sigh of relief. Embarrassing, so embarrassing.","When had he, the esteemed Young Master Shen, ever been so embarrassed?","\"Again!\"","Shen Qingping's fighting spirit remained undimmed.","But after nine more attempts, Shen Qingping's eyes grew vacant, and he began contemplating the possibility of going to the Qingshan Sect to have that strange doctor prescribe him some medicine.","In the end.","Early the next morning.","Shen Mingwen received a letter left by his son:","Going to the Northern Frontier. Back soon. Don't worry.","It was almost exactly the same as the one Emperor Yuanyou had once received.","Clearly, Young Master Shen had slipped away.","Just as Shen Mingwen and Lady Shen were at a loss, Baoxia patted her head. \"I'll use a carrier pigeon to send a message to the Princess explaining the situation. The Princess will also supervise Young Master Shen's boxing practice.\"","What's the use of slipping away?","It just means a different person will be teaching the boxing."]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455: Returning Triumphantly to the Capital and Dropping by to Visit Relatives","paragraphs":["Both Shen Qingping and the carrier pigeon had two legs, so they arrived in the Northern Desert almost simultaneously.","At that time, Song Yu and Song Shihuan were just preparing to lead the troops back to the capital.","\"How did you get here?\"","Both were extremely surprised to see Shen Qingping.","\"To pick you up,\" Shen Qingping said with a smile. Gu Mingning couldn't help but take several steps away from him. When someone who rarely smiles suddenly does, it's truly unsettling.","Song Shihuan successfully received the signal Baoxia was trying to convey, then turned a beaming smile towards Shen Qingping. \"The martial arts routine Master specially wrote for you, Teacher—I suppose you haven't been practicing it these past few days on the road?\"","The smile on Shen Qingping's face instantly froze.","Baoxia!!!","\"Here, let me show you how it's done, Teacher. Baoxia must have missed the key points.\"","Shen Qingping nodded, feeling somewhat comforted.","There's no student who can't be taught, only teachers who don't know how to teach!","Song Shihuan studied the routine for a while, then picked up a brush and began making some adjustments, changing the instructions into phrasing that sounded simpler but still described the same set of movements.","Sure enough, Shen Qingping learned it after just three repetitions.","One could say he thoroughly washed away his previous shame.","\"Teacher, you must remember to do this every day. It can help you live to a hundred.\"","Song Shihuan's expression turned serious, with a clear trace of worry visible in her eyes.","If Master personally wrote a martial arts routine for him, then Teacher's physical condition must indeed be serious enough to affect his lifespan.","\"Don't worry, Princess. Now that I've learned it, I'll practice it every day.\"","\"This prince and Ah Huan are destined for a thousand years. If you don't even make it to a hundred, it would be far too embarrassing,\" Song Yu snorted coldly, then pointed at Shen Qingping. \"Ah Huan, shouldn't he make up for the days he missed these past few days?\"","\"He should.\"","And so.","On the wide-open ground, the imposing Shen Qingping diligently practiced his martial arts routine. Having grasped the essentials, his movements became increasingly fluid, even carrying a faint hint of killing intent.","Gu Mingning, passing by: \"...\"","Even when performing an ordinary exercise routine, the great demon lord looks like he's about to kill someone!","...","In early March, the group set off to return to the capital.","On the journey back to the capital, they happened to pass through Song Yanhong's fiefdom. Song Yu and Song Shihuan exchanged a glance and decided to pay him a visit.","Having received the news, Song Yanhong stood at the city gate every day, craning his neck to look outside. Song Xiling stood beside him, her expression equally expectant.","\"Elder Brother, it's been several years since we parted. I've only heard of the Princess's deeds through rumors, and I've been longing to meet her.\"","The present-day Song Xiling was no longer the girl who lived under the shadow of the Princess of Chu. In the fiefdom, Song Yanhong never restrained her or demanded she live a certain way, giving her the confidence to grow freely.","Thus, Song Xiling's brow now carried the brightness of a young maiden.","She had begun to idolize Song Shihuan through various tales.","\"Yes, I've also been looking forward to seeing the Princess.\"","Suddenly, Song Yanhong's expression shifted. \"They're here! They're here!\"","As soon as Song Yu and Song Shihuan alighted from the carriage, they were surrounded—or more accurately, Song Shihuan was surrounded.","\"Princess, have you been well lately? I've had some excellent fruits prepared. Please try them later. If you like them, feel free to take some back to the capital.\"","\"Princess, I heard you oversaw the campaign against Great Yue, and also in the Northern Desert. You're truly amazing!\"","Song Yanhong and Song Xiling chattered away like a pair of magpies.","Song Shihuan looked at the two before her and slowly smiled.","These two seemed to be living much better than they had in the capital.","\"No need to address me so formally as 'Princess'.\"","\"Ah Huan,\" Song Yanhong ventured cautiously.","\"Elder Sister,\" Song Xiling, seeing that Song Shihuan didn't object, happily rushed over and hugged her. \"Elder Sister, I admire you so much!\"","\"Ahem—\"","Song Yu cleared his throat.","\"Uncle, you look even more dashing than before! A top scholar and the Crown Prince—it's truly unprecedented!\"","Song Yanhong delivered an extremely successful piece of flattery. Song Yu's gaze towards him changed.","\"Good lad. Come, let your uncle see how you've been managing your fiefdom!\"","Song Yu pulled Song Yanhong along as if he had made some firm resolution.","Song Yanhong, however, twisted his body, stretching his hands out longingly towards Song Shihuan.","No, he didn't want to go with Uncle.","Song Xiling laughed, clutching her stomach, then linked arms with Song Shihuan. \"Come, Elder Sister, let me show you around.\"","...","\"Xiling, why don't I see the Princess of Chu?\"","Mentioning the Princess of Chu, Song Xiling's expression didn't change in the slightest.","\"At first, Elder Brother handed all the affairs of the Chu Prince's household over to Mother. But gradually, she kept pushing for Elder Brother to marry, even finding some distant branch descendant of the Sun family from who-knows-where and forcing Elder Brother to marry her.\"","\"Elder Brother then bestowed that Sun girl from the distant branch to Mother as a personal maid, completely breaking with her.\"","Song Shihuan raised an eyebrow. Fourth Brother indeed knew how to counter the Princess of Chu.","\"Elder Brother confined Mother to the residence, forbidding her from managing household affairs or interfering in his and my marriages.\"","\"And the internal affairs of the Chu Prince's household...\"","Hearing Song Shihuan's question, Song Xiling puffed out her chest with some pride. \"I handle them all!\"","\"I manage everything in perfect order. Elder Brother often praises me.\"","\"That's wonderful,\" Song Shihuan said sincerely.","If Song Xiling had never been constrained by the Princess of Chu from the start, she would likely have lived an even better life.","\"Oh, that young lady up ahead is the eldest daughter of the Tian family. Her father is a famous calligrapher,\" Song Xiling said, winking at Song Shihuan. \"Elder Brother has taken a liking to her.\"","Following Song Xiling's gaze, the young woman resembled a noble lady from a painting, her face like a jade plate, her eyes clear and bright. With one glance, Song Shihuan could tell she was an exceptional young woman.","\"If the Tian family is also willing, send me a letter. I'll have His Majesty bestow a marriage upon Fourth Brother.\"","\"Alright.\"","Song Xiling nestled close to Song Shihuan. \"Elder Sister, what I did in the past was wrong. I apologize to you. As a princess of the imperial clan, my perspective shouldn't have been so narrow. I should live my life well and protect the people of Great Qi.\"","\"Just like Elder Sister.\"","Song Shihuan patted the back of Song Xiling's hand. \"It's all in the past.\"","Hearing this, Song Xiling sniffled. What she could do now was help her elder brother manage the fiefdom well, so His Majesty wouldn't have to worry.","\"There will be fireworks tonight, specially prepared by Elder Brother for you.\"","Song Xiling took Song Shihuan's hand and broke into a light jog. \"We need to hurry and get some snacks, or we won't have time to eat them once the fireworks start.\"","At the same time.","Sandwiched between Song Yu and Shen Qingping, Song Yanhong scribbled furiously.","Tears streamed in his heart.","Who he wanted to welcome was the sweet, gentle Princess, not these two imposing figures before him.","\"Hurry up, or you'll miss the fireworks.\"","\"Can't you even sort out these few cases?\"","The light before him was blocked. Song Yanhong looked up in despair to see Gu Mingning's impatient face.","Great. Now there were three imposing figures."]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456: Preparing for the Little Princess's Birthday","paragraphs":["Song Yu and Song Shihuan ultimately did not stay long in Song Yanhong's fiefdom.","Naturally, Song Yanhong did not dare to let these esteemed figures stay much longer either.","In just a few short days, he had received more imperial edicts than in several years in his fiefdom. Song Yanhong watched helplessly as his once deeply revered imperial grandfather's tone shifted from urgent to utterly exasperated in the messages.","It seemed the Emperor might charge over from the capital any second.","Song Yanhong hastily arranged a farewell banquet and sent off the princess he had long awaited.","Long after Song Yu, Song Shihuan, and their large entourage had departed, Song Yanhong and Song Xiling were still gazing into the distance.","\"Elder Brother, I wonder how many years it will be... until we meet again?\"","\"If you miss them, write letters.\"","Song Yanhong curled the corner of his mouth slightly. \"The lives we have now are already the best one could hope for.\"","......","The Capital.","Upon receiving the news that the main party had begun their journey back, Emperor Yuanyou finally let out a long, heavy sigh.","\"Calculating the days, they should return right at the beginning of the fifth month, just in time to celebrate Ah Huan's birthday.\"","Emperor Yuanyou smiled so widely his mustache seemed to curl upwards involuntarily. He looked at Master Qingshan. \"You haven't celebrated Ah Huan's birthday before, have you?\"","Master Qingshan nodded slowly.","Before, he hadn't known when Ah Huan's birthday was.","Now he knew she was born in the fifth month, a time of warm spring and blooming flowers.","\"Fine. This time, you shall be in charge of the preparations.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was uncharacteristically generous, perhaps feeling that Master Qingshan's health was deteriorating, or perhaps acknowledging the difficulty of the years Master Qingshan spent raising Ah Huan.","\"Very well.\"","Master Qingshan merely smiled.","On the day Song Yu and Song Shihuan arrived at the capital, Master Qingshan came early to the city gates. It was another victorious return, another familiar scene of officials gathered to welcome them.","Amidst the uniformed soldiers, there unexpectedly appeared a young girl, so fresh and tender she seemed able to be pinched to release water.","The girl nimbly dismounted her horse and sprinted towards Master Qingshan.","\"Master, how did I fare in the battle against the Northern Di?\"","Her master once said all she lacked was actual combat experience. And now?","\"Ah Huan is this old man's proudest disciple.\"","Sunlight gilded Master Qingshan's figure, and his face, for once, had a touch of healthy color.","After receiving these words from Master Qingshan, Song Shihuan's entire demeanor visibly lightened. She skipped and bounced, following Emperor Yuanyou and Master Qingshan back to the imperial palace.","On the way back to the palace.","They passed a site under construction.","\"What is being built here?\" Song Yu frowned. \"This location...\"","\"This is the princess residence I am having built for Ah Huan.\"","Song Yu's expression changed dramatically.","......","Song Shihuan was about to turn fourteen.","This age filled Song Yu with a rare feeling of bleakness and helplessness.","\"Your Highness, you haven't looked at a single memorial in half a day?\"","Shen Qingping raised an eyebrow. The number of memorials was fixed; the fewer the Crown Prince read, the more he himself had to read.","\"Shen San, next year Ah Huan will be of age for the hair-pinning ceremony.\"","Song Yu's expression was gloomy. \"Yesterday, Cheng Guang told me that in the next couple of years, we could start considering potential candidates for Ah Huan's consort.\"","Shen Qingping showed an expression of sudden understanding. No wonder Cheng Guang had taken leave today.","Considering this, Shen Qingping slowly said:","\"There are many fine young men in Great Qi. Surely there will be some the Princess likes.\"","\"Shen San!\"","\"Does Your Highness intend to forbid the Princess from choosing a consort?\" Shen Qingping shook his head. One must not force a child, or they will rebel.","This was a truth he had discerned from observing the Crown Prince since childhood.","\"No one in this world is worthy of my daughter.\"","The Crown Prince declared fiercely.","\"Your Highness is absolutely right. So, may we start reviewing the memorials now?\"","Nevertheless, Song Yu's words did make Shen Qingping take note. He summoned Yingchun and Baoxia, his expression serious:","\"In the future, as the Princess grows older, do not allow any unseemly or unsuitable young men to appear casually before her, lest they offend her.\"","\"Unseemly or unsuitable?\" Baoxia also became alert. \"Rest assured, leave it to us.\"","Seeing this, Shen Qingping nodded with satisfaction.","The Princess could not be forced.","Then, wouldn't it suffice to simply reduce the number of young men the Princess could encounter?","Shen Qingping gave a light, derisive snort. The Crown Prince was absolutely right; no one was worthy of the Princess.","......","Song Shihuan was completely unaware of Song Yu and Shen Qingping's strict guard.","Upon returning to the capital, she clung to Master Qingshan's side. Emperor Yuanyou, for once, did not fight to monopolize her time, and even Song Yu dutifully applied himself to reading memorials.","\"Master, shall I make you a bowl of almond cream?\"","Song Shihuan suddenly suggested.","\"Very well.\"","Song Shihuan took out the recipe left to her by Lady Chang. Having lived a second life, she no longer loved drinking almond cream herself, but she suddenly wanted to make some for her master to taste.","A bowl of almond cream with a rather disastrous appearance was placed before the old man. He laughed so hard he nearly lost his breath. \"Is this the recipe the late Princess Consort Ping left for you? Presumably, she intended for you to make it for your own children someday.\"","\"I insist on making it for Master to drink.\"","It was sweet, cloying, with the unique taste of almonds.","Master Qingshan looked into those almond-shaped eyes hiding a trace of sorrow and reached out to ruffle Song Shihuan's hair. \"It's delicious. It would have been even better if Ah Huan could have drunk it from the day she was born.\"","To grow up smooth and untroubled, to be a carefree little girl.","\"Then I wouldn't have met Master. That would have been a huge loss.\"","Master Qingshan only smiled, not speaking.","Song Shihuan leaned against Master Qingshan's knee, smelling the faint scent of medicine in the air.","Imperial Physician Mei said that Master's health had suddenly declined, as if something was rapidly consuming his vitality.","Mei Zhilin, renowned as a divine physician, had even suggested inviting the mysterious doctor from the Qingyun Realm to the capital.","This alone showed how tricky the situation was.","\"Ah Huan, tell this old master again about what happened after I left the capital.\"","And so, time slipped by, and Song Shihuan's birthday arrived as scheduled.","This time, it was not a grand banquet inviting all court officials as before, but a celebration only among close family and friends.","Under the expectant gazes of everyone, Song Shihuan made her graceful entrance.","Her jade pendants chimed lightly with a clear, melodious sound. Song Shihuan was dressed in a red gown with gold accents. Her figure was beginning to show the graceful curves of a young maiden, yet still retained a hint of the slenderness and lightness of a child.","Beautifully dynamic, beyond compare.","Song Yu's eyes suddenly stung, and his chest felt tight and full.","The flower bud he had so carefully nurtured had blossomed into a flower of breathtaking beauty.","\"Imperial Grandfather.\"","\"Father.\"","\"Tutor.\"","\"Mingzhu.\"","Song Shihuan addressed each in turn, then her gaze settled on Master Qingshan, her smile exceptionally bright. \"Master.\"","Her fourteenth birthday was more complete than any before.","Although the guests were few, Song Shihuan received many birthday gifts. Gu Mingzhu, in particular, sent a full fourteen gifts, as if determined to empty the Gu family estate.","Knowing what was about to happen next, Gu Mingzhu quickly picked up her charcoal pencil. She had an important mission today!","To accurately record the upcoming scene.","Emperor Yuanyou glanced at Wu Qi. Wu Qi stepped forward and announced in a loud voice:","\"May the Princess of Blessed Peace, perform the formal apprenticeship ceremony.\"","Master Qingshan was the only one present who hadn't caught on.","Song Shihuan walked to a distance of three paces from Master Qingshan. Her eyelids lowered slightly, as if in prayer.","Then.","She straightened her sleeves, bent her knees, and knelt before Master Qingshan."]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457: Critically Ill, Entanglements from a Past Life","paragraphs":["That day.","All the citizens of the capital learned that their Princess had performed a grand formal apprenticeship ceremony for the leader of the Qingyun Sect during her birthday banquet.","Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu were both witnesses.","The news spread swiftly, poised to sweep across every inch of the Great Qi's territory.","Eastern Palace.","\"So the Princess is a disciple of the Qingyun Sect Leader, no wonder she is accomplished in both literary and martial arts, leading Great Qi to victory in battle!\"","\"The Qingyun Sect Leader... that's a figure one usually only reads about in storybooks.\"","\"The Princess is truly blessed by the Bodhisattva, cherished by His Majesty and the Crown Prince, and now she has the backing of the Qingyun Sect Leader...\"","Baoxia mimicked the people's tones of admiration and awe perfectly.","The Qingyun Sect Leader also smiled.","\"Miss Baoxia, how come no one mentions me?\"","Shen Qingping sat by the stone table under the tree, fallen petals clinging to his hair, his unfathomably deep pupils now full of amusement.","\"Ahem...\" Baoxia cleared her throat, her expression turning somewhat guilty, and whispered:","\"Even Lord Shen obeys the Princess's every command, doesn't he?\"","Then her expression shifted again, exaggerating a look of terror:","\"Shh, you dare mention him so casually? Do you have a death wish?\"","It was a thoroughly vivid performance.","Shen Qingping laughed so hard his chest shook. He stood up and walked over to the Qingyun Sect Leader. \"Sect Leader, look at what my reputation has become?\"","\"You must stand up for me.\"","\"I will, I will.\"","Knowing Shen Qingping's temperament, the Qingyun Sect Leader stretched out his hand towards him.","Shen Qingping, for once, was surprisingly docile. He crouched down and placed his hand in the Sect Leader's.","Even Song Yu's eyes widened. Shen the Third had never been this respectful to his own father!","\"A person must know when to be taut and when to relax, one cannot be overly strained. This old man knows you are also an excellent child.\"","\"Sect Leader, between me and the Crown Prince, who is better?\"","\"Shen the Third, give you an inch and you'll take a mile, is that it?\"","Song Yu gritted his teeth. The old man had praised everyone one by one, but had deliberately skipped him.","He was already feeling upset and gloomy inside.","\"You are both good.\"","The Qingyun Sect Leader looked at Song Shihuan and murmured again, \"Both good.\"","...","That night, the Qingyun Sect Leader fell asleep as usual, but the next day he did not wake up. The servant who realized something was wrong ran out to call for help, his face ashen.","Outside the room, chaos ensued.","Inside, the Qingyun Sect Leader's complexion was also extremely grim, sweat continuously beading on his forehead, as if he were trapped in some kind of dream.","In the dream, he was an observer, awake yet agonized, watching scene after scene flash by like a revolving lantern.","He awoke within the Qingyun Sect, much later than in the real world, but his body recovered better than in reality.","He still immediately set out to find Ahuan. By then, Great Qi was no longer ruled by the Song family, but by the Xiao family, who had changed the reign title to Great Zhou. Song Ling had been on the throne for less than a month before being shot to death. All princes and imperial descendants with Song blood were killed.","But who sat on the throne didn't concern the Qingyun Sect Leader; he only wanted to find his Ahuan.","However, when he learned that Great Qi had once recognized a ten-year-old junzhu (princess/consort?), the Sect Leader's blood ran cold.","Most of Great Qi's important ministers had been killed. After many twists and turns, he found the now stooped Shen Mingwen.","Due to his prestige among scholars, Great Zhou had not moved against the Shen family with swords, but had exiled them to the northern deserts, where they suffered humiliation year after year.","When the Qingyun Sect Leader saw Shen Mingwen, the latter was wiping a memorial tablet in his hands, a somewhat eerie scene.","But the Sect Leader felt no fear and asked urgently:","\"What was the princess recognized by Great Qi back then like? Do you remember, Grand Tutor Shen?\"","\"I remember.\"","Shen Mingwen's face was aged, the back of his hands covered in scars, \"But I am no longer Grand Tutor.\"","The more Shen Mingwen described, the paler the Sect Leader's face became.","What happened to this princess?","Shen Mingwen was taken aback, then shook his head, \"After being taken to the Eastern Palace, there was never any news about this princess again.\"","No news... did that mean Ahuan might have been hidden well and was still alive?","The Sect Leader's despairing heart began to beat with hope again.","As he was leaving, the Sect Leader couldn't help but glance at the memorial tablet Shen Mingwen clutched and wouldn't let go of. \"Why isn't this tablet placed on an altar?\"","\"This is my youngest son's memorial tablet. How can a father make offerings to his son?\" Shen Mingwen tapped the tablet with his finger. \"He never let me rest easy since he was a boy. When I die, I'll take the tablet into my coffin. I need to keep an eye on him to feel at ease.\"","\"How did he die?\" The Sect Leader asked, immediately regretting the question as it felt impolite.","\"A moth flying into the flame.\"","The ultimate fool.","...","The Qingyun Sect Leader spent three years in Great Zhou, constantly on the move, until he found palace servants who had narrowly escaped from Great Qi and saw the celebrated policy essays written by the former Great Qi imperial grandsons.","Only then did the Sect Leader piece together the entire truth.","So his Ahuan had been cast into hell from the year of her tenth birthday.","But the people who deserved to die were already dead. He couldn't sleep night after night. The little girl he once held in his palms had been subjected to such humiliation, yet he had arrived even a step too late to take revenge.","The Qingyun Sect Leader's back seemed to bend overnight.","He could not vent his rage upon Great Zhou; the innocent people could not withstand further turmoil and war. And the bodies of those from the Great Qi imperial family had long been disposed of, their gravesites privately dealt with by the Great Zhou royal family.","Thus, the Qingyun Sect Leader returned to Qingyun territory and sought out the Mystic Physician.","You always say I have immeasurable merit.","The Mystic Physician looked up. \"You unified Qingyun territory, ended its conflicts, enforced peace between Qingyun and other nations. Even while traveling abroad to recuperate, you saved many common folk. When I say you have immeasurable merit, I am not wrong.\"","\"Then can I use the remaining years of my life in exchange for a chance to start over?\" The Qingyun Sect Leader sat on a prayer mat.","“No matter what kind of dark arts or sorcery, I am willing to try.”","The Sect Leader leaned forward slightly, grasping the Mystic Physician's hand. \"That child lost her parents at birth. She was well-behaved and sensible from a young age, never making a single mistake. She finally returned to her parents' side, only to be cruelly killed. If I can do nothing, I will die with everlasting regret.\"","This phrase, \"die with everlasting regret,\" finally made the Mystic Physician sigh.","Mystic Physician, I know everyone has their own fate, which cannot be forcibly altered. But now that this blow has fallen upon me, I cannot bear the thought of that child entering the cycle of rebirth covered in wounds.","\"Let her start over. She is clever and quick-witted; she will make good use of this opportunity.\"","The Mystic Physician handed the Qingyun Sect Leader a knife and asked:","\"If the Sect Leader achieves his heart's desire, what is your wish?\"","\"Calculating her age, she should be twenty-four this year. If I have a wish... I would like to see what Ahuan looks like at twenty-four. I miss her terribly.\"","The Mystic Physician gave a slight nod.","The Qingyun Sect Leader smiled.","He spent a day and a night instructing Qingling on sect affairs and establishing numerous rules to ensure Qingyun territory's stability for a century.","Afterwards, the Qingyun Sect Leader once again stood before the Mystic Physician.","Without the slightest hesitation, she plunged the blade into her own chest, piercing the heart.","An offering of heart's blood.","In exchange for a chance for Ahuan to start anew."]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458: It Turns Out It Wasn't God's Favor, But My Master's","paragraphs":["\"Master!\"","In the moment before death within the dream, the Qing Mountain Sect Leader seemed to hear Ah Huan's voice.","As if sensing something, a tear traced its way down the Qing Mountain Sect Leader's cheek.","\"Ah Huan, using heart's blood... a sacrifice, to exchange for a chance for you to start over...\"","\"The vengeance Master cannot personally deliver for you... you must deliver... with your own hands...\"","The scenes in the dream vanished completely, plunging the Qing Mountain Sect Leader into darkness.","In the room, Song Shihuan's eyes were bloodshot, her teeth biting her lips until they bled, her thin shoulders trembling uncontrollably.","Song Yu was also stunned, wanting to speak but his throat felt blocked, wanting to reach out and pat Song Shihuan's shoulder, yet he forcefully withdrew his hand.","The current Song Shihuan looked as if she couldn't bear even the weight of a feather.","She might collapse at any moment.","Mei Zhilin rushed in, losing his composure as he checked the Qing Mountain Sect Leader's pulse. Feeling a faint flutter, Mei Zhilin let out a heavy sigh of relief.","As long as he wasn't dead.","If this old man died just like that, I'm afraid Mei Zhilin's lifelong reputation would be ruined!","\"Your Highness, Princess, the Mystic Physician from the Qingyun Sect has arrived in the capital and will be here shortly.\"","Song Yu nodded, his mind still occupied by the Sect Leader's two faint, fragmented sentences.","He knew of the events of the past life, so he understood, and that's why he was so heartbroken.","And what about Ah Huan?","This was the first time he had seen Ah Huan like this. Ah Huan must have understood too.","After a few breaths, Song Yu raised his hand and slapped himself hard.","The noise made Song Shihuan turn her stiffened face. Seeing Song Yu's reddened cheek and tears, Song Shihuan raised her hand and numbly wiped them for him.","After wiping for a long time, Song Shihuan's hands seemed to lose all strength and dropped heavily.","\"So it wasn't the heavens favoring me, it was Master favoring me.\"","Her chance to start over was bought with her master's life.","...","The Mystic Physician from Qingyun Sect was practically dragged into the palace by Gu Mingning, like a whirlwind.","Pushing the door open, the physician saw a Crown Prince with a swollen face and a princess with tear-streaked makeup.","Resigned, the Mystic Physician sighed, took out a pre-prepared pill, and administered it to the Qing Mountain Sect Leader.","\"Will Master recover after taking this?\"","\"No.\" The Mystic Physician's reply was surprisingly gentle.","Song Shihuan couldn't hold back her tears again, wiping them futilely until her face turned red.","\"I must trouble Your Highness to personally seek out the Holy Maiden of Miaojiang to retrieve the Gu insect,\" the Mystic Physician said, then his expression changed slightly. \"You haven't, by any chance, also attacked Miaojiang, have you?\"","\"No, we have not provoked Miaojiang,\" Song Yu replied immediately.","In fact, it was the Qing Mountain Sect Leader who had proposed peaceful coexistence with Miaojiang.","\"That's good. Otherwise, if Miaojiang were to switch the life-saving Gu insect for a poisonous one, it would be over.\" The Mystic Physician was rather talkative. \"The people of Miaojiang are the most petty and hold the longest grudges. Take this letter with you as well. You must be fast. My pill can only preserve his life for one month.\"","Song Yu left without the slightest hesitation.","The dangers of Miaojiang ranked low in Song Yu's mind at that moment; his head was filled with only one thought... the Qing Mountain Sect Leader absolutely must not die.","The room was left with only Song Shihuan and the Mystic Physician as the healthy, living occupants.","The Mystic Physician watched Song Shihuan for a moment. This young girl, whom the Sect Leader treasured like the apple of his eye, seemed like a string stretched too tight, her eyes clouded with mist.","The physician instinctively felt he should comfort the girl.","\"After the Sect Leader left the capital, Princess, have you been well? Has everything gone smoothly, with peace and happiness?\"","Song Shihuan cried even harder.","No matter how well or happily she had lived, it was all given by her master.","The Mystic Physician stiffened slightly. It seemed he had said the wrong thing.","\"If I speak to Master now, can he hear me?\" Song Shihuan looked up at the physician. In that moment, the Mystic Physician finally understood why the Qing Mountain Sect Leader was so deeply concerned for this child with no blood relation.","\"Yes.\"","The Mystic Physician pressed his tongue against his teeth, telling the first lie of his life.","The man was barely hanging on; perhaps the King of Hell was already below, preparing to check his name off the ledger. What could he possibly hear?","Yet the young girl believed it.","She gathered a pile of ancient books and, from early morning, would run over to read to the Qing Mountain Sect Leader, never seeming to tire.","Every hour, she would put down the book to talk to him, recounting in minute detail how she had driven the Ping Wang Manor faction into a corner.","Listening to it made even the Mystic Physician's hair stand on end.","After finishing with Ping Wang Manor, she moved on to Heng Wang Manor, Chu Wang Manor, Qi Wang Manor...","After recounting everything, the young girl rested her face on the Qing Mountain Sect Leader's hand.","Her voice was very soft:","\"Master, I have avenged all these grievances, one by one.\"","...","\"How can the Princess's health endure this daily routine?\" Yingchun worried so much she also lost weight. The matron prepared all sorts of delicacies every day, yet Song Shihuan barely ate a few bites.","A figure in bright yellow flashed by, and everyone in the courtyard knelt down, their expressions shocked.","\"Pay me no mind.\"","Emperor Yuanyou spoke as he pushed open the door to the room. The Mystic Physician was dozing in a chair, while Song Shihuan kept vigil by the Qing Mountain Sect Leader's bedside.","Hearing the noise, Song Shihuan turned and saw Emperor Yuanyou.","He stopped her attempt to bow, and Emperor Yuanyou lovingly touched Song Shihuan's face. \"Don't be afraid. I am the Son of Heaven, protected by the true dragon. I will keep watch with Ah Huan. Even the King of Hell wouldn't dare come.\"","\"Imperial Grandfather...\"","The emperor of a nation was, at this moment, merely an old man doting on his granddaughter.","\"Sect Leader Qing Mountain has shown you immense kindness. I, too, am grateful to him.\" Emperor Yuanyou looked at the old man on the bed, whose breath was as thin as a thread. \"Your father will certainly bring back the life-saving Gu insect.\"","He knew the dangers of Miaojiang, yet he did not stop Song Yu.","Emperor Yuanyou understood better than anyone.","Without the Qing Mountain Sect Leader, there would be no Ah Huan today.","Without today's Ah Huan, there would be no Crown Prince of Great Qi today.","The cycle of cause and effect dictated that it should be Yu'er who sought the life-saving Gu insect for the Qing Mountain Sect Leader.","The month passed swiftly, and Song Shihuan's anxiety grew, often staring blankly at the Qing Mountain Sect Leader.","She asked several times a day if her father had returned.","The rainy season arrived, bringing constant drizzle.","Except for holding court, Emperor Yuanyou spent all his time accompanying Song Shihuan. Shen Qingping held off the murmurs of the court officials, working late into the night to handle difficult affairs.","Then, with only two days left until the month's deadline.","A clamor arose from outside the courtyard.","Song Shihuan sprinted outside.","There stood Song Yu, soaked through by the rain. His once meticulously groomed hair was disheveled, plastered wetly to his forehead and the nape of his neck. He looked utterly exhausted.","\"Why didn't you use an umbrella?\" Song Shihuan rushed towards Song Yu.","\"I was riding. I was afraid I'd be late.\""]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459: Be Good, Saving the Old Man Is the Priority","paragraphs":["\"Did you bring it back?\"","The Mystic Physician's tone was uncharacteristically urgent. Hearing this, Song Yu quickly retrieved a camphorwood box from his sleeve and handed it over.","The Mystic Physician took it, opened it, and saw it was the desired gu insect.","He looked up at Song Yu. \"We still need the Princess's fingertip blood.\"","\"What kind of method is this? Will it really work?\"","Song Yu couldn't help but ask.","\"It's the only method.\"","\"Can my blood be used instead?\"","The Mystic Physician gave Song Yu a look that said, 'Who do you think you are?'","Song Yu was indignant.","Who was he?","He was the Crown Prince, the princess's father!","But Song Yu ultimately fell silent, watching helplessly as the Mystic Physician led Song Shihuan into the room. His hands still ached from the earlier exertion.","\"Your Highness, you should go back and clean up first.\" It was Shen Qingping's voice.","The two equally haggard men exchanged a glance. Song Yu patted Shen Qingping's shoulder and forced a smile. \"It's fine. I'll wait right here.\"","The rain continued to patter down. Song Yu's thoughts began to drift.","He had suffered quite a bit on this trip to Miaojiang.","The Miaojiang Saintess was eccentric. Even with the Mystic Physician's letter, he had been trapped for a long time in a valley shrouded in mist, with only one winding, narrow path.","He followed the path up to the mountain peak.","As night deepened, he lost count of how many times he had fallen.","Finally, upon reaching the summit, he met the so-called Miaojiang Saintess.","But she was unwilling to give him the gu insect.","He was ordered to shed his fine robes, stand barefoot in simple clothing beside the stone statue in front of the Miaojiang sacred ground, exposed to sun, rain, and poisonous insects, with no one paying him any mind.","Just as Song Yu felt he could no longer hold on and was about to faint, he saw the Miaojiang Saintess again.","\"Do you know what you are asking for is our Miaojiang's Guardian Sacred Gu?\"","Song Yu shook his head.","\"If I give the Sacred Gu to you, within ten years, my Miaojiang may be ravaged by plague. You, as the Crown Prince of Great Qi, the future Son of Heaven, would you choose to take advantage of our weakness and destroy Miaojiang, or would you offer aid?\"","Song Yu's mind exploded with realization. Such a precious thing—what could he offer to gain the Saintess's trust?","No wonder the Mystic Physician had insisted he make this trip to Miaojiang himself.","\"I beg the Saintess to bring the Blood Gu. I, Song Yu, swear a blood oath: within ten years, I will not invade or harass Miaojiang. When necessary, I will provide aid to Miaojiang.\"","If he broke the oath, the Blood Gu would take his life.","Later, the Miaojiang Saintess gave him the Sacred Gu but did not administer the Blood Gu.","She only said, \"The debt owed to the Qingyun Sect is now repaid.\"","In that moment, Song Yu felt a sudden enlightenment: Heaven was always fair.","This life of his, where he gained a precious daughter and transformed from a dissolute prince into the Crown Prince, was exchanged for the life of the Qingyun Sect Leader.","Therefore, he should pay some price to save the Qingyun Sect Leader. Fortunately, it was only some physical suffering.","He rushed back to the capital at full speed, more certain than ever that the Qingyun Sect Leader would live.","Creak—","The door opened. Song Yu's scattered thoughts slowly gathered as he offered a smile to the person emerging.","Song Shihuan, her fingertips bandaged, walked straight to Song Yu and then gestured for him to squat down.","\"Ouch—\"","As he squatted, Song Yu cried out in pain.","......","\"Father is injured.\"","Song Shihuan held an ointment and began applying it to the bruises on Song Yu's face.","\"Minor injuries,\" Song Yu boasted bravely.","\"Teacher Shen said when you were little, aside from getting beaten by Grandfather Emperor, you would complain for a long time over the slightest injury.\" Song Shihuan said with a serious expression. \"Now you're covered in wounds, yet Father only calls them minor injuries.\"","Song Yu felt a bit embarrassed. Shen Qingping had completely sold him out.","Looking at Song Shihuan, Song Yu had much he wanted to say, but it all condensed into one sentence:","\"Be good. Saving that old man is what matters now.\"","Song Shihuan applied the ointment gently, but Song Yu still grimaced in pain.","\"Princess, please leave His Highness to Physician Mei.\"","Shen Qingping, looking at the bandage on Song Shihuan's hand, handed the Crown Prince over to Mei Zhilin without a shred of guilt.","Couldn't he see the Princess's hand was injured?","Song Yu was so angry he wanted to shake his fist at Shen Qingping, but he wilted upon seeing the dark circles under Shen Qingping's eyes. Fine, he was magnanimous.","Several heads waited in the courtyard for a long time. It wasn't until dawn the next day that the Mystic Physician finally emerged from the room.","\"I'm preparing to return to Qingyun Realm.\"","\"My master...\"","\"He'll wake up on his own in a couple of days. The old man over there can handle the rest.\" As the Mystic Physician spoke, he pointed in Mei Zhilin's direction.","Mei Zhilin stiffened his neck. You're the old man, your whole family are old men.","Everyone breathed a sigh of relief upon hearing this.","\"Mystic Physician, shall I escort you?\" Gu Mingning's voice suddenly rang out from outside.","The Mystic Physician, however, reacted as if he had seen some monstrous beast. Without even eating, he hurried to leave. \"No need. Although my nature is like the wind, I don't like the feeling of flying.\"","Gu Mingning didn't understand and could only scratch his head twice to ease the awkwardness.","\"Wonderful! Master is saved.\"","Song Shihuan clasped her hands together. The persistent drizzle also finally stopped, and the sky welcomed long-awaited sunlight.","The Qingyun Sect Leader indeed woke up two days later.","Upon waking, he held onto Song Shihuan's hand and wouldn't let go, as if afraid she would disappear the next second.","\"Master, look. I'm alive and well, and even a princess now.\"","Song Shihuan blinked at the Qingyun Sect Leader. Since his awakening, she had returned to being that happy little princess.","\"Yes, being alive is what matters.\"","The Qingyun Sect Leader spoke softly, his eyes full of affection as he looked at Song Shihuan.","Both master and disciple avoided mentioning the events of their past life.","But the Qingyun Sect Leader understood clearly that his Ah Huan had been reborn with the memories of her previous life.","A few more days passed before the Qingyun Sect Leader fully recovered, becoming the cheerful old man he was before, even able to bicker with Emperor Yuanyou.","\"It's truly good. You have no idea how worried I was during that time.\"","Emperor Yuanyou said with lingering fear. \"From now on, you can come to my palace whenever you wish. After all, we're both old now. Who knows how much time we have left? It's good to talk more often.\"","\"Don't say such inauspicious things.\"","The Qingyun Sect Leader's face was still pale, but his spirit had improved greatly. \"I intend to live at least until Ah Huan is twenty-four.\"","\"Then I shall also live until that time.\"","As they spoke, the two old men began arguing again, this time over who would live longer.","Wu Qi flicked his horsetail whisk, thinking to himself that it would be best if they both lived a hundred years.","......","Song Shihuan wrestled with her thoughts for a long time before seeking out Song Yu again.","\"Father, do you have time tonight? I'd like to talk with you.\"","She had previously hidden from her father the fact that she knew about her past life. Her master's illness had forced her true form into the open.","Whenever she thought of the slap her father had given her that day, her heart felt as if it were being squeezed, unbearably painful.","Song Yu's hand, holding a brush, paused. His agreement was straightforward and swift. \"Alright.\"","But that night.","Two cups of clear tea on the stone table grew warm, then cool, then warm again, yet Song Yu's figure was nowhere to be seen.","For the first time, Song Yu broke his promise."]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460: Finally, Song Yu Received the Best Compliment","paragraphs":["\"Princess, His Highness the Crown Prince left the palace an hour ago.\"","Upon hearing the nanny's words, Song Shihuan merely nodded.","\"Princess, shall we keep the tea warm?\" the nanny ventured to ask again. His Highness had always been at the princess's beck and call; why was he willing to make her wait so long today?","A trace of unease flickered in the nanny's eyes, unsure of what had happened.","\"Keep it warm.\"","Song Shihuan lowered her gaze. Father promised he would come.","Meanwhile, Song Yu was at the Shen residence, downing cup after cup of wine.","\"Since childhood, Your Highness has only come to the Shen residence to drown his sorrows twice: once when he was framed by the deposed Empress, and once today.\"","Under the bright moonlight, Shen Qingping's expression remained calm, having not touched a drop of wine.","In contrast, Song Yu's eyes were hazy with intoxication, his dark hair disheveled, his fingers loosely hooked around a wine cup.","\"Master Qingshan has already recovered. Why are you like this, Your Highness?\"","\"Shen Qingping, I... I'm useless...\"","Song Yu even forgot to use the royal 'We', just drinking incessantly. \"I always prided myself on protecting Ah Huan well. I was truly too foolish and naive.\"","\"At the birthday banquet that day, Ah Huan staked everything on choosing me.\"","\"It wasn't until today that I realized she has endured far more than I ever imagined.\"","Drunk, Song Yu became like a chatterbox, pulling at Shen Qingping and rambling on and on.","Song Yu felt as if he had hit a dead end.","When he realized that the Ah Huan before him was the Ah Huan with memories of her past life, he couldn't bear to look her in the eye for a moment.","He was afraid Ah Huan would find him useless.","Finally, Song Yu wiped his face. \"Shen Qingping, no wonder Master Qingshan was the only one who didn't praise me.\"","Shen Qingping looked at the drunkard before him, who kept muttering things he couldn't understand, yet the sorrow within was so palpable it made him ache in sympathy.","Shen Qingping beckoned to Nian'an and Liuxi.","\"Take His Highness the Crown Prince and toss him over to Master Qingshan.\"","Seeing that Nian'an and Liuxi hadn't yet reacted, Shen Qingping spoke again:","\"Now. Immediately.\"","And still muttering, \"No wonder Master Qingshan was the only one who didn't praise me...\"","Who understands?","Throw him over and let this drunkard ask Master Qingshan himself, to his face, why!","......","Song Yu sobered up.","Under Master Qingshan's puzzled gaze, Song Yu sobered up faster than ever before.","\"Master Qingshan...\"","Song Yu swallowed hard with difficulty.","Master Qingshan stared at Song Yu for a long moment, then placed his hand on the back of Song Yu's. Now aware of the events of the past life, Master Qingshan felt immense gratitude towards Song Yu.","\"Good child.\"","Song Yu was taken aback for a moment, then seemed to make a firm resolution.","\"Master Qingshan, I too have dreamed of the past life.\"","Song Yu recounted in detail the humiliations Ah Huan suffered in the dream of her past life. Master Qingshan listened until his eyes turned red with fury.","He spoke for a full half-hour.","Then, Master Qingshan slowly rose and actually bowed towards Song Yu.","\"Master Qingshan, I did too little. If I could have done more, protected Ah Huan more, she wouldn't have had to suffer so much.\"","\"I am useless.\"","\"You are wrong.\" Master Qingshan's eyes welled with tears. \"Do you know why Ah Huan chose you as her father in this life? She could have chosen the Prince of Chu or the Prince of Qi, yet she chose you.\"","Song Yu shook his head upon hearing this.","\"In her later world of darkness and despair, you were a rare glimpse of light.\"","Song Yu was stunned, his heart pounding like thunder.","\"Therefore, even though you were notorious, the recognized wastrel prince of all Da Qi, she was still willing to choose you. She never once thought you were useless.\"","\"This wasn't a desperate gamble, because you were her only choice.\"","Master Qingshan struggled to stand straight and addressed Song Yu solemnly:","\"Thank you.\"","It was as if a blockage had suddenly cleared within Song Yu.","Many scenes began to surface before his eyes.","When the deposed Empress and Song Ling plotted against him, the final, heavy blow of the raised board had landed on Ah Huan, who had run over to shield him.","When he recklessly confronted the Sun family, Ah Huan beat the Sun heir black and blue to get him out of trouble.","When he was impeached by the officials, Ah Huan exhausted all means to clear his name...","Song Yu's eyes grew brighter and brighter.","\"The day I arrived in the capital and met Ah Huan, she was very happy.\" Master Qingshan smiled. \"I wanted to take Ah Huan back to Qingyun Realm, but do you know what Ah Huan said?\"","\"She said, someone at the Eastern Palace is waiting for her to come home.\"","Song Yu took a few steps back and knelt before Master Qingshan.","\"In the past life, Master offered his heart's blood in sacrifice to give Ah Huan a second chance. Song Yu is endlessly grateful. If ever needed, even my head, I would give it to you without hesitation.\"","With that, he strode away amidst Master Qingshan's laughter.","Behind him, Master Qingshan coughed a few times. \"He should hurry back, or Ah Huan will grow anxious waiting.\"","......","Eastern Palace.","Song Shihuan was growing drowsy, her head nodding like a pecking chick, yet she insisted on waiting for Song Yu's arrival.","A gust of wind blew, and Song Shihuan's sinking chin came to rest in a warm, large palm.","\"Father!\"","The little girl instantly perked up, her almond-shaped eyes bright as she looked at Song Yu.","\"Ah Huan, we are father and daughter destined by fate, right?\"","Song Shihuan nodded emphatically.","\"In the past life, Master was missing, and my blood relatives discarded me like worn-out shoes. It was Father who fished me out of the lake. You and I are connected by fate.\"","Song Shihuan paused. \"Actually, today I only wanted to tell Father one thing.\"","\"Even though the lake water that day was biting cold, I am no longer afraid of lakes now.\"","Instantly, all the unease in Song Yu's heart dissipated with the wind.","Leaving behind a sweetness, three parts full.","\"What I did in the past life wasn't good enough, so now I must treat Ah Huan even better.\"","Song Yu pulled the little girl before him into an embrace. The small figure now reached his chest, completely different from the thin, frail shadow of years past.","Then, a tiny voice spoke:","\"Father, before, I didn't tell you I knew about the past life because I was afraid you would be heartbroken. Now, I can finally truly thank you for your kindness in that past life.\"","\"You are the best father in the world.\"","The three parts of sweetness became ten.","Song Yu finally understood he need not be trapped by the suffering Ah Huan endured in the past life. What he must do is ensure that in this life, Ah Huan does not suffer the slightest harm.","\"Ah Huan, I have received the best praise.\"","Song Yu breathed a heavy sigh of relief. Look forward; from now on, all days will be peaceful and happy.","\"But...\"","Song Shihuan rubbed her eyes. \"Why were you so late today, Father?\"","Song Yu's body stiffened slightly, somewhat embarrassed.","Then he saw Song Shihuan wrinkle her little nose. \"A smell of wine... Father, have you been drinking?\"","What to do?","Now, recalling his drunken antics at the Shen residence that evening, Song Yu only felt shame.","Adhering to the principle of sacrificing one's comrades rather than oneself, Song Yu spoke:","\"It's all Shen Qingping's fault. He was so willful, insisting on dragging me to drink, that's why I lost track of time.\""]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461: The Emperor Not Even a Dog Would Want the Job.","paragraphs":["\"Master, have you been under too much pressure lately, or is there something worrying you, that you dragged Father into drinking last night?\"","Early the next morning, Song Shihuan stood before Shen Qingping, who had just returned from court, her face full of concern.","Recently, the court might seem calm on the surface, but that was entirely because Shen Qingping was there holding things steady. Song Shihuan was afraid he would fall seriously ill again like he did a few years ago after letting up.","Shen Qingping lifted his eyes, the usual coolness in them replaced by confusion.","He dragged His Highness into drinking?","\"This prince thinks he's just under too much pressure.\" Seeing Shen Qingping about to open his mouth to defend himself, Song Yu, standing nearby, quickly spoke up. As he talked, he threw an arm around Shen Qingping's neck in a buddy-buddy manner, his large hand resting on Shen Qingping's shoulder.","\"Last night, he kept talking to me while drinking about all those restless people in the court lately, his tone full of grievance and sorrow. I really couldn't bear to leave him alone at the Shen residence, which is why I missed the time I promised Ah Huan.\"","Song Yu had crafted a perfect excuse to clear his own name, and he didn't forget to pinch Shen Qingping.","The hint was extremely obvious.","Shen Qingping caught on.","But he hadn't touched a drop!","Not a single drop!","After a few moments, Shen Qingping's expression shifted from astonishment to one of grievance, his eyes downcast:","\"Yes, Princess, I've been under too much pressure lately.\"","Last night, before His Highness left, he even said he would give me that glazed inkstone from his study.","Song Yu's eyes widened.","That was a rare treasure he had hunted down from the Great Yue palace!","\"Only right.\" Song Shihuan nodded repeatedly.","\"His Highness also said he would give me two of the royal estates near the capital, so I can go relax often.\"","Song Yu's teeth began to chatter.","\"Father is being very thoughtful this time.\" Song Shihuan looked at Song Yu, her eyes full of approval.","Look at her father, how generous!","\"His Highness also said...\"","\"Shen the Third, are you thirsty?\"","Song Yu was getting anxious.","\"Thank you for your concern, Your Highness. I drank too much wine last night, I'm not thirsty.\"","Shen Qingping took a step forward, causing Song Yu's arm to fall away.","Song Yu looked up to see Shen Qingping raising a brow slightly, looking at him with a faint, knowing smile.","The curses he wanted to utter rolled around in his mouth several times before finally transforming into:","\"Good that you're not thirsty.\"","......","\"I want to rest properly these next few days. His Highness will handle all the court affairs well, right?\"","By the time Song Yu heard these words, his eyes were already glazed over, his face blank with stupor.","He was starting to regret pinning the blame on Shen the Third.","And so, Song Yu was buried under the weight of court duties, unable to leave his study all day.","Cheng Guang, Zheng Fang, Ling Ming... all were affected, each one dragged to the Eastern Palace to serve as labor.","\"Hold on, isn't Young Master Shen, the esteemed Junior Tutor to the Crown Prince, just lounging at home? Is that appropriate?\"","Cheng Guang stole a moment from his busy work to catch his breath.","The Qing Shan Sect Leader's health improving was supposed to be a cause for celebration, but could someone tell him why they were so swamped?","Song Yu shot Cheng Guang a look.","\"Your Highness, my wife has just been found to be with child. I...\"","Zheng Fang's voice sounded. Song Yu put down his brush. \"That's wonderful news. Then you should return to your residence first and accompany your wife properly.\"","Zheng Fang left, expressing a thousand thanks, leaving behind an even more despairing group of people.","That night.","A group of people shuffled out of the Eastern Palace like zombies, their eyes barely moving.","This state lasted a full seven days. Finally, Song Yu couldn't take it anymore.","Carrying fine wine, he arrived at the Shen residence.","Before him, Shen Qingping looked completely at ease, leisurely arranging the white tea on the table.","\"I'll give you two more royal estates.\"","Shen Qingping lowered his head to savor the tea.","\"Four royal estates.\"","Shen Qingping remained silent.","\"Six?\"","\"Shen the Third, if you don't step down from this high horse, this prince will publicly reveal your real purpose for causing that scene at the Spring Welcome Pavilion back then...\"","Before Song Yu could finish, Shen Qingping sprang to his feet.","\"Six royal estates. Deal.\"","Song Yu snorted proudly. He had plenty of ways to handle Shen the Third.","......","Night gradually fell. The two men, dressed in plain clothes, walked along the capital's streets.","Feeling the bustle and liveliness around them, Song Yu felt more relaxed than ever before.","\"When does Your Highness plan to ascend the throne?\"","This sudden question nearly made Song Yu twist his ankle.","\"My father asks me in every possible way, every day. My ears are getting calluses.\" Shen Qingping's lips curved slightly.","\"Emperor? Even a dog wouldn't want the job.\"","Song Yu flicked his sleeves. Now that he had a daughter, he was completely content and in no hurry to ascend the throne.","Shen Qingping didn't press further, just led Song Yu forward.","\"This dilapidated temple used to house many refugees. After Your Highness found out, you issued several decrees. Now there are fewer and fewer refugees, the temple has been repaired, and incense offerings have resumed.\"","\"And over there in the north, that's the second girls' school built with funds you provided. I remember you saying then that clever little girls like the Princess shouldn't be denied an education.\"","\"And also...\"","Shen Qingping seemed to have an intimate knowledge of every place that had undergone great change due to Song Yu's efforts.","His gaze held exceptionally solemn respect as he looked at Song Yu.","Song Yu's heart trembled slightly.","\"Shen the Third, you still have the better memory.\"","He had somewhat forgotten many of these things.","Shen Qingping chuckled softly. \"As an official of the Eastern Palace and the future Prime Minister, it is only natural to commit every one of Your Highness's achievements to memory, regardless of their scale.\"","\"The common people are all grateful for Your Highness's benevolence.\"","Shen Qingping stopped walking.","Under the night sky, two similarly tall and slender figures stood facing each other, one in dark purple with gold accents, the other in plain, cool white.","\"This subject merely wishes to say that, whether Your Highness is willing to ascend the throne or not, you have already begun to carry yourself as a sovereign should.\"","He and His Highness had grown up together since childhood. No one understood better than he what His Highness needed most.","It was affirmation.","Someone called a wastrel for over twenty years needed affirmation most of all.","Song Yu's eyes shone brightly for a moment, then quickly returned to normal. His whole demeanor still held a bit of a roguish, carefree air, utterly pleased with himself:","\"Naturally.\"","\"This prince was molded from the best traits of my father and mother. With a daughter like Ah Huan and a good brother like you, I am bound to be a wise ruler in the future.\"","Song Yu strode forward, waving for Shen Qingping to follow.","Shen Qingping smiled until his eyes curved, quickly catching up.","A quarter of an hour later, the two stopped before the Spring Welcome Pavilion.","Ever since Song Yu forbade officials from entering the Spring Welcome Pavilion, its business had declined sharply. It had now begun to transform, offering only song performances without the sale of flesh.","Suddenly, Song Yu's eyes widened.","A familiar yet somewhat changed figure appeared by the railing on the second floor of the Spring Welcome Pavilion. It was Mei'er, clearly with a large belly, who had bought her freedom several years earlier.","Song Yu patted Shen Qingping, putting on an expression of pity for his good friend:","\"Shen the Third, your old flame is with child. Pity the child isn't yours.\"","A vein twitched on Shen Qingping's forehead.","Back then, he just liked listening to Mei'er sing! That's all!"]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462: Woof Woof Woof","paragraphs":["The court returned to a rare state of calm.","The territory of Da Qi had nearly encompassed all lands within a short span of two years, leaving an increasing number of vacancies in the imperial bureaucracy.","Emperor Yuanyou was somewhat troubled. Having been emperor for so many years, this was the first time he encountered a shortage of officials.","Recruitment needed to be expanded.","Zichen Palace.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Yu with an unusual fondness in his eyes. \"I intend to hold an additional imperial examination next year to select another batch of scholars to enter the court.\"","Song Yu didn't catch on at first and nodded. \"There are indeed too many vacancies in the court recently. Holding an additional examination next year is quite appropriate.\"","The next moment, he saw Emperor Yuanyou open his mouth with a smile:","\"So, for the palace examination next year, Yu'er, would you like to be the chief examiner?\"","The chief examiner for the palace examination had always been the emperor since ancient times.","\"If you ascend the throne before next year's palace examination, as the Son of Heaven selecting the top scholar, you would be choosing a new batch of scholars who are your direct disciples. A single stroke in the history books could leave your name for eternity.\"","Wu Qi, standing to the side, bent his waist even lower.","In many dynasties throughout history, it was not uncommon for fathers and sons to become enemies over the throne. Yet, here in their Da Qi, the Emperor was practically eager for the Crown Prince to don the imperial yellow robe sooner.","Extraordinary.","\"Tsk.\"","Song Yu finally understood.","But unlike before, he didn't dismiss it offhand with a careless refusal. Instead, he pondered for a moment.","The Son of Heaven selecting the top scholar... leaving a name for eternity...","It sounded very impressive!","Seeing that there was a chance, Emperor Yuanyou slowly revealed his trump card:","\"Next May, Ah Huan will have her coming-of-age ceremony. If you are the Son of Heaven, Ah Huan will be the legitimate eldest princess in name and fact.\"","\"The first legitimate eldest princess of Da Qi.\"","\"Father, your son cannot refuse anymore.\" Song Yu lowered his eyes with a light laugh. \"Allow your son to enjoy a few more months of leisure until the end of this year.\"","\"Then I shall hold on for you a few more months.\"","Emperor Yuanyou put on a considerate expression and happily settled the matter of succession with Song Yu.","After Song Yu left, Master Qingshan set down his teacup.","\"Ginger is indeed spicier when old.\"","Abdicating in favor of the Crown Prince early next year would naturally call for an additional imperial examination upon the new emperor's accession, conveniently filling the official vacancies and allowing Ah Huan to legitimately become the legitimate eldest princess at her coming-of-age ceremony.","\"I have been emperor for decades and am truly somewhat weary. Henceforth, the world should be their world.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's eyes were cloudy, his aged appearance evident.","\"All I want now is to be an old man at home, watching Ah Huan grow up bit by bit.\"","Master Qingshan suddenly sat up straight.","\"I heard that the former deposed Crown Prince's family once spoke of a prophecy about a lucky star?\"","Emperor Yuanyou nodded.","\"It is true.\"","Master Qingshan looked seriously at Emperor Yuanyou. \"Ah Huan is not just the lucky star of the Eastern Palace; she is the lucky star of Da Qi. I asked a master to calculate it. Without Ah Huan, Da Qi would have perished in its second generation.\"","Perished in the second generation...","These were words no founding emperor could bear to hear.","Yet they came from Master Qingshan's mouth, both absurd and chillingly real.","Emperor Yuanyou was stunned, his hands beneath his sleeves trembling involuntarily. \"Truly... perished in the second generation?\"","\"To be precise, the second emperor of Da Qi would have reigned for about a month.\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt as if a surge of old blood was stuck in his throat, his heart aching as if being squeezed.","Emperor Yuanyou was an intelligent man.","He knew that without Ah Huan's appearance, the one to succeed likely would not have been Yu'er.","Even now, behind the plaque in Zichen Palace, there still lay an imperial edict, placed there when he initially enfeoffed Song Ling as Crown Prince.","From the very beginning, Emperor Yuanyou had planned a peaceful and smooth life for Song Yu.","An intense wave of relief washed over Emperor Yuanyou.","\"Fortunately, fortunately Ah Huan was found and brought back.\"","Master Qingshan did not reveal any other matters, only looking towards the sky outside the hall.","The reason he spoke of this today","was because Da Qi must treat Ah Huan well.","...","\"Father, you and His Majesty have agreed that you will ascend the throne early next year?\"","Song Shihuan found it strange. This time, she didn't even need to persuade him; her father had come around on his own?","Song Yu nodded.","His peripheral vision catching Shen Qingping laughing so hard she was bent over, Song Yu suddenly realized something, the tips of his ears turning slightly red.","Then, Shen Qingping cleared her throat and imitated Song Yu's manner, saying:","\"Emperor? Not even a dog would want to be one.\"","Song Shihuan also laughed until she was out of breath.","Song Yu's face grew redder and redder, before he helplessly reached out and tapped Song Shihuan's delicate nose:","\"You ungrateful little thing.\"","That day's lunch was shared by the three of them.","\"How does Your Highness plan to spend the remaining six months of this year?\"","\"This prince wishes to travel around, to see how the common people live in various parts of Da Qi.\" Song Yu became uncharacteristically serious. \"Once I become emperor, it will be difficult for me to go out and understand the people's conditions again.\"","\"This prince must bend down and personally ask the common people in each place if they are truly content and secure, what they truly need.\"","\"This prince does not wish to be a deaf and blind emperor.\"","\"Father, I support your idea!\"","A crisp clinking of cups sounded, and Shen Qingping also raised her wine cup, clinking it with theirs.","\"Cheers.\"","Shen Qingping made all the arrangements overnight, even assigning tasks to Shen Mingwen.","She ensured that Emperor Yuanyou wouldn't be overworked to the point of illness, and that officials like Cheng Guang wouldn't be left grumbling with resentment. It was all very fair and reasonable.","Then, on a clear morning.","The three of them, dressed in clothes like ordinary commoners, secretly left the capital on horseback.","Just outside the capital, they heard the sound of hoofbeats approaching from behind.","\"Going out to have such a good time, and you didn't take me?\"","Gu Mingning wore a look of resentment, gazing accusingly at Shen Qingping.","Song Yu initially wanted to tell Gu Mingning to go back where he came from, but changed his mind upon seeing the sword at Gu Mingning's waist. Hmm... Gu Mingning wasn't entirely useless.","He could protect them in critical moments.","\"Alright then, you may follow.\" Song Yu said with an air of granting a great favor.","\"And me!\"","Another head popped out. Song Yu's eyes showed a flicker of alarm, meeting Shen Qingping's gaze. Trouble.","But Song Shihuan happily hugged Gu Mingzhu, not even asking Song Yu's opinion, and directly stated, \"Mingzhu is coming with us too.\"","And so, the party of three became a party of five.","\"This prince will lay down the unpleasant truths first.\"","\"Let's be clear, on this journey we are not young masters and ladies, but ordinary commoners. Our food and drink must be the same as the common people's.\"","As Song Yu spoke, he looked pointedly at Gu Mingzhu.","\"Also, this journey will likely take about six months. The roads will be bumpy; it will involve hardship.\"","\"Your Highness, didn't you say you'd state the unpleasant truths first? Why are you saying such nice things?\" Gu Mingzhu was somewhat puzzled. She had originally wanted to try the food common people ate, and now she could try it for six months!","What a pleasant surprise!","Song Yu looked up at the sky speechlessly.","\"Alright, alright, let's set off.\"","The tall city gates of the capital gradually grew smaller behind the five of them. Wherever they went, dust flew on the roads, yet it could not obscure the overly bright radiance emanating from the five figures.","They melted into the boundless dust and morning light outside the capital.","\"Our goal is!\" Gu Mingning held the reins, brimming with the spirited vigor of youth.","A chorus of voices followed:","\"To measure the breadth of the land!\""]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463: Edict of Abdication, Thrice Offered and Thrice Declined","paragraphs":["Six months passed in the blink of an eye.","When they stood outside the capital once more, the aura of the five companions had undergone a tremendous transformation. Even Gu Mingzhu had grown noticeably more steady.","Yet, the light in their eyes burned even brighter, radiating a dazzling brilliance.","\"Your Highness the Crown Prince, by His Majesty's decree, you and the Princess are to proceed to the Purple Palace Hall immediately.\"","Wu Qi had personally waited outside the capital. In truth, it was because Emperor Yuanyou's abdication edict was already drafted, and he was growing quite impatient within the hall.","Song Yu nodded upon hearing this.","Purple Palace Hall.","\"How was it?\" Emperor Yuanyou asked, his question seemingly out of nowhere.","\"There are still suffering people in various regions, but rest assured, Father. Your son will remember them.\"","Emperor Yuanyou studied his son, whom he hadn't seen in six months. That air of unrestrained boldness had gradually receded, replaced by a steadiness fit for a ruler overlooking the realm.","Emperor Yuanyou was satisfied.","\"What you have seen, you must change.\"","\"I have already prepared the abdication edict. In a few days, it will be New Year's Eve. I intend to announce it to the world on the first day of the new year,\" Emperor Yuanyou paused. \"Yu'er, are you ready?\"","\"I am ready.\"","Hearing this, Emperor Yuanyou no longer looked at Song Yu, but instead turned his gaze to Song Shihuan at his side.","Song Shihuan had now blossomed into even greater beauty, looking more and more like the late empress.","\"Ah Huan, tell me about the things you saw on your journey.\"","Seeing the Emperor eagerly engage his granddaughter, Song Yu pursed his lips. So, that was all the patience reserved for him?","Feeling somewhat slighted, Song Yu turned to leave the Purple Palace Hall. Just then, Emperor Yuanyou's voice sounded from behind:","\"Remember to start thinking recently about how you will confer titles upon the ministers after your ascension.\"","......","\"How to confer titles?\"","For the first time, Song Yu began to seriously consider this question. Up to now, the only thing he was certain of was appointing Shen San as Chancellor.","Shen Mingwen and Ye Shijie also needed titles, and they couldn't be treated differently, otherwise these two would surely come to blows.","Gu Zheng needed a title too, and positions had to be found for Gu Mingning and Yu Fan as well.","Then there was Cheng Guang, eloquent and persuasive. He might make a good Censor, as long as he didn't solely focus on infuriating him.","And Zheng Fang, Ling Ming...","Muttering to himself, Song Yu scribbled and doodled on paper. Even before sitting on the dragon throne, he felt a headache coming on.","Being Emperor was truly difficult.","As Emperor Yuanyou made no attempt to conceal his impending abdication, the turn of the year passed with unusual quietude. No one dared to make a rash move at such a time.","After all, the Crown Prince preparing to ascend the throne was never one to play by convention.","Thus, the New Year's Eve palace banquet that year was exceptionally subdued.","At the banquet, the seats for the Emperor and the Crown Prince remained empty for a long time, and Song Shihuan was also absent.","While the ministers waited with bated breath, the three were in the Purple Palace Hall... trying on clothes.","\"My son, your current robes aren't very becoming. I had one made for you. Try it on and see if it fits.\"","Song Yu looked at the dragon robe presented by Wu Qi, his mouth twitching.","And so, a scene later celebrated through the ages as a classic unfolded.","Two tigers sharing one mountain.","A father and son, both clad in dragon robes, stood facing each other. One was aged, the other in his prime.","Through Song Yu, Emperor Yuanyou seemed to see his own youthful, spirited self from years past.","\"It fits perfectly.\"","Tears glistened in the corners of Emperor Yuanyou's eyes. He wanted to speak with Fen'er again.","To tell Fen'er that it was their son who finally wore the dragon robe.","Wu Qi presented the crown once more.","This time, before Emperor Yuanyou could speak, Song Yu took the crown and placed it upon his head with utmost solemnity and gravity.","It was the twelve-beaded crown.","\"I beg Father to adjust the crown for your son.\"","In the past, when he wore the nine-beaded crown, he complained it obstructed his view.","Now, wearing the twelve-beaded crown, he finally understood its meaning of restraining the sovereign.","Emperor Yuanyou again extended his wrinkled hand, just as he had years ago, to adjust the crown for Song Yu.","\"Truly magnificent.\"","Emperor Yuanyou smiled radiantly. \"Worthy of my son.\"","......","On the first day of the new year, an imperial decree issued from the palace spread to the four corners of the realm with astonishing speed.","\"We, having received the Mandate of Heaven, have reigned for decades, rising early and retiring late, not daring to be negligent for a single day. Now we are aged and frail. Holding the state and the altars of soil and grain paramount, we wish to perform the act of abdication.\"","\"The Crown Prince Song Yu is benevolent, filial, wise, loves the people as his own children, and is accomplished in both civil and military arts. He is surely capable of inheriting the great lineage. We pass the throne to the Crown Prince and retire as Emperor Emeritus. Let all ministers diligently assist and together bring peace to the realm.\"","Even though he had mentally prepared himself, when Song Yu received the edict, his entire body trembled slightly.","Just yesterday, he had secretly complained to Song Shihuan that the ceremonial three refusals and three urgings were merely for show. Yet now, Song Yu found himself sprinting towards the Purple Palace Hall.","Kneeling before Emperor Yuanyou, Song Yu's tears fell uncontrollably.","\"Your son's virtue is shallow. I beg Father to rescind the decree.\"","This was the first refusal.","Clutching Emperor Yuanyou's robes, Song Yu had never felt so acutely that his father had grown old. And he did not want the old man to age.","\"Crown Prince, our resolve is firm. Henceforth, you must prioritize the state and the altars of soil and grain above all, regard the peace and happiness of the common people as your foremost duty. Do not bring disgrace upon our Song family.\"","Emperor Yuanyou reached out to wipe away Song Yu's tears, finally saying softly, \"So grown, and still crying.\"","\"Father is the Emperor of Great Qi. Only with Father here will the people's hearts be at ease.\"","This was the second refusal.","\"In the six months you were away, we received many memorials from local officials praising you extensively. The officials and the common people have already accepted you.\"","Emperor Yuanyou looked out beyond the Purple Palace Hall. The civil and military officials had all entered the palace.","A gust of wind stirred, lifting the white hair at Emperor Yuanyou's temples.","Soon, he would hand over Great Qi to his son.","\"Yu'er, being able to pass the throne to you brings me great joy.\"","Feeling the weight on his shoulders, Song Yu bowed his head to the ground, his voice trembling:","\"Your son will certainly not fail the trust placed in him by Father, nor the trust of the common people under heaven.\"","In that moment, Emperor Yuanyou seemed to see himself from years past, waiting outside the delivery chamber.","The joy of first-time fatherhood was replaced by Fen'er's cries of pain. Clutching a long sword, he paced anxiously in the courtyard, his heart pleading incessantly for the ancestors' protection.","Mei Zhilin was also sweating profusely from nervousness. All the generals waiting outside the courtyard stood rigidly. For everyone present then, this birth represented immense hope.","They waited an entire night.","At the break of dawn, a clear, loud cry rang out. The midwife announced loudly that it was the joy of a \"jade\" (a son).","The generals outside the courtyard immediately erupted in cheers. Inside, he somewhat clumsily opened his arms and, with the midwife's help, held the tiny person in the swaddling clothes close.","\"'Vast as the heavens, if virtue enriches the person, it will not abandon the king's command.'\"","\"Let his name be Yu.\""]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464: She Actually Turned Her Playboy Father into an Emperor","paragraphs":["The abdication ceremony was held in the Fengxian Hall.","Civil and military officials stood solemnly within the hall, where two thrones were set up, the eastern one for the Retired Emperor and the western one for the Emperor.","Emperor Yuanyou entered the hall slowly with Song Yu, and all the officials knelt in salute.","Shen Qingping only caught a glimpse of the hem of Song Yu's robe.","Amidst the solemn and dignified ceremonial music, Wu Qi presented the imperial jade seal, symbolizing imperial authority, to Emperor Yuanyou.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Yu, who also slowly knelt down.","The jade seal was transferred and finally placed into Song Yu's hands.","Song Yu looked up at Emperor Yuanyou and saw a face full of smiles.","\"Please ascend the throne, Your Majesty.\"","The voice of the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial rang out, followed by the resounding crack of whips outside the hall.","\"Please ascend the throne, Your Majesty.\"","The cries of the officials came in waves, like the urgent thunderclaps of a summer storm.","Under the gaze of all the officials, Song Yu sat upon the throne that symbolized the identity of the Emperor.","\"Kowtow—\"","The officials uniformly dropped to both knees, placed their hu tablets at their waists, bowed forward, touched their foreheads to the ground, and held the position for a moment.","\"Rise—\"","After three rounds of kowtows, they performed the grand ceremony of five bows and three kowtows to the newly ascended Song Yu.","\"Long live the Emperor!\"","\"Long live the Emperor!\"","\"Long live the Emperor!\"","Three cries of \"Long live\" rose wave upon wave, pushing the entire abdication ceremony to its climax.","\"All ministers may rise.\"","Song Yu sat upright on the dragon throne. Dressed in imperial robes, his handsome features and commanding presence made it difficult to look directly at him, and the twelve-beaded crown on his head added to his majesty.","Outside the hall.","The officials' mountain-shaking cries of \"Long live\" clearly reached Song Shihuan's ears.","\"Your Highness, the Emperor has ascended the throne.\"","At Yingchun's voice, Song Shihuan realized she had been somewhat lost in thought.","Had she... really managed to nurture her playboy father into an emperor?","Her initial hope for her father to become a dragon—to achieve greatness—had actually come true.","...","Song Yu's accession edict was proclaimed during his first morning court audience after ascending the throne.","\"I reverently receive the great mandate, inheriting the favor of Heaven and Earth, following the instructions of my late imperial father, and hereby change the reign era to Zhaowu.\"","\"I honor my late imperial father as the Sagely and Virtuous Retired Emperor, and posthumously honor my late mother as the Zhaoyuan Empress Dowager.\"","\"My only daughter, Princess Fu'an, is elevated to Princess Chang Fu'an (Eldest Princess Fu'an) and is granted residence in Ming'an Palace.\"","\"I appoint Shen Mingwen and Ye Shijie as Imperial Tutors.\"","\"I appoint Shen Qingping as Chancellor.\"","\"I appoint Gu Zheng as a General of the Second Rank, and his son, Gu Mingning, as a Brigade Commander of the Third Rank.\"","\"...\"","\"A special additional imperial examination is granted to broadly open the path for the virtuous. This is proclaimed within and without, so that all may know.\"","This day's morning court lasted longer than usual, yet everyone was fully alert.","The first year of the Zhaowu era had officially arrived.","After court adjourned.","Shen Qingping was immediately surrounded. Such a young Chancellor—who wouldn't want to step forward and make their presence known?","Even Cheng Guang wore a sour expression. \"Congratulations, Chancellor.\"","\"Imperial Censor Cheng, congratulations to you as well.\"","Cheng Guang nearly gritted his teeth to pieces.","Zheng Fang and Ling Ming were assigned to the Ministry of Revenue and the Ministry of War respectively, and Feng Kuizhi was assigned to the Dali Temple, all holding crucial positions.","\"Chancellor, should we go pay our respects to His Majesty separately?\"","Hearing this, Shen Qingping raised an eyebrow. \"If you go to the Zichen Hall now, you likely won't find His Majesty.\"","He would bet his head that the Emperor had gone straight to Ming'an Palace after court.","Hearing this, the crowd dispersed on their own. Only then did Shen Qingping notice Shen Mingwen, who had been silently watching him.","Shen Qingping straightened his official robes. The first-rank robes worn by him carried a unique elegance.","\"Apologies, but your son's official rank is now too high. You can't scold me so freely anymore in the future, old man.\"","Seeing this, Shen Mingwen rolled his eyes at Shen Qingping. \"Hurry back to the residence.\"","\"What's the rush?\"","\"To pay respects to our ancestors!\"","Throughout the entire morning court, Shen Mingwen's heart had been fluttering uncontrollably. It wasn't until he heard the edict appointing the Chancellor that he finally felt completely at ease.","His Shen family had truly produced a Chancellor.","\"Be a worthy Chancellor,\" Shen Mingwen said.","\"I'm afraid I'll have to disappoint you there, old man. I'll probably be secretly cursed by all the officials.\"","The corners of Shen Qingping's eyes reddened slightly. \"Don't worry, I'm no longer that playboy young master from back then either.\"","...","Ming'an Palace.","\"Ahuan—\"","A gust of wind passed, and Song Yu, dressed in bright yellow, sprawled inelegantly across a lounge chair. Baoxia hurried to pour tea for him.","\"Attending court is so exhausting.\"","The grand ambitions before accession had only lasted through one morning audience.","\"Liuxi, come quickly and massage your emperor-father's shoulders.\"","Song Shihuan looked at Song Yu's appearance and felt like laughing. She tried hard to hold it back, but failed.","\"Father, how does it feel to be emperor?\"","Song Shihuan was somewhat curious.","\"One word: tired.\" Song Yu waved a hand at Song Shihuan.","No wonder that old man had been so insistent on him succeeding, even writing in the edict about being aged and frail—he must have been unable to bear the hardships of being emperor anymore.","\"Is it more tiring than cricket fighting? More tiring than cockfighting? More tiring than listening to operas?\"","Song Yu's movements stiffened. Some past embarrassments were better left unmentioned.","\"Back then, after the birthday banquet when I arrived at the Prince of Qin's mansion, I didn't see a trace of you for several days in a row.\" Song Shihuan propped her head in her hands. \"Whenever I asked the steward, he said you had gone out to listen to operas, with that equally famous Third Master Shen.\"","\"At that time, the matron took me around the Prince of Qin's mansion. The study was overgrown with weeds, and the fighting cocks you raised kept crowing at me. I thought then that I must stew and eat those cocks.\"","And indeed, they didn't live much longer.","\"You must have been terribly heartbroken back then, right?\"","Song Yu immediately shook his head, utterly sincere.","He hadn't been heartbroken at all. Really.","\"Back then, did Ahuán feel that choosing me as a father was particularly unfortunate?\"","Hearing this, Song Shihuan laughed like a kitten who had successfully stolen a treat. She leaned close to Song Yu and whispered:","\"It wasn't all that unfortunate, because I soon discovered a big secret.\"","\"What secret?\" Song Yu also grew curious.","\"You, Father... enjoyed immense imperial favor.\"","Song Shihuan recalled. At that time, her imperial grandfather and father still had estrangement between them. While she and her father were recuperating in the side hall of Zichen Hall, she noticed her imperial grandfather sneaking to the side hall several times a day. He wouldn't go in, just secretly watched from outside.","\"And then I began a grand plan!\"","Looking at Song Shihuan's delicate little face, smiling with pride.","Song Yu suddenly had an epiphany. \"This grand plan of yours... has it already been realized?\"","Song Shihuan nodded, even her hair strands seeming to perk up with joy.","Not only realized, but realized perfectly.","\"Then Ahuán's plan couldn't possibly be...\"","\"Hoping Father becomes a dragon!\"","Song Shihuan and Song Yu said in unison, then looked at each other and laughed until they bent over.","\"So it turns out I should have appointed Ahuán as my Imperial Tutor!\"","Song Yu ruffled Song Shihuan's head, his eyes filled with gentle warmth:","\"Thank you, Ahuán, for not giving up on this truly worthy playboy.\"","Song Shihuan happily squinted her eyes, her smile nearly reaching the back of her ears, putting on a tsundere look as if it were a piece of cake.","\"Relax, it's just a playboy. A little nurturing fixes that right up!\""]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465: Tear Up Those Exam Candidates' Umbrellas","paragraphs":["The first thing Song Yu regretted after ascending the throne was feeling he had been too impulsive; after the ritual three refusals and three urgings, he simply shouldn't have accepted in the end.","Because being emperor meant virtually no rest time; it was utterly inhumane.","Song Yu somewhat admired those emperors with three thousand beauties in the harem and countless children.","To be as tired as a dog during the day and still be energetic and vigorous at night was truly not easy.","The old man, having fathered the four of them, also had it quite tough.","The second thing he regretted was appointing Cheng Guang, that gossipmonger, to a position perfectly suited for him.","For an entire morning court session.","Cheng Guang, with his indiscriminately attacking mouth, had berated almost everyone present in the hall, from major issues like an official's risk of corruption to minor ones like another official favoring a concubine over his wife, tarnishing the image of Da Qi's officials.","Song Yu's headache grew worse.","What to do when an official is too competent?","Just as Song Yu was pondering how to make Cheng Guang shut up, he saw Cheng Guang jump out again. \"Your Majesty, this subject has one more thing to say, though I'm not sure if I should.\"","\"Speak.\"","Song Yu spoke through gritted teeth. If he weren't the emperor now, he would definitely stuff a rag into Cheng Guang's mouth. Unfortunately, he was precisely the emperor.","\"Your speed in handling court affairs is somewhat slower compared to the Retired Emperor. To stabilize the court, please devote more time daily to state affairs.\"","Song Yu was so angry he felt his nose might twist.","His only completely relaxed time now was when he slept. Yesterday, he couldn't even squeeze out time to visit Ahuan.","Wasn't Cheng Guang's meaning blatantly telling him to sleep less and work more?","\"We will improve.\"","Song Yu forced a smile that didn't reach his eyes.","Cheng Guang was satisfied. A censor, after all, must dare to impeach.","His fox-like eyes continued to scan the hundred officials, finally settling on Shen Qingping's face, which wore a faint, ambiguous smile.","Cheng Guang shuddered and fell silent.","Goodness, he always felt the Prime Minister wanted to do him in.","With his ears finally clear, Song Yu rushed to Ming'an Palace right after court adjourned, only to be met with an empty palace.","\"Where is the Princess?\"","\"Replying to Your Majesty, the Retired Emperor sent someone early this morning to fetch the Princess.\"","Song Yu, filled with grievance, charged into the Tai Chi Palace where Emperor Yuanyou was spending his retirement years.","In the courtyard of Tai Chi Palace, Emperor Yuanyou was playing chess with Song Shihuan. The grandfather and granddaughter were chatting and laughing, the scene looking warm and harmonious.","A world of difference from Song Yu's own predicament.","\"Why are you here?\"","Emperor Yuanyou lifted his eyelids slightly. \"You've just finished morning court at this hour. You should be in the Purple Imperial Hall receiving important ministers.\"","\"No important ministers, just a gossipmonger.\"","\"Father, do you think it's possible... for me to abdicate and return the throne to you?\"","The next second, what greeted Song Yu was the familiar sole of a shoe.","\"You treasonous scoundrel! Do you want your old man to go down in history? As the first founding emperor whose offered throne was returned?\"","\"If you dare harbor such thoughts, I'll have to beat this shoe sole to pieces today!\"","And so, the already aggrieved Emperor Zhaowu received another beating.","\"Unless you find your heir, you'll have to sit on that dragon throne until you die.\"","Emperor Yuanyou glanced at Song Yu and threw down the now-tattered shoe sole.","\"Father, does it hurt?\"","Song Shihuan, after all, felt sorry for Song Yu and hurriedly asked.","Seeing this, Emperor Yuanyou snorted coldly. \"It's lonely at the top. Being emperor is always like this.\"","Song Yu grimaced in pain, his mind filled with Emperor Yuanyou's words, \"find your heir.\"","Just then, Song Shihuan's face loomed close before him. Song Yu's eyes rolled thoughtfully.","He left cheerfully.","\"Weirdo.\"","Emperor Yuanyou muttered. \"Ahuan, ignore him. Let's continue, just us grandfather and granddaughter.\"","......","Time flew by.","The specially added imperial examination commenced in February, with Song Yu directly appointing Ye Shijie as the chief examiner.","Shen Residence.","\"My son, why didn't His Majesty let me be the chief examiner?\"","Shen Mingwen's face was full of anxiety, fearing Ye Shijie might gain more imperial favor than himself.","Upon hearing this, Shen Qingping finished the congee before him with an unchanged expression, then meticulously wiped his mouth.","\"Could you share your opinion on this?\"","Shen Mingwen anxiously urged again.","\"Because His Majesty has been through the rain, he wants to tear up the umbrellas of those candidates.\"","Father, rest assured. His Majesty specifically chose Ye Shijie for his eccentric and peculiar exam questions.","Shen Mingwen gasped, his mouth forming a perfect 'O'.","Was he really a step behind Ye Shijie because his questions weren't perverse enough?","At the same time, in the Purple Imperial Hall.","The hall's new master, Song Yu, looked at the exam questions set by Ye Shijie before him and nodded with satisfaction.","“Only questions like these can screen and select the true pillars of talent for us.”","Otherwise, why were the questions difficult when he took the exam, but became easier for others?","That wouldn't be fair.","On the day the exam began, Song Yu specifically instructed Liuxi, \"After the exam ends, send someone to check the expressions of the candidates outside the examination hall.\"","\"Your servant will arrange it immediately.\"","The Emperor is truly childish.","Having satisfied his mischievous interest in these matters, Song Yu found rare patience in handling court affairs.","Upon hearing that all the candidates looked terrible, Song Yu showed an expression that said, 'Just as expected.'","See, Ye Shijie's questions are perverse.","By the time of the palace examination, Song Yu had already become proficient in handling court affairs.","The imperial aura around him had also grown stronger.","On the day of the palace examination, Song Yu watched with great interest as the candidates in the hall picked up their brushes to answer, and slowly stood up.","He would stand before one candidate for a moment, then scurry to another, pretending to look at their examination paper, keeping himself extremely busy.","Two candidates failed regrettably due to improper conduct before the throne.","After the palace examination concluded, Shen Qingping looked helpless.","\"Your Majesty was busier today than the answering candidates.\"","This was our path to get here. We merely let them experience it too,\" Song Yu declared with full confidence. \"Besides, during our palace examination, the old man also scared one candidate into failing.\"","Having said that, Song Yu slumped onto the table.","\"If Imperial Censor Cheng Guang saw Your Majesty like this, he could talk about it for a quarter of an hour during tomorrow's morning court.\"","\"Him? Let's not mention him.\"","Song Yu rolled his eyes exaggeratedly. \"There are a few promising candidates from this palace examination. Remember to keep an eye on them; they'll be the new labor force.\"","Shen Qingping nodded.","During this period, Song Yu had been greatly tormented, and Shen Qingping, the newly appointed Prime Minister, was the same. Both had lost a significant amount of weight.","Comrades in misery.","\"By the way,\" Shen Qingping suddenly spoke, \"According to ritual regulations, there is a selection of consorts every three years. The Ministry of Rites will likely bring this up soon. Your Majesty should be mentally prepared in advance.\"","\"Help.\"","Song Yu didn't even have the strength to lift his hand now.","His daily sleep time was already less than three shichen (six hours).","\"If the Minister of Rites dares to bring it up, We will ask him if he wants Us to die young.\"","Song Yu sneered."]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466: The Emperor Is Too Rebellious, What Should We Do","paragraphs":["Song Yu circled the name of the new top scholar with a vermilion brush.","While circling the name, Song Yu suddenly chuckled.","To think that he, the previous top scholar, was now using the imperial vermilion brush to personally designate the new one.","Perhaps because Song Yu had also climbed his way up from the county-level examinations step by step, he understood all too well the hardships one must endure to become the top scholar.","\"Congratulations.\"","Song Yu softly uttered a word of congratulations to the name on the imperial decree.","\"Your Majesty, Lord Zheng, Lord Ling, and Lord Feng request an audience outside.\"","\"I was just thinking of seeing them.\"","Song Yu laughed, \"Bring wine. Today, I shall drink heartily with these three.\"","When the drinking reached its peak, Zheng Fang giggled foolishly, \"Who would have thought the person who once called us brothers would turn out to be the emperor.\"","\"Indeed, these past two years, I've nearly worn the soil flat in front of my Ling family ancestral graves from kowtowing in gratitude,\" Ling Ming chimed in. \"Such incredible fortune actually landed on me.\"","Song Yu pointed at Zheng Fang, \"How's your eldest daughter doing?\"","Hearing this, Zheng Fang grinned even more foolishly, \"All she does is eat and sleep, plump and fair, just like my wife.\"","\"What a sight.\"","Song Yu simply couldn't bear to look. Back when he wanted to arrange a marriage for Zheng Fang, this fellow was initially unwilling.","\"Then I must hurry and have my wife bear a son, so we can become in-laws in the future.\"","As soon as Ling Ming finished speaking, Zheng Fang's face instantly darkened.","Watching Zheng Fang verbally attack Ling Ming at every turn, Song Yu kept nodding in agreement. No father feels comfortable when someone sets their sights on his daughter.","He understood that perfectly well.","\"Recently, the Ministry of Rites has been talking about the emptiness of Your Majesty's harem.\"","Feng Kuizhi cheerfully spoke up. He was now the Chief Minister of the Court of Judicial Review, and his wife had become the first female coroner ever appointed in the court's history.","The couple was in perfect harmony, extremely happy.","\"Let them talk.\"","Song Yu drank another cup of wine, \"After all, it's not as if I have no heir.\"","Seeing this, Feng Kuizhi understood. It seemed the officials in the Ministry of Rites were about to face some hardship.","......","Tai Chi Palace.","\"Ahuan, your imperial father is heading for big trouble.\"","Song Shihuan was taken aback. The words somehow carried a feeling of... schadenfreude.","\"What happened?\"","Song Shihuan's life recently had been one of extreme leisure. She either spent time at Tai Chi Palace keeping Emperor Yuanyou company, accompanied the Qing Sect Leader on tours around the capital, or visited the Gu residence to see A'Tuan and Gu Mingzhu.","Her complexion had even improved compared to before.","\"The Ministry of Rites is recently plotting matters of selecting consorts.\"","Emperor Yuanyou snorted like a fighting cock, \"In the past, he wasn't the emperor, so his refusals couldn't be faulted too much. But being the emperor is different. Selecting consorts every three years is a rule followed by all previous dynasties!\"","\"Selecting consorts for an emperor is the most troublesome, requiring a balance of interests among various noble families. The slightest misstep could throw both the court and the harem into chaos.\"","Emperor Yuanyou spoke while shaking his head. If one ignored the gleeful look in his eyes, he appeared like a father truly concerned for his son.","Hearing this, Song Shihuan also felt a pang of anxiety for Song Yu. \"However, I haven't heard Imperial Father mention anything about selecting consorts recently.\"","\"That's because he's embarrassed to admit he's being constrained by court officials and ritual regulations.\"","Emperor Yuanyou, convinced he understood Song Yu well, waited cheerfully to see Song Yu besieged by the courtiers. After all, he had been besieged himself!","This kid needed to experience it too.","After the palace announcement ceremony for the new scholars, the courtiers from the Ministry of Rites finally found an opportunity to bring up the selection of consorts.","During the morning court.","\"What? The wind is too loud, I didn't hear clearly.\"","Yet the palace doors were closed, with no trace of wind.","The officials from the Ministry of Rites instantly turned pale, then flushed. Gathering their courage, they spoke again, \"We implore Your Majesty to commence the selection of consorts in accordance with ritual regulations.\"","\"What ritual regulations? Are they rules set by my Song ancestors?\"","The officials' legs went weak, and they knelt on the ground, \"Your Majesty, they are... the regulations of previous dynasties.\"","\"I am the emperor of Great Qi. Why should I follow the rules of previous dynasties?\"","Song Yu curled his lips into a slight smile, \"As far as I know, the Grand Emperor did not hold selections every three years in his later years either. Therefore, I need not follow this tiresome rule.\"","\"I will select consorts whenever I please.\"","\"You'd be better off using your energy to maintain clean conduct yourselves, so Cheng Guang doesn't seize your faults and bother me about them in court. Stop obsessing over the affairs of my harem. Broaden your horizons.\"","With that, Song Yu calmly departed.","He left behind courtiers with stunned expressions and Cheng Guang, whose face had darkened.","The Emperor actually found him bothersome!","The sky was falling.","Tai Chi Palace.","\"What? That scoundrel actually used me as a shield?\"","Emperor Yuanyou was furious, nearly overturning the Go board.","\"I stopped selections because I was old and it was no longer appropriate. How can he be compared to me?\" Emperor Yuanyou felt it was unfair. Why was it that when he was in power, the courtiers wouldn't easily let him off, but when it came to this scoundrel, they couldn't muster a sound?","And they just let that scoundrel slip away so easily?","\"Grand Emperor, Imperial Physician Mei instructed that you must not stir up great anger.\"","Wu Qi felt utterly helpless. Were they really comparing even this?","\"Based on my experience, this group won't give up easily.\"","Emperor Yuanyou clenched his fists, cheering for the officials of the Ministry of Rites in his heart.","......","Several days later, the matter of selecting consorts was brought up again.","This time, Song Yu did not engage with the topic directly. Instead, he leisurely began, \"My eldest princess is about to have her coming-of-age ceremony. Has your Ministry of Rites prepared all the necessary protocols? If there are any mistakes when the time comes, I will have your official caps removed.\"","\"This is the first joyous event since my ascension to the throne. I attach great importance to it.\"","With those two sentences, the officials from the Ministry of Rites fell silent.","Perhaps... they should wait until after the princess's ceremony to bring it up again?","\"The ceremony will be held within the palace, but there must also be public feasts throughout the capital. The silver will come from my private treasury. I am not afraid to spend.\"","\"She is my only child.\"","Hearing Song Yu's words, the matter of selecting consorts was immediately cast aside by the Ministry of Rites officials. The pressing matter now was the princess's coming-of-age ceremony!","Failure would mean losing their posts.","Once again, Song Yu \"averted danger,\" which in turn made Emperor Yuanyou stamp his feet in anger.","However, Emperor Yuanyou also quieted down.","Everyone began preparing for Song Shihuan's coming-of-age ceremony.","Zi Chen Palace.","By the time Song Yu put down the memorial in his hand, the night had grown deep.","\"Your Majesty, the princess said you must light calming incense before sleeping, as it helps you fall asleep faster.\"","\"Ahuan is always so thoughtful.\"","Song Yu walked outside the hall. The coolness of the night air sharpened his senses slightly.","Once again, Song Yu pondered the question that had troubled him for nearly a month: What kind of coming-of-age gift should he give Ahuan?","As a father, his gift must not be outshone by anyone else!","Did they think he didn't know? The old man was also secretly preparing something big recently.","Under the bright moonlight.","Song Yu suddenly had a flash of inspiration. He quickly walked back inside. He knew what gift to give Ahuan!","\"Grind the ink. I am going to draft an imperial edict.\""]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467: Coming of Age Ceremony, All Officials Come to Offer Congratulations","paragraphs":["Even before the coming-of-age ceremony arrived, the Grand Emperor and the Emperor had a major quarrel, so intense that even Cheng Guang fell silent during the morning court assembly.","In the Zichen Hall.","\"Why should he? I am Ahuan's father. It should be me who chooses Ahuan's courtesy name.\"","Song Yu had practically worn out the ancient texts searching, and now Wu Qi came to say the Grand Emperor wanted to choose the princess's courtesy name?","If he could tolerate this, he might as well jump into the imperial gardens and become a ninja turtle!","Song Yu stormed straight to the Taiji Palace.","\"Ahuan grew up under my watch too, and I am your father. I chose your courtesy name, so naturally, Ahuan's should be chosen by me as well.\"","Emperor Yuanyou did not yield an inch. As if he would give in—he had also nearly worn out his own set of ancient texts.","\"You chose Ahuan's title. Choosing her courtesy name should be my turn, shouldn't it?\"","Song Yu stood his ground defiantly. The fact that he hadn't changed Ahuan's title was already giving the old man plenty of face.","With neither father nor son willing to back down, the ones who suffered were the minor officials below.","The Shen father and son were especially unfortunate.","Emperor Yuanyou directly summoned Shen Mingwen to the Taiji Palace.","\"Minister Shen, who do you think should choose Ahuan's courtesy name?\" he asked, adopting an air of expecting Shen Mingwen to judge the dispute.","Similarly, Song Yu summoned Shen Qingping to the Zichen Hall.","\"Shen the Third, who do you say should choose Ahuan's courtesy name?\"","Though in different places, Shen Mingwen and Shen Qingping sighed in unison.","It was so difficult. Trapped between this imperial father and son, they desperately wanted to escape but couldn't.","Finally, Song Shihuan, unable to bear it any longer, stood before Emperor Yuanyou and Song Yu and spoke calmly:","\"Let Master choose the courtesy name.\"","Hearing this, Song Yu instantly deflated like a punctured ball.","\"Then let Master Qingshan choose it.\"","A debt of gratitude spanning two lifetimes—it was Master Qingshan who had first given Ahuan her name. He was more than worthy of choosing her courtesy name.","Emperor Yuanyou shot Song Yu several glances. Why had this kid given up so quickly?","Emperor Yuanyou still wanted to fight for it, but seeing this, Song Yu grabbed Song Shihuan and ran, terrified the opportunity might ultimately fall to the Grand Emperor.","As long as it wasn't the old man choosing it, he could accept not doing it himself.","Master Qingshan, upon learning of the matter, agreed cheerfully. When the snipe and the clam grapple, the fisherman profits.","......","Time passed day by day, and the Great Qi Dynasty welcomed Song Shihuan's coming-of-age ceremony.","It was a ceremony that seemed very strange at first glance but, upon closer thought, was perfectly reasonable.","On the day of Song Shihuan's ceremony, all civil and military officials of the third rank and above in the entire Great Qi entered the palace to celebrate. The great hall was packed with court officials.","The principal officiant for this ceremony was not a respected matron with both sons and daughters, nor was it even a woman.","When the officials saw Emperor Yuanyou appear in the role of principal officiant, they all twitched the corners of their mouths in unison.","For no other reason than this: among the families Song Shihuan was familiar with, there was no such matron with both sons and daughters.","Emperor Yuanyou felt that rather than finding a matron unfamiliar to Song Shihuan, he should take on the role himself. For this, he had practiced the technique of securing the hairpin for a long time.","Seeing this, Song Yu snorted through his nostrils. The reason he wasn't the principal officiant was that he had lost the fight with the old man.","The assistant for this ceremony was Gu Mingzhu.","As ceremonial music began, Song Shihuan appeared slowly behind Gu Mingzhu. She wore her hair in double coiled buns and was dressed in a colorful robe.","Emperor Yuanyou slowly took the first hairpin—the one prepared by Lady Chang for Song Shihuan. Both he and Song Yu, without prior agreement, hoped Song Shihuan would wear it.","They wished for Lady Chang's longing to also watch over and protect Song Shihuan.","\"On this auspicious day and month, we first add the ceremonial headdress. Cast aside your childish inclinations, and cultivate your virtuous character. May you enjoy longevity and everlasting good fortune.\"","As he spoke, Emperor Yuanyou placed this hairpin, engraved with \"My Daughter Ahuan,\" into Song Shihuan's hair.","Song Shihuan returned to the side hall, changed into a plain jacket and skirt matching the hairpin, then re-entered the main hall to perform a bowing ceremony to Emperor Yuanyou, Song Yu, and Master Qingshan.","Song Yu's eyes instantly reddened.","The flower he had so carefully nurtured had truly grown up.","Yet he still felt Ahuan was just a child.","Emperor Yuanyou took the second hairpin, an ornate golden hairpin he had prepared himself. As he placed it in Song Shihuan's hair, he said:","\"We now add your second adornment, observing all rituals in order. With this fine wine, we pray you receive heaven's blessings.\"","Watching Song Shihuan leave once more to change clothes, Emperor Yuanyou also wiped the corner of his eye.","The young girl who had endured so much hardship would henceforth be an adult.","When she appeared again, Song Shihuan was wearing a deep robe with curved hem, and the youthful air from before had completely vanished.","Emperor Yuanyou stared at Song Shihuan for a few breaths, then took the third hairpin, a phoenix hairpin crafted with utmost extravagance according to the regulations for a Grand Princess.","This time, Song Shihuan changed into a grand purple robe with wide sleeves and performed the grand ceremony of three kneelings and nine kowtows to the elders in the hall.","Emperor Yuanyou received the paper bearing Song Shihuan's name. Upon opening it, his eyes contracted slightly but quickly returned to normal.","\"The rituals are now complete. On this auspicious day and month, we proclaim your courtesy name. A fine and fitting name for a distinguished lady. May it bring you good fortune, and may you forever be preserved under its auspices...\"","\"It is... Zhaohua.\"","The great hall instantly fell silent.","Zhao, as in Zhaowu's Zhao.","Zhaohua.","Choosing this name was truly audacious.","But Master Qingshan's expression remained unchanged. He continued to smile warmly at Song Shihuan. His Ahuan was worthy of this name.","If hearts were to change in the future, with this name, those who wished to scheme against Ahuan would have to weigh their actions carefully first.","\"Zhaohua, an excellent name!\"","Song Yu was the first to speak. \"Thank you, Master Qingshan, for bestowing this name upon Ahuan.\"","Master Qingshan slowly rose and walked to Song Shihuan. His opening words were filled with deep reluctance. \"Although you have grown up, to Master, Ahuan will always be a child.\"","The Ahuan in his memory, who had suffered greatly and struggled through two lifetimes, had finally broken through the barriers of fate and stood here on this day of her coming-of-age ceremony.","When it was Emperor Yuanyou's turn, the carefully prepared words he had rehearsed were completely forgotten. He only smiled and patted Song Shihuan's shoulder. \"No matter when, your Imperial Grandfather is here for you.\"","\"That's right, no need to rush growing up. Your Imperial Father will also protect Ahuan forever.\"","On this day, the officials' understanding of the depth of the Grand Princess's favor increased yet another level.","Where had they ever seen a woman's coming-of-age ceremony where the elders' exhortations were declarations of protection?","The officials' minds raced with a hundred thoughts, each pondering whether the gifts they had presented for the ceremony were perhaps too modest.","After the ceremony concluded, Song Yu held a celebratory banquet in the palace, while outside the palace, a continuous feast was set up. Passing commoners all stopped, hoping to partake in a share of the Grand Princess's good fortune.","That night.","Song Shihuan, for once, got to drink fruit wine again.","In a tipsy haze, Song Shihuan stealthily made her way to Song Yu and looked up at the man in dragon robes before her.","\"Imperial Father, I received so many coming-of-age gifts today.\"","Song Yu nodded. \"I've instructed Baoxia to store them all in Ahuan's private treasury.\"","\"And Imperial Father's gift?\"","The girl extended her flawless, fair palm—it turned out she had come to demand a gift.","Song Yu couldn't help but chuckle. With Master Qingshan around, Ahuan hadn't drunk for some time. Today, she was actually drunk.","\"My gift is placed in the Zichen Hall. Does Ahuan want to go fetch it now?\"","\"Yes!\"","Song Shihuan nodded her head like a little chick pecking at rice.","\"Father Emperor must have prepared something special for me, that's why he didn't present it publicly.\"","Song Yu was amused. This little drunkard's mind was still working quite fast.","\"Let's go.\""]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468: Yu Yu Shi Huan [End of Main Text]","paragraphs":["\"Imperial Father, why did you agree to become my father back then?\"","After drinking, Song Shihuan became quite the chatterbox, her mouth moving non-stop. She insisted on following Song Yu along the palace path.","Their figures, one in front of the other, overlapped under the moonlight, creating a warm and serene scene.","\"Because Song Ling and I are natural-born rivals. As long as he's unhappy, I'm happy.\"","Song Yu's thin lips parted slightly, the corners of his mouth curling up uncontrollably.","\"Was that the only reason?\" Song Shihuan tilted her head. \"Wasn't it also because you thought I was pitiful?\"","\"You were indeed quite pitiful.\"","Song Yu recalled the first time he saw the little girl—dirty, so thin a gust of wind might blow her away, and she had just been pushed by Lady Chang.","\"Were there any other reasons?\"","Song Yu's steps suddenly halted. Song Shihuan, carried by momentum, bumped into his back and couldn't help but rub her nose.","Is Imperial Father's back made of a city wall? It hurts so much to bump into.","\"I lost my mother since I was young. You, yours might as well not exist. So we are both motherless children. Since they didn't want you, I will.\"","Song Yu spoke the truest reason hidden in his heart, born from the empathy of shared suffering.","\"So, I gained a father who dotes on me, and Imperial Father gained a father who dotes on you too, right?\"","Song Shihuan's eyes were filled with scattered starlight. Song Yu was taken aback for a moment, then grinned widely:","\"Yes, Ahuan is absolutely right.\"","\"This time, it was me who spoke up and chose you as my Imperial Father. Next time, remember to speak up first and choose me, Imperial Father.\"","......","Zichen Palace.","Song Shihuan's eyes scanned the room but found no trace of any gift.","Just as Song Shihuan was puzzling over it, Song Yu walked directly to the desk and picked up a bright yellow imperial edict.","\"Imperial Father's coming-of-age gift for me... is an imperial edict?\" Song Shihuan was somewhat confused, her mind not catching up due to the lingering effects of the wine.","\"That's right.\"","Song Yu simply unrolled it and read it aloud for Song Shihuan.","\"It is heard that Heaven shows no partiality, but aids only the virtuous. I, having received the Mandate of Heaven, rule over all lands, diligent day and night, never daring to forget the weight of the state. The Eldest Imperial Princess, Song Shihuan, is gifted with innate wisdom, her bright virtue is fragrant. Even the wise rulers of antiquity, how could they surpass her?\"","The drunkenness in Song Shihuan's eyes gradually dissipated, and she even held her breath slightly.","She only heard Song Yu continue reading:","\"In the past, there was Mulan who joined the army in her father's place. Now, my princess, capable of bringing peace to the nation through civil means and securing the state through martial prowess, her virtue matches heaven and earth, her talent spans ancient and modern times. She is truly a treasure bestowed by Heaven upon Great Qi.\"","\"Though a woman, she yields not to men, fully capable of inheriting the great succession, to serve the ancestral temple.\"","\"Hereby, humbly complying with public sentiment and consulting ancient institutions, I bestow upon her the precious register, establishing her as the Crown Princess, granting her the position in the Eastern Palace. All officials shall memorialize to her as befits the heir apparent.\"","After finishing the recitation, Song Yu smiled and handed the edict to Song Shihuan.","\"Imperial Father, this... this is against convention.\"","\"I am the Emperor. My words are the convention.\"","Song Yu looked at Song Shihuan before him. \"This edict bears the imperial seal. It is my gift to Ahuan for her coming-of-age.\"","\"Ahuan need not be alarmed by this. Whether this edict is made public, and when it is made public, is entirely up to Ahuan's own will.\"","Now the Son of Heaven, Song Yu only wished to give everything he possessed to his daughter.","\"If Ahuan's aspirations lie with the common people of the world, when the time is ripe, Ahuan can present this edict. As for the civil and military officials, I will handle them for Ahuan.\"","\"If Ahuan only wishes for carefree freedom, then this edict can be sealed away forever. I will protect Ahuan's freedom for all time.\"","\"Ahuan, your father only wishes for your happiness.\"","Thus, Song Yu placed the power of choice in the hands of his Ahuan.","Song Shihuan's lips quivered, and tears fell like pearls.","What Song Yu could least bear to see were the tears of the young girl before him.","\"What's wrong? Did this edict frighten Ahuan?\" Song Yu, flustered, picked up a handkerchief and carefully wiped Song Shihuan's tears. \"Don't be afraid, Ahuan. This is the best thing I can give you.\"","He simply felt that his Ahuan was worthy of both the title of Crown Princess and of being the carefree, unfettered Eldest Princess.","In short, his Ahuan was the best.","\"That's not it.\"","Song Shihuan's eyes were as red as a little rabbit's. \"Imperial Father's love for me is the best thing.\"","Song Yu slowly knelt down, meeting Song Shihuan at eye level.","\"Ahuan, to me, is also the best.\"","\"Thank you, Ahuan, for choosing me to be your father.\"","From that moment on, a little girl's name was appended after his in the clan registry.","Even someone as seemingly heedless as him had thanked the heavens countless times for this.","Without Song Shihuan, there would be no Song Yu as he is today.","\"Let the mountains and rivers bear witness, the sun and moon shine together. Ahuan and I are father and daughter by destiny.\"","—End of Main Text.","The main text ends here. Next, I will write some extras covering plot points not fully expanded in the main text. Currently, I plan to write an alternate timeline where A-Yu (Song Yu) is reborn with his memories. In this storyline, the premise is A-Yu firmly choosing Huanhuan (Song Shihuan), together exposing and punishing the villains. I will also add more about Tutor Shen's story. Others are still being conceived.","This book has been updated over eight months. I am deeply grateful for everyone's support and companionship. I am delighted by your act of opening this book, grateful for your love for the characters, and I secretly like and browse your creations in the book community, often marveling at how I have gained such amazing readers (bows in thanks).","The characters in this book are the best characterizations I have written to date. Every time I put pen to paper, I am deeply captivated by these characters. Seeing that your affection isn't limited to just Huanhuan and A-Yu truly excites me, because I love every character in this book—Huanhuan, A-Yu, Emperor Yuanyou, Tutor Shen, Little Mingzhu, Grand Tutor Shen, General Gu... too many to list. I did my utmost to shape each character into someone vivid and lifelike.","Fortunately, these characters have been seen and loved by you all.","When I realized A-Yu was about to ascend the throne, I knew the main text should conclude. Writing to this point, I am also particularly reluctant, always feeling the characters in the book will have even more splendid futures. Let's leave that to everyone's imagination. If possible, you can post your thoughts in the book community, allowing me to return as a reader to see them again.","Thank you, my dear reader friends. I truly adore all you lovely people.","October 21, 2025."]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Damn, I Really Got a Second Chance","paragraphs":["The thirty-sixth year of Yuanyou.","Spring Welcome Pavilion.","Shen Qingping looked at Song Yu, who had suddenly slumped unconscious on the table, his brow twitching violently. How strange, he's drunk after just a few cups?","\"Third Master Shen, the palace is urging us urgently. Please, do us a favor and wake our prince up.\"","The servant pleaded miserably. If they were late, it wouldn't just be the prince facing punishment or scolding—his own little life would be in danger too.","Shen Qingping pondered for a moment upon seeing this, then spoke into the air:","\"Song Ling is here!\"","Whoosh—","The instinct to utterly defeat Song Ling jolted Song Yu awake instantly.","The next second, bewilderment filled Song Yu's eyes. What was going on? Hadn't he already finished off Song Ling?","\"Your Highness, the Eastern Palace is hosting the tenth birthday banquet for Princess Fuyun today. Your servant here is anxiously urging you to enter the palace,\" Shen Qingping said leisurely. \"It's just a tenth birthday banquet, is such a fuss necessary? Might as well not go. At worst, it's twenty strokes of the cane, a mere trifle for someone like you, Your Highness.\"","The prince's backside is made of iron!","Song Yu shot to his feet.","\"Today is the thirty-sixth year of Yuanyou? Song Xiyan's tenth birthday?\"","Shen Qingping nodded.","The next moment, he saw Song Yu fly out like a gust of wind, so fast that afterimages seemed to linger in the air.","Holy crap, I really got a second chance!","Song Yu was so excited he nearly rolled his eyes back. \"Liuxi, does this outfit of mine look good today?\"","He had to ensure his first impression on Ah Huan was nothing but handsome.","\"Your Highness, who is... Liuxi?\"","\"Someone who will replace you very soon.\"","Song Yu headed straight for the imperial palace. He had been late for the birthday banquet last time. This time, no matter what, he couldn't give the Eastern Palace the slightest chance to hurt Ah Huan.","......","In the incense-filled grand hall, a small figure followed behind a palace attendant. She was sallow and thin, wearing a thin, tattered gown, only her eyes were startlingly bright.","This was Song Shihuan's first time stepping into such a magnificent place.","The palace attendant had told her that her father and mother were the Crown Prince and Crown Princess of the court.","At this thought, Song Shihuan's heart trembled slightly. Would... would Father and Mother like her?","The people in the hall also looked at Song Shihuan, each with their own thoughts. The Eastern Palace already had Princess Fuyun. Would they still want a little beggar who appeared out of nowhere?","Extremely obvious disgust flashed in Song Ling's eyes as he thought to himself:","\"Something utterly unrefined, a disgrace.\"","Song Ling didn't notice the large tears falling from the Crown Princess's eyes beside him, only feeling that the Song Shihuan before him was a troublesome nuisance.","Emperor Yuanyou glanced at Song Ling, then looked kindly at Song Shihuan. \"Child, what is your name?\"","\"Song Shihuan.\"","\"A good name.\" The smile on Emperor Yuanyou's face deepened a little. \"You've suffered these years outside. Come, let your imperial grandfather introduce you to your father and mother.\"","As soon as Emperor Yuanyou's voice fell,","the voice of a young eunuch sounded from outside the hall, \"Prince of Qin arrives—\"","They saw Song Yu rush into the hall, swiftly pick up the little figure standing there, and grin at Emperor Yuanyou:","\"Well now, where did this little doll come from? I like her very much. I'll take her to raise in the Prince of Qin's residence.\"","\"You scoundrel!\"","Emperor Yuanyou's face fell. \"This is your second brother's daughter.\"","Hearing this, Song Yu put the little one down and crouched himself, his thin lips parting lightly:","\"Your so-called father has rotten morals, and his luck is terrible to boot. The three sons in his household are all useless, the daughter is kind-faced but cold-hearted. That whole family is utterly unworthy of you.\"","\"I have no sons or daughters of my own. If you choose me as your father, everything I have will be yours. I can study and practice martial arts with you, travel the mountains and rivers with you, do anything you like with you.\"","\"My dear Ah Huan, will you choose me as your father?\"","He was openly snatching someone!","Emperor Yuanyou's face turned green with anger, and Song Ling beside him was also fuming at Song Yu's words.","But Song Ling did not speak up to stop it. Just a little beggar—if Song Yu loved picking up trash, let him take her. He was just worrying about how to get rid of this stain.","Song Shihuan, however, was stunned. The warmth from being picked up moments ago seemed to still linger around her.","Her eyes fluttering slightly, Song Shihuan saw clearly the appearance of the person before her: handsome brows and starry eyes, the most good-looking person she had ever seen in her life.","\"Okay.\"","As if guided by a ghost, Song Shihuan nodded.","Song Yu, usually fastidious and obsessed with cleanliness, now showed not the slightest disdain as he tidied the little one's hair, his eyes filled with affection that seemed about to overflow. Good, this time Ah Huan didn't have to hear those hurtful words.","He had made it in time.","\"Enjoy your food and drink. This prince will take his daughter back to his residence first.\"","Everyone was still in a daze, completely unable to react.","Just as Song Yu was about to leave the hall, his steps paused. \"Father Emperor, your son's legitimate eldest daughter surely deserves a princess title, doesn't she?\"","\"Are you truly decided?\"","Emperor Yuanyou suddenly felt he couldn't quite understand this son before him.","But then he saw Song Yu let out a scoff, covering Song Shihuan's ears with both hands. \"You can see it too. Song Ling doesn't like this daughter. She has suffered greatly living outside. Please, dote on her this once, and dote on your son who has no children this once.\"","\"The legitimate eldest daughter of the Prince of Qin is granted the title Princess Fu'an.\"","As Emperor Yuanyou's words fell, the Crown Princess fainted from crying.","The birthday banquet ended hastily.","......","Half an hour later.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at the little figure before him, grandfather and granddaughter staring at each other, wide-eyed.","\"Father Emperor, watch the child for half an hour for me. I'll come pick her up in half an hour.\"","As he spoke, Song Yu sprinted wildly towards the Prince of Qin's residence. Half an hour—he had to quickly get rid of all the messy things in the Prince of Qin's residence.","Ah Huan clearly didn't carry memories from before. This was his chance to rebuild a majestic image!","\"Ahem, Ah Huan, have you studied any books?\"","Emperor Yuanyou wasn't quite sure how to be alone with his granddaughter, awkwardly searching for a topic.","\"Yes, I have.\"","This time, Song Shihuan hadn't suffered the slightest neglect or disdain. Her eyes were full of curiosity towards her family, and her courage had grown.","\"The characters on here, I can understand them all.\"","Song Shihuan pointed at the open memorial on Emperor Yuanyou's desk, reading out crisply.","A brilliant light shone in Emperor Yuanyou's eyes. \"Then does Ah Huan understand the meaning of this memorial?\"","Song Shihuan nodded somewhat shyly.","Her master had taught her, so she understood.","Half an hour later, when Song Yu, sweating and panting, arrived at the Zichen Hall intending to take the little one away, he saw her being held affectionately in the old man's lap. Grandfather and granddaughter were looking at memorials together!","Alarm bells rang loudly in Song Yu's heart. This was bad.","\"Father Emperor, I've come to take Ah Huan back to the Prince of Qin's residence.\"","Song Yu emphasized the word \"back.\"","But Emperor Yuanyou didn't even bother to look up at Song Yu. \"I've had Wu Qi tidy up the side hall of the Zichen Hall. Ah Huan will stay in the Zichen Hall tonight.\"","Song Yu just felt this was utterly bizarre.","Why was this old man trying to snatch her from him at every turn?"]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470: The Dandy Father's Favoritism Towards Me: The Most Triumphant Episode","paragraphs":["\"No need, I've already prepared a room for Ahuan.\"","Without another word, Song Yu directly took the little girl from Emperor Yuanyou's arms and spoke with a thin, insincere smile, \"I won't trouble you to bother.\"","\"Oh, and I've sent you a few chickens. Have the imperial kitchens stew them for you to nourish yourself.\"","With that, Song Yu left with Song Shihuan, not looking back.","Emperor Yuanyou was both angry that this scoundrel had taken his granddaughter away and curious about when this scoundrel had developed a sense of filial piety, even sending him chickens.","When Emperor Yuanyou saw the familiar fighting cocks, he immediately ordered:","\"Stew them at once.\"","\"Stew them until they're very tender. My teeth aren't what they used to be.\"","Damned birds, they had nearly driven him to fury before!","\"Wait, how could that scoundrel bear to give me his fighting cocks?\" Emperor Yuanyou only then realized something was off. \"Shen Xiao, go investigate what Prince Qin did after returning to his mansion.\"","Prince Qin's Mansion.","\"Your father usually dislikes extravagance, so there aren't many servants in the mansion.\"","Song Shihuan nodded, her eyes looking at Song Yu with a new trace of admiration. To hold such a high position yet remain frugal and simple—Father is so impressive!","\"This is the study where your father usually reads. It's also the place he spends the most time.\"","The weeds were quickly cleared away, leaving the study spotless.","\"Ahuan, you may enter the study anytime in the future.\"","\"Come, let Father show you your courtyard now.\"","Behind them, the matron and the steward's faces both stiffened.","They recognized every word His Highness had just said, but put together, they couldn't understand them.","The little Song Shihuan, thoroughly coaxed by Song Yu, looked up at him with her small face:","\"Father, I want to be someone as amazing as you when I grow up.\"","Song Yu was elated.","This was the most triumphant episode of his life, both in his past and present lives!","Meanwhile, in the Zichen Hall.","\"Deceiver!\"","Emperor Yuanyou nearly tore the memorial in his hand to shreds. \"Such a grown man, deceiving a child. My old face is utterly shamed.\"","Truly shameless.","\"Let's see how this scoundrel will handle it when his lies are exposed!\"","Emperor Yuanyou fumed indignantly, all his resentment stemming from his granddaughter being snatched away.","This was his newly discovered genius granddaughter!","......","Early the next morning.","When Song Shihuan opened her bleary, almond-shaped eyes, she saw two strikingly handsome faces suddenly magnified before her.","Drowsily, she called out:","\"Father.\"","Her voice was milky and soft, making Song Yu feel his heart melt.","\"Did Ahuan sleep well last night?\"","Shen Qingping felt a chill, goosebumps rising all over. Where did that disgustingly sweet, affected voice come from?","\"The bedding was soft and smelled nice. Ahuan slept very well.\"","\"Then time to get up. The sun is almost shining on your bottom.\"","Song Yu scooped the little one up in one motion. Immediately, new faces entered holding trays to attend to Song Shihuan's washing and dressing.","\"Father, Ahuan only needs to wear one dress.\" Song Shihuan looked at the dozen or so dresses before her, somewhat troubled. Father, Granny, and Master were all the same—they'd rather suffer themselves and give the best to her.","\"It's not enough. Ahuan can wear a different one every day.\"","Shen Qingping couldn't take it anymore. He got up and walked outside into the courtyard, taking deep breaths of fresh air.","\"Has your prince been possessed by something?\"","The matron shook her head, saying cautiously, \"If he has, it's by something good.\"","Shen Qingping looked up at the sky in speechless despair.","Just yesterday he was drinking with him at the Yingchun Pavilion, and today he's become an upright prince who loves his daughter as his own life?","Shen Qingping found this breakfast utterly tasteless.","Song Yu, however, was busy and delighted, one moment picking food for Song Shihuan, the next trying to feed her congee.","He also didn't forget to badmouth the Eastern Palace.","Now, in Song Shihuan's eyes, everyone in the Eastern Palace was like a flood or a fierce beast.","\"A crown prince should be virtuous and benevolent, otherwise disaster is inevitable. Since the Crown Prince is like this, wouldn't it be better for Father to become the Crown Prince instead?\"","Song Yu was so excited he immediately gave Song Shihuan a thumbs-up.","Shen Qingping helplessly held his forehead. Little Princess, do you think your father is any better?","\"Ahuan is right. So, for the sake of the common people and the Great Qi's peace for a hundred years, I have decided to contend for the position of Crown Prince!\" Song Yu looked at Song Shihuan. \"Will Ahuan support Father?\"","\"Support!\"","Song Shihuan's eyes shone brilliantly.","\"Since Father has such lofty ambitions, is this gentleman Father's strategist, the future Chancellor?\"","Shen Qingping's previously slouching posture instantly straightened.","He then revealed an extremely amiable smile to Song Shihuan. \"The Princess has keen insight. I am Shen Qingping, indeed His Highness's strategist and the future Chancellor.\"","From now on, he, Shen the Third, would raise the banner only for the Princess!","While Song Shihuan was practicing her fist forms in the courtyard, Shen Qingping sidled up to Song Yu. \"Your Highness truly intends to contend for the Crown Prince's position?\"","Song Yu nodded.","\"This prince never lies to his daughter.\"","\"But Your Highness, you...\" Shen Qingping gave Song Yu a look that said 'you know what I mean'.","Song Yu cleared his throat, putting on an unbearably pretentious air.","\"A wastrel? That's merely my protective coloring.\"","......","The little one finished practicing her forms and came running over, her expression conflicted.","\"Father, throughout history, contending for the crown prince's position has always involved bloodshed and is fraught with danger. I'm worried something might happen to you.\"","Shen Qingping's gaze towards Song Shihuan had changed. A ten-year-old princess, understanding so much?","Could the prince have casually picked up a genius daughter?","\"Ahuan, don't worry. Father is different from others, so Father's method of contending for the crown prince's position will also be different.\"","\"How is it different?\" Song Shihuan was curious, and so was Shen Qingping.","\"This prince can simply go tell your imperial grandfather that I want to be the crown prince.\"","Song Yu curled the corner of his mouth. \"Ahuan just needs to help plead for mercy when Father gets a beating.\"","Shen Qingping: ......","Is this reliable or not?!","He really wants to be Chancellor!","A few days later, Song Yu used personal practice to answer Shen Qingping.","For several consecutive days, Emperor Yuanyou had sent people to the Prince Qin's Mansion trying to bring Song Shihuan into the palace. Finally, Song Yu, annoyed beyond endurance, mercifully allowed the grandfather and granddaughter to meet.","Zichen Hall.","Emperor Yuanyou held Song Shihuan, unwilling to let go.","\"There's something I want to tell you.\"","\"Speak.\" Emperor Yuanyou still didn't even look up.","\"I want to be the crown prince.\"","With a clatter, the memorials on the desk were accidentally knocked to the floor by Emperor Yuanyou.","\"I am not the wastrel you believe me to be. I have the talent of a top scholar and the ability to govern and bring stability to the state. The reason I've concealed it all along was to protect myself.\"","\"Now that I have Ahuan, I don't want to continue like this.\"","\"In terms of status, I am nobler than Song Ling. In terms of learning, I have many times more knowledge in my belly than Song Ling. In terms of benevolence, I have more conscience than Song Ling.\"","For the first time, Song Yu had put on such a grand performance in front of the old man.","He felt thoroughly invigorated. All the hardships he endured for the imperial examinations in his past life had now become his confidence.","Song Yu looked at Emperor Yuanyou:","\"Father, choose me as crown prince. It's a sure profit, no loss.\""]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471: The Doting Father, the Spoiled Heir: The Crown Princess's Support","paragraphs":["Song Yu was shooed away by Emperor Yuanyou as if he were a chick.","\"Whether you're truly a wastrel or a fake one, I know better than you do.\"","Emperor Yuanyou simply thought Song Yu had lost his mind. How much substance his own son had in his belly, he could grasp with absolute certainty.","\"You can test me if you don't believe it.\"","Song Yu insisted.","The response to Song Yu was the slamming shut of the palace hall doors.","Song Yu stomped his foot in frustration. He never expected that upon returning, the biggest obstacle would be the old man.","The old man was firmly convinced he was a good-for-nothing.","\"Wait, Father Emperor, you forgot to give my daughter back to me.\"","Ahuan was still inside the Zichen Hall.","\"Get out!\" Emperor Yuanyou's voice boomed with vigor.","Inside the hall, Song Shihuan pursed her lips and said softly, \"Imperial Grandfather, Father Prince is not a wastrel.\"","\"Father Prince is knowledgeable in the classics, kind-hearted, and very familiar with the situations in various regions of Great Qi. He knows that Laijin Prefecture needs flood control, that the northern deserts lack grain, that...\"","Emperor Yuanyou fell silent. \"Is what Ahuan says true?\"","It didn't sound like his son at all.","\"During these past few days at the Prince of Qin's residence, I've also heard how people outside speak of Father Prince.\" At this point, Song Shihuan's eyes dimmed slightly. \"I am young and don't understand grand principles. I only know that if a profoundly learned person uses the guise of a wastrel to protect himself, he must have suffered immense injustice.\"","She refused to believe in some wastrel prince who was utterly ignorant!","Hearing this, Emperor Yuanyou's heart wavered a little. Could it be that scoundrel was really pretending?","\"Imperial Grandfather, people outside also say Father Prince spends all day playing with crickets and fighting cocks, that his study is overgrown with weeds. But that's simply not true. There isn't a single cricket or fighting cock in the Prince of Qin's residence. His study is clean and full of books.\"","\"Imperial Grandfather, one should believe one's own eyes.\"","The corner of Emperor Yuanyou's mouth twitched. The doubt he felt moments ago instantly vanished without a trace.","His gaze towards Song Shihuan held a bit more helplessness. Silly child, what the people outside say...","is all true!","That day, the chicken your father prince brought wasn't an ordinary chicken; it was a fighting cock!","...","Kunning Palace.","\"Imperial Grandmother, Imperial Grandfather has been paying far too much attention to that wild girl lately, sending Wu Qi to fetch her from the Prince of Qin's residence every few days.\" Song Xiyan was so jealous her nose was almost crooked. \"She's just a wild child raised on handouts from various families. What's so great about her!\"","\"Imperial Grandmother, if this continues, I fear Uncle's favor with the Emperor will only grow stronger.\" Song Yanzheng also spoke with a furrowed brow. Sensing the situation was turning unfavorable, he had already sent letters urging Song Yanchao and Song Yanming to return to the capital quickly.","\"Crown Princess, what is your view?\" The Successor Empress looked at the distracted Crown Princess, her expression displeased. \"Ever since that birthday banquet, you've been absent-minded. Xiyan has cried several times, and you haven't even comforted her.\"","The Crown Princess forced a slight smile. Comfort?","She wished she could strangle Song Xiyan.","She wanted to perish together with everyone in the Eastern Palace.","\"Ahuan is also my child. Seeing His Majesty fond of her, I am genuinely happy for Ahuan from the bottom of my heart.\"","Kunning Palace instantly fell silent. Song Yanzheng and Song Xiyan both looked at the Crown Princess with disbelief.","\"Mother Consort, I am your daughter.\"","\"Ahuan is too.\" The Crown Princess lowered her eyes, looking at the ground.","\"Enough, you may return now. This palace wishes to speak with the children a while longer.\"","Knowing the Successor Empress was sending her away to devise plans against the Prince of Qin and Ahuan,","the Crown Princess's face showed a trace of mockery. In this life, the Prince of Qin was clearly reborn with his memories. For these people to try and scheme against Ahuan was undoubtedly digging their own graves.","\"Prepare the carriage, to the Chang residence.\"","She was going to sever the Chang family's support for the Eastern Palace.","One hour later, Chang Residence.","Chang Qing and Madam Chang looked at the Crown Princess before them, feeling she had changed somewhat, but couldn't pinpoint how.","\"Elder Brother, immediately return the shops seized from the Prince of Qin's estate over the past few years and compensate for the profits.\"","\"Also, from now on, do not support the Eastern Palace so wholeheartedly. If possible, do not make an enemy of the Prince of Qin.\"","A bitter taste filled Chang's mouth. \"The marriage arrangement between Ling'er and Song Yanzheng is henceforth not to be mentioned again.\"","\"Your Highness, are you perhaps speaking nonsense?\" Chang Qing couldn't help but straighten up. \"You are a daughter of the Chang family. The Eldest Imperial Grandson carries Chang blood. The Chang family should support the Eastern Palace.\"","\"And what if the price of supporting the Eastern Palace is the execution of the entire clan?\"","\"If Elder Brother doesn't believe me, go check the incense in Ling'er's room. It contains substances that can cause infertility in women.\"","Clang! Madam Chang collapsed to the floor.","The residence physician confirmed the issue with the incense. Madam Chang held Chang Ling'er, weeping bitterly, cursing Song Yanzheng between sobs.","\"Elder Brother, Song Ling is treacherous and cunning. He will not achieve greatness.\" The Crown Princess's face was deathly pale. \"The Chang family sacrificing one me is enough.\"","Chang Qing's hands trembled, his eyes red with fury.","The Crown Prince and the Imperial Grandsons had never trusted his Chang family.","\"Support the Prince of Qin. He will be a better Crown Prince.\"","The Crown Princess staggered as she left. Chang Qing couldn't help but speak, his voice filled with remorse and pain.","\"It was I... who broke off your engagement with the Prince of Qin back then...\"","But the Crown Princess stopped and shook her head:","\"Being able to give birth to Ahuan, I do not regret marrying Song Ling either.\"","...","Prince of Qin's Residence.","Song Shihuan looked curiously at the Crown Princess before her, her little eyes stealing glances again and again.","Father Prince said the Crown Prince, the several Imperial Grandsons from the Eastern Palace, and that Princess Fuyun were all no good.","But Father Prince didn't say the Crown Princess was no good.","Did that mean her mother was somewhat a good person?","\"Ahuan, I am your mother consort.\" The Crown Princess spoke carefully.","\"Mother Consort.\"","Song Shihuan obediently called out.","But after she called out, the beautiful woman before her began to shed tears.","For the Crown Princess, after her mistakes, she had waited for this 'Mother Consort' for a very, very long time.","\"Yes.\" The Crown Princess, afraid of frightening Song Shihuan, forcibly held back her tears. Then, noticing the history book in Song Shihuan's hands, she paused. \"When I was your age, I also liked reading history books.\"","The Crown Princess stayed at the Prince of Qin's residence for a long time, even using the small kitchen to make a bowl of almond tea for Song Shihuan.","After finishing, the Crown Princess seemed to remember something and scooped a spoonful of honey onto the almond tea.","\"Is it good?\"","Song Shihuan nodded. \"Mother Consort, this almond tea is sweet.\"","The Crown Princess's eyes grew hot.","\"Yes, it has always been sweet. Not bitter.\"","\"Whenever you want to drink it in the future, just tell me. I'll make it for you.\"","Just as the Crown Princess wished to stay longer at the Prince of Qin's residence, Song Yu couldn't bear it any longer.","\"Crown Princess, it's time you returned to the Eastern Palace.\"","He had already yielded Ahuan for a full two hours. Wasn't that enough?","The Crown Princess felt an inexplicable trepidation facing Song Yu, but before leaving, she mustered her courage to ask, \"May I come to see Ahuan often in the future?\"","Song Yu's eyes grew vacant.","Another one coming to fight him for the child."]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Enemies Lock Eyes with Burning Rage","paragraphs":["\"No, Your Highness, you can actually do these?\"","Inside the Qin Prince's mansion, Shen Qingping looked as if he had seen a ghost, holding in his hand several policy essay questions he had specifically asked Shen Mingwen to devise.","Watching Song Yu scribble away with his answers, Shen Qingping completely lost his composure.","\"This is but a trifling matter for this prince.\"","Half an hour later, Shen Qingping looked at the policy essay written by Song Yu, rubbed his eyes in disbelief, and after confirming something, he abruptly took several steps back.","\"Your Highness truly wishes to appoint me, Shen Qingping, as your strategist?\"","\"And one day... appoint me as your Chancellor?\"","\"Absolutely true.\" Song Yu raised an eyebrow. \"If one day I become the Son of Heaven, besides you, I will appoint no other as Chancellor.\"","\"But Your Highness has bided your time for so many years; you must have your own plans and calculations. What could I possibly do for you?\" Shen Qingping felt as if a pie had fallen from the sky.","Who would have thought!","He, Shen the Third, by sheer luck, had actually picked the most formidable one!","\"You have already done a great deal for me.\"","Through the present Shen Qingping, Song Yu seemed to see the young Master Shen of before, who had fallen ill in bed. A pang of sorrow surfaced in Song Yu's heart.","This time, while protecting Ah Huan, he would just conveniently protect Shen the Third as well.","\"Right now, there's an even more important matter to entrust to you.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Teach Ah Huan to play the zither.\"","Song Yu chuckled softly. \"Him calling you Uncle Shen the Third doesn't sit right with me; it sounds more proper for him to call you Tutor Shen.\"","Shen Qingping was stunned. Why did the prince's words sound so strange?","\"Uncle Shen the Third is here again?\"","Song Shihuan came skipping over. Song Yu's eyes immediately softened. \"Ah Huan, from now on, you must call him Tutor.\"","\"Tutor.\"","Song Shihuan obediently spoke.","Shen Qingping felt he must have gone mad. Upon hearing this address of 'Tutor,' he actually felt a sense of perfect fulfillment, as if this was how it was always meant to be.","......","The policy essay answered by Song Yu was delivered by Shen Qingping to Shen Mingwen.","\"Father, take a look at how these answers are.\"","Shen Mingwen took it and, the more he read, the brighter his eyes became. \"Who answered these? I, this old man, declare this person has the talent of a top scholar!\"","It's just that the answering style somewhat resembled that old stubborn rock, Ye Shijie?","\"It was Prince Qin who answered them.\"","Shen Mingwen nearly became the first Grand Tutor to choke to death on his own saliva.","\"It's absolutely true.\" Shen Qingping grabbed Shen Mingwen's hand. \"The prince's reputation as a wastrel is false. He is far more suitable to be Crown Prince than Song Ling. The prince promised me that one day he would appoint me as Chancellor.\"","\"Appoint you as Chancellor?\"","Shen Mingwen made the same choice as Emperor Yuanyou, thinking Shen Qingping had lost his mind.","Shen Qingping was driven out of the study, nearly getting his nose pinched in the door just like Song Yu had.","\"You've followed the prince since childhood, cockfighting, chasing dogs, drinking, and listening to tunes. If you became Chancellor, the entire Great Qi would be doomed.\"","Shen Mingwen's roar made Shen Qingping cover his ears.","\"Just remember to present this policy essay to His Majesty.\" A deep-seated intensity, like a long-dormant volcano erupting, flashed in Shen Qingping's eyes. \"Your son, me, I have great things to do.\"","If the prince is determined to challenge the Crown Prince, I, Shen Qingping, will stake my entire fortune on the prince's victory.","......","Shen Mingwen did indeed present the policy essay to Emperor Yuanyou.","Only then did Emperor Yuanyou believe Song Yu's words. His eldest legitimate son had been using the guise of a wastrel to protect himself all along.","How utterly absurd.","Zichen Palace.","\"Why?\"","Emperor Yuanyou asked, though what he wanted to ask was far more than just these three words.","Hearing this, a shadow of complexity flashed in Song Yu's eyes. When he looked up again, his expression was one of deep melancholy.","\"Because my birth mother died early, and my stepmother is unkind.\"","\"Father, do you truly believe that the son of you and mother would do something like secretly meeting with a palace maid? After that false accusation, I was utterly disheartened, my reputation in ruins. If I hadn't pretended otherwise, would I even be alive today?\"","Song Yu was getting rather addicted to acting, driving the knife forcefully into Emperor Yuanyou's heart.","In his past life, Ah Huan had said the rift between him and his father was mainly due to not understanding the power of words. Well then, this time he would use his mouth more.","He was best at emotional scenes! He'd act Song Ling and his family to death!","Emperor Yuanyou was as if struck by lightning.","Seeing this, Song Yu familiarly walked towards a certain spot, took out a portrait of Empress Yuan, and knelt down:","\"I swear in the name of my departed mother, the events of that year were all plots by the step-empress and Song Ling. I never had any intention of a secret meeting.\"","Emperor Yuanyou let out a sharp, almost shrill cry. \"The step-empress! The Crown Prince! They dare scheme against the child of Zhen and Fen'er!\"","Was evidence even needed?","The child was swearing before Fen'er's portrait; this was the most irrefutable proof!","\"Zhen will go and demand an explanation for you right now.\"","\"Father, I will demand the explanation myself. I will also prove to you that I am the most suitable heir.\" Song Yu straightened his expression. At the beginning of his struggle with Song Ling in his past life, he hadn't known the suffering Ah Huan endured, so he had let Song Ling die too easily.","This time, he wanted Song Ling to beg for death but find it impossible.","\"Father, if you truly wish to do something for me, then give Shen the Third an official post. Your son stands alone in court now; it's not a fair fight against Song Ling.\"","\"Very well.\"","After Song Yu left, Emperor Yuanyou slumped weakly into his chair and wiped his face.","All these years, what had he, as a father, been doing......","......","Several more days of calm passed before the East Palace could no longer hold back, suggesting a family banquet together at Kunning Palace.","\"A family banquet is excellent. This prince loves family banquets the most.\"","Song Yu dismissed the little eunuch who had delivered the message and then began with extreme patience to dress up Song Shihuan.","Kunning Palace.","The table was full, with only Song Yu and Song Shihuan missing.","\"Yu'er is really... he must be playing wildly at the Yingchun Pavilion again. It's fine for me, but how can he keep His Majesty waiting like this?\" The step-empress spoke gently and softly, confidently awaiting Emperor Yuanyou's outburst.","But Emperor Yuanyou merely took a sip of tea. \"Does the Empress have eyes that see a thousand miles, able to see the Yingchun Pavilion from Kunning Palace?\"","The step-empress's face paled.","The Crown Princess nearly laughed out loud. Now she finally knew from whom Prince Qin had inherited his sharp tongue.","Song Yu and Song Shihuan arrived late.","Seeing the two seats deliberately left open, the farthest from Emperor Yuanyou, Song Yu spoke directly, \"Wu Qi, move the chairs next to Father. This prince and Ah Huan will sit one on the left and one on the right.\"","The step-empress instinctively looked at Emperor Yuanyou, only to see he showed no displeasure whatsoever. Instead, he even beckoned to Song Shihuan with a doting expression.","\"Yu'er, it's fine for a family banquet, but you mustn't be like this outside, lest people say you lack refinement.\"","\"Who are you saying lacks refinement?\" Emperor Yuanyou was like a mother hen protecting her chicks.","\"Who are you saying lacks refinement?\" Song Shihuan, for once, pulled a long face, his usual smile gone.","\"Pfft—\" Song Yu snorted with derision.","\"Empress, this prince is the legitimate eldest son. At a family banquet, I should sit in the very last seat?\"","\"You have so many schemes in your heart, you might as well dive into the lake in the imperial garden and become a section of lotus root.\""]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473: The Dandy Prince Spoils Me: The East Palace Only Produces Fools","paragraphs":["The Successor Empress was so angry her nose was crooked, yet Emperor Yuanyou showed not the slightest intention of blaming Song Yu or Song Shihuan. Instead, he cheerfully served food to Song Shihuan.","Song Ling couldn't hold back any longer and said with a frown:","\"Ah Huan, from the moment you entered until now, you haven't paid your respects to your Imperial Grandmother. You must not be so rude.\"","\"But, Father said my Imperial Grandmother is in heaven.\"","Ahem—","Song Yu choked on his food, his neck turning red. He tried to hold back but couldn't suppress his laughter, his whole body shaking like a sieve.","\"Outrageous! How can you be so crude and have no manners at all?\"","\"Before, everyone said I had a father but wasn't raised by him, so I truly don't know any better,\" Song Shihuan said with an innocent look.","Song Ling was panting with rage at Song Shihuan, while Song Yu was slapping his thigh in amusement.","To make matters worse, Emperor Yuanyou was taking sides, looking at Song Ling disapprovingly. \"Why pick on a child? Don't be so petty.\"","Song Ling felt so disgusted he nearly vomited up the previous night's meal.","Song Shihuan secretly winked at Song Yu; father and daughter were in perfect sync.","This Crown Prince, nominally her father, actually didn't like her one bit. Coincidentally, she didn't like this Crown Prince either.","They could have had a peaceful meal, but the Successor Empress was unwilling to let the Eastern Palace lose face so easily.","\"Yanzheng, didn't you recently write a policy essay? Recite it for your Imperial Grandfather to hear.\" Knowing full well that Song Yu was unlearned, the Successor Empress was eager to showcase the Eastern Palace's scholarly achievements.","Upon hearing this, Song Yanzheng promptly recited the policy essay he had prepared in advance.","Instead of receiving praise from Emperor Yuanyou, he was met with a sigh that sounded like a little adult's:","\"Lamenting the hardships of the people... the person who wrote this essay must have personally witnessed much of the world's suffering.\"","Chirp—","Song Yu instantly understood and followed up immediately.","\"When did you ever have such experiences?\" Song Yu shot a disdainful glance at Song Yanzheng. \"Feigned agony. A policy essay written like this is worthless.\"","\"Why must Uncle speak of me with such malicious disdain?\"","\"Disdain you?\" Song Yu curled the corner of his mouth. \"Then let this prince test you with a policy question.\"","\"Yu thought of those drowning in the world; he deemed it not enough to merely discuss it.\"","After saying this, Song Yu buried his head in his meal. Questions crafted by Ye Shijie were tricky; one could attempt them but dare not make a sound.","Song Yanzheng truly deserved this.","By the time Song Yu had eaten his fill, Song Yanzheng still hadn't answered, standing to the side drenched in sweat.","\"As an elder, you bully a junior. Could you even answer this question yourself?\" Song Ling said contemptuously.","Song Yu sat up straight.","Thanks for the invitation, he had been waiting for this moment.","He was best at answering Ye Shijie's questions.","When Song Yu answered with extreme fluency, even Emperor Yuanyou seemed somewhat unaccustomed to it, glancing at Song Yu several times in a row.","\"Uncle must have memorized the answer beforehand,\" Song Xiyan accused.","\"Hearts that are dirty see dirt in everything.\"","Song Shihuan's dark almond eyes turned to Song Xiyan. \"Such questions are mere casual answers for my father. I don't know about your scholarship, but your character is lacking.\"","\"You!\" Song Xiyan shot to her feet.","\"Alright then, let's make a bet.\"","Song Yu smiled as he looked at Song Ling. \"You can ask any six questions, and I will answer them. If I answer them all, you will stand outside the Kunning Palace and shout four times, 'The Eastern Palace only produces stupid eggs.' How about that?\"","\"The Four Books and Five Classics, choose any topic.\"","Song Ling was somewhat tempted. \"And if you can't answer?\"","\"Then I am the stupid egg,\" Song Shihuan pointed at herself. \"After all, Father only has me, this one egg, right now.\"","Emperor Yuanyou thought of the most painful events in his life but still couldn't help letting out a laugh.","\"Fine, I'll take the bet.\"","After Song Ling spoke, he looked up and met Song Yu's unfathomably deep eyes, feeling inexplicably creeped out.","Song Yu smiled.","He would use a blunt knife to cut flesh, making Song Ling watch clearly as the Crown Prince position changed hands, be condemned by the world, watch his own children turn on each other, and suffer unbearably.","Watch how the opponent he once looked down upon most would openly crush him in every aspect.","\"Good.\"","Song Yu leisurely straightened his robes and then pinched Song Shihuan's little cheek. \"Don't worry, Father won't let you become a stupid egg.\"","......","For the first question Song Ling posed, Song Yu answered without even thinking.","Song Yanzheng and Song Xiyan exchanged a subtle glance at Song Ling. Was Father going easy? This concerned the dignity of who between them and Song Shihuan was the stupid egg.","Sure enough, the difficulty of the second question increased sharply.","Song Yu answered with his feet propped up, extremely relaxed.","Song Ling, caught in the situation, hadn't yet realized, but the Successor Empress was already looking at Emperor Yuanyou's satisfied expression with horror. How could the Prince of Qin...","All six questions in a row, Song Yu answered them.","After answering, Song Yu kindly made a \"please\" gesture towards Song Ling.","\"Shout four times, 'The Eastern Palace only produces stupid eggs.'\"","\"Your Majesty...\" the Successor Empress couldn't help but speak up.","\"A bet is a bet,\" Emperor Yuanyou only tossed out these four words.","Song Ling, eyes bloodshot, walked out of the room and stood outside the Kunning Palace. Having suffered the greatest humiliation of his life, he shouted four times:","\"The Eastern Palace only produces stupid eggs.\"","\"Ah Huan, do you know why it's four times?\" Song Yu leaned against the railing, looking dotingly at the little one beside him.","\"I know, because the Eastern Palace has four eggs.\"","\"Clever Ah Huan.\"","Song Yu lifted his eyes to scan the surroundings: the Successor Empress, furious but holding it in; Song Ling, eyes full of hatred; Song Yanzheng, face full of humiliation; Song Xiyan, features twisted in anger; and... the Crown Princess, who remained aloof...","In this very atmosphere, Song Yu looked at Emperor Yuanyou:","\"So, about your son becoming Crown Prince... is there a chance?\"","Boom—","A clap of thunder sounded in the sky, making the faces of the Eastern Palace party turn ashen.","......","\"Yu'er, what do you mean by that?\" The smile on the Successor Empress's face could no longer be maintained as she forced out the words.","\"Isn't the meaning clear? I also want to be Crown Prince.\"","Song Yu chuckled softly. \"I am both the legitimate eldest son and the eldest by birth, the most suitable candidate for the Crown Prince position, am I not?\"","\"But you...\"","\"Me what? That I'm unlearned? Or a dissolute playboy? Or perhaps that I had an illicit affair with a palace maid from my stepmother's quarters, showing improper conduct?\"","Song Yu pressed step by step. \"Before, I didn't want to compete, so I didn't bother with these dirty tricks. But now I want to compete.\"","\"Even so, I wouldn't use such despicable means to fight. What skill is there in bringing down a brother? Making the people's lives better is what makes a good Crown Prince.\" For the first time, Song Yu stood on the moral high ground, feeling both thrilled and immensely satisfied.","Emperor Yuanyou nodded excitedly repeatedly.","Seeing this, Song Yu raised an eyebrow. \"Father, please treat your soon-to-arrive perfect heir well.\"","This old man was getting off cheap.","Before, he clearly couldn't wait to pass the throne to him.","From now on, he mustn't hit him with a shoe sole anymore!","\"Ah Huan, Father will take you to see the Eastern Palace first, to pick a courtyard you like in advance.\"","Song Yu took Song Shihuan's hand and headed straight for the Eastern Palace, his sense of ownership overwhelmingly strong."]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Nonsense About Being an Isolated Support","paragraphs":["Song Yu brought Song Shihuan to the Eastern Palace and set fire to the woodshed that had once held her captive.","When Song Ling stormed in, furious and wanting Emperor Yuanyou to uphold justice, he was met with the sight of Song Yu and Song Shihuan wearing utterly innocent expressions.","\"Father, 'If one cannot manage a single room, how can one manage the empire?' Song Ling cannot even properly manage the Eastern Palace, to the point it catches fire. Does he have the capability to govern the entire Great Qi?\"","\"Ahuan and I just went in to take a look, and it inexplicably caught fire. Could it be a deliberate attempt to kill us?\"","Song Ling stared at Song Yu in disbelief. How had his eldest brother become so difficult to deal with, as if a different person now inhabited his body?","\"I didn't...\" Song Ling felt utterly unable to defend himself.","\"Drunkards also claim they're not drunk,\" Song Yu clicked his tongue and shook his head.","\"Song Ling, return and reflect on your mistakes.\"","Emperor Yuanyou didn't even deign to address him as Crown Prince anymore.","Song Ling's heart sank to the depths. He had never realized before just how blatantly biased his father was.","Back at the Qin Prince's residence, Song Shihuan quietly approached Song Yu. \"Father, why did you burn that woodshed?\"","\"I consulted a master. That woodshed is inauspicious for the Qin Prince's residence. It had to go.\"","Instantly, Song Shihuan's eyes filled with admiration as she looked at Song Yu.","Her father was truly wise, decisive, and knew how to plan ahead.","A breeze blew past. Song Yu looked at the visibly excited Shen Qingping before him, glanced at Shen Qingping's hand tightly clutching his sleeve, and parted his thin lips slightly:","\"What? Received an official post, so you're so excited you want to call me 'father' like Ahuan too?\"","Shen Qingping instantly calmed down, the corner of his mouth twitching.","\"When will Your Highness attend court?\" Shen Qingping asked irritably.","Who could understand? All the welled-up emotion vanished the moment it met the prince's mouth.","\"No hurry. This prince will first go recruit some followers. Otherwise, attending court lacks presence.\"","Song Yu spoke leisurely. A question mark slowly materialized above Shen Qingping's head. Was having him alone not enough for the prince?","......","The Gu Residence.","\"His Majesty has ordered Ahuan to attend the Imperial Study daily with the imperial grandsons, so she needs a study companion.\"","Gu Zheng blinked at the Qin Prince before him, who usually had nothing to do with him.","So... what did this have to do with him?","\"This prince and Ahuan have taken a liking to your family's Mingzhu.\"","\"Impossible, absolutely impossible!\" Gu Zheng reacted as if facing a great enemy. \"My daughter is unruly and has disliked studying since childhood. If she becomes the princess's companion, I fear she will lead the princess astray.\"","Song Yu nodded inwardly.","Gu Zheng's assessment of his own daughter was quite accurate.","\"Is that so...\" Song Yu adopted a rather regretful tone. \"This prince was prepared to order a daily supply of various pastries so Ahuan and the Second Young Lady Gu wouldn't go hungry in the study. Since it's like this...\"","Father! To be chosen by His Highness and the princess is my great honor!","Gu Mingzhu darted out from behind the screen. Gu Zheng scratched his head in embarrassment.","Gu Mingzhu looked at Song Shihuan with utmost sincerity, as if gazing at her favorite pastries.","\"Mingzhu, is it? What a lovely name, as clever and spirited as you are. Thank you for being willing to be my study companion.\"","Song Shihuan took Gu Mingzhu's small hand. Gu Mingzhu's face gradually turned red.","\"Everyone says I'm dull-witted...\"","\"That's not true at all.\" Song Shihuan studied Gu Mingzhu's eyes. \"People with clear, bright eyes are all treasures favored by heaven.\"","Aww—","Gu Mingzhu hugged Song Shihuan and yelled at her father, \"I, Gu Mingzhu, will be the county princess's companion! If you don't agree, I'll run away from home and move into the Qin Prince's residence!\"","Before Gu Zheng could react, Song Yu immediately panicked.","\"It's settled then.\"","He absolutely must not let this little ancestor go to the Qin Prince's residence.","That night.","After Song Shihuan fell asleep, Song Yu left the Qin Prince's residence and arrived at a pleasure boat filled with song and dance.","Prince Chu and Prince Qi were there, full of complaints, cursing Song Ling for controlling many key positions in the court and restricting them at every turn.","Suddenly, a voice rang out:","\"Well said.\"","Prince Chu and Prince Qi, looking at the suddenly appearing Song Yu, choked on their wine, faces turning red.","\"You two want to be Crown Prince?\"","\"Cough, cough, cough—\"","Prince Qi choked until his eyes rolled back. He felt he might be dying a little.","\"What a shame. This prince also wants to be Crown Prince.\"","Song Yu poured himself a cup of wine. \"Within one hour, if you can name three areas where you surpass this prince, this prince will help you secure the Crown Prince's position.\"","After recovering, Prince Chu and Prince Qi's eyes shone brightly.","\"I am well-versed in the Four Books and Five Classics,\" Prince Chu said eagerly.","\"Then let's compare.\"","One incense stick's time later, Prince Chu began to question his life.","\"My archery is decent; I can hit an apple,\" Prince Qi followed closely.","\"Let's compare.\"","Song Yu curled the corner of his mouth. What a coincidence. In his past life, he had secretly practiced just to prove himself in front of Ahuan.","After a few arrows were shot, Prince Qi rubbed his eyes, unable to believe it.","For the rest of the time, no matter what Prince Chu and Prince Qi said, Song Yu's response was a calm:","\"Let's compare.\"","That one hour felt exceptionally long to Prince Chu and Prince Qi.","The man before them was actually a monster who was good at everything!","\"If you pledge your loyalty to this prince, in the future, this prince will lead you to conquer Great Yue and the Northern Desert. Your names will be recorded in history, and I will ensure your wealth and prosperity, with rich and fertile fiefdoms.\"","Song Yu's voice drifted leisurely. \"If not...\"","\"The Northern Desert will be your future residence.\"","Prince Qi felt an inexplicable chill all over. He felt these words carried great malice.","Song Yu waited quietly for Prince Chu and Prince Qi's answer. In this life, he didn't want to waste so much effort on these two fools.","\"Loyalty, of course we pledge our loyalty.\"","Prince Chu and Prince Qi spoke in unison. What did they have to compete with such a legitimate son of the late empress?","Their handsome and dashing faces?","\"Good. Then help this prince with the first task.\" Song Yu curled his lips.","\"What is it?\" Prince Qi asked warily. \"I have principles, you know.\"","\"Go and do your utmost to provoke Song Ling for me. Regardless of the consequences, this prince will cover for you.\"","\"Consider it done.\" A smile instantly appeared on Prince Chu's face. This temptation was irresistible.","\"Leave it to the two of us, Elder Brother. You can rest one hundred percent assured.\" Prince Qi also nodded with restraint, though in reality, he was trembling with excitement.","In the face of such a good deal, what were principles?","......","Several days later, Song Yu attended court for the first time.","Gu Zheng, for the sake of his little ancestor, hurried over cheerfully to greet Song Yu.","Prince Chu and Prince Qi also obediently called him \"Elder Brother.\"","When Song Ling entered the hall, Prince Chu and Prince Qi both moved closer to Song Yu.","They had to stay away from Song Ling.","Otherwise, Elder Brother might misunderstand!","Shen Mingwen looked at the surreal scene before him, feeling his head buzz. Yesterday, the Emperor had summoned him to the Zichen Hall and rambled for a full hour, just to express his distress that Prince Qin would be isolated and unsupported in court.","Was this what 'isolated and unsupported' looked like?"]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475: The Doting Father's Favor: The Chang Family's Defection","paragraphs":["Throughout the entire morning court session, Emperor Yuanyou's gaze scarcely strayed from Song Yu.","Why had he never noticed before that this scoundrel could look so proper and presentable when he put his mind to it?","As he watched, Emperor Yuanyou's mind began to wander. This scoundrel truly did have more the bearing of a crown prince now. Fen'er really knew how to bear good sons.","As the emperor, it was rare for Emperor Yuanyou to be distracted during morning court.","It wasn't until he realized everyone's eyes were on him that he coughed lightly, somewhat embarrassed. \"What is it?\"","\"Your Majesty, the Prince of Qin requests you assign him an official post,\" Shen Mingwen reminded him, steeling himself.","Song Yu's bright, star-like eyes were now fixed eagerly on Emperor Yuanyou, like a fledgling eagle waiting to be fed. \"Father, do you think your son is suited for the Ministry of Revenue? I just finished auditing the Prince of Qin's estate shops a few days ago and feel I have some talent for managing accounts.\"","Shen Qingping, standing at the very end of the line of officials: \"...\"","The one with the talent was him, Shen Qingping, alright? That certain prince hadn't so much as moved his lips the entire time!","\"Quite suitable,\" Emperor Yuanyou nodded, rather cherishing his son's dependent demeanor.","\"And what about the Ministry of War? Your son also feels suited there. I get along famously with General Gu Zheng and would like the chance to gain experience in the Ministry of War. In the future, I can expand our territories for you, Father, and help you become a wise ruler celebrated in history.\"","Upon hearing his name, Gu Zheng's eyebrow twitched, feeling the prince was greatly exaggerating their rapport.","\"Suitable, suitable,\" Emperor Yuanyou, already thoroughly charmed, grinned broadly.","He had completely forgotten that the Ministry of War was currently Song Ling's domain.","Hearing this, Song Yu revealed an extremely shy smile, then, as if somewhat embarrassed, spoke again. \"And then there's the Ministry of Personnel. Chang Qing told me many things about the Ministry of Personnel a few days ago, and I'm quite interested in that as well.\"","Song Ling was now like a balloon filling with air, on the verge of exploding.","The Ministry of Personnel, the Ministry of War, and the Ministry of Justice in his hands—and just like that, two were taken away with a few words?","And Chang Qing, what on earth was going on!","\"Interest is good,\" Emperor Yuanyou's gaze towards Chang Qing grew even more benevolent. \"Chang Qing, you must assist the Prince of Qin properly from now on.\"","\"Thank you for the trust of Your Majesty and His Highness the Prince of Qin.\"","Chang Qing kowtowed to express his gratitude, never once meeting Song Ling's eyes throughout.","Prince Chu and Prince Qi beside him had their backs soaked with cold sweat.","Thank goodness they had chosen to pledge their allegiance.","Otherwise, the Ministry of Rites and the Ministry of Works in their hands would probably be gone too.","The entire court was already dumbfounded.","The Prince of Qin, long notorious as a wastrel, had suddenly shed his foolishness. With a silver tongue, he had coaxed the Emperor into a beaming smile.","And without lifting a finger, he had secured three of the Six Ministries.","Prince Qi, recalling Song Yu's previous instructions, rolled his eyes thoughtfully. \"Elder Brother, why didn't you ask for the Ministry of Justice?\"","Song Ling's face instantly turned ashen. The Ministry of Justice was all he had left now.","\"Too much at once is hard to digest. Once I have these three ministries properly arranged, I will ask Father for the Ministry of Justice.\"","Song Ling: !!!","What a thoroughly sweat-drenching morning court session.","......","After court adjourned, Song Ling directly intercepted Chang Qing.","\"Chang Qing, what is the meaning of this? First, you voluntarily gave silver to the Prince of Qin's estate, and now you're working for the Prince of Qin. What, are you counting on this crown prince to die soon?\"","Hearing this, Chang Qing smiled. If he really did die, he would certainly set off a string of firecrackers outside the Chang residence.","\"Your Highness the Crown Prince, the Chang family has been a distinguished official lineage for generations. We have never been anyone's vassal. We have the right to choose,\" Chang Qing looked directly into Song Ling's eyes. \"The Prince of Qin is honorable and will not drive our Chang family to utter ruin.\"","\"You!\"","\"Our Chang family has done many dirty deeds for you. Looking back, what has our Chang family gained?\" Thinking of his wife and daughter who had cried themselves into faints at home, a flash of ruthlessness passed through Chang Qing's eyes.","\"This crown prince has already made it clear to you. One day, Ling'er will be Yan Zheng's principal consort.\" Song Ling could not bear to hand over the Chang family, his greatest asset, to Song Yu.","\"A principal consort... who cannot bear children?\"","Chang Qing laughed coldly. \"Your Highness the Crown Prince, the fact that the Chang family has not chosen mutual destruction with the Eastern Palace is already out of consideration for Her Highness the Crown Princess.\"","With that, Chang Qing turned and jogged towards Song Yu.","Seeing Chang Qing catching up, Song Yu's lips curled slightly.","Destroying one's spirit after killing them was indeed satisfying.","Eastern Palace.","The Crown Princess looked at the violently enraged Song Ling before her and the four children watching intently, then calmly picked up her teacup and took a sip.","\"Lixian, you are the Crown Princess of the Eastern Palace. How could you let the Chang family support Song Yu? Now the Eastern Palace is constrained at every turn. Go to the Chang family at once and persuade Chang Qing to return.\"","Faced with Song Ling's accusation, the Crown Princess scoffed.","\"I will not go.\"","\"Mother, you and Father have always been in perfect harmony. For your sake, Father hasn't taken a single concubine. How can you be so heartless?\" Song Yanzheng protested indignantly.","The Crown Princess felt as if she had been blinded by lard all these years.","Slowly standing up, the Crown Princess mustered all her strength and slapped Song Yanzheng across the face.","\"You wretched thing! Was giving Ling'er the medicine to make her barren your idea alone?\"","The Crown Princess, always known for her weakness and incompetence, had suddenly found her backbone, leaving everyone in the Eastern Palace stunned.","\"My Chang family married a daughter into the Eastern Palace and exhausted itself for its sake. And you, Song Yanzheng, repaid kindness with enmity by striking against my Chang family. I, Chang Lixian, am ashamed to have such an unfilial son. I would have no face to see the Chang ancestors after death.\"","\"And you three. I had you read history books to understand principles since childhood, yet you pretended to be obedient before me while being different behind my back. Did all that learning go to the dogs?\"","\"And you, Song Ling, are a thorough hypocrite.\"","Seeing Song Ling's hand raised high to strike, Lady Chang took a step forward and challenged him:","\"Hit me. Go on, strike.\"","\"Right now, the Prince of Qin is looking for your mistakes. If, right after the Chang family pledges allegiance to the Prince of Qin's estate, I am humiliated in the Eastern Palace, do you think my elder brother would expose all the past affairs and fight you to the death?\"","Song Ling ultimately did not dare to strike.","Seeing this, the mockery in the Crown Princess's eyes grew even more pronounced. She turned and instructed the palace servants, \"Pack my things. I am returning to the Chang family for a visit home.\"","The plaque at Li Garden—just seeing it nauseated her.","She urgently needed to see Ah Huan to soothe her eyes, which felt like they were about to get styes.","Lady Chang left decisively, leaving the Eastern Palace occupants staring at each other.","......","Chang Residence.","A knocking sound came at the door.","Chang Ling'er, her eyes swollen from crying like walnuts, sobbed towards the door, \"Don't bother me. I said I don't want to see anyone.\"","The next second, the door was kicked to splinters.","Gu Mingzhu sheepishly retracted her leg. She had used too much force.","She meant to apologize to Chang Ling'er, but upon seeing her state, Gu Mingzhu couldn't help exclaiming:","\"Your Highness, she can cry her eyes into such a state. How impressive.\"","\"If I could cry like that, my father surely wouldn't have the heart to beat me.\"","Song Shihuan quickly approached Chang Ling'er, her almond eyes filled with carefree innocence. \"Cousin Ling'er, I'm Ah Huan. Mother has moved to stay at the Chang residence. Mingzhu and I will come to play at the Chang house from now on.\"","\"Don't cry anymore. Come play with us.\""]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Do You Think My Buttocks Are Okay, Family","paragraphs":["Kunning Palace.","Song Yanzheng and his three siblings wept bitterly, their faces streaked with tears and mucus, while Song Ling's eyes were also bloodshot.","\"He took control of three of the six ministries on his very first court appearance. The Chang, Gu, and Shen families are now all on Song Yu's side. That old traitor from the Shen family is everywhere proclaiming that Song Yu has the talent of a top scholar. Even those two fools, Prince Chu and Prince Qi, have been utterly bewitched by Song Yu,\" Song Ling said, growing more furious with each word. \"Mother Empress, I fear my position as Crown Prince is about to be lost.\"","\"Nonsense!\"","The Successor Empress forcefully slapped the table. \"As long as I am here, your position as Crown Prince is as solid as a rock.\"","\"How can a man of such flawed personal character, who engaged in an illicit affair with a maid from his stepmother's palace, possibly become the heir apparent?\"","A flash of venom crossed the Successor Empress's eyes. \"We only need to widely publicize this fatal flaw of Song Yu's, and those old-fashioned ministers at court will never accept him as Crown Prince.\"","\"Imperial Grandmother, can we have the Xu family help us spread the word?\"","Song Yanzheng's eyes were brimming with tears. In just a few days, he could keenly feel the change in attitude the court officials showed towards him.","He had always been fiercely proud; how could he accept such treatment? Yet now, the only ones firmly supporting the Eastern Palace seemed to be the Xu family.","Hearing this, the Successor Empress thought of Elder Lady Xu and let out a heavy sigh. \"I will personally visit the Xu family.\"","The Xu family should not refuse her face.","But no sooner had the Successor Empress sent someone to deliver her message to the Xu family than Song Yu arrived at the Xu residence, bringing Song Shihuan with him.","\"Father, will Elder Lady Xu like me?\"","Hearing this, Song Yu pinched Song Shihuan's little cheek. \"Since Ah Huan returned to the palace, aside from those in the Eastern Palace who have eyes on their backsides, has Ah Huan met anyone who didn't like you?\"","Song Shihuan shook her head.","Father liked her, Imperial Grandfather liked her, her tutor liked her, Mother Empress liked her, Mingzhu liked her...","She was so happy.","Arriving at the Xu residence, after paying her respects, Song Shihuan proactively pattered over to Elder Lady Xu. The seven parts fondness in Elder Lady Xu's heart instantly turned to ten.","\"You've suffered, little princess.\"","Elder Lady Xu stroked Song Shihuan's slender arm. It was clear Prince Qin was raising her well, but having come through hardship, she still looked delicate and thin.","\"Thank you for your concern, Grandaunt. I don't feel it was suffering. Seeing you today, you truly are, just as Father said, a good person like a Bodhisattva.\"","\"I like Grandaunt just as much as Father does.\"","Song Yu raised an eyebrow. Could such words have come from his mouth?","Elder Lady Xu laughed, the wrinkles around her eyes deepening. \"This old woman only has one granddaughter, Yayu. She's not as clever or sweet-tongued as you, Princess. Someone, open my dowry chest and let the Princess pick what she likes.\"","The old maidservant beside her was stunned. Elder Lady's dowry chest had only been opened once before, when the eldest young master took a wife.","Song Shihuan spent less than an hour at the Xu residence and received a full carriage of gifts.","When leaving, Elder Lady Xu held her in her arms, reluctant to let go, calling her 'darling' and 'treasure'.","\"Grandaunt, Ah Huan will come see you often.\"","Song Shihuan waved her little handkerchief reluctantly, then boarded the carriage with her most precious father.","Indeed, Elder Lady Xu liked her too.","Behind them.","The smile on Elder Lady Xu's face gradually faded. She summoned Xu Jinruo.","\"Plead illness tomorrow, do not go to Kunning Palace. From now on, the Xu family will follow Prince Qin's lead.\"","\"Mother?\" Xu Jinruo was somewhat taken aback. \"Didn't you say before that Prince Qin held no particular affection for the Xu family?\"","“Prince Qin of the past was cold and unyielding. Even the Emperor couldn't make him obey meekly. The throne would not be handed to him.” Elder Lady Xu let out a long sigh. “But now, with the little princess, Jinruo, Prince Qin is different.”","\"He is, after all, the child of the late Empress. He is blessed.\"","\"I will follow your instructions, Mother.\" Xu Jinruo's only virtue was his filial piety.","“Also, I will write you a list later. Have people purchase the items and send them to Prince Qin's residence for the princess. What a delightful child. When you think about it, she is also of Xu family blood. The Xu family must protect her.”","That evening, Xu Jinruo looked at the list stretching down to the floor before him, his face expressionless.","Was Mother's decision to have the Xu family follow Prince Qin's lead really not just because she liked the princess?","...","The next day, the Xu family pleaded illness, which directly infuriated the Successor Empress into taking ill herself.","Song Xiyan led a group of people and aggressively blocked Song Shihuan's path to the Imperial Study.","\"Song Shihuan, you are so cunning and deceitful, actually sowing discord between my Imperial Grandmother and my Grandaunt.\"","Thinking of her father in the Eastern Palace, smashing teacups and roaring in anger, Song Xiyan looked at Song Shihuan with utter hatred in her eyes.","\"Today, I will make you understand the price of offending the Eastern Palace.\"","\"Fool.\"","Song Shihuan stood before Song Xiyan and deigned to utter a single word.","At this moment, there was a natural, awe-inspiring calm about Song Shihuan.","\"You dare call me a fool?\"","\"I'm calling you exactly that. If your ears are blocked, go find a night soil collector to clean them out.\" Gu Mingzhu stepped in front of Song Shihuan, putting on an even more arrogant air than Song Xiyan. \"Our princess is granted the Emperor's favor to attend the Imperial Study for lessons. If you delay the princess's study time, aren't you afraid the Emperor will hold you accountable?\"","\"The Emperor is my Imperial Grandfather too, not hers alone.\"","“Yes, yes, yes.” Gu Mingzhu rolled her eyes. “May I ask if Princess Fuyun can attend the Imperial Study daily as well? If you don’t hurry to the girls’ school, I’ll report you for skipping class!”","Skipping class meant getting your palms punished. Gu Mingzhu had personal experience; it hurt.","Song Xiyan was furious to the point of frenzy.","Song Shihuan seemed amused by Gu Mingzhu's protective stance and continued, \"Grandaunt is ill today. I was planning to visit her after my lessons. As for what you said about sowing discord, I don't understand.\"","How could the children raised in the Eastern Palace be so foolish?","Little Song Shihuan couldn't help but feel a flicker of relief. Fortunately, Father had acknowledged her early; otherwise, she might have become foolish too!","\"Fine, you don't understand? Then go explain it to the sticks.\"","Song Xiyan gave a look to the little eunuchs behind her, who immediately raised their sticks and advanced.","A look of anticipation flashed in Song Xiyan's eyes. She couldn't wait to see Song Shihuan covered in bruises, kneeling and begging for mercy.","But Song Shihuan wasn't flustered in the least.","Father had assigned her hidden guards. Probably in a few more steps, those little eunuchs would get a beating.","Song Shihuan was already contemplating how to lodge a complaint with Emperor Yuanyou.","What Song Shihuan didn't expect was that Gu Mingzhu, like a whirlwind, charged at the group of little eunuchs, fists flying.","While fighting, she wailed towards Song Shihuan:","“Don't worry, princess, I will definitely protect you!”","\"Just please don't tell my father, I'm afraid my backside won't survive!\""]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477: The Prodigal Prince's Doting Father: Dancing on Emperor Yuanyou's Last Nerve","paragraphs":["The Hall of Purple Splendor.","Three young girls stood in a row. Emperor Yuanyou first glanced at Song Shihuan. Seeing she was unharmed, his heart, which had leapt to his throat, slowly settled back down.","Then, the Emperor looked at Song Xiyan, whose face was bruised and swollen, and Gu Mingzhu, whose cheek bore a scratch from a fingernail.","Song Xiyan was wailing loudly, but Gu Mingzhu held her neck stiff and high, not shedding a single tear.","She, Gu Mingzhu, had fought against five and even managed to hit Song Xiyan. She was feeling quite triumphant.","Emperor Yuanyou hurried forward, pointing at Gu Mingzhu's face as he asked Mei Zhilin, \"Is it serious? Will it scar?\"","Mei Zhilin shook his head.","The Emperor's heart completely returned to its place. Good, it was just a minor scuffle.","If it had scarred, Gu Zheng probably would have torn this Hall of Purple Splendor apart.","\"Summon their fathers.\"","Half an hour later, Song Yu, Song Ling, and Gu Zheng had all gathered in the Hall of Purple Splendor.","After confirming Song Shihuan was fine, Song Yu immediately pulled Gu Mingzhu and charged up to Song Ling. \"Song Ling, how have you raised your child? At such a young age, she knows how to stir up trouble, even bringing people to commit violence within the palace! A crooked stick will have a crooked shadow!\"","He looked even more protective than Gu Zheng himself.","\"Xiyan has been beaten like this too. Gu Mingzhu assaulted her superior and should be punished!\" Song Ling retorted.","\"Song Xiyan said I was sowing discord between her Imperial Grandmother and her maternal uncle's grandmother.\"","Song Shihuan suddenly spoke.","\"But maternal uncle's grandmother was simply ill today and couldn't enter the palace. Why are you all so anxious? Could it be you wanted to entrust something to maternal uncle's grandmother? Something to use against me and my father?\"","Song Xiyan instantly jumped up. \"That's not it at all!\"","But her reaction was tantamount to a confession.","Song Ling's imposing manner also immediately weakened.","\"Today, you initiated the conflict. The little eunuchs behind you were all holding clubs. If Mingzhu hadn't protected me, it would be my face scratched now.\"","\"This is too much!\" Song Yu directly pointed at Song Ling's nose. \"The fault of the child lies with the father. Imperial Father, you cannot only punish Song Xiyan; Song Ling must be punished as well.\"","Emperor Yuanyou had long been stirred to anger by Song Shihuan's words.","He understood perfectly well the current situation of the Eastern Palace. What good could come from seeking out the Xu family at a time like this?","\"Song Xiyan, you are to copy the 'Admonitions for Women' one hundred times. You may not leave your residence until it is finished.\"","\"As for Song Ling, you are confined to your residence for a month of reflection.\"","Emperor Yuanyou spoke slowly. One month should be enough for that scoundrel to firmly establish his footing in the court.","\"Why?\"","Song Xiyan, who had suffered nothing but setbacks since Song Shihuan's return, finally couldn't hold back. Shaking off Song Ling's hand trying to cover her mouth, she cried out loudly.","\"She's just a wild girl raised outside the palace. Why does everyone like her?\"","\"My father has worked so hard for all these years, yet it can't compare to a few words from the Prince of Qin. Is Imperial Grandfather really so heartless, truly intending to give the Crown Prince position to the Prince of Qin? My father is also your son. My brothers and I are also your grandchildren!\" Song Xiyan wept uncontrollably. They all said she was the Eastern Palace's lucky star, so today she would demand justice for the Eastern Palace!","\"The Prince of Qin is someone who could have an illicit affair with a palace maid from the Empress Dowager's palace. How can someone with such character become the Crown Prince of a nation?\"","Silence.","The air in the entire hall grew still.","Even the usually fearless Gu Mingzhu couldn't help but shrink her neck. There was a killing intent!","Emperor Yuanyou, furious to the extreme, laughed instead. Every sentence of Song Xiyan's speech was dancing on his thunderous triggers.","Song Ling had already sensed a hint of danger and wanted to take Song Xiyan away.","Then Emperor Yuanyou's voice rang out, \"Wu Qi, go to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility and request the Empress's presence.\"","\"What happened back then, We will settle it today.\"","......","\"Your Majesty, this subject shall take his leave first...\"","Gu Zheng felt utterly uncomfortable. Such royal secrets—the less one knew, the better.","\"No need. We will summon several other senior ministers, as well as Prince Chu and Prince Qi, to listen together.\"","Hearing this, Song Yu glanced at Emperor Yuanyou, suddenly very curious how the old man would clear his name this time.","The Empress arrived quickly. Seeing her, Song Xiyan threw herself forward, crying incessantly.","Though the Empress was seething inside, on the surface she could only force a smile.","This granddaughter of hers, why did she cause such ruin at a critical moment involving major principles?","Half an hour later, all the senior court ministers had assembled.","Prince Chu and Prince Qi were also summoned to the palace, utterly confused.","Seeing this formation, the Empress suddenly felt a strong sense of foreboding.","\"We have summoned you all today to clarify a matter.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's voice sounded somewhat detached, but everyone's ears perked up.","Good news generally doesn't need clarifying; what needs clarifying is usually bad news.","\"Our eldest son by the Empress, his affair with the palace maid back then was not intentional but caused by someone drugging him. All these years, he has been wronged.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, the hall erupted in an uproar.","\"Imperial Father, elder brother was at the age for marriage back then. If he hadn't been drugged and branded with infamy, how could the position of principal consort remain vacant to this day? This fully shows the ruthlessness of the person behind it. You must investigate this person clearly and have them executed!\"","Prince Qi immediately spoke up, also stealing a glance at the Empress.","If the Empress fell, his own mother could live more comfortably.","\"Yes, Imperial Father, elder brother has suffered too much, bullied to the point where he could only pretend to be a wastrel to preserve his life. If our late Empress Mother in heaven had awareness, she would surely be heartbroken.\"","Prince Chu, sharing the same thought, added more fuel to the fire.","The Empress could no longer maintain the smile on her face.","She realized the Emperor had set a trap, tightly ensnaring her. She could not question the Emperor's words, as doing so would be no different from confessing that she was the one behind it.","She even had to follow the Emperor's lead and help clear Song Yu's name.","But... had the Emperor actually traced it back to her?","The Empress felt uneasy, her face turning pale.","Song Yu suddenly smiled.","So this was how easily an emperor could truly protect someone when he wanted to.","So he didn't need to exhaust himself searching for evidence.","\"We have almost finished investigating the person behind this. How to deal with them is Our decision to make.\"","After throwing down these words, Emperor Yuanyou dismissed everyone.","Returning to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, the Empress's legs gave way and she collapsed to the floor.","\"Imperial Grandmother...\"","A slap struck Song Xiyan's face. \"Why did you go provoke Song Shihuan? And why did you defy your Imperial Grandfather in the Hall of Purple Splendor? Do you not know that because of you, the Eastern Palace is nearly finished?\"","Song Xiyan covered her face helplessly. \"Imperial Grandmother, I felt sorry for you and Father...\"","\"Enough! They call you a lucky star? To this palace, you seem more like a jinx! Get out of my sight! Go back and copy the 'Admonitions for Women' as your Imperial Grandfather ordered!\"","Song Xiyan returned to the Eastern Palace. Her three elder brothers, who had once doted on her, now ignored her completely. Song Yanzheng even instructed the kitchen to only give her plain congee.","Song Xiyan cried as if the sky had fallen dark.","She didn't understand. Why were even her own family members treating her so cruelly?"]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478: My Dandy Father Dotes on Me: Is the Deposed Crown Prince Troublesome","paragraphs":["The Gu Household.","Gu Mingzhu followed behind Gu Zheng, grimacing in pain but not daring to make a sound, afraid he might remember he had forgotten to give her a proper spanking.","She then saw Gu Zheng silently take out the ointment specially provided by Song Yu, bend down, and carefully apply it to her face bit by bit.","\"Does it hurt?\"","Gu Mingzhu shook her head. Why wasn't her father yelling at her anymore? She was starting to feel a bit unaccustomed to it.","\"Foolish girl, you take after your mother not one bit.\" Gu Zheng looked at the scratches on Gu Mingzhu's face, his heart aching terribly. \"The Princess had already told you there were hidden guards, why didn't you stop?\"","\"With Song Xiyan's despicable behavior, I wouldn't be able to sleep well if I didn't hit her myself.\" Gu Mingzhu said while mimicking a punching motion, but accidentally tugged at her wound. \"Ouch...\"","\"Stay still.\"","Gu Zheng rapped Gu Mingzhu's head with a mix of exasperation and affection. \"Today was just a minor scuffle. If you encounter real danger in the future, acting like this could cost you your life.\"","\"If I ever face real danger and don't step forward, then it would be the Princess's life on the line.\"","Gu Mingzhu became uncharacteristically serious. \"Father, the Princess treats me exceptionally well. Today in the Zichen Hall, she seemed fine, but she actually cried when she saw Song Xiyan scratch me. She told me not to be so reckless in the future.\"","\"And His Highness the Prince, though he's always teasing me with his words, today he also stood up for me and demanded an explanation. He even went to Mei Zhilin to get this top-quality ointment for me and sent over my favorite pea cakes.\"","\"And His Majesty the Emperor, before you arrived, before even assigning blame, he first asked Imperial Physician Mei if my face would scar.\"","Gu Mingzhu's little mouth opened and closed, her words leaving Gu Zheng momentarily stunned.","\"Father, so what I did was worth it.\"","\"I really don't know whether to call you clever or foolish.\" Gu Zheng sighed and continued applying the medicine.","\"The daughter of the great General Gu could never be foolish.\"","Gu Mingzhu smiled, her eyes curving like crescents. That Song Xiyan, she had wanted to give her a good beating for the longest time.","Suddenly, the smile on Gu Mingzhu's face widened.","Her backside was saved!","......","As the legitimate eldest son, Song Yu held authority over half of the Six Ministries and entered the Zichen Hall daily.","The Emperor personally cleared his name of past grievances and specifically decreed that his daughter, Princess Fu'an, was to receive treatment equal to that of a royal grandson and study in the Imperial Study.","Meanwhile, Crown Prince Song Ling was punished with confinement for reflection, the Crown Princess was sent back to her maiden home in the Chang family for an extended stay, and the once-unrivaled Princess Fuyun was punished with copying texts.","This series of actions sent a clear signal, instantly making the Qin Prince's residence a hub of activity.","\"Liu Xi, accept all gifts from anyone who comes to offer them.\"","Song Yu lay on a reclining chair, speaking like a lord.","It was still most comfortable having Liu Xi by his side.","It had only been just over a month since Ah Huan was recognized, yet Song Yu already felt invincible.","A few moments later, Shen Qingping swept in like the wind.","\"Your Highness, I've found the person you asked me to look for.\"","Song Yu glanced up and instantly sprang to his feet.","\"You... you are Cheng Guang? Cheng Guang from Dayue?\"","The man before him had a head of hair like a bird's nest, his clothes were disheveled, looking completely different from the man in his memories.","Cheng Guang nodded.","He had just been expelled from the Dayue Prince's residence when he was captured and brought all the way to Daqi.","Song Yu chuckled.","So, Cheng Guang hadn't gained prominence yet at this time.","\"Follow me, and I'll ensure you live a life of luxury.\"","Cheng Guang had heard about the changes in Daqi's Qin Prince during his journey. His eyes shifted craftily. \"If I can help Your Highness secure the throne, may I contend for the position of Chancellor?\"","Thud—","Cheng Guang was struck from behind and fell to the ground, unconscious.","Song Yu looked at Shen Qingping, who wore an innocent expression.","\"Your Highness, my apologies. My hand acted on its own just now.\"","Daring to covet his future chancellorship?","Song Yu massaged his forehead helplessly. Some rivalries truly transcended lifetimes.","\"Rest assured, I have important uses for him. The Chancellor's position is still yours.\" Song Yu's gaze slowly drifted into the distance. \"Next, we must accomplish some major tasks during this one month while Song Ling is confined.\"","......","Over the following month, Emperor Yuanyou received a succession of good news from his suddenly prodigal son.","\"Your Majesty, Prince Qin sent someone to manage the flood control in Laijin Prefecture. They also dealt with the incompetent officials there and received a 'Ten-Thousand-People Umbrella' from the grateful citizens.\"","\"Your Majesty, Prince Qin used his own funds to purchase large quantities of grain sent to the northern frontier. General Gu was so moved he hugged Prince Qin and wept, insisting on taking His Highness on a tour of the military camp. Prince Qin delivered an impassioned speech that greatly boosted the soldiers' morale; they are now eager for battle every day.\"","\"Your Majesty, Prince Qin has uncovered and resolved several wrongful convictions across various regions.\"","\"Your Majesty...\"","Emperor Yuanyou was stunned for a moment, then turned to Wu Qi. \"Wu Qi, pour me a cup of wine.\"","\"And also, summon Shen Mingwen.\"","Heavens, was he dreaming?","His formerly wayward son had suddenly become the model child everyone envied!","Nowadays, during court sessions, the old ministers looked at him with envy in their eyes, jealous that he had such an outstanding son.","Upon receiving the summons, Shen Mingwen prepared himself to listen to Emperor Yuanyou's ramblings for another half hour. However, when he arrived at the Zichen Hall, he found a slightly tipsy Emperor.","Emperor Yuanyou slowly spoke:","\"Minister Shen, is deposing a Crown Prince troublesome?\"","Instantly, Shen Mingwen's eyes widened like copper bells.","It was known that his third son had said if Prince Qin ever ascended the throne, he would appoint him as Chancellor.","Then...","His Shen family was going to produce a Chancellor!","Thus, Shen Mingwen replied with a beaming smile, \"Your Majesty, actually, it's not troublesome at all.\"","\"How so?\" Emperor Yuanyou was clearly very interested.","\"It's a matter of a single edict.\"","Shen Mingwen even felt like having a few drinks with the Emperor right then.","Emperor Yuanyou was also pleased to hear this. If it was that simple, he would find a time to settle the matter.","\"Alright, I understand.\"","When Shen Mingwen left the Zichen Hall, his surface was calm, but inwardly he was ecstatic.","Returning to the Shen residence, he dragged Shen Qingping, who had just returned to the capital covered in dust and was catching up on sleep, out of bed.","Shen Qingping, bleary-eyed with sleep, frowned slightly, showing clear annoyance at having his good dream disturbed.","\"You little rascal, you've hit the jackpot! The Emperor just asked me if deposing the Crown Prince is troublesome!\"","\"What's so surprising about that? His Highness the Prince surpasses Song Ling in every aspect. Deposing the Crown Prince is inevitable. No matter how troublesome, His Majesty will do it.\" Shen Qingping rolled over. \"I'm exhausted. I don't have time to burn incense for our ancestors right now.\"","The words Shen Mingwen hadn't yet spoken were thus blocked.","\"Oh, and after this trip, the common folk have started calling me the 'Living King of Hell'.\"","\"You might want to think about how to protect the Shen family's good reputation first.\"","With that, Shen Qingping fell into a deep sleep.","Shen Mingwen stood as if struck by lightning.","How on earth could his Shen family be associated with the term 'Living King of Hell'?"]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: The World Collapsed After Song Ling Came Out","paragraphs":["After the court session.","\"Lord Shen, indeed a tiger father does not beget a dog son. Your son has only been in court for just over a month, and his official position has already risen to Chief Minister of the Dali Temple.\"","\"Yes, Young Lord Shen's methods for solving cases are swift and severe. Many criminals from various prefectures and counties surrender themselves upon merely hearing Young Lord Shen's name.\"","Listening to the officials' flattery, Shen Mingwen wanted to laugh but couldn't quite manage it, only forcing out a few dry chuckles.","He had topped the imperial examinations as the Zhuangyuan, held the position of Grand Tutor, and in the eyes of the world, the Shen family was a distinguished scholarly household of refined nobility.","For such a family to produce a Chief Minister of the Dali Temple felt rather odd.","Shen Mingwen could only nod and quickly made his escape, slipping away.","Prince Qin's Mansion.","\"Father, why did you have the tutor go work at the Dali Temple?\"","Song Shihuan propped her chin in her hands, her appearance already bearing some resemblance to the late empress.","\"Only this way can we make Song Ling understand that the Ministry of Justice will remain ours, no matter what.\" Song Yu gently tapped Song Shihuan's nose. \"Besides, Ah Huan, don't you think the aura of the Dali Temple suits Shen the Third perfectly?\"","Extremely cold, extremely ruthless.","\"Liu Xi says that now even the little children on the street cry when they hear the tutor's name, but the tutor catches bad people.\" For the first time, Song Shihuan did not echo Song Yu's words. \"The tutor isn't cold and ruthless at all. The tutor's heart is warm, just like Father's.\"","Just then, Shen Qingping entered the courtyard. Hearing these words, his stern face softened like ice melting, and he handed a stick of candied hawthorn berries to Song Shihuan.","Nian'an behind him stared at the candied hawthorn in Song Shihuan's hand.","His Third Master was currently swamped with work, yet he still insisted on taking a detour before coming to Prince Qin's Mansion to personally buy a stick of candied hawthorn for the young princess.","He hadn't understood the reason before.","Hearing the princess's words just now, Nian'an suddenly saw the light.","Song Yu, watching Shen Qingping's aura transform so abruptly, spoke helplessly, \"Shen the Third, if you have nothing to do, go back and rest. Go to the Yingchun Pavilion for some wine and music.\"","He really didn't want Shen the Third to work himself to exhaustion again.","\"How could that be acceptable?\"","Shen Qingping immediately replied, \"As His Highness's future trusted aide, I cannot be a freeloader.\"","Besides, there was still that Cheng Guang watching like a tiger eyeing its prey.","\"As you wish.\" Song Yu seized the moment to snatch one candied haw berry from Song Shihuan. Song Shihuan didn't mind, quietly eating the rest beside them.","Shen Qingping, however, shot Song Yu several pointed glances.","\"If Your Highness wants to eat, go buy your own.\"","\"What you buy for Ah Huan is bought for this prince.\" Song Yu squinted from the sourness. \"Tomorrow, Song Ling will be allowed out of the Eastern Palace. Shen the Third, the weather is about to change.\"","\"It has already changed.\"","Shen Qingping also sighed with feeling.","Suddenly, Song Yu signaled Shen Qingping to come closer and whispered a long passage to him. Afterward, Shen Qingping left with a meaningful look.","\"Father is having a secret talk with the tutor behind my back.\"","Song Shihuan turned her back, presenting the back of her head to Song Yu.","She would sulk a bit, so Father would have to coax her.","On the other side, Nian'an was also quite curious.","\"His Highness told me to take care of a few people who have personal grudges against him before he gets appointed Crown Prince. He also said to find someone to give the Sun family's Sun Hu a beating first.\"","What, after becoming Crown Prince, he'll have to watch his image?","......","The next day.","The ban forbidding Song Ling from leaving his quarters was lifted, and he hurriedly attended the morning court session.","But wherever Song Ling's gaze fell, everyone deliberately avoided meeting his eyes.","In contrast, whenever Song Yu spoke, many officials would voice their agreement.","A strong sense of foreboding rose in Song Ling's heart.","After court, Song Ling stopped Censor Geng, who had always looked down on Song Yu. \"Censor Geng, why did you agree with Prince Qin's words today?\"","\"What he said benefits the nation and the people. Naturally, I agree.\"","Seeing officials passing by one after another, Censor Geng quickly took a step back, maintaining distance from Song Ling.","\"But before, you were the most...\"","\"Your Highness the Crown Prince, times have changed. The current Prince Qin is a completely transformed man.\" Censor Geng pursed his lips. \"In the past month, Prince Qin has accomplished many things. Now, all civil and military officials in court are convinced by him. You... Prince Qin is, after all, your elder brother...\"","Having said his piece, Censor Geng also quickly departed.","When Song Ling learned what Song Yu had done, he felt as if the sky had fallen.","\"So, isn't this prince more suitable to be Crown Prince than you?\"","Song Yu arrived uninvited, sitting in the seat within the Eastern Palace that rightfully belonged to Song Ling.","\"You're merely relying on Father Emperor's favor.\"","\"Don't deceive yourself. What this prince has done in one month is more substantial than what you've done in ten years as Crown Prince.\" Song Yu glanced at Song Ling. \"Admit it, you are inferior to this prince.\"","These words directly made Song Ling's eyes redden.","\"How is that possible? I, Song Ling, am the Crown Prince of Great Qi!\"","\"You won't be for much longer.\"","Song Yu leisurely poured himself a cup of tea. \"Oh, right, why isn't Song Xiyan here? Has she been confined? Is she treated as a harbinger of misfortune by all of you, denied proper food and drink, left to be bullied at will by the servants?\"","Seeing Song Ling's trembling lips, Song Yu smiled mockingly.","\"Only knowing how to blame failure entirely on one person—truly the hallmark of you father and sons.\"","\"Did you come today just to mock this crown prince?\" Song Ling glared angrily at Song Yu.","Song Yu simply nodded, revealing an almost mischievous smile:","\"Correct.\"","\"This prince made a special trip just to see you make a fool of yourself.\"","\"Song Ling, if this prince hadn't been provoked by you and Lady Xu the Younger since childhood, hadn't believed Father Emperor loved you more, you wouldn't even have had the chance to become Crown Prince.\" Song Yu stood up and stood before Song Ling, lightly patting his face. \"What you stole from this prince's hands like a thief, this prince will now take back openly and aboveboard.\"","\"Thank you for managing it on this prince's behalf all these years, allowing this prince to be free and unfettered outside.\"","Every word Song Yu spoke felt like a knife twisting in Song Ling's heart.","Pfft—","A large mouthful of blood sprayed out. Song Ling had actually been angered to the point of vomiting blood by Song Yu's few sentences.","\"When this prince becomes Crown Prince later, he will properly enshrine you, the deposed crown prince, along with your four children. He will definitely take care of your whole family... very... well.\"","Song Yu patted his butt and left, leaving the Eastern Palace in chaos.","On the way back to Prince Qin's Mansion, Song Yu happily hummed a tune.","He didn't need to lift a finger against Song Ling at all. In just one month, the entire court had seen the gap between Song Ling and himself.","This was far more satisfying than having Song Ling die early in his previous life.","He had always regretted that Song Ling didn't get to see him appointed Crown Prince and ascend the throne.","Returning to Prince Qin's Mansion, Song Yu couldn't find Song Shihuan.","\"Where's Ah Huan?\"","Replying to Your Highness, the princess has gone to sleep.","Song Yu frowned. \"Usually, Ah Huan waits for this prince every day to tell her stories. Why did she go to sleep by herself today?\"","\"This old servant speaks out of turn, but perhaps you haven't fully appeased the princess since yesterday.\" The matron spoke carefully.","Hearing the matron's words, Song Yu's features contorted.","Ah Huan was actually sulking with him for two days just because he said one negative thing about Shen the Third!"]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: The Stepmother Has Gone Mad","paragraphs":["\"Why isn't the Prince asleep so late at night?\"","Shen Qingping was roused from sleep once again, looking at Song Yu with a face full of resentment.","Song Yu's expression was even darker than Shen Qingping's. He struggled for a long time before forcing out the words, \"Tomorrow, help me put in a good word for me in front of Ahuan.\"","Shen Qingping was instantly wide awake, his interest piqued.","\"How did Your Highness offend the young mistress? She has always relied on you greatly, how could she be angry with you?\"","Hearing Shen Qingping's sarcastic tone, Song Yu's face grew even darker.","\"It's because I said you have a cold and ruthless nature, so Ahuan got angry.\" Song Yu spoke through gritted teeth. \"Ahuan said you have a warm heart, just like... me!\"","Every word was uttered with his back teeth clenched.","Shen Qingping only felt his chest swell. It was just a casual joke, yet the young mistress had actually taken it to heart.","But it was precisely this kind of young mistress that made him equally willing to protect with his life.","\"I only said it offhand, don't I know your temperament?\" The Prince of Qin, who had been basking in success for the past month, now looked crestfallen. \"It must be because of the recent gossip about you that Ahuan overheard.\"","\"The young mistress feels sorry for me.\"","Shen Qingping smiled, the corners of his mouth curling up. \"Your Highness, rest assured, I will go speak with the young mistress tomorrow.\"","But then he saw Song Yu smile too.","\"It's good that Ahuan is willing to act a little spoiled and throw small tantrums in front of me now.\"","Shen Qingping: ???","Song Yu gave Shen Qingping a look that said 'you wouldn't understand'.","A ten-year-old girl is exactly at the age for acting a little spoiled. He had been hoping Ahuan wouldn't be so overly well-behaved.","Early the next morning.","Shen Qingping arrived at the Prince of Qin's mansion very early, having deliberately worn a set of red robes that Ahuan liked the most. Song Yu frowned as soon as he saw them.","He immediately went back to his room and changed into his own purple robe.","Thus, when Song Shihuan opened her eyes, it was as if she saw two peacocks strutting about in full display.","\"Father, Tutor.\"","\"Ahuan went to sleep early yesterday, are you still angry with your father?\" Song Yu bent down, gently coaxing the little girl before him. Seeing this, Shen Qingping also stepped forward. \"What your father said was all in jest. I grew up with His Highness since childhood, we're used to talking to each other like that.\"","Song Shihuan paused, then pouted. \"People outside all say Tutor is a living King of Hell. How could someone who does good deeds be a living King of Hell?\"","\"Your father has thought of a solution for you.\"","Song Yu ruffled Song Shihuan's head. \"Let's go find an opera troupe. We'll have Shen the Third's stories of eradicating evil and promoting good written into a script for the troupe to perform. That way, everyone will know the truth.\"","\"Great idea!\" Song Shihuan clapped her hands excitedly. \"Such a wonderful method, Father, how did you think of it?\"","Song Yu choked on his own saliva, coughing until his handsome face turned red.","Silly Ahuan, it was you who thought of it.","......","The father and daughter made up, which actually left the watching Emperor Yuanyou feeling a bit regretful.","He had been planning to add fuel to the fire, but didn't expect them to be reconciled so quickly.","\"Ahuan, is Shen the Third that important in your eyes?\" Emperor Yuanyou asked, rather put out. \"What if one day your Imperial Grandfather is also wrongfully accused?\"","\"Then Ahuan would have to take action and hit someone.\"","Song Shihuan said seriously, \"Imperial Grandfather is the Emperor. Anyone who dares to wrongfully accuse the Emperor will have to answer to my fists.\"","Laughter erupted from the Zichen Hall. Song Yu, whose footsteps had just reached the entrance, paused.","Well, it seems unlikely he'll be able to take her back today.","\"How has things been over at Kunning Palace recently?\" Song Yu asked. Upon hearing this, Wu Qi quickly bowed and replied respectfully:","\"I heard there's something wrong with the mind of the one in Kunning Palace.\"","\"Something wrong with her mind?\" Song Yu was somewhat surprised. \"Does Father Emperor know?\"","Wu Qi nodded cautiously.","Song Yu understood. That meant he knew but had no intention of having her treated.","\"I'll go take a look.\"","Song Yu headed straight for Kunning Palace. He hadn't paid attention to Kunning Palace this past month either. He never expected his hypocritical stepmother had developed a mental problem.","Kunning Palace.","The once magnificent palace now exuded an air of deathly silence everywhere.","The palace servants who attended there had all been transferred away, leaving only an old cleaning maid and a personal attendant.","Standing outside the door, Song Yu saw his stepmother sitting before a bronze mirror.","\"Has the Emperor found out about me?\"","The attendant's face was expressionless; she was used to being asked the same question hundreds of times a day.","\"No, definitely not. Otherwise, the Emperor would have dealt with me.\" The Empress seemed not to expect an answer, asking and answering herself.","\"No, the Emperor must have found out. Otherwise, he wouldn't have transferred everyone from Kunning Palace away. The Emperor doesn't want to see me anymore...\"","Song Yu raised an eyebrow. So, the Empress had driven herself mad.","Ever since Father Emperor cleared his name of the false accusations, the Empress had been constantly tormented, wondering if the Emperor had discovered her involvement. After a month of this torment, she went mad.","\"Has Song Ling been here?\"","The old maid hurriedly replied, \"The Crown Prince has not come. None of the imperial grandsons have come either.\"","A trace of mockery appeared on Song Yu's face.","\"Why hasn't Ling'er come to see me? And Yanzheng...\"","Song Yu didn't listen to the rest. He felt that being lucid yet mad like this was far more torturous than being directly executed in his previous life.","The news of the Empress's madness was spread under Emperor Yuanyou's direction. First, Song Yu's wrongful accusation was cleared, then immediately after, the Empress went mad. Everyone speculated about the connection.","Thus, Song Ling was completely isolated and without support in the court.","Former allies of the Eastern Palace now dared not have the slightest association with Song Ling, wishing to stay as far away as possible.","The once bustling Eastern Palace quickly became desolate.","Song Ling attended court each day like a ghost, only to find he couldn't get involved in any matters. Even the Ministry of Justice was given to Song Yu by Emperor Yuanyou, on the grounds of Shen Qingping's merit in solving cases.","This blatant favoritism made Song Ling's daily existence agonizing.","Until one day, someone secretly sought Song Ling out.","\"Vice Minister Xiao.\"","Song Ling looked at the usually inconspicuous Vice Minister of Rites, Xiao Bingsheng, standing before him, somewhat puzzled. He and the Xiao family had never had any dealings before.","Moreover, this Xiao Bingsheng was known for being the best at self-preservation and was very timid.","\"Your Highness the Crown Prince is currently being harmed by treacherous individuals. The Xiao family values ritual and law above all. If the heir apparent has committed no major fault, he cannot be easily deposed. Your Highness, please rest assured.\"","Faced with the olive branch extended by Xiao Bingsheng, Song Ling was overjoyed and immediately treated Xiao Bingsheng as a most honored guest.","When the news reached Song Yu's ears, he took a sip of tea, looking as if he had expected it.","\"Well, these two people I wanted to deal with have gotten together. Perfect timing.\"","\"Why would Xiao Bingsheng support Song Ling?\" Shen Qingping was somewhat puzzled.","\"Because Song Ling is stupid enough.\""]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Song Ling Digs His Own Grave","paragraphs":["Prince Qin's Mansion.","\"Cheng Guang, how goes the investigation into the Xiao family I tasked you with?\"","The Cheng Guang before him had now taken on a proper appearance. Benefiting from his time as a censor when he could even uncover what a minor concubine in an official's household was up to, the first task Song Yu had given him was to investigate the Xiao family.","\"I've even found out who Xiao Bingsheng sleeps with every night.\"","With Cheng Guang's loud declaration, Shen Qingping felt his hand itching again.","\"Xiao Bingsheng is extremely cautious, but his second son, Xiao Zhang, is ridiculously easy to investigate. Your Highness, I believe the Xiao family is problematic,\" Cheng Guang said with rare seriousness. \"And it's a significant problem.\"","\"I believe the Xiao family harbors rebellious intentions.\"","Shen Qingping shot to his feet. To make his reaction seem reasonable, Song Yu deliberately feigned shock:","\"Heavens, such a thing could happen?!\"","\"I merely thought that Xiao Zhang was too arrogant and wanted to find an opportunity to teach the Xiao family a lesson. How could it come to this...\"","Seeing Song Yu's reaction, Cheng Guang, fearing disbelief, hurriedly handed over a pile of materials. \"Your Highness, I'm truly not speaking without evidence.\"","\"The Xiao family are considered nobility, yet there's a small dog hole in their garden leading outside the estate. I've seen figures moving at night—if it's not illicit affairs, it's rebellion.\"","\"A few days ago, for the Old Madame Xiao's birthday celebration, I secretly checked the gifts. Several sent from outside the capital were far beyond the proper specifications.\"","Cheng Guang was striving to prove his point, unaware that Song Yu had been satisfied from his very first sentence.","Though, to even discover a dog hole... no wonder he was suited to be a censor.","\"This matter is grave indeed.\"","Song Yu appeared deeply distressed. \"Song Ling is actually involved with such people.\"","\"This is absolutely perfect.\"","Shen Qingping suddenly spoke up, amused.","When luck runs out, even drinking water makes you choke.","...","Over at the Eastern Palace, things also felt strange.","\"Father, it's odd that the Xiao family is willing to help us but only from the shadows.\"","Song Yanzheng's brows were tightly furrowed. What they lacked now were people who could openly voice support for the Eastern Palace.","\"He said he could provide us with what we need—people, grain, weapons...\" Song Ling's expression darkened. \"A mere Vice Minister of Rites, how could he possess so much? This Xiao Bingsheng is no simple character.\"","It was possible they were merely using each other, the Eastern Palace and him.","\"Father, should we still cooperate with the Xiao family then?\"","A choice lay before Song Ling.","Knowing the Xiao family was problematic, should they cooperate?","\"We have no other path.\" After a moment of contemplation, Song Ling spoke again, sealing the Eastern Palace's fate. \"We can only cooperate with Xiao Bingsheng. Yanzheng, are you willing to forever remain beneath others, kowtowing and paying homage to Song Yu?\"","Song Yanzheng shook his head.","\"Then we can only cooperate with the Xiao family.\"","Xiao Bingsheng dared to reveal his hand to him, betting precisely on the fact that Song Ling now had no other choice.","\"Then we... are we rebelling?\"","Song Yanzheng asked with great difficulty. In just over a month, why had they fallen from being masters of the Eastern Palace to this state?","Song Ling did not answer, silently drinking his wine instead.","Within the Eastern Palace, Song Xiyan was under house arrest. Song Yanzheng vented all his anger on her.","\"If not for you, how could the Eastern Palace have come to this?\"","At that moment, Song Xiyan, copying the \"Admonitions for Women,\" was in tears. How had it become her fault alone?","...","Song Ling began competing openly with Song Yu.","If Song Yu donated grain to the northern frontier, Song Ling would donate grain too.","If Song Yu resolved an old case, Song Ling would also start reinvestigating old cases.","With Xiao Bingsheng's support behind him, Song Ling's courage grew.","Zichen Hall.","\"Don't you think your son has been acting a bit strange lately?\" Song Yu said.","\"You're the one who's strange, suddenly turning over a new leaf. Even I'm having trouble getting used to it.\"","The corner of Song Yu's mouth twitched. He was asking about Song Ling.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Shihuan, growing fonder the more he looked. Suddenly, the Emperor paused, his voice even trembling slightly.","\"You rascal, look... does Ah Huan not look remarkably like... your mother?\"","Song Yu rolled his eyes. Although he knew the resemblance was strong.","But was the old man losing his mind? Logically, he shouldn't know what Mother looked like when she was young...","\"Have I ever seen what Mother looked like when she was young?\"","Emperor Yuanyou glared at Song Yu. Useless thing.","\"Wu Qi, quickly summon Mei Zhilin here.\"","At this moment, Emperor Yuanyou could care less about anything else. Upon hearing Mei Zhilin's confirmation, the Emperor trembled as he drew Song Shihuan into his embrace.","\"Good child, your grandmother is watching over you from the heavens.\"","How marvelous. The child who looked most like Fen'er had, no matter what, ultimately ended up with the Prince of Qin's household.","\"Imperial Grandfather, do I really look like Imperial Grandmother?\" Song Shihuan's expression was particularly adorable.","Seeing Emperor Yuanyou nod, Song Shihuan pursed her lips:","\"Then if Imperial Grandfather misses Imperial Grandmother, just summon Ah Huan to the palace. Ah Huan will keep you company.\"","What a wonderful granddaughter!","Emperor Yuanyou's heart melted, wishing he could hand over all the keys to his private treasury.","After another long bout of doting between grandfather and granddaughter, Song Yu finally couldn't help but speak up again. \"Father, I was asking if you think Song Ling has been acting strange lately.\"","\"What has he been doing lately?\"","Right.","A wasted question.","\"Old man, I think Song Ling has a problem, a huge problem!\"","Song Yu addressed Emperor Yuanyou directly. Finally, the Emperor's gaze returned to Song Yu, a shoe sole still in his hand.","\"How dare you address me like that, you little brat? Feeling bold, are you?\"","Thus, the next scene in Zichen Hall featured the Prince of Qin running circles around a pillar.","\"Father, Father, please calm down!\"","\"That Song Ling is colluding with rebels. This is a major issue, concerning whether you'll be standing or kneeling when you meet our ancestors in the future!\"","Emperor Yuanyou stopped.","Pointing at Song Yu, he said, \"Speak. Explain everything clearly to me.\"","He, a founding emperor, absolutely could not be kneeling when he met the ancestors!","\"Xiao Bingsheng. I suspect he harbors treasonous ambitions. The evidence is almost all gathered.\"","Song Yu looked at Emperor Yuanyou with a complex expression. The old man had it quite comfortable as emperor, didn't he? Not having to lift a finger while rebels were uncovered.","So, let the old man stay on that dragon throne a few more years this time.","\"Your son has been in very close contact with Xiao Bingsheng recently. The Xiao family is even supplying grain to the Eastern Palace. If they give grain today, who knows if they'll give troops and horses tomorrow.\" Song Yu clicked his tongue. \"The Crown Prince of a nation colluding with rebels... tell me, wouldn't this... make our ancestors rise from their graves in fury?\"","\"Fool!\"","Emperor Yuanyou threw down the shoe sole in his hand, fuming with anger.","How could he have fathered such a stupid son? It must have been the Empress's fault!"]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482: The Dandy Father's Favoritism: I Send Cheng Guang to the Battlefield","paragraphs":["The Hall of Purple Splendor.","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Cheng Guang before him, then shifted his gaze to Song Yu. \"And this is...\"","\"Imperial Father, this is a capable man under my command, named Cheng Guang.\"","As Song Yu spoke, Cheng Guang slowly straightened his back.","\"The evidence of the Xiao family's treason was uncovered by Cheng Guang.\"","\"Explain in detail.\" Emperor Yuanyou's gaze was sharp. As the emperor, what he could least tolerate was anyone harboring rebellious intentions.","Cheng Guang began his account from the dog hole at the Xiao residence, then mentioned the eccentric Old Madam Xiao, thereby unraveling the Xiao family's arrangements outside the capital.","Cheng Guang talked until his lips were dry.","\"However, without obtaining concrete evidence, this remains mere speculation.\" Emperor Yuanyou released his full imperial pressure. Cheng Guang paused, then spoke:","\"His Highness the Crown Prince should... be the evidence, no?\"","Emperor Yuanyou's fury instantly escalated from seven parts to ten.","That useless thing, a complete disgrace.","\"Summon the Crown Prince.\"","At this moment, Emperor Yuanyou no longer merely wished to depose the Crown Prince; he wanted to strip Song Ling of his royal status and expel such a fool from the Song family registry.","Seeing Wu Qi hastening towards the Eastern Palace, Song Yu quietly spoke, \"Imperial Father, please do not be angry later. Just let Cheng Guang question Song Ling.\"","Our side only needs to send Cheng Guang alone to handle the battle.","...","Song Ling used to look forward to coming to the Hall of Purple Splendor, but now, just hearing the name filled him with dread, always feeling it boded no good.","Yet, thinking of the proper matters he had attended to recently, Song Ling felt slightly reassured.","Perhaps his father intended to praise him.","But as soon as Song Ling stepped into the Hall of Purple Splendor, a memorial thrown at him struck his head, its corner nearly scratching his eye.","\"Kneel!\"","Song Ling thudded to his knees. \"Imperial Father, your son is wronged.\"","\"I haven't even said what the matter is, and you're already wronged?\"","Emperor Yuanyou was both angered and amused by Song Ling's foolish appearance. \"Did you know the Xiao family had problems?\"","Seeing the evasiveness in Song Ling's eyes, Emperor Yuanyou spoke to Wu Qi with difficulty, \"Summon Mei Zhilin.\"","He felt himself nearly overcome with anger.","Song Yu gave Cheng Guang a meaningful look. Cheng Guang immediately understood:","\"Might I ask Your Highness the Crown Prince, where did the recent grain and manpower come from?\"","\"Who are you? Who gave you the audacity to question this Crown Prince like this?\"","\"I gave him the audacity!\"","Emperor Yuanyou's roar echoed. Cheng Guang adjusted his sleeve, inwardly thrilled and jumping for joy.","The Great Yue dynasty was indeed not as comfortable as the Great Qi.","\"Please answer my question, Your Highness the Crown Prince.\"","\"The grain was bought with profits from shops under my command, and the manpower is mine.\"","Song Ling spoke, suppressing his anger.","\"However, as far as I know, the Eastern Palace has not been procuring grain recently. On the contrary, the Xiao family has been stockpiling grain. Those manpower are scattered across various prefectures of Great Qi, and they all just happened to send birthday gifts to Old Madam Xiao some time ago.\"","Cheng Guang smiled slightly. \"Your Highness the Crown Prince and the Xiao family are on very good terms.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Your Highness, you have been in close contact with the Xiao family recently. With your intelligence, you must have noticed their impropriety. Yet you still cooperated with such people. Is the position of Crown Prince more important than the safety of Great Qi?\"","Song Yu could barely restrain himself from applauding Cheng Guang.","That sentence was the finishing blow! It was the true grain of sand his old man could not tolerate.","Sure enough, before Song Ling could even open his mouth to refute, Emperor Yuanyou's voice rang out again:","\"Song Ling, if you continue to help the traitors conceal the truth, I will have your head today to console the soldiers who died in the war to found our nation.\"","His father wanted to kill him...","Feeling an unmistakably clear killing intent, Song Ling's legs went weak.","\"I... I'll talk... I'll tell everything...\"","During the period of cooperation, Song Ling had naturally also sensed the Xiao family's impropriety.","But Song Ling wanted the Xiao family's help, so he had no choice but to help conceal their actions.","The more he heard, the more Emperor Yuanyou's anger burned.","Finally, Emperor Yuanyou looked calmly at Song Ling. \"Guards, take him away and hold him under guard.\"","Countless pleas for mercy died on Song Ling's lips when he saw Emperor Yuanyou's expression.","He dared not speak...","\"Shen Xiao.\"","\"Your subject is here.\"","\"Tonight, place a phoenix crown among the birthday gifts for Old Madam Xiao. Tomorrow, take men to raid the Xiao residence and convict the Xiao family on charges of treason using the phoenix crown as evidence.\"","Without concrete evidence, then create evidence.","\"Outside the capital, in all regions, arrest anyone suspected of conspiring with the Xiao family.\"","After speaking, Emperor Yuanyou lowered his head wearily.","Cheng Guang's eyes grew brighter. Truly worthy of a founding emperor; crushing a person was simpler than crushing an ant.","Song Yu curled the corner of his mouth. Indeed, both times, the old man dealt with the Xiao family swiftly and decisively.","After leaving the Hall of Purple Splendor, Cheng Guang trotted happily after him.","\"Your Highness, how was my performance today?\"","\"Not bad.\"","Cheng Guang immediately felt comfortable, utterly satisfied.","\"If Your Highness requires assistance with the subsequent interrogation of the Xiao family, you may summon me at any time.\"","His words could bring more despair than the ten great tortures.","\"Don't worry, you'll have your part.\"","Song Yu hummed a cheerful tune, calculating. The old man was about to depose the Crown Prince.","Tsk.","The Eastern Palace was too weak; it was nearly dead after just a little play.","...","When the Xiao residence was surrounded, Xiao Bingsheng was still pondering which part of his plan had gone wrong.","Upon seeing the phoenix crown that was searched out, Xiao Bingsheng began to doubt his very existence.","He had checked all of his mother's birthday gifts; there absolutely could not have been a phoenix crown.","But who would have the audacity to plant a phoenix crown in the Xiao residence and then use it to imprison the family?","Suddenly, Xiao Bingsheng realized something, his legs giving way as he collapsed to the ground.","Shen Xiao, seeing this, slowly walked to Xiao Bingsheng's side, a bloodthirsty smile in his eyes. \"Lord Xiao, you could have done anything, but you had to engage in treason.\"","\"Now it's fine; all the Xiao family members will keep you company on the road to the Yellow Springs.\"","\"You're framing me!\"","\"Whether it's a frame or not, you know best in your heart.\"","The downfall of the Xiao family came suddenly, but with Emperor Yuanyou's wrath, no one in the court dared utter half a word in their defense.","Under Cheng Guang's mental torment, Xiao Zhang could bear it no longer and began to talk.","Following the clues, Song Yu dug out many more accomplices of the Xiao family.","Half a month later, the Xiao family affair came to a temporary conclusion.","Emperor Yuanyou specially held a palace banquet to dispel the impact the Xiao family incident had on the court.","At the palace banquet.","Emperor Yuanyou drank several extra cups of wine. Recent events flashed through his mind one by one, and his gaze towards Song Yu softened considerably.","It had only been two months since recognizing Ah Huan until now.","Yet many things had undergone earth-shaking changes.","Emperor Yuanyou slowly rose to his feet.","His movement was somewhat unsteady due to the intoxication.","Yet he walked straight to Song Yu and, looking at him, said:","\"Good child, I am very pleased.\"","\"I believe I have truly found a perfect heir to the throne.\""]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483: The Doting Rogue Prince Spoils Me: Verifiable Military Achievements","paragraphs":["The great hall instantly fell silent, even the clinking of cups quickly vanishing.","\"I told you long ago, choosing me as Crown Prince is a sure bet.\"","Song Yu also slowly rose to his feet, swirling the wine in his cup as he extended it towards Emperor Yuanyou. \"So, shall we, father and son, have a toast?\"","\"Cheers.\"","Emperor Yuanyou smiled, the wrinkles at the corners of his eyes deepening as he drained the fine wine in his cup.","\"But I always feel your previous playboy persona wasn't an act.\"","Song Yu laughed.","Emperor Yuanyou pointed a playful, admonishing finger at Song Yu. Regardless, as long as Yu'er was happy, that was all that mattered. Now that Yu'er was willing to become the Crown Prince, he was naturally even more pleased.","This overt display by Emperor Yuanyou did not escape the eyes of the civil and military officials. Their gazes towards Song Yu grew exceptionally fervent.","The Prince of Chu and the Prince of Qi patted their chests in lingering fear. Some of their own subordinates had been uncovered recently. Fortunately, they hadn't obstructed their elder brother's investigation at the time; otherwise, they'd probably be facing a purge now. The two brothers exchanged a look, the same thought surfacing in their hearts: loyalty, they must pledge their loyalty.","\"What are your plans next?\" Emperor Yuanyou was somewhat eager to enjoy the pleasures of grandchildren.","\"Naturally, to help Your Majesty expand the territory, make you bigger and stronger, and secure your throne firmly.\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt the phrasing was odd, but couldn't quite pinpoint why. He simply opted to lower his head and continue drinking.","That night, emboldened by wine, Emperor Yuanyou wrote two edicts: one deposing the Crown Prince and one deposing the Empress.","They were formally announced at the early court session the next morning.","Lady Xu the Younger was confined to the Cold Palace, forbidden to step beyond its gates for eternity.","Song Ling and his family were stripped of their titles and reduced to commoners, confined to a manor on the outskirts of the capital.","As for Lady Chang, she returned unscathed to the Chang residence, all because of Song Shihuan's single sentence: \"Mother Consort treated me very well.\"","Zichen Palace.","\"The Chang family cannot be heavily relied upon in the future, but there's no need to exterminate them either,\" Emperor Yuanyou said while reviewing memorials. \"After all, the Chang family's hands aren't clean either. Regarding Lady Chang, I've already shown exceptional mercy.\"","\"Lady Chang was a qualified mother consort.\"","Song Yu lowered his gaze. \"A child without a mother is pitiful. Since sparing her life can make Ahuan happy, why not do it?\"","Emperor Yuanyou also nodded repeatedly. \"Ahuan is a clever and quick-witted child, quite talented in martial arts too. But you must not let Ahuan overexert herself. She's only a ten-year-old child. If it's really too much, you can send Ahuan to Zichen Palace...\"","\"When it comes to being good to Ahuan, your son understands better than you.\"","With that, Song Yu patted his behind and left. Whenever it involved Ahuan, he and the old man couldn't see eye to eye.","Behind him, Emperor Yuanyou gritted his teeth. \"Wu Qi, what kind of attitude is this rascal showing now? I merely said a few words. Ahuan would be better off raised by my side.\"","Your Majesty, the Eastern Palace is very close to Zichen Palace. In the future, you and the little commandery princess can see each other whenever you wish.","Wu Qi tried to smooth things over with a laugh, thinking of the saying 'when gods fight, little devils suffer'.","Emperor Yuanyou thought this made sense and, throwing down the memorial in his hand, began writing the edict to formally appoint the Crown Prince.","...","The moment he received the edict appointing him Crown Prince, Song Yu felt the weather was clear and everything in the world delightful.","He had returned to where it all began.","In two months, he had protected the childlike innocence in Ahuan's eyes.","Toppled Song Ling and his family.","And gathered the various generals back under his command.","A verifiable track record!","\"Father Prince, you really have become the Crown Prince!\"","Perhaps because he had seen what Ahuan looked like at her coming-of-age ceremony, Song Yu cherished her current appearance, still bearing a hint of baby fat on her face, all the more.","On a whim, Song Yu reached out and pinched her cheek.","\"Yes, from today onwards, Ahuan is the sole daughter of the Crown Prince.\"","Song Yu said with a hooked smile, \"No one can bully Ahuan anymore. Ahuan is going to be the happiest little girl in the whole world.\"","\"Father Prince, I already am.\"","Song Shihuan, dressed in a goose-yellow ruqun skirt, looked as exquisite as an immortal child beneath the seat of Guanyin.","\"I've been thinking lately, it's a good thing Father Prince chose me as his daughter. Otherwise, I'd still be confined in that manor, shedding tears every day.\"","Song Shihuan looked up at Song Yu. \"Thank you, Father Prince, for choosing me as your daughter.\"","Song Yu felt a momentary daze.","One was the innocent and lively Ahuan under his protection; the other was the Ahuan who had gone through countless hardships to find him.","\"I should be the one thanking Ahuan.\"","Thank you, Ahuan, for choosing me as your father prince.","And thank you, Ahuan, for giving me a chance to choose again.","Song Yu's Crown Prince investiture ceremony was extremely grand. Shen Mingwen nearly wore out the books of rites, striving to give Song Yu the most magnificent display within the bounds of protocol.","This time, the ceremonial crown sat perfectly straight on Song Yu's head.","After seeing it, Emperor Yuanyou said with a smile, \"I never thought your temperament would allow that crown to sit so properly on your head.\"","\"The crown must be worn straight.\"","Song Yu, clad in the bright yellow python robe of the Crown Prince, flashed a grin at Emperor Yuanyou. \"If I don't wear it straight, Father will just nag me again.\"","Emperor Yuanyou held Song Yu's hand, listening as the hundred officials hailed \"Long live the Crown Prince.\"","This wasn't Emperor Yuanyou's first time experiencing such a scene, but when he had invested Song Ling as Crown Prince, he hadn't felt this stirred. Back then, his mind was full of whether Song Ling would treat his brothers kindly in the future and not wipe them out.","After the ceremony concluded, Song Yu moved into the Eastern Palace with Song Shihuan.","Once everything was settled, Song Yu ran to Zichen Palace, said something to Emperor Yuanyou, and was chased out by the emperor's shoe sole.","Song Yu wasn't angry. Instead, he called out loudly towards the hall, \"Your son will take that as your agreement!\"","Then he returned to the Eastern Palace and led Song Shihuan towards the direction of the Cold Palace.","...","The Cold Palace was gloomy and sinister; even in the heat of July, it made one's whole body feel cold.","Seeing Lady Xu the Younger again, Song Yu was dressed in the Crown Prince's python robe, and Song Shihuan was also splendidly attired. The contrast with Lady Xu the Younger, who sat withered on a chair, was like heaven and earth.","\"So, in the end, it's you who became Crown Prince.\"","That bright yellow stung Lady Xu the Younger's eyes.","\"I still didn't surpass my elder sister.\"","\"The Emperor is truly ruthless,\" Lady Xu the Younger said with a bitter smile. \"He believed you without hesitation, casting me and Ling'er into the abyss, without even giving us a chance to explain.\"","\"Weren't you the one who framed me all those years ago? Still pretending at this point.\"","Song Yu rolled his eyes. \"I came today simply to tell you, your suffering isn't over yet. I did vow to make you beg for death but find it impossible.\"","\"Actually, I somewhat regret it. If I had told Father when I was young that you were a venomous, scheming woman, then Song Ling probably wouldn't have become Crown Prince either.\"","\"Can't be helped. Who made me Mother Empress's son? Father loves me to the bone.\"","Every word from Song Yu was like a needle stabbing into Lady Xu the Younger.","Finally, Song Yu ruffled Song Shihuan's head.","\"The only good thing you did was give birth to Song Ling, who then gave birth to Ahuan. Tell me, that child I strangled with my own hands back then—do you think the King of Hell recorded that debt on my account, or on yours?\"","With that, Song Yu strode away triumphantly.","Leaving Lady Xu the Younger behind, clutching her head and weeping."]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Sorry, It Seems Your Son-in-Law is Gone","paragraphs":["\"Father, where are we going now?\"","In the carriage, Song Shihuan asked while nibbling on pastries.","\"To the estate in the outskirts of the capital, to deliver good news to Song Ling.\"","Song Yu's brows lifted, brimming with triumph. He couldn't even imagine what kind of spectacular expression Song Ling would make upon seeing him in the Crown Prince's python robe.","\"The books say this is called... kicking someone when they're down.\" Song Shihuan tilted her head, thinking that 'kicking someone when they're down' didn't seem like a nice phrase.","\"Exactly, we're going to kick him while he's down.\"","Song Yu had even considered whether to bring Cheng Guang along, but ultimately decided against it for fear of angering Song Ling to death.","After all, he still needed Song Ling to witness his ascension to the throne with his own eyes.","Half an hour later, the carriage arrived at an estate.","Song Ling sat in the courtyard, his eyes vacant. Screams from Song Xiyan and the angry shouts of Song Yanzheng and the others echoed out from time to time.","They were neither human nor ghost.","It wasn't until Song Yu and Song Shihuan appeared before Song Ling that a glint finally sparked in his eyes—one born of sheer fury.","\"You've become the Crown Prince?\"","Song Ling's eyes reddened with rage.","\"What, isn't this attire obvious enough?\"","Song Yu even turned around rather narcissistically, allowing Song Ling a clear view of his robes.","\"No sooner was I deposed than you were immediately installed as Crown Prince. His Majesty truly couldn't wait.\"","\"Attendants, slap his mouth.\"","Song Yu's face suddenly turned stern. Liuxi immediately stepped forward and delivered two loud slaps to Song Ling's face.","\"Now that you are a commoner, how dare you address the Emperor as 'Father'?\"","\"Song Ling, after all your meticulous scheming for so long, when you fell, no one intervened on your behalf. Instead, I was enfeoffed as Crown Prince, becoming the choice favored by all. If I were you, I'd be so ashamed I'd slit my own throat.\"","Song Yu shook his head repeatedly. Nothing was more satisfying than sitting in your enemy's former position and looking down upon them.","\"And what about her? I am already a commoner. She is my daughter, so she should be a commoner too.\"","\"Liuxi, slap him again.\"","The previous two slaps from Liuxi had landed on Song Ling's left cheek. This time, Liuxi struck the right cheek without hesitation, making it perfectly symmetrical.","\"Liuxi, tell Song Ling who stands before him.\"","Upon hearing this, Liuxi promptly cleared his throat:","\"It is the Great Qi Crown Prince and his only daughter, the Fu'an County Princess.\"","\"Song Ling, abandon your unspeakable schemes. Keep your eyes wide open and watch how I am revered by the masses. My birth is superior to yours, and everything about me will surpass you.\"","Song Ling stared blankly at Song Shihuan.","Suddenly, Song Ling spoke, \"You are the lucky star.\"","Yet, Song Shihuan's eyes held no trace of fear towards Song Ling. He was merely her father's defeated foe, one who hadn't even lasted two months.","\"That's right. Both Father and His Majesty the Emperor have said that I am the lucky star.\"","As Song Shihuan turned to leave, the sound of Song Ling's wretched laughter came from behind, chilling to the bone.","\"Ahuan, how is your fist technique practice coming along lately?\"","\"Quite some progress.\" Song Shihuan was evidently being somewhat modest.","Hearing this, Song Yu chuckled softly. \"None of the children Song Ling sired are any good. Go use them as punching bags, give them a beating. Help those they bullied vent their anger.\"","\"Really? Can I?\"","Song Shihuan's eyes uncontrollably lit up.","Although, apart from Song Xiyan, these people hadn't really offended her much, she just had an overwhelming urge to hit someone.","\"Of course you can. Go ahead.\"","Soon after, the successive screams of several people could be heard, especially from Song Yanzheng and Song Xiyan, whose cries were the most piercing.","Song Shihuan pounded on them for a full half-hour before returning, panting and out of breath, to stand before Song Yu. Her eyes were gleaming brightly, and beads of sweat had formed on her forehead.","\"Feel better now?\" Song Yu asked with a smile.","\"Much better.\"","It felt absolutely wonderful. She couldn't wait to go to the Gu residence immediately to share this good news with Mingzhu. This counted as personally avenging Mingzhu.","Thinking of this, Song Shihuan asked:","\"Father, can we go to the Gu family?\"","\"Of course we can.\"","In high spirits, Song Yu directly took Song Shihuan to the Gu residence.","...","At the Gu residence.","Just listening to Song Shihuan's account, Gu Mingzhu felt immense satisfaction.","\"County Princess, for such delightful matters in the future, could you take me along?\" Gu Mingzhu rubbed her hands eagerly. \"Otherwise, your hands might hurt from hitting them.\"","Such tasks should be handled by her, Gu Mingzhu!","Song Shihuan was both amused and exasperated.","Beside them, Song Yu shot several sharp glances at Gu Mingzhu. This little girl was quite fierce, no wonder Gu Zheng had always shielded her from contact with the royal family before.","Song Yu and Song Shihuan stayed for a simple meal at the Gu residence.","At the dining table, Gu Zheng seemed somewhat troubled.","\"General Gu, is something troubling you?\"","\"To be frank with Your Highness, it's my eldest daughter. She has reached marriageable age. Recently, I've reviewed many potential candidates, but none seem suitable.\" Gu Zheng said while downing a cup of wine. \"Seeing her days being delayed like this, I'm growing anxious.\"","Song Yu's previously relaxed posture instantly tensed up.","Oh dear, trouble's brewing.","He had sent a lot of grain to the northern frontier. Would Yu Fan still come seeking her in the capital?","Had he accidentally ruined Gu Zheng's perfect son-in-law?","Seeing Song Yu's sudden tension, Gu Zheng misunderstood and hurriedly explained, \"I absolutely have no intention of marrying my daughter into the Eastern Palace.\"","Song Yu grew even more tense.","After struggling for a long time, he only managed to blurt out, \"General Gu, perhaps you could try a martial contest to choose a husband?\"","\"A martial contest to choose a husband... that is indeed a good method.\"","Gu Zheng didn't dwell too much on Gu Mingliu's marriage matters, instead continuing to discuss future military campaigns with Song Yu.","But Song Yu could hardly focus on listening.","This won't do. A fine son-in-law like Yu Fan—he couldn't be the one to ruin a good match.","Under Song Yu's vigorous urging, the martial contest for marriage was scheduled for August.","Song Yu specifically ordered someone to spread this news to the village in the northern frontier where Yu Fan's family lived.","\"What on earth is in the northern frontier?\"","Shen Qingping looked puzzled. For the past few days, His Highness hadn't attended to a single piece of official business, just kept his eyes fixed on the northern frontier.","\"There's a person.\"","Song Yu was worried, so worried he'd even lost a strand of hair.","\"They say it's better to destroy ten temples than to break up a single marriage. Look at the mess I've made.\"","He still needed to rely on Yu Fan for future battles.","If it weren't for the fact that the person before him was Song Yu, Shen Qingping would have cursed him as a lunatic.","Song Yu haunted the reports from the northern frontier like a ghost.","Only when news came from the northern frontier that a thin, frail young man had set off for the capital, seemingly to participate in the martial contest for marriage, did Song Yu finally let out a heavy sigh of relief.","The moment Yu Fan arrived in the capital, Song Yu grabbed him by the collar and dragged him before Gu Zheng.","Straightening his spine, Song Yu bellowed at Gu Zheng:","\"General Gu, cancel the martial contest. Your son-in-law has arrived.\""]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485: The Dandy Father's Favoritism Towards Me: Drawing the Defense Deployment Maps of Dayue and the Northern Di","paragraphs":["Gu Mingliu and Yu Fan's grand wedding ceremony placed Song Yu at the head table.","Unlike before, when Yu Fan only began his loyalty to the Prince of Qin's household after being introduced by Gu Zheng, this time, Yu Fan knelt directly before Song Yu.","\"Thank you, Your Highness the Crown Prince, for your aid to the northern frontier. Yu Fan is willing to dedicate all his abilities and pledge his loyalty to Your Highness.\"","Song Yu merely smiled and helped Yu Fan to his feet. \"Are the people in your village all receiving grain now?\"","Others only praised Song Yu for sending grain to the northern frontier, unaware that he had nearly exhausted half the Prince of Qin's household fortune to do so.","The grain sent north was enough to provide the frontier people with sustenance for a considerable time.","\"They are,\" Yu Fan replied, his eyes glistening with tears. \"Erya was nearly starved to death. She was fortunate to survive thanks to the grain you sent; now she's alive and kicking.\"","\"As long as it was useful.\"","Song Yu thought for a moment before speaking again. \"Your loyalty is not just to me, but to Great Qi. To become a general trusted by the people of Great Qi—do you have the confidence?\"","\"Can I... really become a general?\"","\"Yu Fan, you can.\"","Song Yu made a fist with his right hand and playfully thumped Yu Fan's chest.","Yu Fan's eyes, fierce as a tiger's, reddened. To receive such trust from the Crown Prince left him with no regrets in this life.","Song Yu was unusually drunk. Seeing his high spirits, no one stopped him. Song Shihuan had long been dragged off by Gu Mingzhu to buy all sorts of snacks on the street, so the inebriated Song Yu was escorted back to his residence by Shen Qingping.","\"Shen the Third.\"","Song Yu looked at Shen Qingping. \"Does it hurt?\"","\"Your Highness, that's a strange question. I'm not injured, why would I be in pain?\"","Shen Qingping assumed Song Yu was drunk and turned to instruct Liuxi to prepare some sobering soup for him.","Song Yu buried his face in the pillow.","After the Qing Mountain Sect Leader awoke, he and Ah Huan had secretly asked if the Sect Leader knew about Shen Qingping's fate in their previous life. The Sect Leader had been stunned for a long moment before telling them.","Shen Qingping had died.","Like a moth flying into a flame.","As for the specific details of his death, the Sect Leader said he hadn't dared to ask.","Under those circumstances, he simply couldn't bring himself to ask a father grieving the loss of his child about the cause of Shen Qingping's death.","Ah Huan had cried for a long time that day.","She wept for their wretched ends in that past life—all three of them.","\"Your Highness, remember to drink the sobering soup later. Otherwise, when the Princess returns and sees you in this state, she'll ignore you for days again.\"","\"Also, all those court matters have been settled. The officials are now as meek as mice. If you wish to lead troops on a campaign, the opportunity is there.\"","Listening to Shen Qingping's chatter, Song Yu took a deep breath.","\"Shen the Third.\"","\"What is it?\" Shen Qingping found Song Yu particularly odd tonight.","\"Nothing. It's late, hurry back to your residence. Don't always worry so much; you'll age quickly.\"","\"Your Highness is several years my senior. If anyone ages first, it will be you.\"","Song Yu laughed. He had known since childhood that this study companion of his was exceedingly clever.","He just preferred not to show it, his great wisdom appearing as folly.","Now, he would not let the moth fly into the flame again. Shen the Third would only become the Chancellor of Great Qi.","His trusted confidant, Ah Huan's tutor, would stand in a position second only to one, above ten thousand others.","......","In the ninth month, the new Crown Prince brought a completely revitalized atmosphere to the court.","The officials all behaved themselves, because Cheng Guang had formally entered the court and, upon Song Yu's strong recommendation, had been appointed as a Censor.","A single man censoring a hundred, he gave Emperor Yuanyou a headache so severe it became an ailment triggered merely by the sight of Cheng Guang.","In the Zichen Hall.","\"Cheng Guang requested leave tomorrow? Excellent!\"","Emperor Yuanyou had never approved an official's leave request so swiftly.","\"It's just Cheng Guang, is it really such a big deal?\" Song Yu remarked from the side, mimicking Emperor Yuanyou's previous tone.","Back then, when Cheng Guang had given him splitting headaches, the already-retired Emperor Yuanyou had fancied adding fuel to the fire, watching the commotion without concern.","It had infuriated Song Yu to the point of wanting to return the imperial seal on the spot.","This time, it was Emperor Yuanyou who was hopping mad.","\"This Cheng Guang is nothing but a troublemaker! He even impeaches officials for spending a few extra nights in their concubines' chambers, forcing me to deal with such trivial nonsense.\"","\"It's to prevent courtiers from favoring concubines over their wives. Nowadays, no one dares visit the Spring Welcome House anymore, Father. That's Cheng Guang's merit.\" Since the trouble wasn't landing on his own head, Song Yu was happy to play the good guy. \"People with real talent often can't be treated ordinarily. Please bear with him a little more, Father.\"","\"You're so magnanimous and tolerant. Why don't you take over as emperor?\"","Emperor Yuanyou smiled at Song Yu. With this Cheng Guang around, not only were the civil and military officials cautious in their conduct, even he, the emperor, was on tenterhooks, fearing Cheng Guang might impeach him too.","\"Father, you flatter me too much.\"","Song Yu suppressed a laugh. \"I was just about to discuss with you my plans to lead a military expedition.\"","\"Lead an expedition?\" Emperor Yuanyou set down the memorial in his hand. \"Who do you want to fight?\"","\"Great Yue and the Northern Di. Both.\"","\"Great Yue is a match for Great Qi. Conquering them outright won't be easy.\" Emperor Yuanyou, an emperor who had risen through military campaigns, naturally understood how difficult a war with Great Yue would be.","Song Yu gave a low chuckle, then looked up at Emperor Yuanyou.","\"Father, what if I could draw their defense maps?\"","Emperor Yuanyou's breath hitched.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I mean, I can draw detailed defense maps of Great Yue and the Northern Di, precise down to the commanders of each prefecture and the number of troops stationed there. Wouldn't that make the fight much easier?\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt he was dreaming. Of course, Song Yu must be dreaming too.","It wasn't until Song Yu summoned Gu Zheng and the other military commanders and, in front of everyone, spent a full half-hour drawing, completing the defense map of Great Yue, that Emperor Yuanyou fully snapped back to reality. He reached out and slapped his own face. It hurt. This wasn't a dream.","\"You... where did you obtain such top-secret information?\"","\"During the years I pretended to be a wastrel, I sent spies to infiltrate Great Yue and the Northern Di multiple times. This defense map was gradually compiled from their intelligence.\"","Gu Zheng's eyes also burned with fervor. With this map, attacking Great Yue would be far too easy.","\"Your Majesty, Heaven favors Great Qi!\"","The assembled generals knelt and proclaimed loudly. Emperor Yuanyou was beside himself with joy.","\"The campaign against Great Yue and the Northern Di is approved! Let the Crown Prince serve as the commander-in-chief. Depart on an auspicious day!\"","With that, Emperor Yuanyou hurriedly left the Zichen Hall. He had to go offer three sticks of incense to the ancestors and to Fen'er, thanking them for granting him such an excellent son.","Basking in the admiration of all present, Song Yu gave a roguish smile.","To tell the truth, the defense map of Great Yue at this time was actually something Cheng Guang had later bragged about to him, just to show off how capable he was in helping Emperor Mingde ascend the throne.","He just happened to have a good memory, that's all.","For this performance to be so perfect, he really owed Cheng Guang a big thank you."]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486: The Dandy Prince Spoils Me: How Dare the Great Qi Envoy","paragraphs":["The Eastern Palace.","\"What... Your Highness intends to... to attack Dayue...\"","Looking at the sickly Cheng Guang before him, Song Yu twitched the corner of his mouth fiercely.","\"You've rarely taken leave. Rest properly at your residence today.\"","This relentless drive of his is truly a match for Shen San's. No wonder they both managed to prop up that useless Emperor Mingde onto the throne.","\"I am very familiar with Dayue. Allow me to accompany you on this campaign. Perhaps it could save the lives of several soldiers.\"","For a moment, Song Yu seemed to see the former Dayue Prime Minister from his past life, who had tried to take his own life after being captured.","\"Very well. Once you have recovered your health, I will take you along. It will also give His Majesty some peace and quiet.\"","Upon hearing this, Cheng Guang hurriedly expressed his gratitude, not even minding the teasing in Song Yu's words.","\"Your Highness, have you considered under what pretext we will launch this campaign?\"","Song Yu fell silent, evidently also constrained by this very question.","Previously, it was because Rong Lingchen secretly harmed His Majesty, giving Dagi a justifiable reason to send troops. But what about this time?","\"I have a plan.\"","\"Find someone terminally ill and nearing death. Promise them sufficient wealth and reputation to secure their wife and children's prosperity for life. Then, order them to serve as an envoy to Dayue and die there.\"","Song Yu was stunned.","But Cheng Guang gave a foolish-seeming laugh. \"Throughout history books, the death of an envoy is the vanguard for an army pressing at the borders!\"","The envoy's death is the bugle call for attack.","\"Allow me to think on this.\"","After Cheng Guang left, Song Shihuan emerged from behind the screen.","\"Ahuan, do you think Cheng Guang's plan is feasible?\"","Song Shihuan pondered for a moment before speaking slowly, \"Whether it's feasible is not for me to say, nor for you, Father. It is for those who meet the conditions to decide.\"","\"If someone is willing to go as an envoy, then it is feasible.\"","\"If no one is willing, then we should not force it.\"","\"I understand,\" Song Yu said, gently pinching Song Shihuan's little face. \"For this campaign, how about I take you along, Ahuan? I heard you mention before that your master taught you many battle formations. They might come in handy this time.\"","Song Shihuan nodded, yet a touch of desolation appeared.","\"I wonder where Master is now... if he has abandoned me.\"","Thinking of the Qing Mountain Sect Leader, the smile on Song Yu's face faded slightly.","\"Your master taught you so much, which shows he is very fond of you, our Ahuang. He must have encountered some difficulty. After the war, I will take you to find him.\"","Song Yu's words moved Song Shihuan. Yes, how could her master abandon her?","Thinking of this, a hint of urgency appeared in Song Shihuan's eyes. \"Alright. When the time comes, Father will accompany me to find Master. I miss him very much.\"","......","After several days of searching, they indeed found a veteran soldier who perfectly met the requirements.","\"If you are willing to serve as an envoy to Dayue, your wife and children will be well cared for and live in peace and comfort for the rest of their lives,\" Song Yu personally met with this veteran. \"If you are unwilling, I will have you escorted safely back home.\"","The veteran soldier knelt before Song Yu. \"Your Highness the Crown Prince, this humble general is old, but my heart is not old. I long to kill on the battlefield once more, and would be willing even to die.\"","\"Now that such an opportunity exists, even without any reward, this humble general is willing to do it.\"","\"If my dying body can be exchanged for Dagi's territory expanding twofold, I have no regrets.\"","His time was already short. If he could, in his final days, exchange it for an opportunity to found his own branch on the family register, it would be a blessing from heaven.","\"What is your name?\" Song Yu couldn't help but ask.","\"This humble general is Xin Ling.\"","Before Xin Ling departed, Song Shihuan came running out to see him off.","\"This is a flower unique to Dagi. I dried it. Please carry it with you. There is no need to long for Dagi, for in the near future, every place beneath your feet will belong to Dagi.\"","At this moment, Song Shihuan's eyes and brows were radiant with confidence, as vibrant as Dagi's future blooming with flowers.","\"Thank you, Princess. This humble general... bids farewell.\"","Xin Ling went to Dayue under the pretext of celebrating the old Emperor of Dayue's birthday. On the second day after his arrival, during the old Emperor's birthday banquet, he made outrageous statements.","He said the old Emperor had only one month left to live.","\"How dare you! How dare you speak such insolence! Are all those raised by Dagi as ill-mannered as you?\"","Xin Ling, enraged to the point of vomiting blood, pointed at the noses of the Dayue imperial family. \"You may insult me, but insulting Dagi is unacceptable! How can my Dagi suffer such humiliation!\"","With that, he rushed towards a guard's waist sword, drew it, and slit his own throat.","Everything happened too suddenly. Dayue, looking at the lifeless Xin Ling, was utterly dumbstruck.","The envoy from Dagi was... strange.","It wasn't until Dagi's battle drums sounded the charge, and they attacked several Dayue cities under the pretext of seeking justice for Xin Ling, that Dayue realized they had been tricked.","Yet, the Dagi soldiers, who seemed to know Dayue's defenses inside out, descended like divine troops. No matter what, they always struck at the places Dayue couldn't grasp, delivering fatal blows.","Add to that Cheng Guang, who understood the temperament of the Dayue imperial family like the back of his hand, overseeing the army.","And Song Shihuan, who employed troops with god-like skill...","Song Yu hardly needed to do anything. With just a few simple words to boost morale, the army advanced straight to the capital of Dayue.","Standing once again outside the walls of the Dayue capital, Song Yu was filled with emotion.","This war was fought much more easily than before.","He had completely won by lying down.","\"Your Highness, once we breach the capital, Dayue will be ours!\" Cheng Guang's eyes shone, wishing he could charge right in.","He showed no sense of consciousness befitting someone originally from Dayue.","\"Yu Fan.\"","Song Yu called to Yu Fan. At this moment, Yu Fan was surrounded by a palpable aura of killing intent. Throughout this campaign, the number of enemies Yu Fan had slain was countless.","\"Your subordinate is here.\"","\"Once we attack the capital later, remember to capture the Second Prince Rong Sheng and his son Rong Lingchen for me. I have some personal grievances with these two and need to settle them separately.\"","Hearing Song Yu's gritted-teeth tone, everyone present silently lit three metaphorical candles in their hearts for this father and son.","At this stage, offending the Crown Prince was no different from offending heaven itself.","......","At Song Yu's command, the army stormed into the Dayue capital.","Song Yu and Song Shihuan met the decrepit old Emperor of Dayue.","\"How did our Dagi envoy offend you?\" Song Yu asked with a somewhat roguish smile, but the young girl beside him had reddened eyes.","\"He... he said I had only one month left to live.\"","The old Emperor's voice was full of panic. \"If someone said that to your face, you would be angry too! And he slit his own throat; I did not order his death.\"","\"Our Dagi envoy is dead. I have no heart to debate right and wrong now.\"","Song Yu, holding a dagger, swiftly plunged it into the old Emperor's heart.","\"He wasn't wrong. You did indeed have only one month left to live, because one month later is now.\"","The old Emperor died, and the Dayue imperial family was captured in its entirety.","The once equally matched Dayue thus vanished from the pages of history.","\"Ahuan, this past month, did you fight to your heart's content?\"","\"To my heart's content. It was exhilarating.\"","Song Shihuan rode her blood-sweating steed, her body slightly leaning forward, holding the reins. Her brow was filled with high spirits:","\"Father, one day, all lands touched by the sun and moon, all places reached by rivers, will be the territory of our Dagi.\""]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487: The Dandy Father's Favoritism: When Shen Ye Crosses Paths, Kings Avoid Each Other","paragraphs":["Song Yu had thoroughly consolidated his position as Crown Prince through the Great Yue campaign. On the day of his triumphant return to the capital, Emperor Yuanyou was uncharacteristically sentimental.","\"Minister Shen, I feel as if I'm dreaming.\"","In just half a year, everything had turned upside down.","And all the changes had begun from the day Ahuan was found and brought back.","\"I... I also feel as if I'm dreaming.\"","Watching Song Yu return laden with military achievements, now eloquent and learned, Shen Mingwen couldn't shake the feeling that something had been stolen from him.","He had discreetly asked the Emperor several times if he had secretly found a tutor for the Crown Prince, but the Emperor had flatly denied it each time.","Could the Crown Prince have become so accomplished through self-study?","Shen Mingwen shook his head regretfully. He had even dreamt of becoming the Emperor's teacher himself.","\"Your son has fulfilled the mission and returned victorious.\"","Song Yu stood tall and clear-eyed, his bearing dignified.","\"Elder Brother, next time there's such a good opportunity, take your younger brother along, alright?\"","Before Emperor Yuanyou could speak, Prince Qi jumped out. Now that the streets and alleys were all praising his elder brother, if he could fight and win a battle alongside him, wouldn't he share in the fame? Prince Qi was eager to prove his own worth.","\"The next battle might be against Mobei,\" Song Yu said, his gaze towards Prince Qi carrying a hint of deeper meaning.","\"Mobei is excellent!\" Prince Qi grinned, revealing his white teeth. \"Little brother loves fighting Mobei the most. To be honest, just hearing 'Mobei' fills me with an inexplicable hatred, a firm resolve to wipe them out!\"","\"Good. I'll take you next time.\" Song Yu looked at Prince Qi, thinking he now resembled a silly roe deer.","Seeing this, Prince Chu, who was standing nearby, also spoke up timidly, \"I... I want to go too...\"","Prince Chu had recently had many people around him get into trouble. Although he had chosen to uphold justice by cutting ties with them, he still found it somewhat difficult to meet Song Yu's eyes directly.","\"Everyone goes together.\"","With Song Yu's one sentence, Prince Chu immediately began bobbing his head and followed behind him. Seeing this scene, Emperor Yuanyou suddenly smiled as well.","\"Let's go, into the palace.\"","Emperor Yuanyou, holding little Song Shihuan's hand, had taken just one step when he stopped again. He called out towards a head that wasn't well-hidden on the city wall, \"You little rascal from the Gu family, come into the palace with us as well.\"","Gu Zheng's eyelid twitched.","Gu Mingzhu quickly ran down, bowed to Emperor Yuanyou, but her bright eyes remained fixed on Song Shihuan.","A day apart felt like three years.","She missed the princess, Song Shihuan, sincerely every day.","Third Uncle Shen had said that once her martial arts improved a bit more, she could also go to war and even become a female general.","...","At the palace banquet.","Song Yu smiled faintly as he clinked cups with Shen Qingping. \"Chief Minister Shen of the Dali Temple has uncovered so many cold cases; your governance is truly effective.\"","Seeing Song Yu's feigned manner, Shen Qingping couldn't help but lower his head. \"It cannot compare to Your Highness's merit of expanding our territory.\"","\"Teacher, I just heard Nian'an say there's a particularly skilled female coroner at the Dali Temple?\" Song Shihuan's face slowly leaned in.","\"I've heard about that too. Third Uncle Shen often takes that female coroner on cases,\" Gu Mingzhu chimed in, propping her chin on her hand. \"I even ran into them once.\"","The two girls' curiosity, however, instantly turned into alarm for Song Yu.","\"What is that female coroner's name?\"","\"Yue Qing,\" Shen Qingping replied. \"Her methods of examining corpses are exceptional. She contributed greatly to solving those cold cases.\"","\"Shen the Third, you haven't taken a fancy to her, have you?\" Song Yu wore a look of utter distress. \"You two aren't suitable, truly not suitable.\"","Good heavens, Yue Qing is Feng Kuizhi's wife.","One mustn't play matchmaker recklessly.","Song Yu felt as if facing a great enemy. He even glanced towards the two families who, in his previous life, had married their daughters to Zheng Fang and Ling Ming. Surely they wouldn't be arranging marriages for their daughters this early now?","In that short moment, Song Yu's mind had already staged a whole drama of wrong bride, wrong groom.","Shen Qingping twitched the corner of his mouth speechlessly. What he wanted to say got stuck for a long while, finally transforming into one sentence:","\"Is the Crown Prince perhaps thinking of taking a Crown Princess?\"","\"Ah?\" Song Yu's mouth fell open.","\"Someone who is thinking of marriage sees everyone else as wanting to marry.\" Shen Qingping said expressionlessly, \"My relationship with Yue Qing is strictly professional. Your Highness should go and wash your eyes.\"","\"Father, how does one wash their eyes?\"","Meeting Song Shihuan's teasing gaze, Song Yu pinched her cheek.","\"Daring to make fun of your old man now?\"","\"Hel...p...\" Song Shihuan wailed.","...","That night, Shen Mingwen got thoroughly drunk.","The servant behind him couldn't hold back Shen Mingwen, who was heading straight for the Ye residence.","The Ye residence was a small house, devoid of any valuable objects. After Shen Mingwen knocked, it was even Ye Shijie himself who opened the door.","Seeing the drunken Shen Mingwen before him, Ye Shijie didn't think twice and made to shut the door, but Shen Mingwen shoved it open.","Grabbing Ye Shijie by the collar, Shen Mingwen roared:","\"Ye Shijie, have you been secretly teaching the Crown Prince his lessons?\"","Ye Shijie: ???","\"You old thing, your ambition never dies! You were so infuriated by His Highness back then it made you spit blood, and yet you still sneak around trying to mold a future ruler.\" Shen Mingwen at this moment looked very much like a husband catching his spouse in infidelity. \"You just want to be the Emperor's Teacher, don't think I don't know.\"","\"What are you talking about? I don't understand.\" Ye Shijie frowned. He had heard about the Crown Prince pretending to be a wastrel while actually being learned.","But he would stake his head on it—the one who infuriated him to the point of spitting blood back then was a genuine, bona fide wastrel.","If there had been even half a drop of ink in his belly, he couldn't possibly have been angered to that extent.","So, Ye Shijie had actually suspected Shen Mingwen of secretly tutoring the Crown Prince.","\"You didn't teach him? Then why... why does His Highness's policy essay bear traces of your style?\" Shen Mingwen felt as if his heart was being sliced by a knife, pulling out a policy essay from his robe.","When Ye Shijie saw it, he felt like he was looking in a mirror.","\"That's not right. The Crown Prince's policy essay clearly bears traces of your style.\" Ye Shijie also pulled out a policy essay from his own robe.","When Shen Mingwen saw it, he also felt like he was looking in a mirror.","\"Huh?\" Shen Mingwen was bewildered.","\"Huh?\" Ye Shijie was also somewhat dumbfounded.","\"It seems there is another master giving guidance...\" Shen Mingwen sniffed. \"Someone familiar with both our styles, combining the strengths of various schools, taught His Highness.\"","\"If that's truly the case, then I accept it.\" Ye Shijie looked at Shen Mingwen, and his attitude suddenly improved.","It was a pity that the Emperor's Teacher wasn't himself.","But as long as it wasn't Shen Mingwen, then it wasn't so bad after all.","A quarter of an hour later, wine cups were placed before both of them.","\"Don't let me find out who the future Emperor's Teacher is!\"","Shen Mingwen issued a fierce threat.","Ye Shijie's gaze was also growing hazy. \"Old Shen, do you think if I had held back and not spat out that mouthful of blood back then, the future Emperor's Teacher would have been me?\"","Shen Mingwen shot a glance at Ye Shijie:","\"Don't do that to yourself.\""]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488: The Dandy Father's Unconditional Favor: Tearing Up Everyone Else's Umbrellas","paragraphs":["\"Why didn't your father attend court today?\"","After the morning court session, Song Yu looked curiously at Shen Qingping. Shen Mingwen's attendance at court was as diligent as Cheng Guang's; he would never request leave without an important reason.","\"He's drunk.\"","Shen Qingping had never imagined a day when his father would be too hungover to get up for court.","Song Yu couldn't help but widen his eyes. \"Who did he drink with to end up like that?\"","\"Ye Shijie.\"","Song Yu suddenly felt a pang of guilt.","When those two got together, he wanted to stay as far away as possible.","\"Let's go. Weren't we supposed to go to the Shen residence today to see my two potted flowers?\" Shen Qingping walked a few steps forward but noticed the person behind him remained rooted to the spot as if nailed to the ground.","\"Your Highness, why aren't you coming?\"","\"Suddenly remembered I have some matters to attend to...\"","In merely the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, Song Yu swiftly disappeared from Shen Qingping's sight.","\"Third Master, His Highness seemed a bit strange today,\" Nian'an whispered.","\"Is there any day His Highness isn't strange?\"","Nian'an was taken aback for a moment; it seemed His Highness was indeed strange every day.","Song Yu walked idly along the palace path, feeling as if he couldn't return home.","\"Liuxi, what if I go back now and chase Lady Chang away?\"","Liuxi's mouth twitched involuntarily. \"Your Highness, Lady Chang already follows your rule, visiting the Crown Princess only once every half month for just two hours each time. If you drive her away now, the Crown Princess will be upset.\"","Song Yu's features contorted briefly.","Steeling himself, he headed towards the Eastern Palace.","......","Eastern Palace.","Song Shihuan nestled in Lady Chang's embrace. Lady Chang held Song Shihuan's hand, patiently teaching her how to paint.","Midway, Song Shihuan mischievously wriggled her right hand, causing a drop of ink to splatter onto the paper. Song Yu, peeking from outside the courtyard, felt his scalp tighten at the sight.","He suddenly began to doubt whether making Gu Mingzhu Ahuan's study companion was a good idea.","Ahuan's behavior was exactly like a carbon copy of Gu Mingzhu!","\"Naughty.\"","Lady Chang wasn't angry. With a few brushstrokes, she seamlessly incorporated the stray ink blot into the painting.","\"Mother, you're amazing.\"","Song Shihuan lifted her little face. \"Mother is well-versed in the Four Books and Five Classics, proficient in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting. Grandaunt told me that Mother was once the most accomplished noble lady in the capital. I am Mother's daughter, I must not bring you shame.\"","Lady Chang kissed Song Shihuan's fair, tender cheek. \"Ahuan, I will teach you anything you wish to learn. But you don't have to measure yourself by others' standards. As long as Ahuan is happy, that's all that matters.\"","Song Yu watched the scene in the courtyard, his expression gradually growing complex.","In the courtyard, after finishing the painting, Song Shihuan pestered Lady Chang to style her hair, chattering nonstop about her favorite hair ornament styles, gesturing with her little hands as she spoke. Lady Chang nodded continuously.","\"Mother will go buy them for Ahuan later.\"","\"I also want a little rabbit sachet. Mingzhu said General Gu bought one for her, and it's especially pretty.\"","Song Yu's expression changed abruptly.","Why didn't Ahuan ask him, her father, to buy it?","\"Mother, I want to hear a lullaby. Grandma used to sing them to me. It's been so long since I've heard one.\"","By the time the two hours were up, Song Shihuan had already fallen asleep on the reclining chair.","Lady Chang carefully covered Song Shihuan with a thin blanket and walked towards the courtyard exit.","His Highness the Crown Prince was excellent in every way, except for being overly petty. If she overstayed, he would find ways to prevent her from seeing Ahuan again.","As she reached the courtyard exit, Lady Chang saw Song Yu.","Song Yu gave a slight nod and strode past Lady Chang.","It was good.","What he never had, Ahuan now possessed.","Song Yu carried the little one back to her room. Then, he personally went out of the palace to buy several little rabbit sachets, finally returning home satisfied.","In matters like this, the spotlight should still be on the father!","......","October.","The territories originally belonging to Great Yue were completely annexed by Great Qi. Officials were gradually assigned to various regions, leading to a shortage of personnel at court. It was at this time that Song Yu proposed the addition of a special imperial examination.","\"Excellent. This year, with the investiture of the Crown Prince and the conquest of Great Yue, it is fitting to hold a special examination to select more talents.\"","Emperor Yuanyou agreed without hesitation.","\"Regarding the chief examiner, I have an immature idea.\" A smirk played on Song Yu's lips. Those familiar with him knew someone was about to be in trouble.","Several senior ministers in the Zichen Hall all turned their gaze to Song Yu.","\"I think Ye Shijie is quite suitable.\"","As soon as Song Yu's words fell, the entire Zichen Hall fell silent.","Ye Shijie? Hadn't this person been sidelined long ago?","And wasn't he once so infuriated by His Highness that he spat blood...?","Everyone's minds raced, but no one could connect Song Yu and Ye Shijie.","\"The chief examiner for the imperial examinations must be someone of unwavering integrity like Lord Ye. Whether for the county-level exams or the metropolitan exams, Lord Ye is qualified to be the chief examiner.\" Song Yu gave a sly smile. \"Therefore, I suggest assigning Lord Ye... to conduct inspection tours of examinations across the regions.\"","\"So, We would have to specially create a new official post for Ye Shijie—'Imperial Examination Inspection Commissioner'?\"","Emperor Yuanyou was also amused.","\"Your Majesty is wise.\"","\"Are you serious?\" Emperor Yuanyou couldn't remain calm.","\"After learning about Lord Ye's scholarship, I deeply repent for what happened in the past. So, I wish to place Lord Ye in a position truly suited for him, as a gesture of my apology.\"","Song Yu spoke with great emotion, though inside, a mischievous little version of himself was already jumping for joy.","Imperial Examination Inspection Commissioner?","Perfect for Ye Shijie!","\"Since the Crown Prince puts it this way, We grant it.\"","Emperor Yuanyou considered Ye Shijie's temperament and actually thought he was quite suited to be an examiner.","Under Shen Qingping's puzzled gaze, Song Yu's grin nearly reached his ears.","He had been drenched by the rain before, so now he would tear up the umbrellas of other candidates!","Tear them to shreds!","......","\"Your Highness, I still don't understand,\" Shen Qingping couldn't help but ask.","\"I don't understand either...\" Cheng Guang quickly chimed in.","\"Big Brother, we don't understand either...\" Prince Chu and Prince Qi also wore identical looks of confusion.","Seeing this, Song Yu smiled slightly and said to Liuxi, \"Liuxi, go ask Lord Ye to prepare a set of exam papers at the county-level difficulty. Tell him His Majesty wishes to test Prince Chu and Prince Qi.\"","Then he turned to the others. \"Don't worry, you'll find out tomorrow.\"","The next day.","Four small desks were neatly arranged in the courtyard of the Eastern Palace.","Shen Qingping glanced at the exam paper and chose to lay his head on the desk to sleep.","Cheng Guang was so anxious he scratched his ears and cheeks, inwardly cursing Ye Shijie countless times.","Prince Chu and Prince Qi looked as if their souls had left their bodies, staring blankly at the empty papers.","Prince Qi mustered his courage and looked at Song Yu:","\"Big Brother, if Ye Shijie becomes the chief examiner, won't it truly incite public outrage?\"","Song Yu hesitated for a moment, then still shook his head.","Suddenly, Cheng Guang jumped up, shouting at the top of his lungs, \"With this set of questions, if anyone among us here can get a perfect score, I, Cheng Guang, will kneel before him and call him 'Father'!\"","Song Yu was stunned.","Super... super promotion in seniority?"]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489: The Dandy Father's Unwavering Favor: A Resemblance of an Old Acquaintance","paragraphs":["\"This exam is too difficult, it's bound to cause public outrage.\"","Shen Qingping looked at the blank exam paper before him, with no intention whatsoever of picking up his pen to answer. He spoke idly.","Based on his understanding of His Highness, this move by the prince was definitely intentional.","When did those candidates preparing for the imperial examinations offend His Highness?","Hearing Shen Qingping's words, Song Yu seemed to ponder for a moment before speaking, \"Then have Ye Shijie prepare some practice booklets in his own style. Let those candidates get a bit mentally prepared first.\"","See, what a benevolent Crown Prince he was!","\"So Your Highness means those candidates should start enduring such physical and mental torment even before the exam?\"","Song Yu glared at Cheng Guang, who didn't dare to act up anymore.","\"This isn't torment, it's called early adaptation.\"","Song Yu said with a curled smile. He had written so many practice booklets back in the day, even getting personally scolded by Ye Shijie in a letter. Why should others be exempt?","A certain Crown Prince's heart was wildly secreting the poison of jealousy.","Half a month later, Ye Shijie's practice booklets circulated, plunging the entire literary circle into an eerie silence.","Upon learning of this, Emperor Yuanyou only tactfully instructed Shen Xiao to increase the protection around Song Yu.","Fearing Song Yu might be assassinated.","Late October.","\"Father Emperor, when shall we attack the Northern Di?\"","In the Zichen Hall, Emperor Yuanyou for the first time took a proper look at his youngest son.","Prince Qi's cheeks were flushed with excitement, and he looked full of vigor.","Emperor Yuanyou did not directly answer Prince Qi's question. Instead, he put down the vermilion brush in his hand and asked, \"How are things in your manor lately?\"","\"Quite well.\" Prince Qi was somewhat at a loss.","\"Haven't you always wanted a royal grandson? Since there's no royal grandson born in your manor yet, you dare go to the battlefield?\"","Emperor Yuanyou looked at Prince Qi. His youngest son, from some point on, seemed to have his head muddled, looking down on Xiyao all day long.","Those who respect others are always respected in return. Over time, he had grown weary of seeing Prince Qi's household.","\"Father Emperor, I am no longer fixated on the matter of a royal grandson.\"","Prince Qi had never had much to say to Emperor Yuanyou, so he appeared particularly restrained.","\"Ever since Ah Huan returned, I see every day how eldest brother treats Ah Huan, and I feel more and more ashamed. Xiyao is a good child, I treated her poorly before.\" Prince Qi pursed his lips, \"Children are a matter of fate, they cannot be forced.\"","\"Father Emperor, all I want now is to help Great Qi conquer the Northern Di.\"","A quarter of an hour later, Prince Qi walked out of the Zichen Hall in a daze.","Then, as if awakened, he frantically ran towards the palace gates.","Prince Chu's Manor.","Prince Qi rushed in like a gust of wind, his eyes red as he looked at Prince Chu and choked up:","\"Third Brother, Father Emperor praised me.\"","\"Father Emperor said I've made progress, that I'm starting to act like a prince.\"","As he spoke, Prince Qi squatted down, hugging his head and wailing loudly.","\"The first time... the first time he praised me...\"","......","\"What? You're not going to attack the Northern Di anymore?\"","Emperor Yuanyou's hand itched again, making as if to bend down and pick up a shoe sole.","Seeing this, Song Yu immediately pulled Song Shihuan, who was munching on pastries, in front of himself.","Emperor Yuanyou met Song Shihuan's almond-shaped eyes and finally straightened up, \"My back was a bit uncomfortable just now.\"","\"Imperial Grandfather, with General Gu in the northern frontier and the defense maps, this battle is certain to be a great victory.\" Song Shihuan paused, \"Father says he's taking me to find my master.\"","\"Your Majesty has more than just one son. The third and fourth princes should contribute some effort too. Send them both to the northern frontier as deputy generals, under Gu Mingning's command.\" Song Yu spoke in his usual provoking manner, \"Ah Huan hasn't seen her master in years. I'm worried something might have happened to him.\"","Song Shihuan listened, nearly anxious to the point of tears.","\"What kind of ominous talk is that? You're scaring the child.\" Emperor Yuanyou pulled Song Shihuan to his side, \"Ah Huan, tell your Imperial Grandfather about your master. Perhaps I might know.\"","Whoever taught Ah Huan so well certainly couldn't be an ordinary person.","Upon hearing this, Song Shihuan began to recount the events of that year in detail. Song Yu listened with utmost seriousness. Substituting Master Qingshan's face into the story, Song Yu truly understood Master Qingshan.","Raising Ah Huan had exhausted all of Master Qingshan's energy; naturally, he regarded Ah Huan as more important than his own life.","Song Yu's lips moved slightly as he spoke:","\"It sounds a bit like Master Qingshan of the Qingyun Realm.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was stunned for a moment, his eyes instantly lighting up, \"Ah Huan, your father is right! This master of yours matches Master Qingshan!\"","\"Indeed, only someone like Master Qingshan could teach a disciple as exceptionally skilled in formations as Ah Huan.\"","Emperor Yuanyou told Song Shihuan about Master Qingshan.","Song Shihuan's eyes grew somewhat distant, \"Master Qingshan...\"","\"He's unconscious. Could he be in mortal danger?\"","\"I'll take Ah Huan to the Qingyun Realm.\"","Song Yu voiced the thought that had weighed on his heart for months. This time, he would take Ah Huan personally to find Master Qingshan.","Emperor Yuanyou granted permission.","If it truly was Master Qingshan, then he was a benefactor to the Song family.","......","Along the journey, Song Shihuan was uncharacteristically quiet the whole time.","Song Yu slowly told Song Shihuan about Master Qingshan's deeds. Song Shihuan listened with great attentiveness, gazing at the distant, continuous mountain peaks. \"Father, I have a feeling. He is my master.\"","\"I misunderstood my master. I resented him for so long.\"","\"Master Qingshan would not blame Ah Huan.\" Song Yu ruffled Song Shihuan's head, \"If he is Ah Huan's master, he would fear nothing more than Ah Huan suffering. Beyond that, he fears nothing.\"","Not even death.","From the capital of Great Qi to the Qingyun Realm, Song Yu and Song Shihuan traveled post-haste for twelve full days.","Upon arriving at the Qingyun Realm, they happened to run into Qingling and his fellow disciples.","\"Who are you? Outsiders may not enter the Qingyun Realm freely.\"","Seeing this, Song Yu remained unperturbed. Instead, he looked gently at Song Shihuan, \"Ah Huan, don't be afraid. They seem to be disciples of Master Qingshan.\"","\"Ah Huan, go spar with them using a few fist techniques.\"","Song Shihuan nodded. If everything was as she surmised, the people before her were her senior brothers.","\"Song Shihuan of Great Qi, here to seek instruction.\"","With that, Song Shihuan moved towards Qingling with sharp, forceful fist strikes.","At first, Qingling's eyes were full of killing intent.","But the moment he crossed hands with Song Shihuan, an incredible realization exploded in his mind like fireworks.","The youngest, Qingchi, directly ignored the force of their punches and inserted himself between the two.","Everyone stared at the girl before them. Why did every move and stance of this young girl resemble their master's?","\"You... why have you come to the Qingyun Realm?\" Qingling asked, his voice trembling.","\"I've come to find my master.\"","Song Shihuan's eyes also reddened.","\"I was raised by my master's hand since childhood. Now that my master is gravely ill, I should attend to him at his side.\"","Qingling knelt on one knee, tears falling in large drops.","Their master lay unconscious.","They prayed day and night.","Thus, heaven bestowed upon them a clever, lovely young girl, bearing their master's imprint in every aspect."]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490: The Doting Father King Dotes on Me: I Am Not an Unloved Child","paragraphs":["\"Master.\"","After several years apart, Song Shihuan saw her master again, only now he was completely different from the man she remembered.","Her master should always be smiling kindly, wiping her sweat after she finished practicing her martial forms, and standing guard outside her door when she was afraid.","Not like this, lying pale-faced on a bed.","Song Shihuan walked to the bedside and carefully grasped Master Qingshan's hand. \"Master, it's Ah Huan. I've found you.\"","\"Grandma was seriously ill. I sold everything I could to pay for her treatment, but she still couldn't pull through. Yet even as she was leaving, she was still deeply concerned about you.\"","Outside the room, Qingling and the others stood quietly.","Song Shihuan recounted in detail to Master Qingshan all she had experienced since he left, talking for over an hour.","Finally, her emotions completely gave way. She slumped by Master Qingshan's bedside, sobbing,","\"Master, why won't you open your eyes and look at me?\"","\"Just look at me, please?\"","The sound of Song Shihuan's crying gradually filled the room. Song Yu's eyes darkened as he looked at Qingling. \"Where is your Mysterious Doctor?\"","\"This prince has some urgent business with him.\"","Seeing Song Yu's demeanor, which looked ready for a fight, Qingling swallowed the words that came to his lips. \"What business with the Mysterious Doctor?\"","That old man had a very strange temper. If Qingling just handed him over without asking, he'd surely face the old man's wrath later.","\"To save your master.\"","Song Yu firmly believed that as long as Ah Huan was here, Master Qingshan would surely be safe and sound.","Arriving at the Mysterious Doctor's dwelling, Song Yu was met with a closed door.","\"Even if you were the Emperor of Heaven himself, I won't see you!\"","\"This prince is not the Emperor of Heaven. This prince's daughter is the disciple Master Qingshan raised from childhood.\"","Bang—","The door swung open.","The Mysterious Doctor's face was full of astonishment. His hands kept moving as if calculating something, then he irritably ruffled the hair on his head. \"It shouldn't be... How could they have come to the Qingyun Realm at this time?\"","He didn't perform divinations often, but they were usually highly accurate.","Seeing this, Song Yu's imposing manner weakened somewhat for once.","Could this old man have divined his abnormality?","......","One hour later.","The Mysterious Doctor looked at Song Shihuan, whose eyes were swollen like walnuts, and circled her again and again.","He circled so much it made Song Yu feel a bit dizzy.","\"Can you cure him or not? Why do you keep staring at this prince's daughter?\"","The Mysterious Doctor shot Song Yu a glare.","Then he looked at Song Shihuan. \"Your master can be cured, but I have a condition.\"","\"What condition?\" Song Shihuan's voice was still somewhat hoarse. \"As long as it saves my master, I agree to anything.\"","\"The condition is simple. Tell me about the details of your interactions with your master in the previous years, and I will save him.\"","As soon as the Mysterious Doctor finished speaking, he received sharp glances from Qingling and the others.","If he could save him, why hadn't he done so before?","The Mysterious Doctor spoke up, \"Before, there was no medicinal catalyst. Now that the catalyst is present, he can naturally be saved.\"","Everyone then looked at Song Shihuan.","\"I agree.\"","Song Shihuan pressed her lips together. \"To save my master, will you be harmed?\"","Suddenly, the Mysterious Doctor's usually placid heart stirred unusually.","The reason he proposed this condition was his curiosity about what kind of bond was worth Master Qingshan protecting with his very life.","Now, he felt he was beginning to understand.","Inside the room.","Everyone sat together, waiting for Song Shihuan to speak.","Even Song Yu, who had already heard it once, sat up straight.","Song Shihuan's gaze fell upon Master Qingshan on the bed, filled with immeasurable dependence and reverence:","\"Because of Master, I was not an unloved child.\"","\"From the age of three, Master began teaching me martial arts. Every morning, I had to practice horse stance. Master was especially strict back then. Whenever my posture was incorrect, he would threaten me with a small wooden stick in his hand, but that stick never once landed on me.\"","Qingchi's face twisted.","Why didn't the stick fall on Little Junior Sister, but always on him?","Go ask anyone in the Qingyun Sect—who hadn't been hit by Master's stick!","\"When I started learning fist techniques, Master stopped using the stick. He said I had exceptional talent, encouraged and praised me every day for practicing well, and bought me all sorts of delicious treats in various ways. I was full of drive back then.\"","Song Yu's expression turned odd, finally understanding where Ah Huan's endless encouragement towards him came from.","So this was how Master Qingshan taught Ah Huan.","A direct inheritance.","\"Later, Master began teaching me formations. Every day, Master rose very early, setting up the sand divination board before calling me to get up. Day after day, it was like this. My heart ached for Master's labor, so I studied with extra diligence. I memorized every formation book Master gave me backwards and forwards.\"","With every sentence Song Shihuan spoke, someone in the room showed a strange expression.","This time it was Qingling's turn.","Steady as Qingling was, he couldn't help feeling a sour twinge in his heart.","Master had never treated them with such patience!","“Master didn't just teach me martial arts; he also taught me to read and write. My literacy enlightenment was started by Master. Every essay and discourse was guided by him. Master's kindness to me is as weighty as a mountain.”","A crystal tear slid from the corner of Song Shihuan's eye.","Because she had Master and Grandma, she never grieved over not having parents' love.","\"So I also did my best to be good to Master.\"","Song Shihuan spoke slowly, \"I knew Master had a weak heart, and old leg injuries. So I had to learn things faster and better, so Master wouldn't have to exert himself as much. And the better I learned, the happier Master was.\"","\"Master disliked greasy food, disliked cloudy days, loved wearing dark-colored clothes, liked the scent of sandalwood, and often had nightmares. I knew all these things, just as Master knew what I liked.\"","Qingling and the others suddenly paused, the sourness in their hearts instantly swept away.","This uniquely good treatment from Master was what Little Junior Sister deserved!","Especially Qingchi, who loved greasy things like braised pork knuckle, seemed to finally understand why every time he shared a meal with Master, he was nitpicked and punished with horse stance.","So it was because their tastes didn't align.","\"In the beginning, I was terribly afraid of thunder. Later, whenever it thundered, Master would stand guard outside my room, coughing now and then. After that, I was no longer afraid of thunder, because when it thundered, Master would be outside.\"","\"So whenever Master had nightmares, I would also go light sandalwood incense for him. That way, as soon as Master smelled the sandalwood, he would know I was by his side and wouldn't be afraid.\"","The Mysterious Doctor fell silent.","He understood why Master Qingshan was willing to protect her with his life.","\"Your fingertip blood is one of the medicinal catalysts. Paired with another catalyst, it can save your master.\"","Having said this, the Mysterious Doctor looked at Song Yu. Song Yu suddenly had a feeling that something very bad was coming.","He wouldn't have to go to Miaojiang again, would he?","\"You are the Crown Prince of Great Qi, so you need to go to Miaojiang to retrieve the other catalyst.\"","Boom—","Song Yu felt as if struck by lightning.","\"What? Is the Crown Prince unwilling?\"","\"Of course not. This prince will set off immediately.\" Song Yu smiled bitterly, feeling strongly that the Mysterious Doctor was deliberately messing with him.","Recalling the previous hardships of enduring wind, sun, and rain, Song Yu felt a sour ache in his very teeth.","That Miaojiang Saintess was truly difficult to deal with.","...","Song Yu, who had just arrived at Qingyun Realm, was promptly packed up and ready to be shipped off to Miaojiang.","Before leaving, Song Yu was as anxious as an ant on a hot griddle.","\"Leaving Ah Huan alone in Qingyun Realm, your father really can't rest easy,\" he fretted.","Song Shihuan looked at him with innocent confusion, not quite understanding where his worry stemmed from.","\"That Mysterious Doctor seems rather eccentric and shady. Ah Huan, you must keep your distance from him.\"","\"And then there's Qingling and the others. They're not as handsome as your father, nor as clever. Ah Huan, you don't need to be on overly friendly terms with them either...\"","Song Yu practically badmouthed everyone in the entire Qingyun Realm.","\"Father, then who will I talk to every day?\"","Faced with Song Shihuan's question, Song Yu's expression contorted.","That... seemed reasonable. He couldn't very well have Ah Huan talking to red bricks all day.","\"It's fine. Father will write a letter and have Gu Mingzhu come to keep you company.\"","The more he thought about it, the more Song Yu felt this plan was feasible. So, he penned a letter and sent it to the capital of Great Qi.","Only then did he reluctantly leave Qingyun Realm.","Little did he know, this trip would result in the number of people vying for his daughter's affection multiplying several times over.","...","While Song Yu was suffering hardships in Miaojiang, Gu Mingzhu packed her little knapsack, waved her small handkerchief to bid farewell to her old father, and left the capital with a face full of delight.","Behind her stood Gu Zheng, his face clouded with worry.","And Qingyun Realm welcomed its happiest, most joyful period.","As the only little girl in Qingyun Realm, Song Shihuan became the treasure cherished in everyone's palms. Each day, after spending time with Master Qingshan, she would be taken by her senior brothers to climb trees and rob birds' nests, or go down to the river to catch fish and shrimp.","Even the little cats and dogs of Qingyun Realm adored Song Shihuan, following behind her and barking joyfully without end.","\"Are you happy, Ah Huan?\" Qingling asked with a smile.","\"Very happy! If only Father could come back sooner, I'd be even happier!\"","Upon hearing this, Qingling clicked his tongue. The little girl played happily every day, yet not a single day passed without her keeping Master company or without her mentioning her father.","She was so well-behaved it made people want to give her the very best things in the world.","One day, Song Shihuan was fast asleep on an ancient tree, a handkerchief still covering her face.","Suddenly, a clamor of noise arose in the distance. Song Shihuan's ears twitched. Realizing something, she shot upright in an instant.","Meanwhile, outside Qingyun Realm.","Gu Mingzhu and Qingchi standing before her were staring each other down, wide-eyed.","\"Who are you?\" Gu Mingzhu asked.","\"And who are you?\" Qingchi retorted. He had probably guessed Gu Mingzhu's identity, but the thought of someone diverting his little junior sister's attention made his eyes shift craftily. \"No outsiders are allowed into Qingyun Realm.\"","\"You're calling me an outsider?\"","Gu Mingzhu threw down the knapsack slung over her shoulder and began stretching her limbs.","\"You look like an idiot, so you must be Qingchi. This lady's name is Gu Mingzhu. I'll only say it once, so you better remember it.\"","With that, Gu Mingzhu swung her fist straight towards Qingchi's forehead."]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491: The Spoiled Prince Dotes on Me: Indulging in Pleasure and Forgetting to Return","paragraphs":["\"One of our own, don't fight!\"","Song Shihuan came trotting over and saw the two people wrestling with each other.","Gu Mingzhu and Qingchi each had the other's arm locked in a hold, the bizarre posture leaving both of them unable to move.","\"Princess, this Qingchi clearly knows who I am, yet still called me an 'unauthorized person'. He really is just as 'missing a screw' as His Highness the Crown Prince said in his letter,\" Gu Mingzhu complained, never one to suffer in silence, her little mouth running a mile a minute.","\"A gentleman uses his words, not his fists, understand? You threw the first punch!\"","Qingchi increased the pressure in his grip. Gu Mingzhu's small face visibly flushed red from the strain. Clenching her teeth, she suddenly exerted force as well, making Qingchi nearly yelp in pain.","\"Let go first, then we'll talk.\"","Song Shihuan urged anxiously.","\"Let him let go first!\" Gu Mingzhu roared.","\"Let her let go first!\" Qingchi retorted, not backing down.","\"I'll count to three. Whoever doesn't let go, I'll ignore them!\" Song Shihuan said sternly. When she reached three, the two obediently released their holds at the same exact moment.","Neither had gained the upper hand.","Gu Mingzhu immediately linked her arm with Song Shihuan's. \"Princess, in the capital, I missed you so much I couldn't eat, couldn't sleep. I rushed here post-haste. Now that I see you, my heart feels all sweet.\"","Faced with such sweet talk, a smile immediately spread across Song Shihuan's face. She was coaxed away by Gu Mingzhu without so much as a backward glance at Qingchi.","Qingchi stood there dumbfounded.","It wasn't until Qingling patted him on the back. \"You, kid, rely on being the youngest to run wild all day in Qingyun Realm. Had your arrogance checked today, didn't you?\"","\"That Gu Mingzhu, her mouth runs faster than anyone's. The flesh on her cheeks jiggles when she walks, yet she 'couldn't eat'?\" Qingchi acted as if his tail had been stepped on. \"I must make Little Shimei see Gu Mingzhu's true colors!\"","Hearing this, Qingling facepalmed, beginning to reflect on how he and the other senior brothers had raised their youngest junior brother to be so naive.","\"Qingchi, is it possible, just maybe, that Little Shimei knows Miss Gu better than you do, and Little Shimei simply likes it when Miss Gu talks that way?\"","Qingchi felt the world spin.","Favoritism!","......","Gu Mingzhu's arrival turned the formerly harmonious Qingyun Realm completely upside down.","Because whenever Gu Mingzhu and Qingchi were put together, they were a force of chaos on the level of troublemaking demons.","\"My bird eggs?\" Qingchi stared at the empty nest and let out a sharp cry.","\"The bird eggs were... were all roasted and eaten by Miss Gu.\"","Third Senior Brother Qing Zi was the most honest. Watching the furious Qingchi, he pursed his lips. Would these two start fighting again?","\"Qingchi, they were actually quite tasty.\"","They had all gotten a share.","Qingchi's face instantly contorted. She had roasted all his bird eggs and didn't even save any for him!","Brimming with anger, Qingchi went to the lakeside, only to find Gu Mingzhu and Song Shihuan roasting fish and steaming shrimp.","\"So it was you who roasted my bird eggs?\"","\"Are you a bird that you call them 'your' bird eggs?\" Gu Mingzhu shot Qingchi a disdainful look. \"You dummy, I saved one for you, so stop your whining.\"","Qingchi, at maximum fury, had a bird egg shoved into his hands.","He awkwardly chewed a few bites and found it rather delicious.","\"I, the magnanimous one, shall not stoop to the pettiness of a lesser person.\" Qingchi swallowed the egg and started eyeing the fish and shrimp greedily.","\"Aren't you a general's daughter? How do you have these skills?\"","\"General Gu campaigns abroad year-round and knows best how to prepare things in the wild. Mingzhu is General Gu's daughter, so she's also very skilled at these things.\" Song Shihuan sat to the side, clean and pristine from head to toe, like a fairy.","This was actually because Gu Mingzhu had personally fussed over Song Shihuan's appearance.","Then, deciding the dressed-up Song Shihuan was too beautiful, she insisted Song Shihuan not enter the water.","Qingchi's gaze towards Gu Mingzhu instantly changed.","\"So it's Heroine Gu. My apologies, my apologies.\"","Anyone with skills like this was destined to be his playmate.","\"This old lady will let you off this time. Consider us friends forged through a fight.\" The flesh on Gu Mingzhu's little face still looked plump, but Qingchi could now somehow see a certain cuteness in it.","\"I'll be your assistant.\"","Qingchi eagerly trotted after her, busying himself happily.","Only Song Shihuan, who wanted to go into the water but couldn't, sighed.","Her life was hard. Really.","......","Great Qi, Zichen Hall.","Everyone in the hall was trembling with fear. The Emperor these past days was like a balloon ready to pop at any moment.","\"Third Prince, Fourth Prince, you are to lead troops and depart for Mobei immediately.\" Emperor Yuanyou's voice rang out, making everyone's hearts leap into their throats. \"Once there, remember, you are merely delivering the troops. How to deploy them is up to Gu Mingning. If anyone causes a major misstep due to your actions, I will have your heads.\"","Thud. The two princes knelt on the floor.","\"Your sons... your sons receive the command.\"","Then Emperor Yuanyou looked at Cheng Guang and couldn't help saying to him, \"You usually dare to impeach even me. Now that the Crown Prince is delayed in returning, why aren't you impeaching him?\"","\"This official does not dare.\" Cheng Guang wished he could vanish on the spot.","The Crown Prince and the Princess went to find their master. By reason or by sentiment, there was no fault to find. How could he impeach them?","Impeach them on what grounds?","\"You don't dare? Go back and reflect deeply on why you don't dare!\"","In less than half an hour, everyone present had been subjected to Emperor Yuanyou's indiscriminate verbal attacks, except for Shen Qingping.","\"Shen the Third, you can't always be busy handling cases. You must find time to write some letters to the Crown Prince and Ah Huan, telling them to come back and help share my burden.\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt bitter inside, having inexplicably become a lonely old man.","\"Your Majesty, this official will write shortly. But whether His Highness listens or not, this official cannot be sure.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was taken aback. Thinking of Song Yu's temperament, his anger flared up again.","\"Indulging in pleasure and forgetting home, this is simply indulging in pleasure and forgetting home!\"","He must find an opportunity to pass the throne on.","......","One month later, Song Yu returned to Qingyun Realm, utterly exhausted.","Unlike his previous stoic refusal to admit pain, this time Song Yu staggered the moment he stood before Song Shihuan, the grime on his face not even wiped away.","\"Father, you're injured!\"","Seeing Song Shihuan's worried expression, Song Yu forced a smile, then immediately hissed in pain, putting on a theatrically pitiful act:","\"Ah Huan, I brought the thing back. As long as we can save Master Qingshan, no amount of suffering on my part matters.\"","Having said that, Song Yu rubbed his knees for a moment, then supported his waist, putting on an act of being in pain everywhere.","Qingchi, standing nearby, couldn't help but speak up:","\"Your Highness, are you itchy? Bitten by bugs? If it's itchy, I actually have some ointment.\"","Song Yu's nostrils flared with anger.","Really, how was this Qingchi as troublesome as Gu Mingzhu?","So, Song Yu spoke through gritted teeth:","\"Thank you. This prince is not itchy. This prince is in pain.\""]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492: The Doting Father King Spoils Me: Master Is Fine, the Crown Prince Is Not","paragraphs":["The Mystic Physician seemed to sense the peculiar atmosphere. He quickly pricked Song Shihuan's finger with a silver needle before retreating into the house, closing the door swiftly behind him.","One must steer clear of trouble.","Song Shihuan stood before Song Yu, her almond eyes brimming with heartache that was about to overflow. She then turned to Qingling. \"Eldest Senior Brother, could you please take my royal father to change his clothes? Here is some excellent medicinal ointment. If there are places he cannot reach, I must trouble you, Senior Brother.\"","Song Yu suddenly regretted having cried out in pain earlier.","Rather than making Ah Huan sad, it would have been better to grit his teeth and bear it himself.","After Song Yu had changed and applied the ointment, Qingling's gaze towards him held several degrees more respect.","Once outside, Qingling grabbed Qingchi by the collar and started dragging him away.","\"Hey, Eldest Senior Brother, why are you grabbing my collar? I can barely breathe!\"","\"I've noticed you've been particularly fond of speaking out of turn lately. It seems the tasks assigned to you are still insufficient. Master will wake soon. If he sees you haven't made any progress, you'd better watch your hide.\"","Qingling's eyes were shadowed with complex thoughts. Just moments ago, he had seen marks on the body of this Crown Prince of Great Qi, signs of insect bites. It seemed he had indeed suffered greatly to rescue their Master.","Meanwhile, Song Yu felt the air had become much fresher after Qingchi left.","\"Let me see... feels like you've even gained a little weight on your face.\"","Song Yu reached out and pinched Song Shihuan's cheek. \"Father is fine. I was just exaggerating earlier. Qingling helped me apply the medicine; I'll be better in a couple of days.\"","Song Shihuan tugged at Song Yu's sleeve. \"Thank you, Father.\"","\"Why would there be any need for thanks between father and daughter?\"","Just as Song Yu was preparing to quietly enjoy a pleasant moment with his daughter, a familiar voice rang out, causing a vein on Song Yu's forehead to immediately begin throbbing.","He had just gotten rid of one Qingchi, and now here came Gu Mingzhu.","Gu Mingzhu came running over, sweating profusely, holding a letter high in her hand. \"Your Highness, Your Ladyship, it's a letter from Uncle Shen San!\"","Song Yu raised an eyebrow. Shen San could write letters?","Upon opening the letter, a single short line met his eyes:","\"His Majesty longs for your return with great anxiety. All at court are trembling with fear. Return with haste.\"","\"Father, what did the Teacher write?\" Song Shihuan, not as tall as Song Yu, couldn't see the letter in his hand.","\"He says we should stay at Qingyun Realm a while longer and properly relax,\" Song Yu said with a flawless, smiling expression.","\"Teacher is so kind,\" Song Shihuan said sincerely. \"I thought he was going to tell us to return.\"","\"Uncle Shen San is the best!\" Gu Mingzhu, hearing they could stay at Qingyun Realm longer, also jumped for joy.","Song Yu meticulously folded the letter and placed it back in the envelope.","Return with haste?","Not a chance.","...","Early the next morning, Master Qingshan awoke.","This time, upon waking, Master Qingshan's complexion was rosy, with no trace of illness about him.","Moreover, the first person Master Qingshan saw upon opening his eyes was Song Shihuan.","\"Master, you're finally awake!\"","Master Qingshan was momentarily stunned, then reached out to ruffle Song Shihuan's hair. \"Wonderful. I thought I might not see Ah Huan again.\"","\"From now on, whenever Master wishes to see me, you will.\"","Master Qingshan's heart settled completely, and his expression gradually relaxed.","Only then did he have the energy to look at the several disciples around him.","The usually most boisterous Qingchi was now as docile as a mouse seeing a cat, standing behind Qingling.","Master Qingshan nodded. Even the youngest disciple had tempered his nature. Time truly was the greatest teacher.","\"Qingling, you have worked hard.\"","\"As long as Master has recovered, this disciple's efforts are nothing,\" Qingling replied, also very excited, not even noticing Qingchi's peculiar demeanor.","The Mystic Physician examined Master Qingshan once more and finally pronounced:","\"Perfectly sound and well.\"","Everyone finally let go of their worries completely.","\"Master Qingshan, I am Mingzhu, the Young Lady's companion,\" Gu Mingzhu spoke up, following Master Qingshan's gaze. \"Your full recovery today is a joyous occasion for Qingyun Realm. Let's have the kitchen prepare a feast tonight to celebrate!\"","Song Yu facepalmed.","Qingchi secretly applauded.","With Master Qingshan's awakening, Qingyun Realm came fully back to life. Cheerful laughter could be heard in every corner. It wasn't until December that Song Yu, feeling a slight pang of conscience, proposed returning to the capital.","\"So soon?\"","Master Qingshan, holding Song Shihuan close, was clearly unwilling to let her go.","\"Master Qingshan, if Ah Huan and I are not back by New Year's Eve, my imperial father will most likely come charging here himself,\" Song Yu said with a weary look. If he could, he wouldn't want to return to the capital either.","Returning meant being beaten with a shoe sole and being impeached by gossiping court officials.","\"Then you go back by yourself. Leave Ah Huan here.\"","\"To be frank, whether I return or not isn't the main concern. In my imperial father's eyes, what matters is Ah Huan,\" Song Yu directly revealed the \"family hierarchy\" to Master Qingshan.","Master Qingshan was also caught in a dilemma.","\"Why doesn't Master come with us to Great Qi?\"","Song Shihuan tilted her head. \"You can also see the place where we used to live, see Grandmother, and see what Great Qi is like now.\"","Master Qingshan's heart was stirred.","Seeing an opportunity, Song Yu also quickly joined in persuading him, finally convincing Master Qingshan to nod in agreement.","On the day the group departed Qingyun Realm, Gu Mingzhu, looking at Qingchi following behind Master Qingshan, felt her eyelid twitch. \"Why are you coming too?\"","\"Eldest Senior Brother and the others were worried about the Master, so they asked me to accompany him to Great Qi.\"","\"But why you?\" Gu Mingzhu couldn't figure it out.","\"Naturally because I'm considerate and meticulous, capable of taking good care of the Master,\" Qingchi said while rubbing his nose.","In truth, it was because everyone else had important duties, and he was the only idler.","Gu Mingzhu nodded suspiciously upon hearing this, feeling the reason was rather odd.","\"Well, alright. When we reach the capital, I'll take you to my favorite food shops.\"","\"Great! I love eating.\"","...","On the twenty-fifth day of the twelfth lunar month, the group finally arrived at the capital.","Belatedly, Song Yu began to feel somewhat guilty. After settling Master Qingshan and Qingchi, he planned to sneak Song Shihuan directly back to the Eastern Palace.","Unexpectedly, as soon as they entered the palace gates, they encountered the expressionless Emperor Yuanyou.","Beside him were a resentful-looking Cheng Guang and Shen Qingping, who wore a helpless expression.","\"What a coincidence, Imperial Father, running into you here,\" Song Yu said, so embarrassed he wished he could sink into the ground.","\"No coincidence. I was waiting for you.\"","Emperor Yuanyou glanced towards the shadows. \"Shen Xiao, take the Young Lady to the Zichen Hall first to warm up. I'll be there shortly.\"","And so, before Song Shihuan could react, Shen Xiao whisked her away to the Zichen Hall in an instant.","Left behind, Song Yu's internal danger radar was blaring incessantly.","One moment, Emperor Yuanyou was smiling slightly. \"Did you enjoy your time at Qingyun Realm?\"","The next, he took off his shoe and advanced towards Song Yu with the sole in hand.","\"If I don't give you a thrashing today, I'm not your father!\"","\"Owwww~~\""]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493: The Dandy Father's Unwavering Favor: Victory in the Northern Di Campaign","paragraphs":["\"Father, your son also suffered greatly to retrieve the medicine for the Green Mountain Sect Leader,\" Song Yu shouted as he ran, occasionally getting hit a couple of times by Emperor Yuanyou, the pain making his eyes bulge out slightly.","Cheng Guang hesitated upon seeing this. As a subordinate of His Highness, should he step forward in this situation to shield the Crown Prince?","Thinking this, Cheng Guang looked up at Shen Qingping.","He saw Shen Qingping standing with his arms crossed, looking on as if watching a spectacle.","\"Why doesn't Minister Shen intervene?\" Cheng Guang couldn't help but ask softly.","\"One is the Emperor, the other is the Crown Prince. If you wish to intervene, Censor Cheng, please go ahead,\" Shen Qingping's tone didn't waver in the slightest. \"Moreover, you will witness scenes like this many times in the future. You'll get used to it.\"","The corner of Cheng Guang's mouth twitched.","It was the first time he had seen the imperial father and son so... down-to-earth.","\"Father, if you keep hitting, your shoe is going to wear out!\"","\"Father, if you keep hitting, Ah Huan will be waiting anxiously in the Purple Heaven Palace.\"","The last sentence had an effect. Emperor Yuanyou stopped his pursuit.","\"Pack your things right now and prepare to ascend the throne!\"","Shen Qingping felt a bit unsettled, having heard something rather astonishing.","\"Father, please just continue hitting me.\"","Song Yu even stepped right in front of Emperor Yuanyou, no longer dodging. \"That dragon throne is truly a hot seat. My backside can't take the heat, only the beating.\"","Joking aside, this precious chance to start over wasn't meant for being emperor, toiling like an old ox handling court affairs every day, not to mention having Cheng Guang on the side watching him like a hawk with a little whip.","Emperor Yuanyou was so angry he choked on his breath.","\"Then when are you willing to ascend the throne?\"","\"When the mountains crumble and...\"","Emperor Yuanyou laughed. \"Fine. Let's see just how much beating that backside of yours can take.\"","......","Purple Heaven Palace.","\"Imperial Grandfather, where is my father?\"","Seeing only Shen Qingping and Cheng Guang behind Emperor Yuanyou, Song Shihuan couldn't help but ask.","\"Oh, your father said the journey was tiring and wanted to rest early at the Eastern Palace.\"","Emperor Yuanyou said with a beaming smile, then took Song Shihuan's small hands to warm them. \"Are you happy to have found your master?\"","\"Very happy!\"","\"But your Imperial Grandfather was forgotten by Ah Huan in the Purple Heaven Palace for a long time.\"","Shen Qingping and Cheng Guang almost simultaneously averted their gaze; the scene was somewhat hard to watch.","Seeing this, Song Shihuan thought for a moment before speaking slowly, \"Then Ah Huan will stay in the side hall of the Purple Heaven Palace for two days to properly keep Imperial Grandfather company.\"","\"So good.\"","Emperor Yuanyou was easily appeased by Song Shihuan. Even hearing that Song Shihuan had been catching fish and shrimp in the Green Cloud Realm, he specially took her to the imperial garden to cast a net, hauling up his usually beloved goldfish one by one.","A picture of a decadent ruler.","The pitiful Song Yu was left alone and forlorn in the Eastern Palace.","\"With the Emperor targeting you so obviously, is Your Highness still unwilling to yield and ascend the throne?\" Shen Qingping asked with a smile.","\"Impossible, absolutely impossible!\"","Song Yu clenched his fists. This time, even if the bait were to confer the title of Grand Princess upon Ah Huan, he would not yield.","He would ascend the throne sooner or later anyway; Ah Huan's position as Grand Princess would be as easy as reaching into a bag to get something, a matter of time.","He had been completely fooled and led around by the old man before!","Seeing this, Shen Qingping laughed even louder. Such father-son rivalry was a great show!","\"Shen San, quickly tell me about recent court affairs. I have a feeling the old man is going to deliberately make things difficult for me and embarrass me during the morning audiences these next few days.\"","Song Yu sighed helplessly.","When there's no danger, the old man is the greatest danger.","......","The news of the great victory over the Northern Di arrived in the capital of Great Qi on New Year's Eve.","Using the defense maps provided by Song Yu, Gu Mingning led elite troops to thoroughly rout the Northern Di.","What Emperor Yuanyou found hardest to believe was that the one who personally slew the Northern Di general was Prince Qi.","At the New Year's Eve palace banquet.","\"Father, why are you hiding and withholding the victory report instead of announcing it publicly?\" Song Yu asked, somewhat puzzled.","\"The report says the fourth prince slew the Northern Di general. I feared the report might be erroneous and wanted to verify it further,\" Emperor Yuanyou still cared about face.","Hearing this, Song Yu was amused. \"You can rest assured, the report is definitely true. Take advantage of today, New Year's Eve, to let everyone share in the joy.\"","Who would have thought that the former songbird could now slay a Northern Di general.","Once the victory report was announced, the atmosphere of the palace banquet reached a climax.","Song Yu and the officials drank merrily together, enjoying great delight.","Meanwhile, Song Shihuan sat at a separate table for the children.","\"Eldest Sister, is the Green Cloud Realm fun?\" The one asking was Song Xiling, her eyes full of curiosity and innocence.","\"Eldest Sister, can you tell us about the Green Cloud Realm?\" Song Xiyao also chimed in, even snuggling up to Song Shihuan to act coquettishly.","Seeing this, Gu Mingzhu straightened her chest. \"Two Princesses, let me tell you!\"","This would save the Princess from getting a dry throat.","She, Gu Mingzhu, was the Princess's most loyal guard.","A few moments later, the table was filled with exclamations of \"Wow!\"","Song Shihuan was doubled over with laughter from Gu Mingzhu's vivid and animated storytelling. Seizing a gap while everyone was laughing, Gu Mingzhu quietly leaned closer.","\"Princess, in the future, I want to be a female general.\"","\"Good.\"","Their whispered conversation was overheard by Song Yu, who had walked over. For a moment, Song Yu seemed to see the shadow of himself and Shen Qingping from years past in Song Shihuan and Gu Mingzhu.","He had willingly appointed Shen Qingping as his Chancellor.","Ah Huan, in the future, would likely also willingly appoint Mingzhu as her general, right?","He and Ah Huan both had important, trusted confidants. How wonderful.","......","When Prince Chu and Prince Qi returned triumphant, their first action wasn't to ask Emperor Yuanyou for rewards, but to run up to Song Yu, looking at him with shining eyes.","\"Eldest Brother, we won the battle.\"","\"This Prince has seen the victory report. Courageous and strategic, truly worthy of our Song family.\"","Prince Chu and Prince Qi immediately puffed out their chests proudly like victorious roosters.","After all, Song Yu was now the person they admired most. Praise from their idol was sweeter than honey.","\"Third Uncle, Fourth Uncle.\" Song Shihuan called out sweetly.","Seeing this, Prince Qi immediately ran over, pulling out an exquisite little trinket from his robe. \"Here, Fourth Uncle specially brought this back for Ah Huan.\"","Gu Mingning, at the front of the procession, couldn't help but look over upon seeing this.","So this was the Fuan Princess whom his hopeless younger sister wrote in her letters, swearing to serve unto death?","Thinking of Gu Mingzhu, a smile also touched Gu Mingning's face.","After guarding the border for many years, he could finally return to the capital to reunite with his family.","\"It's getting late today. Everyone, return to your residences and spend the New Year well with your families,\" Emperor Yuanyou was also very happy. \"In a few days, I will bestow rewards according to your merits.\"","The territory of Great Qi had expanded severalfold within half a year.","This was something Emperor Yuanyou wouldn't have dared to dream of.","Thinking of this, Emperor Yuanyou looked at Song Yu. \"Come, let's go offer incense to our ancestors.\""]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494: The Doting Father Spoils Me: He Says Mother Is a Wonderful Person","paragraphs":["Facing the ancestral tablet, Song Yu devoutly offered three sticks of incense to his forebears.","\"Kowtow separately for your mother.\"","Emperor Yuanyou suddenly spoke. Song Yu was taken aback for a moment, but then, without asking any questions, knelt on the prayer cushion and kowtowed three times with solid thuds.","The atmosphere in the room suddenly grew quiet.","In truth, when the father and son were alone together, Emperor Yuanyou rarely mentioned his deceased first wife, to the point that Song Yu had previously been completely unaware of the resemblance between Song Shihuan and the late empress.","Even the portrait of the late empress kept in the Zichen Hall, Song Yu had only ever glanced at a few times.","More often, it was Emperor Yuanyou reminiscing alone.","But today, on this day of national celebration, Emperor Yuanyou was suddenly overcome with an irrepressible urge to confide.","\"Your mother was an exceptionally good person.\"","Emperor Yuanyou began slowly, his gaze fixed on the tablet full of sorrow. His once vibrant wife was now just a cold, wooden tablet.","\"We met in humble circumstances. On the day she married me, I swore I would give her a good life.\"","Song Yu remained kneeling, not interrupting the Emperor's words.","\"But not long after our marriage, I began fighting wars all over, placing her in danger. We were apart more than together. Yu'er, your mother never blamed me. Every time I returned home, there was always a warm meal waiting. Your mother always worried about me suffering hardships away from home. It has been so long since I last tasted your mother's cooking.\"","\"Whenever I think of these things, I feel I failed your mother.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's gaze slowly shifted from the tablet to Song Yu. \"Yu'er, I was overjoyed on the day you were born. I even secretly kowtowed to the heavens, thanking them for granting me a child born of your mother.\"","\"I have also wondered countless times what would have happened if, on that day, your mother hadn't taken the arrow for me, and I had died instead.\" Emperor Yuanyou gave a wry smile. \"If that had truly been the case, your mother, wise and perceptive, would surely have raised you to be just as fine a man as you are now.\"","\"Unlike me, who let you suffer grievances for so many years.\"","\"Father, taking that arrow for you was Mother's own willing choice.\" With this one sentence from Song Yu, tears began to stream down Emperor Yuanyou's face.","Emperor Yuanyou was suddenly overwhelmed with grief. Addressing the tablet, he said:","\"Fen'er, if your spirit watches from above, look well upon our son. He is accomplished and kind-hearted, and he has a daughter who looks very much like you.\"","\"If only you were still here... that would be wonderful...\"","Emperor Yuanyou staggered away. Song Yu remained kneeling on the cushion for a long time.","All these years, the imperial harem had only a handful of consorts. Once, a court official presented the Emperor with a beauty who resembled his mother, but the Emperor instead stripped that official of his post.","As for his own formerly dissolute and unrestrained behavior, while his father seemed harsh on the surface, readily ordering beatings with the bamboo, in reality, he had also been indulgent.","Song Yu smiled, showing his white teeth to the tablet.","\"Mother, the man you married is rather decent, though not as good as your son.\"","Then his expression dimmed somewhat. \"If only you were still alive. Then you could dote on me, just as Lady Chang dotes on Ahuan.\"","\"Forget this lifetime. In the next life, whether as royalty or commoners, I will still be your son.\"","...","That evening, the portrait of the late empress from the Zichen Hall was carefully delivered to the Eastern Palace by Wu Qi.","\"Your Highness, His Majesty says this portrait rightfully belongs to you.\"","Wu Qi's voice was somewhat hesitant as he spoke, for when the Emperor handed over the painting, his expression was one of utter agony, as if having flesh cut away.","It was entirely possible he would want it back in a few days.","Seeing this, Song Yu nodded. Only after Wu Qi had left did he, with trembling hands, unroll the portrait.","It was the first time Song Yu had examined the late empress's face so carefully.","He was so absorbed that he didn't notice Song Shihuan approaching his side.","\"Is this Grandmother Empress? Indeed, I resemble Grandmother Empress the most.\" Song Shihuan gazed at the portrait with fascination, unable to resist reaching out to touch the face in the painting.","A strange feeling welled up in Song Shihuan's heart.","She shared a similar face with the person in the portrait, and her father was the bond connecting them.","\"Yes, this is Ahuan's Grandmother Empress.\"","Song Yu looked at Song Shihuan for a moment, then suddenly spoke again. \"We must hide this portrait well, so your imperial grandfather doesn't ask for it back.\"","No one knows a father better than his son. He understood the old man's temperament perfectly.","Sure enough, just two days later, Emperor Yuanyou wanted the portrait back.","\"Once a gift is given, it shouldn't be taken back.\"","In the Zichen Hall, father and son stared each other down.","\"I am the Son of Heaven. What I say goes,\" Emperor Yuanyou declared righteously. \"Return it to me at once. Otherwise, I feel as if something is missing from my heart.\"","\"No. I still need to speak with Mother every day now.\"","Song Yu refused decisively. \"Mother has listened to you call out 'Fen'er...' for decades. Shouldn't she hear me call her 'Mother' a few times?\"","Fen'er, look at how rebellious this scoundrel is!","Emperor Yuanyou had just finished this thought in his mind when he realized Fen'er's portrait was already in the Eastern Palace.","\"Will you give it back to me or not?\"","\"No.\"","Song Yu met Emperor Yuanyou's gaze directly. \"Ahuan also needs to speak with Grandmother Empress. This portrait should belong to your son now.\"","In the end, Emperor Yuanyou did not get the portrait back, and in his anger, he couldn't eat a bite that day.","Wu Qi was frantic with worry.","The next day, Song Yu went to the Zichen Hall again. Seeing Song Yu's empty hands, Emperor Yuanyou's hopeful spirit deflated once more.","But then Song Yu spoke directly. \"I had a dream. I dreamed of Mother.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's ears perked up subtly.","\"I dreamed that no one died in that assassination attempt. The Imperial Guards had laid their plans in advance, so you did not die, and Mother did not die either.\"","\"I dreamed that Mother resided permanently in the Kunning Palace, and the Zichen Hall was practically deserted, as you would rush to Kunning Palace the moment court adjourned. I grew up under the guidance of you and Mother. I possessed both your foresight and Mother's decisive courage and kindness.\"","\"Within a year of my beginning my studies, you established me as Crown Prince, ordering important court ministers to cultivate me into a man accomplished in both civil and military arts. You always said I was your and Mother's pride.\"","\"In that court, everyone praised Mother as a virtuous empress and called me the future of Great Qi. We were all exceptionally happy.\"","\"When I reached marriageable age, Mother personally selected my Crown Princess. Two years after our wedding, we had a daughter, named Ahuan. On that day, the sky was filled with rosy clouds, and songs of celebration seemed to echo across the land.\"","\"Father, that is happiness, isn't it?\"","Emperor Yuanyou couldn't help but imagine the scene from the dream Song Yu described.","It was exactly the same as what he had envisioned countless times himself.","Emperor Yuanyou nodded involuntarily.","\"Father, the dream felt so real.\"","Song Yu's lips curved into a smile. \"So I believe it was a dream sent by Mother, wanting to tell us that she is always with us.\"","As long as they do not forget, the departed never truly fade away.","Perhaps, somewhere, he was indeed living such a happy and peaceful life."]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495: The Spoiled Prince's Unwavering Doting on Me [Complete]","paragraphs":["The thirty-seventh year of Yuanyou.","The Great Qi had already swallowed the lands of Great Yue and the Northern Di. Miaojiang voluntarily expressed its willingness to pay annual tribute to Great Qi, while the Qingyun Realm directly announced to the outside world that Great Qi's Princess Fu'an was the only female disciple of the Qingyun Sect.","Thus, the land under heaven was, in essence, unified.","Shen Qingping's official rank was promoted again, directly becoming the Minister of Personnel, in charge of the evaluation of officials.","The Eastern Palace.","Master Qingshan had been staying at the Eastern Palace ever since arriving in the capital of Great Qi at the end of the previous year, showing no intention whatsoever of returning to the Qingyun Realm.","Upon hearing this, Gu Mingning also started visiting the Eastern Palace every now and then, chasing after Master Qingshan, insisting on calling him master, and would have a small quarrel with Qingchi every three days and a big one every five.","The Eastern Palace was bustling with noise and excitement every day.","Having just finished dealing with thorny court affairs, Shen Qingping stepped into the Eastern Palace, but upon hearing the clamor, he immediately wanted to retreat.","Shen Qingping felt a headache coming on.","\"Young man of the Shen family.\"","Master Qingshan called out to Shen Qingping and tossed him a book of boxing techniques.","Seeing Shen Qingping's astonished expression, Song Yu couldn't quite manage a smile. He hadn't expected that even in this second chance, Third Shen was almost working himself to exhaustion again, just like before.","\"I know you're busy, old man, but you must also take care of your health.\"","Master Qingshan always felt an inexplicable pity for Shen Qingping, always hoping he would be strong and healthy, living a long life.","\"Master, I've never practiced boxing since I was a child,\" Shen Qingping smiled awkwardly; he was completely clueless in this area.","\"Have Qingchi teach you, or that young man from the Gu family, either is fine.\"","Master Qingshan chuckled happily, \"You must practice it well. This old man has come to understand that the Eastern Palace relies on you.\"","\"Of course,\" Song Yu slowly interjected, \"Master, back then when I chose him as my study companion, he didn't refuse. Once he boarded my pirate ship, he can't get off.\"","\"Pirate ship? What pirate ship? Where are the pirates?\"","Qingchi, in between scuffling with Gu Mingning, still found time to ask, \"If there are any, you must take me along!\"","The smile instantly vanished from Master Qingshan's face.","Some disciples posed no threat to him in martial arts, yet they could utterly ruin his reputation among the master circles.","He must have been blind when he woke up back then to think this kid Qingchi had changed his ways.","\"Qingchi.\"","Hearing Master Qingshan's voice, Qingchi immediately stood obediently before him. \"Master, what do you need from your disciple?\"","\"Have you finished practicing today's boxing techniques?\"","\"Your disciple will go practice right now.\"","Qingchi swiftly slipped away. The smoothness of his movements made Song Yu nod repeatedly. He could learn this trick for later use against the old man.","Of the thirty-six stratagems, fleeing is the best.","......","Song Yu hadn't expected this move to come in handy so soon.","One month before Song Shihuan's birthday, Emperor Yuanyou began harping on about abdication again.","\"This emperor is old and useless...\" Emperor Yuanyou put on a mournful, sentimental air.","\"Your Majesty is extremely hale and hearty. You can still beat me so hard you break the sole of your shoe,\" Song Yu simply didn't buy Emperor Yuanyou's act.","Emperor Yuanyou was left speechless.","\"Ah, next month is A'Huan's birthday. It's the first birthday since she was found and brought back. If you could enfeoff her as the Grand Princess during the birthday banquet...\"","Song Yu wore an expression of 'just as I expected.' The same old routine, but he was no longer the naive self of the past!","\"When you're truly too old to carry on, then I, your son, will succeed and enfeoff A'Huan as the Grand Princess. From what I see, A'Huan isn't particularly eager for that title of Grand Princess either.\"","Having said that, Song Yu imitated Qingchi's style and whooshed away, disappearing from before Emperor Yuanyou.","Emperor Yuanyou was stunned for a moment, then swore a curse at the empty air.","Shen Mingwen was urgently summoned to the palace.","The moment he saw Emperor Yuanyou, he was bombarded with a question that left him dizzy.","\"Minister Shen, is there any way to make the Crown Prince ascend the throne immediately?\"","Shen Mingwen was taken aback. \"Your Majesty, is the Crown Prince unwilling?\"","Emperor Yuanyou felt a bit embarrassed, but for the sake of his own happy life, he nodded with restraint.","Shen Mingwen couldn't believe his ears and eyes.","How could there be a Crown Prince who didn't want to become emperor?","\"Perhaps... have the Princess persuade him?\"","\"Do you think this emperor hasn't tried?\" Emperor Yuanyou sighed. \"That scoundrel has already tipped off A'Huan. Whenever I mention ascending the throne, A'Huan starts evading the topic, making this dragon throne seem like a hot potato.\"","As he spoke, Emperor Yuanyou's eyes suddenly lit up. \"How about having your third son help this emperor persuade him?\"","\"Ah?\" Shen Mingwen's face was a picture of shock.","\"Your third son has followed the Crown Prince since childhood, as close as if they grew up sharing the same pair of trousers. If your third son speaks, he will surely be able to persuade the Crown Prince.\"","The more Emperor Yuanyou thought about it, the more reliable it seemed, and he directly entrusted this glorious mission to Shen Qingping.","......","That night, Shen Mingwen looked at Shen Qingping, not knowing how to begin.","Should he say, 'Son, your father went to the palace and brought back a huge task for you'?","\"Father, is there something on my face?\"","Shen Qingping couldn't help but reach up and touch his own face.","\"My son, His Majesty wants you to persuade the Crown Prince to ascend the throne as soon as possible.\"","Upon hearing this, Shen Qingping was momentarily stunned. He was probably the person who best understood why His Highness was unwilling to ascend the throne—afraid of being worked to death on the dragon throne.","In the past, he had been full of aspiration to become Prime Minister. Now, just being the Minister of Personnel, he already felt utterly exhausted.","Not only did His Highness want to delay ascending the throne, but he himself also wanted to become Prime Minister later.","Thinking of this, Shen Qingping righteously and sternly refused Shen Mingwen.","\"Father, your son dares not presumptuously discuss matters of the imperial throne.\"","With that, he also imitated Song Yu and Qingchi and made a swift escape.","Several days later.","\"Sigh.\" Song Yu sighed.","\"Sigh.\" Shen Qingping echoed with a sigh.","\"Sigh?\" Song Shihuan didn't know why the two were sighing and instinctively sighed along. \"Father, Teacher, what's wrong?\"","\"A'Huan, your father doesn't want to become emperor so quickly. Being emperor is so tiring—rising earlier than the rooster, sleeping later than the dog, being watched by the censors every day, unable to leave the palace freely.\" The more Song Yu spoke, the more he felt the old man had ill intentions. Last time, he at least held on until A'Huan's coming-of-age ceremony. This time, he wanted to shirk his duties so early.","\"And your Imperial Grandfather is in the prime of his life, at an age where he should be striving hard.\"","Song Yu glanced in the direction of the Zichen Hall. \"He can't always be thinking about having fun.\"","As he spoke, Song Yu suddenly came up with a good idea. \"A'Huan, how about after your birthday banquet, your father takes you traveling around?\"","Out of sight, out of mind.","Shen Qingping also nodded on the side. If you're going traveling, please be sure to take me along, thank you.","Before Song Shihuan could answer, a voice full of anger sounded from behind the three of them.","\"Thinking of slipping away?\"","Emperor Yuanyou sneered. \"Shen Xiao, tie up the Crown Prince.\"","A few moments later, Song Yu was trussed up.","Emperor Yuanyou reached out and patted Song Yu's shoulder:","\"Come, your Imperial Father will take you to experience what it feels like to sit on the dragon throne.\"","Behind them, Song Shihuan stood there dumbfounded.","Wait... is Father going to become emperor so soon?"]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496: Extra: Even an Emperor Needs to Dare to Slack Off (1)","paragraphs":["The first year of Zhaowu, June.","Once Song Shihuan's coming-of-age ceremony had passed, the officials from the Ministry of Rites once again brought up the matter of selecting consorts for the imperial harem, with a determination that bordered on threatening to dash themselves to death against the palace pillars if Emperor Song Yu refused.","In response, the retired Emperor Yuanyou just smirked, thoroughly enjoying the spectacle.","\"Ah-Huan, you'd better not go to the Zichen Hall these days. Come play at my place instead; it's too vexing over there,\" Emperor Yuanyou said leisurely, reclining on his lounge chair. \"This time, I'm quite curious to see how your father plans to handle those court ministers.\"","\"In my opinion, he should just select a few consorts to enter the palace. That's how an emperor should be.\"","And then spend every day being led around by the nose by scheming concubines.","That's the burden an emperor ought to bear!","Song Shihuan's mouth twitched. Ever since her grandfather abdicated, his back no longer ached, his legs became nimble, and he spent his days fishing, teasing birds, and occasionally watching her father's troubles for amusement.","Thinking of her father's temperament, Song Shihuan shot a discreet glance at Emperor Yuanyou.","\"I'm afraid Father won't let himself be controlled by the court ministers.\"","\"Any emperor must yield to balance the various factions!\"","Emperor Yuanyou grew so animated that flecks of spittle flew. \"I was like that in my day, and your father will certainly be the same.\"","A hint of a smile touched Song Shihuan's eyes.","But... her father had once been a genuine, unadulterated playboy, with a temperament even her grandfather couldn't pin down.","Considering this, Song Shihuan propped her head in her hands. If Grandfather was preparing to watch her father's spectacle, then she... would prepare to watch the court ministers' spectacle instead.","...","Zichen Hall.","Song Yu was so furious smoke seemed to be rising from his head.","\"These people are kneeling outside my Zichen Hall, blocking my way to see Ah-Huan!\"","And every now and then, they would shout a few times, \"We beg Your Majesty to issue an edict for the selection of consorts.\"","What an utterly infuriating bunch.","It drove Song Yu to the brink.","\"Your Majesty, this servant will go fetch Her Highness the Princess immediately,\" Liuxi hurriedly offered. At this moment, Song Shihuan was like a divine savior who could extinguish the fire in Liuxi's mind.","But Liuxi didn't even get to see Song Shihuan.","Seeing Liuxi return empty-handed, Song Yu let out a cold laugh. \"What, did the old man stop you?\"","\"The Grand Emperor said not to bother the Princess with vexing matters.\"","A series of cold chuckles followed. Liuxi felt that His Majesty had most likely gone mad.","Shen Residence.","Shen Qingping entered the study and addressed Shen Mingwen, who was leisurely practicing calligraphy:","\"Father, the people from the Ministry of Rites are making rather excessive trouble this time.\"","\"If no one was backing the Ministry of Rites this time, would they dare to be so bold?\" Shen Mingwen sighed. \"With the rear palace completely empty, all the noble families are waiting. Even I cannot dissuade them.\"","Even the most ordinary commoners have wives and children at home. What kind of affair is it for the emperor of a nation to sleep alone in the Zichen Hall every night?","\"Father, perhaps you didn't grasp my meaning.\" Now serving as Prime Minister, Shen Qingping commanded an awe-inspiring presence without needing anger. \"My meaning is, if those officials from the Ministry of Rites don't restrain themselves soon, His Majesty will truly begin to discipline them.\"","\"Don't forget, from the very beginning, His Majesty was never what one might call a 'good sort'.\"","Shen Mingwen felt the urge to cover his son's mouth again.","But his son's official rank was a bit too high now. Shen Mingwen awkwardly withdrew his hand. \"How can you speak of His Majesty that way?\"","\"Based on my understanding of His Majesty, he has already reached his limit of tolerance.\"","Shen Qingping looked at Shen Mingwen. \"If His Majesty truly resorts to countermeasures, you, as the Imperial Tutor, should also be mentally prepared in advance.\"","With that, Shen Qingping strode away.","These fools at court, if they still think the Emperor will be like the Grand Emperor, they are gravely mistaken.","A scoundrel who feared nothing from childhood—do they truly think a few years of behaving properly means his nature has changed?","...","Song Shihuan and Emperor Yuanyou made a pact not to interfere in this matter.","But Song Shihuan was genuinely worried about Song Yu, so she ordered the small kitchen to send him fire-reducing tea three times a day, each time with a different preparation.","\"He's a grown man,\" Emperor Yuanyou said, his tone dripping with jealousy.","Song Shihuan merely smiled without replying.","Suddenly recalling the time her father was impeached by the officials, she had a premonition that the court ministers' comfortable days were about to end.","Zichen Hall.","Song Yu looked at the fire-reducing tea placed before him. Even before drinking it, his anger began to subside rapidly.","\"Your Majesty, the Princess sends the tea three times a day, precisely on schedule. It shows she keeps you in her thoughts.\"","These words hit right at Song Yu's heart.","The old man might be able to snatch Ah-Huan's person away, but Ah-Huan's heart would always remain with him, her father!","\"I know Ah-Huan's feelings/heart's intent. I'm not angry. Liuxi, prepare the meal.\"","Not only would he eat, he would eat heartily.","Then he would properly contend with these court ministers who seemed to have forgotten who was in charge.","That day, a small table was placed before each of the court ministers kneeling outside the Zichen Hall.","\"Esteemed Ministers, His Majesty pities you for kneeling and has specially bestowed this fire-reducing tea upon you.\"","The ministers, nearly suffering heatstroke, looked up one after another.","Were their ears failing? They actually heard that the Emperor was bestowing tea upon them.","After drinking the tea, the court ministers left the palace, each believing the Emperor had finally realized the importance of selecting consorts and was prepared to agree.","Everyone's steps as they left the palace were light.","After all, kneeling every day was taking a toll on their constitutions.","Upon receiving the news, Emperor Yuanyou stood with his hands on his hips, looking triumphant:","\"See! I knew he couldn't hold out for long!\"","\"Grandfather, it's your turn to place a piece.\"","Song Shihuan suppressed a smile and, after Emperor Yuanyou made his move, slowly placed another piece.","The smile gradually vanished from Emperor Yuanyou's face, and he began trying to take back his move.","\"Ah-Huan, how has your chess skill improved so much lately? I can never win against you anymore!\"","It's quite embarrassing to admit.","...","Early the next morning.","The court ministers entered the palace for the morning court session with almost a swagger, especially those who had been bestowed the fire-reducing tea the day before. They all felt certain the matter of selecting consorts could be finalized at today's court session.","The officials took their positions in the court hall as usual, awaiting Song Yu's arrival.","But they waited a full quarter of an hour, and the dragon throne remained empty.","Everyone began whispering among themselves. Some even dared to ask Shen Qingping, who simply kept his eyes closed in meditation, not even sparing a glance in their direction.","See? The Emperor has made his move.","The civil and military officials stood in the court hall like a bunch of fools for half an hour, only to be met by Liuxi:","\"Esteemed Ministers, His Majesty is feeling unwell today and will not attend the morning court. If there are urgent matters, please trouble Prime Minister Shen to handle them for His Majesty.\"","Feeling unwell?","Everyone was stunned. That old man Mei Zhilin has even left the capital for leisure travel. How could His Majesty possibly be unwell?","\"Oh, and also, His Majesty says he will not attend tomorrow's morning court either,\" Liuxi said with a smile.","Don't ask. If you do, the answer is he's feeling unwell."]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497: Extra: Even an Emperor Needs to Bravely Slack Off (2)","paragraphs":["\"What? He's actually not holding court?\"","Emperor Yuanyou's voice rose an octave. Wu Qi, frightened, hurriedly brought water to the emperor. Why didn't the Grand Emperor realize he was old now, an elderly man?","Before Imperial Physician Mei left, he had given repeated instructions: they must not let his travel plans be ruined, and they must keep a close watch on the Grand Emperor's health.","\"Grand Emperor, His Majesty is feeling unwell. It's only right for him to recuperate in the Zichen Hall for a couple of days.\"","\"His constitution is tougher than a dog's! How many times has he ever been 'unwell' since he was a child?\" Emperor Yuanyou downed the tea in one gulp and then began pacing in circles. \"That scoundrel is definitely skipping court on purpose. Good heavens, how am I supposed to explain to our ancestors that I chose an emperor who doesn't hold court?\"","\"Well, well, Father's health is truly remarkable.\"","A voice sounded. When Emperor Yuanyou saw Song Yu, his eyes widened like bronze bells. He knew it! The scoundrel was perfectly fine!","He simply didn't want to hold court.","\"Why aren't you holding court?\" Emperor Yuanyou asked sternly. \"As the emperor, holding court is mandatory.\"","\"Isn't holding court just for handling state affairs?\"","Song Yu sat down on his own, looking utterly at ease. \"Right now, state affairs are handed over to Shen San and Zheng Fang to handle on my behalf. If there's anything they truly can't manage, I'll step in personally. Not holding court doesn't delay anything.\"","\"You!\"","\"What about me?\" Song Yu looked at Emperor Yuanyou with an innocent expression. \"Those old fogies were bullying me. If I let them push me around once, there would be countless times after.\"","\"Father, those court officials gave you plenty of trouble back in the day too. Don't you want to see me put them in their place?\"","Emperor Yuanyou was taken aback. Of course he did.","But he also didn't want to see this scoundrel having an easier time than he did when he was emperor!","Seeing the conflicted look on Emperor Yuanyou's face, Song Yu chuckled softly. \"Don't worry, I'll help you vent your anger.\"","By the time Song Yu left, Emperor Yuanyou still hadn't fully processed what happened.","An hour later, a roar of fury shook the Imperial Garden, startling birds into flight.","\"That damned scoundrel!\"","\"He actually used venting my anger as an excuse and managed to rope me into his scheme!\"","Bullying me in my old age and weakness!","......","The next day, Song Yu did not hold court.","On the third day, Song Yu still did not hold court.","By the sixth day, the officials were thoroughly panicked.","\"When will His Majesty's health recover?\" Unable to see the emperor, the officials could only muster their courage to pull Shen Qingping aside and ask.","By now, Shen Qingping's resentment was potent enough to nurture an evil sword immortal. These past few days, he had been worked so hard his back was about to break. The emperor and the court officials were locked in a battle of wits, so why was his desk piled high with memorials? Why was he the one suffering?","\"You guess.\"","Shen Qingping's smile sent chills down the officials' spines.","\"Think carefully about how His Majesty actually fell ill.\"","If they didn't figure it out soon, the one falling ill would be Shen Qingping himself.","Zichen Hall.","Song Yu looked at the expressionless Shen Qingping before him, a rare flicker of guilt rising in his starry eyes.","\"Liuxi, quickly serve the Prime Minister some tea. Brew the new premium tea I just acquired. I haven't even been willing to send any to the Grand Emperor.\"","\"When does Your Majesty plan to resume court sessions?\"","Shen Qingping got straight to the point. If he had even an ounce of rebellious intent, he could probably drag the emperor off the throne right then and there.","\"I'm waiting for them to beg me to hold court!\"","Song Yu slumped in the dragon throne, thinking it was nowhere near as comfortable as a reclining chair—too hard and rigid.","\"They were practically riding roughshod over me before. If I don't show them who's boss, I might as well let you be the emperor.\"","Shen Qingping: ......","\"I can't hold out much longer,\" Shen Qingping finally managed to say after a long pause.","Song Yu immediately gave Shen Qingping a look that said 'I understand.'","\"Don't worry, I'm planning to add some spice for the officials. They'll soon be begging me to properly hold court.\" Song Yu took a sip of tea. \"Actually, I don't think being emperor requires working oneself to the bone.\"","\"Basking in the sun and listening to music every day, that's the life of an immortal.\"","Shen Qingping immediately grew wary. This was bad. He had a feeling the emperor was reverting to his former playboy ways.","A pressing question: What to do when the emperor wants to slack off?","......","The next day.","Song Yu ordered several fighting cocks to be brought into the palace, along with quite a few crickets, looking very much like he intended to take up his old pastimes.","That very night, news spread that the emperor was hosting cockfights in the Zichen Hall with several young eunuchs!","This time, Shen Mingwen and Ye Shijie were directly approached by the officials.","\"Lord Shen, Lord Ye, you two are the Emperor's tutors. You must advise His Majesty.\"","Now the officials were genuinely terrified. Had they actually driven a perfectly good emperor back to his former dissolute ways?","The most terrifying part was that, currently, Song Yu was truly the only person fit to sit on the throne.","The Prince of Chu had inexplicably shaved his head and entered the Buddhist path.","The Prince of Qi had been saddled with the reputation of a 'lark' and was happily hunting and roaming the northern borders.","There was no one left to rival the emperor!","Shen Mingwen's eyelid twitched. \"My fellow ministers, we all know His Majesty's former temperament. Now that His Majesty has been pushed to this state, the only one who can get a word in with him is the Grand Emperor.\"","Shen Mingwen dared not mention Song Shihuan's name.","Hadn't they noticed that both the Grand Emperor and the Emperor had, without consultation, kept the Princess out of this affair?","Thus, the officials went to beg before Emperor Yuanyou.","Seeing the very courtiers who had once stubbornly opposed him now coming to plead, Emperor Yuanyou felt a perverse sense of satisfaction.","But his refusal was equally blunt.","\"I won't go.\"","\"I'm old. I can't lift a shoe sole anymore. He is the emperor now, the most powerful person under heaven. You caused this mess, you deal with it. Don't bother me.\"","He was already annoyed that the scoundrel had successfully manipulated the officials.","After much further agonizing, and upon seeing several jars of fine wine being transported into the palace, the officials finally capitulated. One by one, they knelt again outside the Zichen Hall.","Their previous kneeling was to force Song Yu to select consorts; now, their kneeling was to beg him to hold court.","\"Now you know to come beg me?\"","Song Yu wore a look of haughty pride. \"It was you lot insisting I select consorts that made me ill!\"","What a massive black pot to lay at their feet.","The courtiers felt they could no longer stand straight.","\"We beg Your Majesty to hold court and to refrain from touching those mind-numbing distractions like fighting cocks and crickets.\"","\"Who are you calling mind-numbing?\" Song Yu raised an eyebrow.","\"This minister misspoke.\"","Song Yu nodded. This was more like how courtiers should behave.","\"Fine. Then I will reluctantly drag my ailing body to court tomorrow.\"","Watching the officials express their profuse gratitude, Song Yu's mind began to stir again.","This time, he had successfully not held court for a full nine days.","Didn't that mean he could potentially hold court only once every three days in the future?","That would give him two days to sleep in every three days.","The more Song Yu thought about it, the more feasible it seemed.","He just needed to find another opportunity to test the limits of the court officials.","He was determined not to let the old man's habit of enduring hardship and toil be passed down smoothly!"]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498: Extra: Even an Emperor Needs to Bravely Slack Off (3)","paragraphs":["Song Yu finally attended court and decisively handled many long-pending matters.","His solutions could all be considered perfect.","At this point, the civil and military officials could no longer focus on the matter of selecting concubines. With tearful eyes, they looked at Song Yu. Such a wise and mighty emperor, if he didn't want to select concubines, then so be it. Perhaps one day the Emperor himself would propose it.","As long as the Emperor was willing to attend court and handle state affairs, everything was negotiable.","Even Cheng Guang broke precedent and praised Song Yu a few times.","Song Yu simply felt refreshed and invigorated. Indeed, being an emperor required character; one couldn't always indulge these court officials.","After court adjourned, Song Yu gleefully ran to Emperor Yuanyou to show off how effectively he managed his subordinates.","\"Father, you are simply too soft-hearted, which is why you were led by the nose by the court officials.\"","Emperor Yuanyou tightened his grip on the teacup in his hand, suppressing the impulse to splash the tea in Song Yu's face.","\"Some methods work once, but if used repeatedly, they lose their effectiveness,\" Emperor Yuanyou said with a forced smile.","So infuriating.","\"No matter, your son has plenty of such methods.\"","Before leaving, Song Yu didn't forget to take Song Shihuan with him, claiming grandly, \"Thank you, Father, for recently helping your son take care of Ah Huan. Your son plans to make an incognito inspection tour in a few days, so I'll take Ah Huan with me.\"","Emperor Yuanyou's breath hitched.","Incognito inspection tour?","This scoundrel, as emperor, still wants to casually go on incognito tours? In his dreams.","......","Inside the Zichen Hall.","Song Yu looked at the travel plan submitted by the Ministry of Rites, his brows furrowed tightly enough to crush a fly.","\"We are going incognito. Do we need this many people?\"","\"This... since ancient times, the standard for an emperor's incognito tours has always been like this.\" The Minister of Rites, having learned from past mistakes, now dared not directly oppose Song Yu.","\"My travel route is strictly confidential. There's no need to inform local officials in advance of where I'm going. I intend to observe the true conditions of the people. As for my safety, entrusting it to the Imperial Guards puts me at ease.\"","The Ministry of Rites naturally did not agree.","If it were truly done this way, the Ministry of Rites would likely be criticized by all officials.","But the next day, the ministers once again saw the empty dragon throne.","A vein throbbed on Shen Qingping's forehead. He was numb, truly.","If he had known that being Prime Minister meant cleaning up after the Emperor, perhaps letting Cheng Guang take the position wouldn't have been so bad.","With the experience from the first time, the officials weren't overly panicked this time; they even felt they could wage a war of attrition with the Emperor.","However, the news Liuxi brought this time wasn't about Song Yu being unwell.","But rather...","\"Honorable ministers, His Majesty set off with the Princess early this morning and will return in a month.\"","The civil and military officials widened their eyes in disbelief, the scene both comical and absurd.","The Emperor just... slipped away?","After court adjourned, Liuxi, under immense psychological pressure, approached Shen Qingping. \"Prime Minister, His Majesty left an imperial decree for you.\"","A few moments later, looking at the decree appointing him as Prince Regent, Shen Qingping's smile grew increasingly unsettling.","\"Liuxi, I cannot accept this decree. Keep it to return to His Majesty.\"","Prince Regent?","If he were to accept this decree, he dared to wager his own head that the Emperor wouldn't spend more than half the year in the palace!","Song Yu merrily took Song Shihuan traveling all over, leaving behind a fuming Emperor Yuanyou and a resentful Shen Qingping.","One after another, dismissal orders came from various regions. Local officials became apprehensive and began genuinely striving to be good officials who loved the people as their own children.","After all, the Emperor was elusive, and one never knew when he might wander into their jurisdiction.","If anything went wrong, their lives would be at risk.","A month later, Song Yu finally brought Song Shihuan back to the capital.","Shen Residence.","\"Prime Minister, you must advise His Majesty.\"","For the first time, Cheng Guang showed such respect to Shen Qingping, mainly because the Emperor truly lacked ambition!","Holding the largest territory in history, yet not studying new policies to benefit the people, and now even morning court had become less than three times a week.","Shen Qingping slowly put down the brush in his hand. \"But don't you think the effects of His Majesty's month-long tour were better than if he had stayed in the palace?\"","Cheng Guang, Zheng Fang, and others were stunned.","\"On this trip, His Majesty dealt with six local officials. Now, local officials no longer dare to be as negligent as before.\" A flicker of hesitation passed through Shen Qingping's eyes. \"Could it be that His Majesty has found the true way of being a sovereign?\"","This question had puzzled Shen Qingping for several days.","Could it be that inaction is the true form of action?","Cheng Guang looked horrified. Was their diligent Prime Minister also going to be led astray?","If that were the case... the consequences would be unthinkable.","......","In the second year of Zhaowu, the civil and military officials' bottom line for Song Yu had dropped to its lowest.","As long as Song Yu was willing to hold court once every three days, the officials considered him a diligent emperor.","As for incognito inspection tours, they had become commonplace.","Song Yu had already left the capital three times, each time infuriating Emperor Yuanyou.","Why did this scoundrel find being emperor so enjoyable?","Later, Emperor Yuanyou figured it out: because Song Yu had a good Prime Minister.","Zichen Hall.","\"Shen San, will you be the Prince Regent or not?\"","Song Yu sat on the dragon throne, but his desk was covered with all sorts of strange curios, while the desk in front of Shen Qingping was piled with memorials.","\"No.\"","Shen Qingping answered crisply and decisively. \"I have requested many times to rest at home, but Your Majesty has never granted it.\"","Song Yu coughed lightly a few times. If Shen San rested, then he would be completely unable to rest.","Good brothers are meant to be useful at times like this.","A few moments later, Shen Qingping looked up with a serious expression. \"Your Majesty, I would like to confirm something with you.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Can the Princess... approve these memorials?\"","Shen Qingping appeared calm on the surface, but his palms were sweating. The crucial question that would determine whether he could catch his breath was this pivotal one right now!","\"She can.\"","Song Yu hadn't considered Shen Qingping's ulterior motives at all and answered naturally. \"Ah Huan is even smarter than I am. Of course she can handle memorials. She'd probably do a better job than both of us.\"","\"However... Ah Huan is very busy now. Not only does she keep the old man company, but the Qing Sect Leader also often asks for her company. I'm afraid she doesn't have the time.\"","\"No matter. It's enough for me to know that the Princess can approve memorials.\"","Shen Qingping let out an almost imperceptible sigh of relief.","Dawn. He had finally seen the dawn.","Meanwhile, Song Shihuan, who was accompanying Emperor Yuanyou, sneezed heavily.","\"Ah Huan, have you caught a chill?\"","Emperor Yuanyou quickly asked.","\"It's nothing. I just feel like someone is talking about me.\"","Song Shihuan rubbed her nose, and her right eyelid twitched a few more times.","She had a feeling... it wasn't anything good they were saying."]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499: Extra: Even an Emperor Needs to Bravely Slack Off (4)","paragraphs":["\"Grand Tutor, you asked for me?\"","Inside the Zichen Hall, Song Shihuan looked somewhat puzzled at Shen Qingping, while Song Yu beside her stole a glance before quickly lowering his head again.","Anyway, whatever Shen San said next had nothing to do with him.","\"Your Highness, there are numerous affairs of state at present. If you are willing, I would like to seek your instruction on matters I cannot decide. What do you think?\"","Song Shihuan was a bit slow to react. \"Grand Tutor can seek instruction from His Majesty the Emperor.\"","\"His Majesty is not often in the capital.\" Shen Qingping uttered these words almost through gritted teeth.","\"That's fine.\"","Years later, Song Shihuan would regret these three words countless times.","Hearing Song Shihuan's reply, Shen Qingping felt completely at ease. He even felt that if the Emperor left the capital again now, his heart wouldn't ripple at all—as long as the Princess was left here for him.","Shen Qingping returned to the Shen residence in high spirits.","Even the memorials in his hand seemed adorable.","A princess participating in governance was not without precedent, but it required a reasonable opportunity. Whenever Shen Qingping had a free moment, he began thinking about how to create such an opportunity.","Until a month later, Shen Qingping came to the Zichen Hall again.","\"I request Your Majesty to leave the capital once more for an incognito inspection tour.\"","Song Yu's head shot up with a whoosh, his face full of question marks.","What did Shen San just say? He didn't quite catch it.","\"While Your Majesty is on the inspection tour, I will release several long-pending major issues. At that time, with no one in the court able to make a decision, the ministers will naturally beg the Princess for help. Then the Princess can rightfully handle the affairs of state.\"","\"Does the Chancellor think I am useless?\" Song Yu pointed at himself incredulously.","Shen Qingping gave a slight nod.","Song Yu cursed.","\"If Your Majesty could be as diligent as the Retired Emperor, I wouldn't have to resort to such a plan.\"","Shen Qingping looked at Song Yu. Even Cheng Guang couldn't impeach Song Yu effectively now—if he tried, the man simply wouldn't attend court the next day.","It could be said to be the most devastating chapter in Cheng Guang's career as a censor.","\"Fine! So I just have to leave, right? I'll pack up and go immediately!\"","Song Yu packed his luggage overnight and began his days of traveling abroad.","......","\"This matter is of great importance, not something we officials can resolve.\"","In the court, the hundred officials were as anxious as a pot of boiling porridge.","\"But we can't reach His Majesty now. Perhaps we should invite the Retired Emperor to preside over this.\"","The officials then sought out Emperor Yuanyou. On the way, they suddenly felt a deep nostalgia for the days when Emperor Yuanyou was on the throne—those were truly happy times.","But they did not get their wish to see Emperor Yuanyou.","\"Your Excellencies, the Retired Emperor has been feeling unwell recently and has already retired to rest.\"","'Feeling unwell' again.","The ministers' faces twisted, already having a conditioned response to the phrase 'feeling unwell.'","Just as everyone was at a loss, Shen Qingping suddenly spoke up. \"Why not ask the Princess to decide?\"","\"The Princess?\" The courtiers hesitated.","\"Now the Retired Emperor is ill, and His Majesty is who-knows-where. The only one who can decide this is the Princess.\" Shen Qingping pretended to sigh. \"Gentlemen, don't forget, the Princess is capable of both literary governance and martial prowess. She will certainly have no problem handling such matters.\"","\"It's just that we fear...\"","\"Fear what?\" a courtier couldn't help but ask.","\"We fear the Princess might be unwilling to step forward.\"","Thus, the officials' line of thinking shifted from 'how can we let the Princess preside' to 'how can we get the Princess to preside.'","When Song Shihuan saw the hundred officials begging before her, the corner of her mouth twitched.","She had a strong feeling she was being set up.","\"Your Highness, the common people cannot wait!\"","Facing the earnest gazes of the officials, Song Shihuan sighed and offered a perfectly sound solution. Shen Qingping seized the moment to bring up several other thorny issues. Song Shihuan handled them one by one, resolving everything swiftly.","The way the officials looked at Song Shihuan had completely changed.","Who said a princess couldn't participate in governance?","......","Song Yu was away from the capital for a full two months this time.","When he returned, there were no ministers squatting at the palace gate waiting for him, no censors with runny noses and tears demanding he uphold justice.","Everything was eerily quiet.","\"Liuxi, where is everyone?\" Song Yu felt somewhat unaccustomed to it.","\"Your Majesty, they are all with the Princess.\"","A quarter of an hour later, Shen Qingping slowly arrived at the Zichen Hall. Over the two months, the weariness around Shen Qingping had completely vanished, replaced by a leisurely calm.","\"Shen San, quickly tell me what has happened in the last two months!\"","Song Yu couldn't wait.","Shen Qingping felt he was a genius.","He had discovered the Princess's talent for statecraft.","Speaking of how Song Shihuan handled court affairs, Shen Qingping talked nonstop for a full two hours.","\"I mentioned to the Princess that the burden I carried was too heavy while other court officials were too idle, so the Princess made some adjustments. Now I also have one or two hours of leisure time each day.\"","Indeed, sometimes inaction is the greatest action.","Compared to Your Majesty, the Princess is bolder in employing people, more decisive in handling matters, and effortlessly skilled in tackling difficult state affairs.","It's as if... she is a natural-born... decision-maker.","That night.","The ruler and his minister lay in their respective recliners, enjoying the cool in the courtyard of the Zichen Hall.","\"Shen San, it's better to take it easy.\"","Song Yu felt even the air carried the scent of flowers. Compared to toiling away in the hall approving memorials, this kind of life suited him better.","Shen Qingping also took a deep breath. \"Yes, this kind of life is the good life.\"","\"Shen San, won't this tire Ah Huan out?\" Song Yu secretly resolved that if Ah Huan felt too tired, he could reluctantly reduce the frequency of his trips out of the capital.","But Shen Qingping shook his head.","\"During Your Majesty's absence from the capital, the Princess only spent one hour each day handling the most pressing government affairs.\"","\"For those less urgent matters, the Princess arranged for court officials to handle them crosswise, then spent another quarter-hour spot-checking to ensure the officials' handling was reasonable.\"","\"Even the Retired Emperor has praised the Princess's method highly.\"","Shen Qingping glanced at Song Yu. Not only that, the Princess also had time to accompany the Retired Emperor and the Qing Shan Sect Leader, and could even go shopping with Little Mingzhu.","Song Yu was truly convinced.","\"Indeed, even an Emperor must have the courage to be himself.\"","\"Why does Your Majesty say that?\"","\"If not for this, how could we have discovered Ah Huan's ability so quickly?\"","Song Yu swung his feet. He would probably be the most leisurely and carefree emperor in the history of Great Qi, right?","Shen Qingping glanced at Song Yu, not wanting to puncture his statement.","Not only the most leisurely emperor.","But also the first emperor who managed to get his court officials completely in line!"]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500: Extra: Even an Emperor Needs to Bravely Slack Off (5)","paragraphs":["Ever since the civil and military officials discovered Song Shihuan's talent for governance, they suddenly became indulgent towards the occasionally slacking-off Song Yu.","Even when Song Yu deliberately skipped court for five days, the ministers had no reaction.","They also stopped scrutinizing Song Yu's harem and instead began selecting suitable consorts for Song Shihuan.","\"What?\" In the Zichen Hall, Song Yu jumped three feet high. \"Finding a consort for Ahuan? Drive them all away! Not a single candidate on this list is acceptable.\"","Song Yu was so angry his liver ached. These ministers were really meddling in things that were none of their business.","Liuxi silently shrank his neck back.","See, it would have been better if these people had directed their energy towards the Emperor instead.","The Gu Residence.","\"What? I'm on the list too?\" Gu Mingning stumbled, nearly twisting his ankle, then turned to look at Gu Zheng with a pleading expression. \"Father, save your son!\"","That wasn't a list of consort candidates; it was a list from the Book of Life and Death!","There were always those who were blind and wanted to harm him!","Before Gu Zheng could speak, he first let out a sigh. \"Do you have a girl you fancy? If so, I'll arrange a marriage for you immediately.\"","\"How do those officials from the Ministry of Rites always manage to dance right on the Emperor's red line?\" Even Gu Mingzhu couldn't help but speak up. \"The more the Emperor dislikes something, the more determined they are to do it.\"","With the way the Emperor treasures the Princess, it's highly likely he'll want someone to marry into the family in the future.","Gu Mingning wore an expression of utter despair.","He spent every day immersed in the military camp, just wanting to focus on training soldiers properly.","...","To facilitate Song Shihuan's handling of government affairs, Song Yu specially prepared a separate desk for her in the Zichen Hall.","Sometimes, when he was too bored, Song Yu would leisurely watch Song Shihuan discuss matters with the officials.","One day.","\"Currently, the assessment of Da Qi's officials is of utmost importance. If the Ministry of Personnel cannot conduct careful evaluations and makes further mistakes, I suggest you all retire and enjoy your old age at home. At least you can preserve your reputations.\"","The officials from the Ministry of Personnel knelt on the ground, not daring to rise.","The corner of Song Yu's mouth twitched. Ahuan's words were even more direct than his own.","\"Da Qi's national treasury is prosperous; there is no need for harsh taxes. Instead, what is taken from the people must be used for the people. If the Ministry of Revenue cannot adapt to Da Qi's development and make changes, we should promote some new scholars to refresh the thinking there.\"","\"...\"","Those thorny tasks that had the ministers complaining incessantly were all resolved by Song Shihuan in just a few words, leaving Song Yu utterly dumbfounded.","Finally, Song Shihuan slowly raised her eyes. \"I heard you have recently been selecting candidates for my consort?\"","The hall instantly fell silent. No one dared to speak first.","\"I do not need you to make selections for me. Do you understand?\"","Song Shihuan's words carried heavy pressure as they swept towards the courtiers. Everyone hurriedly responded:","\"Your subjects acknowledge our fault.\"","The Eldest Princess of Da Qi, the sole female direct disciple of the Qingyun Sect's leader, naturally had the final say. She did not need them to arrange consort candidates.","When only the father and daughter remained in the Zichen Hall, Song Yu swallowed hard. \"The matter of the consort... is resolved just like that?\"","Then what about back when he, to avoid selecting concubines, feigned illness and stayed cooped up in the palace for several days? What did that count for?","Song Shihuan nodded. \"If I don't like something, I just tell them directly that I don't like it.\"","\"If they comply with me, then the matter is dropped.\"","\"If they don't comply, I will take direct action myself. This is what Imperial Grandfather taught me.\"","Song Yu nearly ground his silver teeth to dust. Why didn't the old man teach him? He only knew how to watch his jokes!","...","By the sixth year of Zhaowu, Song Yu had completely thrown the burdens of state onto Song Shihuan, spending his own days traveling outside the capital.","From large prefectures down to county magistrates.","For every place where Song Shihuan issued a government decree, Song Yu would go to see how it was being implemented. Letters from all corners of the realm streamed back to the Zichen Hall, and Song Shihuan would read each one carefully, then adjust the decrees based on the actual situation.","By then, public sentiment throughout Da Qi for both Song Yu and Song Shihuan had reached an unprecedented high.","Emperor Yuanyou had also grown old and no longer spent his days wanting to see Song Yu make a spectacle of himself.","Instead, as if realizing something, he was eager to impart all his skills to Song Shihuan.","\"Ahuan, now that we have the hearts of the people, we must never betray this trust.\"","\"No one is perfect, and the same goes for those in court. You must utilize their strengths and grasp their weaknesses. Only then can you make them serve loyally and wholeheartedly. Ahuan, do you understand?\"","\"Imperial Grandfather, water can carry a boat but also overturn it. I understand these principles.\"","Song Shihuan, now twenty years old, had completely shed her childishness. Dressed in fiery red Eldest Princess robes, the phoenix crown on her head accentuated her majestic and awe-inspiring presence.","\"Yesterday, I dismissed the Minister of Rites. Before Father left, he didn't take the imperial seal, so I took it out myself and stamped the decree.\"","Song Shihuan's tone was light, but the smile on Emperor Yuanyou's face did not diminish in the slightest. \"For what reason?\"","\"The Ministry of Rites is in charge of rituals, sacrifices, and imperial examinations. If its vision is limited only to the family affairs of nobles and royalty, it's better for them to return home and farm the land, so we can select new people to take charge.\" Song Shihuan looked into the distance. \"He has a daughter who has long been waiting to be married, and a son around my age. This man's ambitions have grown too large.\"","Emperor Yuanyou laughed even more heartily.","Ahuan's methods were sharper and more severe than his or Yu'er's. Sometimes, she even greatly resembled that kid Shen San.","After all, calling him 'Teacher' for a time had subtly influenced Ahuan.","\"Imperial Grandfather, Da Qi is now thriving. Your granddaughter wishes to issue a decree to mobilize the entire nation's strength to build schools extensively, so that all children have a place to study. Only through reading can they understand reason. When the new generation grows up, Da Qi will truly achieve the passing of the torch, generation after generation, without end.\"","\"An excellent plan.\"","Emperor Yuanyou looked at his granddaughter in the prime of her youth, possessing a drive and courage that neither he nor Yu'er had anymore.","Two more years passed. Song Yu took Song Shihuan out of the palace to observe the people's conditions.","Wherever they went, the common people lined the streets to welcome them. Shouts of \"Long live the Emperor\" and \"Long live the Princess\" soared to the skies.","The people all looked towards Song Shihuan. Any commoner who could meet her gaze became so emotional that they welled up with tears.","Then, Song Shihuan walked through the crowd and finally stopped in front of a little girl.","The little girl's clothes were dirty, but her eyes were very bright.","\"Good child, how old are you? Have you learned to read?\"","\"Replying to Your Highness the Eldest Princess, I am ten. The school reduces the fees by half for wandering children like me, and lets me copy books to cover the tuition, so I have learned to read.\"","\"Thank you, Your Highness the Eldest Princess.\"","A wave of warmth came from the top of her head. Disregarding the dirt on the little girl, Song Shihuan actually reached out and gently ruffled her hair.","The little girl's eyes instantly reddened, filled with excitement and disbelief.","Song Yu, standing to the side, also smiled.","This trip out had made him realize just how fervent the people's support for Ahuan was—far more, it seemed, than for him, the Emperor.","Tsk.","Good thing he had bravely chosen to slack off."]}]);
